"heading","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"url":"/config-updates#the-guard-and-the-client-threshold","content":"The guard and the client threshold"},"867":{"id":"/config-updates-39","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"**What's on this page**"},"868":{"id":"/config-updates-40","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Which files go stale and why `git pull` cannot fix them"},"869":{"id":"/config-updates-41","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"The two passes of `update-configs`, and the flags that select one"},"870":{"id":"/config-updates-42","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"That env comments always refresh from the twin, even when values stay"},"871":{"id":"/config-updates-43","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Where the command may run, and where it refuses to"},"872":{"id":"/config-updates-44","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"The long form of the `.env.sample` comments: GitHub external auth, Grok profile mode, public hosts, the Spark `agent` group"},"873":{"id":"/config-updates-45","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"That the vault rewrites the managed keys before a bring-up interpolates them, and\nnothing else in the file"},"874":{"id":"/config-updates-46","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"**What this enables**"},"875":{"id":"/config-updates-47","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Bringing an old checkout back to a runnable state with one command"},"876":{"id":"/config-updates-48","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Telling a ported env key apart from a value you set yourself and must keep"},"877":{"id":"/config-updates-49","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Two kinds of file go stale in this repo, and because neither of them is\nchecked in, `git pull` cannot fix either one for you. `update-configs` is the\none command that refreshes both, and it is written to be safe to run when you\nare not looking closely at the diff."},"878":{"id":"/config-updates-50","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"These four sections are also the long form of the `.env.sample` comments that\npoint here: GitHub external auth, Grok profile mode, public hosts, and the\nSpark `agent` model group. Where a topic page already owns a subject, this page\npoints at it instead of restating it."},"879":{"id":"/config-updates-51","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#keeping-a-checkouts-config-current","content":"Run it after you pull, not before: a pull is what changes the templates these\ntools copy from. `bazelisk run` feeds the real checkout (`BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY`),\nnot the runfiles copy, so the env pass rewrites the live `.env` beside\n`docker-compose.yml`."},"880":{"id":"/config-updates-52","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"**The env files.** `docker-compose.yml` builds its variable references in two steps:"},"881":{"id":"/config-updates-53","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"`${VAR}` inside `expose` expands during the shell phase, so compose never sees those\nvariables and a changed value needs a rebuild"},"882":{"id":"/config-updates-54","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"an unset variable collapses to `127.0.0.1:57620:57620/tcp`, which fails to bind"},"883":{"id":"/config-updates-55","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"So the host ports and addresses live in a key=value env file - `.env` for the stable\nstack, `dev-stack.env` for the dev one - and each has a checked-in twin beside\nit that carries the keys and explains them in the comment lines above."},"884":{"id":"/config-updates-56","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"A pull that renames, adds or retires a key silently changes what the stack runs on."},"885":{"id":"/config-updates-57","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"**The workspace config.** `~/.grok/AGENTS.md`, `~/.tmux.conf` and the `~/.coder`\nand `~/.agents` seeds are materialised inside each workspace when it first boots\nand are never revisited after that."},"886":{"id":"/config-updates-58","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"`~/.grok/config.toml` and the code-server `~/.local/share/code-server/User/settings.json`\nare the two rendered files: each is that workspace's own, written from the template on every\nstart, so a temporary hand-edit there survives until that workspace restarts and reaches no\nother workspace, while a re-push plus a restart re-renders it from the latest template."},"887":{"id":"/config-updates-59","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"The shared overlay `~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` is a rendered file too, but\nthe boot writes it only while absent, so the API keys an operator put there\nsurvive every restart."},"888":{"id":"/config-updates-60","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-goes-stale","content":"A re-pushed template only reaches workspaces\nthat have been **start**ed or **restart**ed since the push - **stop** and\n**start** is what re-runs the provisioning script and therefore re-runs\n`before_config`."},"889":{"id":"/config-updates-61","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"`env` reconciles one env file with its twin. It:"},"890":{"id":"/config-updates-62","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"keeps every value you have set"},"891":{"id":"/config-updates-63","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"fills a key the twin adds with the twin's default (or a reusable value already\nset in a sibling live file - `.env` filling `dev-stack.env`)"},"892":{"id":"/config-updates-64","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"moves a key the twin no longer declares into a commented trailer at the end of the\nfile - parked, with its value and its explanation still readable, rather than deleted"},"893":{"id":"/config-updates-65","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"Comment lines always come from the twin, even when every value stays as you\nset it, so a pull that only rewrote an explanation still lands in `.env`. The\nrewrite lands in a staging file and replaces the live file only at the end,\nwith mode `600` kept."},"894":{"id":"/config-updates-66","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"On a TTY the pass then walks every key that is new this pull or still a placeholder\n(`change-me…`, `NOTSET`, `YOUR_LAN_IP`)."},"895":{"id":"/config-updates-67","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"An empty value whose example default is also empty is the intended value (LAN-only\n`STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS`, a parked MCP flag) and is not asked again."},"896":{"id":"/config-updates-68","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"Enter keeps a sibling's value or the example default."},"897":{"id":"/config-updates-69","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-env-pass","content":"A missing live file is created from the twin only after a `Y/n` confirm.\n`--non-interactive` (and `--dry-run`) list those keys and write no answers. A\n`summary:` line closes the pass."},"898":{"id":"/config-updates-70","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"One other writer touches the env files, and it is not this tool."},"899":{"id":"/config-updates-71","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"With `INFISICAL_ENABLED` on, `bazelisk run //scripts:dev-stack -- up`,\n`bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack -- up` and `bazelisk run //scripts:update-stack` each\npull the env file from the vault immediately before compose interpolates it, through\n`infisical_pull` in `scripts/lib/infisical.sh`."},"900":{"id":"/config-updates-72","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"That pass **does** overwrite values you set, and only the twelve it manages: the keys\nlisted in `infisical/managed-secrets.txt`, which are the stack's service credentials.\nEvery other key in the file - the ports, the hosts, the naming parts, the URLs, the\nfeature flags - keeps what you set."},"901":{"id":"/config-updates-73","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"A managed key the vault does not hold, or holds empty, is left alone too, with one\n`warning:` naming the key instead of a blanked line, and a failed export leaves the\nfile untouched so the bring-up runs on the credentials it already has."},"902":{"id":"/config-updates-74","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"With the flag off - the shipped default - that branch never runs and the file keeps\nevery value it has, and `bazelisk run //scripts:update-stack -- --dry-run` plans the\nfetch and writes nothing."},"903":{"id":"/config-updates-75","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-writer-of-the-env-files","content":"operate/secrets.md owns the vault, its inventory and its verbs."},"904":{"id":"/config-updates-76","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-workspace-pass","content":"`workspace` re-materialises the stack-owned config inside the targets you name."},"905":{"id":"/config-updates-77","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"The reseed set is the home-relative targets the templates seed, listed by\n`seed_seed_targets` in `scripts/lib/config_seed.sh`:"},"906":{"id":"/config-updates-78","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"`~/.tmux.conf`, `~/.grok/AGENTS.md`, `~/.coder/AGENTS.md`,\n`~/.agents/INSTRUCTIONS.md`, the two `grok-build-delegation/SKILL.md` copies"},"907":{"id":"/config-updates-79","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"the six `ez-learn`, `ez-skillify` and `ez-create-skill` `SKILL.md` copies\n(two homes each)"},"908":{"id":"/config-updates-80","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"the sixteen `ez-bazel-first`, `ez-strong-types`, `ez-trunk-based-repo` and\n`ez-micro-plan` copies (four `SKILL.md` and four python helpers, two homes each)"},"909":{"id":"/config-updates-81","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json`"},"910":{"id":"/config-updates-82","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"The same rule applies as in `refresh-configs`: a file is replaced only while it\nstill carries its stack marker:"},"911":{"id":"/config-updates-83","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` comment"},"912":{"id":"/config-updates-84","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"the `\"__evoT1Stack\": true` JSON key (settings files) or the `__evoT1Stack = true` TOML\nkey (`~/.grok/config.toml`)"},"913":{"id":"/config-updates-85","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-reseed-set","content":"So a config you hand-edit in a terminal is your\nfile and this tool will not move it. `--force` overrides that, per run, and says\nso."},"914":{"id":"/config-updates-86","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"The six skill copies are the stack's three skill commands, each seeded at\n`~/.coder/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and twin-copied to its `~/.agents` twin:"},"915":{"id":"/config-updates-87","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"`/ez-learn`, which turns a session into durable memory (this stack's copy of the\nupstream `/flush`, `/dream`, `/remember` and `/memory` - the CLI's own commands, not\nskills: flush the conversation into a session log, dream those logs into organized\nmemory, save one note, browse or manage the store. Three of the four are gated on a\nmemory store that is off by default, so they stay hidden until one is configured)"},"916":{"id":"/config-updates-88","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"`/ez-skillify`, which captures the session that just worked"},"917":{"id":"/config-updates-89","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"`/ez-create-skill`, which scaffolds one from a description"},"918":{"id":"/config-updates-90","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"The sixteen other skill copies are four more commands, seeded the same way into\nthe same two homes:"},"919":{"id":"/config-updates-91","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"`/ez-bazel-first`, `/ez-strong-types` and `/ez-trunk-based-repo`, which convert\nwhatever repository the workspace is sitting in"},"920":{"id":"/config-updates-92","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"`/ez-micro-plan`, which cuts one change into micro tasks for a fleet of subagents\nand checks the cut before wave 1"},"921":{"id":"/config-updates-93","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-seeded-skill-commands","content":"Eight of those sixteen are the python helpers three of them run, under a `scripts/`\nsubdirectory of the same skill directory; a reseed recreates that directory when\na workspace lost it."},"922":{"id":"/config-updates-94","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#taking-a-seeded-copy-over","content":"To take a seeded copy over, edit it and\ndelete the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker line: a marker-free file is\nuser-owned, and the seeder leaves it alone unless you pass `--force`."},"923":{"id":"/config-updates-95","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#taking-a-seeded-copy-over","content":"A deletion is undone - the workspace boot writes the file again whenever it is absent, and\n`refresh-configs` re-seeds an absent target, so the next boot restores the stack's\ncopy."},"924":{"id":"/config-updates-96","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#taking-a-seeded-copy-over","content":"To hide one of the slash commands, set `disabled = [\"ez-learn\"]` (or\n`ez-skillify`, `ez-create-skill`, `ez-bazel-first`, `ez-strong-types`,\n`ez-trunk-based-repo`, or `ez-micro-plan`) under `[skills]` in\n`~/.grok/config.toml`."},"925":{"id":"/config-updates-97","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#taking-a-seeded-copy-over","content":"An edited copy which keeps its marker is still rewritten\nback to its `templates/common/ez-<name>.SKILL.md` by this tool."},"926":{"id":"/config-updates-98","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#taking-a-seeded-copy-over","content":"The pass also retires the two\n`skills/learn/SKILL.md` paths this skill occupied before the rename, and only while\neach still carries the stack marker, so a leftover copy cannot keep offering a `/learn` the\nstack no longer maintains, and a file someone took over stays."},"927":{"id":"/config-updates-99","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-all-pass","content":"`all` runs `env` and then `workspace`."},"928":{"id":"/config-updates-100","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag        | Effect                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--dry-run` | print the plan, write nothing |","table":"table-0"},"929":{"id":"/config-updates-101","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag                  | Effect                                                                       |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-i`, `--interactive` | stop and ask about every key that still needs a value (the default on a TTY) |","table":"table-0"},"930":{"id":"/config-updates-102","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag                | Effect                                 |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `--non-interactive` | never prompt; list what would be asked |","table":"table-0"},"931":{"id":"/config-updates-103","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag      | Effect                                                      |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--force` | reseed workspace files that carry none of the three markers |","table":"table-0"},"932":{"id":"/config-updates-104","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag           | Effect                                                   |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--from <dir>` | read the payloads from that checkout instead of this one |","table":"table-0"},"933":{"id":"/config-updates-105","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag           | Effect                                          |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `--home <dir>` | treat that host directory as a workspace `HOME` |","table":"table-0"},"934":{"id":"/config-updates-106","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flags","content":"| Flag                 | Effect                        |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--container <name>` | address one container by name |","table":"table-0"},"935":{"id":"/config-updates-107","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#flag-position","content":"Every flag goes **after** the subcommand, so `update-configs --dry-run env` is a\nusage error and prints the usage rather than guessing."},"936":{"id":"/config-updates-108","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-bare-target-is-a-container","content":"A target named without a flag is a container, the same reading `refresh-configs`\ngives a bare word, so these two lines address the same container:"},"937":{"id":"/config-updates-109","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-bare-target-is-a-container","content":"Anything that carries a prefix other than `c:` (container) or `h:` (host\ndirectory) is reported as unrecognized and counted in the closing summary's\nskipped tally. A target never leaves the pass unheard."},"938":{"id":"/config-updates-110","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#prompting-on-a-tty","content":"On a TTY the env pass asks by default (`-i`/`--interactive` is then a no-op;\n`--non-interactive` turns it off)."},"939":{"id":"/config-updates-111","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#prompting-on-a-tty","content":"For every key that is new this pull or still\n`change-me…`/`NOTSET`/`YOUR_LAN_IP` it prints the explanation the twin carries\nabove that key and prompts for a value:"},"940":{"id":"/config-updates-112","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#prompting-on-a-tty","content":"Enter keeps a reusable value already set in a sibling env file, or the example default."},"941":{"id":"/config-updates-113","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#prompting-on-a-tty","content":"A key whose name carries `KEY`, `SECRET`, `TOKEN` or `PASSWORD` is echoed nowhere -\nthe report says `set` or `empty` and the prompt does not echo what you type - so a\nscreenful of this output is safe to paste into an issue."},"942":{"id":"/config-updates-114","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#prompting-on-a-tty","content":"With no terminal to prompt through the pass warns and leaves those keys alone, which is\nwhy `--dry-run` / `--non-interactive` is the shape that belongs in a script or CI."},"943":{"id":"/config-updates-115","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#where-to-run-it","content":"`workspace` addresses docker, so run it from a **host** shell. A terminal inside a\nworkspace is not a host shell: the `docker` CLI there is only installed so you can\ndrive that workspace's own DinD sidecar, so `docker ps` answers empty and an empty\n`docker ps` means \"wrong vantage\", not \"stack down\"."},"944":{"id":"/config-updates-116","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#where-to-run-it","content":"The pass now prints which\ndaemon it addressed and tells you to use a host shell, or to name the target:"},"945":{"id":"/config-updates-117","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#where-to-run-it","content":"`--home` takes a host directory shaped like a workspace `HOME`, which is also how\nyou try a change on a scratch tree before pointing a live stack at it. See\ntroubleshooting.md for the docker-vantage rules."},"946":{"id":"/config-updates-118","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"It never prints an env value that looks like a credential."},"947":{"id":"/config-updates-119","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"It never drops a key your env file still sets; retired keys are commented out\nin place."},"948":{"id":"/config-updates-120","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"It does not touch `~/.grok/config.toml`. That file is rendered *inside* the\nworkspace, and it is a per-workspace file on that workspace's own home volume:"},"949":{"id":"/config-updates-121","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"the model list, the session-affinity key, the `[ui]` theme and the `[ui]`\napproval mode belong to one workspace, so a copy pushed from the host would\nstamp this checkout's defaults over what that workspace's own create-form\nanswers rendered - the approval mode is one of those answers\n(`grok_permission_mode`, default `always-approve`)"},"950":{"id":"/config-updates-122","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"A **start/restart** re-renders it from this checkout, which is the only way a\nper-workspace value gets in, and the pass says so after it reseeds."},"951":{"id":"/config-updates-123","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-it-will-not-do","content":"`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` is the one rendered target it does reseed, and\nit re-*renders* rather than copies: `${litellm_url}` and the `$${...}`\ndollar-brace unfoldings are rewritten, and that workspace's own `cline.apiKey`\nand `roo.openaiApiKey` are carried forward."},"952":{"id":"/config-updates-124","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"Inside a running container the same targets are `refresh-configs`'s job too: same reseed set, same marker rule, `--json` for a machine-readable\nanswer, and `--litellm-url <url>` for a stack environment that publishes\nLiteLLM on a port other than 4000 (the reseeded `settings.json` then still\nnames that stack's own model transport)."},"953":{"id":"/config-updates-125","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"A third tool covers the same set on a host home rather than a container:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:seed-dev-env -- --home <dir>` materialises it into a laptop or\nCI home, and it takes the fan-out knobs from the environment while it renders the config:"},"954":{"id":"/config-updates-126","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_SUBAGENTS_LANE` names the lane the writers ride"},"955":{"id":"/config-updates-127","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT` the width"},"956":{"id":"/config-updates-128","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_DEPTH` the nesting depth (the `grok_subagent_max_depth` template\nvariable)"},"957":{"id":"/config-updates-129","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_EXPLORE_LANE`, `GROK_PLAN_LANE` and `GROK_REVIEW_LANE` the aliases the\nreader, the planner and the skeptic ride"},"958":{"id":"/config-updates-130","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_THEME` (default `grokbuild`) the `[ui]` theme name"},"959":{"id":"/config-updates-131","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-other-two-seeders","content":"`GROK_PERMISSION_MODE` (default `always-approve`) the `[ui]` approval mode - the\nsame choice the create form makes with `grok_permission_mode`, over the same accepted\nset (`default`, `ask`, `auto`, `always-approve`)"},"960":{"id":"/config-updates-132","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-width-the-fleet-ceiling-and-the-depth","content":"The width default is this knob's\nown shipped 15 (three Spark boxes at `PARALLEL` 5), the same literal 15 the\ntemplates ship on `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`, on every lane rather than one\nnumber per lane."},"961":{"id":"/config-updates-133","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-width-the-fleet-ceiling-and-the-depth","content":"A pinned lane only ever keeps one box's streams busy, so an\noperator who pins everything sets `GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT` by hand."},"962":{"id":"/config-updates-134","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-width-the-fleet-ceiling-and-the-depth","content":"`GROK_SWARM_WIDTH` is the fleet's own ceiling, and here it feeds only the\n`# fleet-width:` line the seeder renders beside `max_concurrent` - the same line\nthe templates render from `grok_swarm_width`, so the two agree because each one\nships 15, not because the seeder falls back to the fleet."},"963":{"id":"/config-updates-135","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-width-the-fleet-ceiling-and-the-depth","content":"Dropping\n`GROK_SWARM_WIDTH` alone now moves that ceiling line and leaves a 15-wide home, so\nset `GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT` with it: 15 streams over a 10-stream fleet is\nrefused by the box with `NoRoom`."},"964":{"id":"/config-updates-136","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-width-the-fleet-ceiling-and-the-depth","content":"The depth default is 2, which\nlets a child spawn read-only mappers of its own, and the seeder holds the value to 1..3,\nwith 1 putting nesting back off (`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh:187-197`)."},"965":{"id":"/config-updates-137","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"A value the seeder cannot use is refused with\na `note:` line naming the key, and the derived default goes in, so a typo lands as output\nyou read rather than as an unusable key in the rendered `~/.grok/config.toml`. It cannot\nuse:"},"966":{"id":"/config-updates-138","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"a lane that is not a bare model id"},"967":{"id":"/config-updates-139","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"a width that is not a count or sits past 32"},"968":{"id":"/config-updates-140","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"a depth that is not a count or sits past 3"},"969":{"id":"/config-updates-141","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"an approval mode outside `default` / `ask` / `auto` / `always-approve`"},"970":{"id":"/config-updates-142","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-value-the-seeder-cannot-use","content":"grok-build-and-agents.md covers the profile\nvolume and what seeds on first boot."},"971":{"id":"/config-updates-143","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#github-external-auth-and-coderenv","content":"`.env.sample` deliberately carries no GitHub credential of any kind, so the env\npass has nothing to reconcile here: the twin declares no `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_*`\nkey and `update-configs` will never add one. Those keys belong in `coder.env`\nbeside `docker-compose.yml` (gitignored), which is not a file this tool touches."},"972":{"id":"/config-updates-144","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#an-empty-key-is-still-a-configured-provider","content":"**A defined-but-empty key crash-loops the server.** Any `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_*`\ncounts as a configured provider even when its value is empty, and an empty key\nmakes `coder server` exit at boot with `external auth provider \"\" doesn't have a\nvalid id` - which the compose restart policy turns into a crash loop."},"973":{"id":"/config-updates-145","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#an-empty-key-is-still-a-configured-provider","content":"Do not set\nonly `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_APP_INSTALL_URL` either: it suppresses the injected\nApp like any other key in the set."},"974":{"id":"/config-updates-146","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#an-empty-key-is-still-a-configured-provider","content":"A custom GitHub App belongs in `coder.env`\nfully filled, including\n`APP_INSTALL_URL=https://github.com/apps/<slug>/installations/new`."},"975":{"id":"/config-updates-147","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-usual-case-no-coderenv","content":"**Leave `coder.env` absent for the usual case.** Coder CE injects its own GitHub\nApp (provider id `github`, device flow) and both templates declare that id by\ndefault, so `bazelisk run //scripts:push-template` works with no extra file.\nWorkspace owners connect GitHub under Settings -> Tokens / external auth."},"976":{"id":"/config-updates-148","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-custom-github-oauth-app","content":"**Create `coder.env` only for a *custom* GitHub OAuth app**, and fill EVERY key -\n`ID` names the provider and `TYPE` says what kind it is. Restart coder to apply\nthe file."},"977":{"id":"/config-updates-149","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-custom-github-oauth-app","content":"`CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_REGEX` is only for telling providers or hosts apart;\nomitted, it matches every `github.com` remote."},"978":{"id":"/config-updates-150","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-custom-github-oauth-app","content":"`push-template.sh` reads `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_ID` from `coder.env` and\nforwards it as `--var github_auth_id=` so the templates declare the same id.\nChanging the id orphans existing GitHub account links."},"979":{"id":"/config-updates-151","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-custom-github-oauth-app","content":"Then connect your GitHub account in Coder (Settings -> Tokens / external auth)\nand link the same provider to **both** workspace templates (Templates -> edit\n-> External Auth)."},"980":{"id":"/config-updates-152","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-custom-github-oauth-app","content":"The callback URL on the GitHub side is\n`<CODER_ACCESS_URL>/external-auth/<id>/callback` - `github` for the injected\nApp, `primary-github` for the sample app above."},"981":{"id":"/config-updates-153","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#installing-the-coder-github-app","content":"**Device-flow login is not the App install.** Private repos need the Coder GitHub\nApp installed from\ngithub.com/apps/coder/installations/new\n(the workspace \"Install GitHub App\" button), then a restart so `GH_TOKEN` remints."},"982":{"id":"/config-updates-154","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#installing-the-coder-github-app","content":"The grant must include the repos you clone, or a connected credential authenticates\nand is still 403."},"983":{"id":"/config-updates-155","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-token-in-the-agent-environment","content":"**How the token reaches a workspace.** It arrives as `GH_TOKEN` and `GITHUB_TOKEN`\nin the agent environment, and that pair is a snapshot: Coder mints it when the\nworkspace starts and never refreshes it, so it expires about an hour later while\nthe workspace keeps running."},"984":{"id":"/config-updates-156","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-token-in-the-agent-environment","content":"The template's `gh_token_refresh` coder_script\nre-mints on start and every 20 minutes (`0 */20 * * * *`) into the **gh auth store**,\nwhich is the copy that stays live. git asks its credential helper, and the\nstack's helper reads the store through a form that clears the stale pair first,\nso push follows the store and not the frozen environment."},"985":{"id":"/config-updates-157","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-token-in-the-agent-environment","content":"Check it with\n`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- check <repo-url>` - pass the repository,\nbecause without it the doctor lists credentials and never asks the write\nquestion."},"986":{"id":"/config-updates-158","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-token-in-the-agent-environment","content":"`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- fix <repo-url>` repairs a\nworkspace that cannot push."},"987":{"id":"/config-updates-159","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-token-in-the-agent-environment","content":"coder-templates.md owns\nthe template-side detail."},"988":{"id":"/config-updates-160","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-pat-installed-per-workspace","content":"**Never a static PAT in `.env`.** `.env.sample` used to carry a `GITHUB_TOKEN=`\nline holding a long-lived fine-grained PAT, which `push-template.sh` forwarded to\nboth templates as a template variable, into every workspace's environment."},"989":{"id":"/config-updates-161","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-pat-installed-per-workspace","content":"That path is gone: there is no such template variable and no such key in the twin."},"990":{"id":"/config-updates-162","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-pat-installed-per-workspace","content":"A workspace's GitHub credential comes from the External Auth provider alone, so an\nowner who connected nothing has no GitHub credential anywhere - and the only way\nto add one by hand is per workspace, after `check` has answered `REFUSED-GRANT`,\n`NOT VISIBLE` or `REJECTED` (a passing read is not that answer):"},"991":{"id":"/config-updates-163","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#a-pat-installed-per-workspace","content":"That pipes a PAT straight into that container's `gh` credential store - no `.env`\nedit, no template push - and `gh auth logout` inside the container, or a rebuild,\nremoves it. The repositories a token can reach are whatever that GitHub app\ninstallation was granted."},"992":{"id":"/config-updates-164","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"`GROK_PROFILE_MODE` in the twin is the default for the template variable\n`grok_profile_mode`, which the create form also shows per workspace as the **Grok\nprofile** dropdown."},"993":{"id":"/config-updates-165","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"Read once per push, so changing the default here needs\n`bazelisk run //scripts:push-template`. Overriding it for one workspace happens on\nthat dropdown and needs a rebuild, like `dind`."},"994":{"id":"/config-updates-166","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"`shared` (the default): every workspace of a user mounts three of that user's\nvolumes nested inside `/home/coder` - `grok-notes-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/notes`,\n`grok-memory-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/memory`, `grok-sessions-<owner-id>` at\n`~/.grok/sessions` - so the notes, the memory and the sessions are one set of state\nthat account's workspaces share, and they survive a rebuild."},"995":{"id":"/config-updates-167","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"`config.toml` is not\npart of the share: each workspace renders its own on every start, so this\nworkspace's model, theme and extras are its own and no sibling's boot overwrites\nthem."},"996":{"id":"/config-updates-168","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"`private`: no per-owner volume at all. Notes, memory and sessions then live on that\nworkspace's own home volume, differ per workspace, and die with the workspace;\n`config.toml` is per workspace either way."},"997":{"id":"/config-updates-169","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"A workspace moving `shared` -> `private` starts on whatever those three directories\nalready hold on its own home volume: nothing is copied and the owner's volumes are\nleft alone."},"998":{"id":"/config-updates-170","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"Switching either way is a **rebuild**, not a stop/start, because the nested mount\nis decided when the workspace is built."},"999":{"id":"/config-updates-171","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#grok-profile-mode","content":"grok-build-and-agents.md covers what the state volumes\nhold and what seeds on first boot; the `workspace` pass above never\nreseeds `~/.grok/config.toml` for exactly that reason."},"1000":{"id":"/config-updates-172","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#public-hosts-and-the-dashboard","content":"`STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` is the one switch, and it has three states:"},"1001":{"id":"/config-updates-173","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#public-hosts-and-the-dashboard","content":"Empty keeps everything below LAN-only and every derived `STACK_*_URL` stays empty."},"1002":{"id":"/config-updates-174","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#public-hosts-and-the-dashboard","content":"`auto` composes the seven names from the naming parts - `STACK_DOMAIN_BASE`,\n`STACK_SUBDOMAIN_SUFFIX`,\n`STACK_ENV_LABEL` and the per-service `STACK_*_NAME` prefixes, all documented in\n`.env.sample`."},"1003":{"id":"/config-updates-175","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#public-hosts-and-the-dashboard","content":"A comma-separated list is the hand-pin: those names are used verbatim."},"1004":{"id":"/config-updates-176","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#rules-for-the-entries","content":"Entries are DNS names, not URLs: no scheme, no port, no path. The entry with no\nprefix is the dashboard."},"1005":{"id":"/config-updates-177","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#rules-for-the-entries","content":"Each service name is **one label** under the zone and carries its prefix with a\n**HYPHEN**: a wildcard certificate covers exactly one label, so the dotted\ntwo-label form has no certificate at the public edge."},"1006":{"id":"/config-updates-178","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#rules-for-the-entries","content":"Under `auto` the parts are the source of truth and `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` is output\nonly: bootstrap writes the resolved list back and records the intent in\n`STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS_MODE=auto`, so a later run re-composes and a list edited by hand\nin `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` is ignored. Bootstrap prints a `note:` naming the key to\nclear when that happens."},"1007":{"id":"/config-updates-179","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-the-names-feed","content":"`bootstrap.sh` derives `STACK_DASHBOARD_URL` / `STACK_CODER_URL` /\n`STACK_KASM_URL` / `STACK_LITELLM_URL` / `STACK_HERMES_URL` / `STACK_GRAFANA_URL` /\n`STACK_INFISICAL_URL` from the prefix on each entry (`coder-` / `kasm-` / `litellm-` /\n`hermes-` / `grafana-` / `infisical-`, dotted form still\nrecognised) and upgrades `CODER_ACCESS_URL` to the coder name, so Coder builds\nworkspace links on a secure context with a real certificate."},"1008":{"id":"/config-updates-180","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-the-names-feed","content":"Compose sets\n`HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL` from `STACK_HERMES_URL` (the Chat tab's Host and\nOrigin)."},"1009":{"id":"/config-updates-181","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#what-the-names-feed","content":"The names also go into `HOMEPAGE_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (compose appends this raw value)\nand into the Coder certificate's subjectAltName."},"1010":{"id":"/config-updates-182","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-traefik-on-the-other-box","content":"The Traefik on the other box owns TLS for those names and must forward plain\nHTTP to this box's router container **with the original Host header intact** -\n`STACK_ROUTER_CONF` names the conf that container mounts (`proxy/router.gen.conf`,\nrendered by bootstrap from `proxy/router.conf.template`, or the checked-in\n`proxy/router.conf` while the key is empty), and it picks the service from\n`$http_host` on `STACK_PROXY_HTTP_PORT` (default 8080). A rewritten Host comes back\nas `421`."},"1011":{"id":"/config-updates-183","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-traefik-on-the-other-box","content":"That box needs one file, and the paste-ready version of it - one `loadBalancer`\nat `:8080`, a router per name, Authelia on the six interactive names, the\nlong-lived timeouts - is\npublic-access.md#traefik-configuration."},"1012":{"id":"/config-updates-184","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#applying-the-rename","content":"Set the parts in `.env`, and in `dev-stack.env` too when a dev stack runs beside\nthe stable one, then re-run `bazelisk run //scripts:bootstrap` and recreate the\nstack you switched."},"1013":{"id":"/config-updates-185","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#applying-the-rename","content":"That one command is the whole rename: it re-renders the router's\nvhost table and rewrites the derived URLs, so a hostname is no longer an edit split\nacross `proxy/router.conf`, `scripts/bootstrap.sh` and `docker-compose.yml`."},"1014":{"id":"/config-updates-186","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#applying-the-rename","content":"A `hermes-*` or `hermes.*` entry is part of that list:\nbootstrap writes `STACK_HERMES_URL`, and the LAN `:9119` listener stays either\nway. Leave the hermes name out and the Homepage card keeps the LAN URL."},"1015":{"id":"/config-updates-187","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#applying-the-rename","content":"public-access.md owns the naming rule, the measured\n`ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH` on the dotted form, the request path and the\nchecks to run on the Traefik box."},"1016":{"id":"/config-updates-188","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"The `agent` model group is three deployments behind one LiteLLM alias, one per\nSpark box, and these are the keys that fill it:"},"1017":{"id":"/config-updates-189","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`SPARKn_HOST` is where each box is named - once. docker-compose.yml composes\nevery Spark URL from it plus the port below, so a box that gets a new\nDHCP name or a static IP is edited in this one place and the LiteLLM\ndeployments, the dashboard's per-box cards, and the host list\n`//scripts:spark-verify` / `//scripts:spark-configure` probe all move\ntogether."},"1018":{"id":"/config-updates-190","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"The shipped placeholders do not resolve on purpose: leave a box you\ndo not run empty and its alias and its card both report down."},"1019":{"id":"/config-updates-191","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`SPARK_HTTP_PORT` (default 8888) is the port every box of the recipe answers\non - TensorFold's `/v1` and `/health`, for the `agent` lane and the cards."},"1020":{"id":"/config-updates-192","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`SPARKn_OPENAI_URL` is the OpenAI-compatible `/v1` endpoint. It is an\noverride, kept commented in the twin: set it when that box answers somewhere\nthe host plus port cannot express (https behind a reverse proxy, two boxes on\none host)."},"1021":{"id":"/config-updates-193","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"A value set there wins outright, and that box's dashboard card does\nnot follow it - name the same host in `SPARKn_HEALTH_URL` too."},"1022":{"id":"/config-updates-194","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"A workspace\npins its session to one healthy `/v1` box; fresh session-id-less traffic fans\nout by `least-busy`, shortest in-flight queue first."},"1023":{"id":"/config-updates-195","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`SPARK_n_API_KEY` is the bearer token for each endpoint. TensorFold is\nvLLM-lineage, so treat it like vLLM/SGLang: any non-empty string is accepted\nunless the server was started with `--api-key`, in which case set the REAL key\nper box."},"1024":{"id":"/config-updates-196","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"Empty is not a working value - LiteLLM v1.102.1 fails every request at\nclient construction (`AuthenticationError`, before reaching the box) and `agent`\nfalls back to `coder`."},"1025":{"id":"/config-updates-197","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"The placeholder `local-spark` is not a secret and is\nignored by a keyless backend."},"1026":{"id":"/config-updates-198","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`SPARKn_HEALTH_URL` (kept commented in the twin) feed the dashboard's per-box\nSpark cards - one widget per box, so no card assumes one \"usual\" box. Compose\nbuilds each from `SPARKn_HOST` plus `SPARK_HTTP_PORT`; nothing but the\ndashboard reads them."},"1027":{"id":"/config-updates-199","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"`AGENT_MODEL_URL` is the single `/v1/models` URL the \"Agent backend\" card uses\nfor both its browser link and its status probe. It defaults to box 2 - same\n`SPARK2_HOST`, same `SPARK_HTTP_PORT` - and all three boxes serve the same\nmodel id, so point it at any reachable one when you want the card to follow a\nparticular box."},"1028":{"id":"/config-updates-200","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-keys-that-fill-the-group","content":"The per-box health keys are what tell you which one answered."},"1029":{"id":"/config-updates-201","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#when-no-spark-host-is-set","content":"With no `SPARKn_HOST` and no `SPARKn_OPENAI_URL` set, compose takes the host from\n`STACK_LAN_HOST`, which is at least a machine this stack owns: `agent` stays\ndefined but unusable and LiteLLM falls back to `coder`, the Arc alias."},"1030":{"id":"/config-updates-202","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#when-no-spark-host-is-set","content":"That\nfallback is what the \"Agent backend\" card exists to catch - Grok Build, Cline and\nRoo need structured tool calls, which the Arc IPEX-LLM Ollama returns as plain text\nfor the Qwen2.5-Coder weights."},"1031":{"id":"/config-updates-203","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#when-no-spark-host-is-set","content":"litellm-routing.md owns the alias\ntable, the picker, the pin, and the measured tool-call limitation (including which\naliases do emit real calls)."},"1032":{"id":"/config-updates-204","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"**The fast-compaction hop has five keys of its own.** On `agent-xhigh-fast` and\n`agent-swarm-fast` only, the proxy callback `litellm/compaction_router.py` recognises\nthe CLI's conversation-summary call and re-serves it from somewhere cheaper than the\nSpark box it arrived on, in one of two tiers:"},"1033":{"id":"/config-updates-205","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"the Arc group `compaction-fast` for a summary small enough for that window"},"1034":{"id":"/config-updates-206","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"the Spark group `agent-low` for one too big for it"},"1035":{"id":"/config-updates-207","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"A summary needs no extra-high thinking, which is what\nthe Spark lane charges for it."},"1036":{"id":"/config-updates-208","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"The Grok Build CLI has no compaction-model\nsetting, so nothing in a client config points that call anywhere and the hop can\nonly live in the proxy - with the flag off, both lanes behave exactly like their\nnon-fast parents."},"1037":{"id":"/config-updates-209","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"All five are read in that one module and set in the compose\nlitellm service, the three that read a blank as unset as `${KEY:-default}` and the\ntwo tier targets as `${KEY-default}` so a blanked target stays blank, which is how\na tier is parked. A dotenv line overrides each one."},"1038":{"id":"/config-updates-210","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-fast-compaction-hop","content":"litellm-routing.md owns the mechanism."},"1039":{"id":"/config-updates-211","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION` (default on) is the kill switch: `0`, `false`, `off` or\n`no` stop the hop outright, and a value that is none of those nor `1`, `true`,\n`on`, `yes` leaves it off too, with one warning line naming what was read."},"1040":{"id":"/config-updates-212","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_LANES` (default `agent-xhigh-fast,agent-swarm-fast`)\nnames the model groups that may hop - name one of them to narrow the hop to\nthat lane alone."},"1041":{"id":"/config-updates-213","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_TARGET` (default `compaction-fast`) is the tier a\nsummary under the guard is moved to."},"1042":{"id":"/config-updates-214","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT` (default `24000`) is the guard, and it\npicks a tier rather than ending the hop."},"1043":{"id":"/config-updates-215","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"The Arc weights are a 32768-token\nmodel and Ollama clamps an over-long input instead of refusing it, so a\nsummary above that estimate is never handed over to be quietly truncated."},"1044":{"id":"/config-updates-216","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"The guard is a ceiling the module may lower and never raise: the Arc target\ngroup's own `max_input_tokens` in `litellm/config.yaml` caps it, and a value\nset above that window forks there anyway with one warning line naming both\nnumbers. A group that declares no window leaves the guard whole, and the\nmodule logs one line saying the fork runs on this key alone."},"1045":{"id":"/config-updates-217","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` (default `agent-low`) is where a summary\nabove the guard goes instead: a Spark group, so it carries the 262144-token\nwindow a full-size summary needs, at thinking baked `low` rather than `xhigh`."},"1046":{"id":"/config-updates-218","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-five-keys","content":"Blank it, or name the lane the call arrived on, and an oversized summary stays\nwhere it is - the pre-hop behaviour."},"1047":{"id":"/config-updates-219","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-guard-and-the-client-threshold","content":"**Read the guard beside the client threshold: that pairing picks the tier.** Both fast\naliases declare a `context_window` of 262144 and the shipped `[session]` block sets\n`auto_compact_threshold_percent` to 70, so a session on either one reaches its\nauto-compaction at about 183,500 tokens - over the guard, so the Arc was never going to read\nit and the call goes to the Spark tier instead."},"1048":{"id":"/config-updates-220","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-guard-and-the-client-threshold","content":"`agent-low` is what makes that work cheaper\nthan its parent: the 262144-token window stays and the baked `xhigh` thinking goes, which is\nthe cost the hop exists to stop paying. That is a routing choice with its own trade, not a\nfree win - the summary still runs on a Spark box, at a thinking level turned down."},"1049":{"id":"/config-updates-221","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-guard-and-the-client-threshold","content":"Neither tier has a timing of its own yet: the hop has not served a summary on a running\nstack, so the only numbers attached to this feature are the 107 s to 1915 s and 18-of-36\nfigures for the Spark lane before it existed, both swept out of the session logs in\ntroubleshooting.md."},"1050":{"id":"/config-updates-222","page_id":"/config-updates","tags":["env","config","update-configs","maintenance"],"type":"text","url":"/config-updates#the-guard-and-the-client-threshold","content":"`bazelisk test //tests:bats_litellm_config_test`\npins the config and the compose passthrough, and `docs/troubleshooting.md` names the one log\nline that shows the hop firing."},"1051":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"page","content":"Building with Bazel","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel"},"1052":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-0","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","content":"Bazelisk as the ingress for tests, lint and the operator CLIs, and what the runfiles layout means for a script you just added."},"1053":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-1","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Building with Bazel"},"1054":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-2","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-contributor-path","content":"The contributor path"},"1055":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-3","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#stack-host-bootstrap","content":"Stack-host bootstrap"},"1056":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-4","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#recovery-and-dns","content":"Recovery and DNS"},"1057":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-5","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#ci-repeats-the-gate","content":"CI repeats the gate"},"1058":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-6","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"Daily commands"},"1059":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-7","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"The Makefile shims"},"1060":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-8","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#operator-runs-are-bounded","content":"Operator runs are bounded"},"1061":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-9","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"What Bazel brings"},"1062":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-10","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"Persisting the repository cache in CI"},"1063":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-11","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#script-targets-and-runfiles","content":"Script targets and runfiles"},"1064":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-12","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-generated-launcher","content":"The generated launcher"},"1065":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-13","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#declared-libs-and-payload-groups","content":"Declared libs and payload groups"},"1066":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-14","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-real-checkout-fallback","content":"The real-checkout fallback"},"1067":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-15","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#a-new-payload-directory","content":"A new payload directory"},"1068":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-16","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"The dependency maps and their gate"},"1069":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-17","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-reports","content":"What the scan reports"},"1070":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-18","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"What the scan counts as prose"},"1071":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-19","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#when-the-scan-cannot-see-a-pairing","content":"When the scan cannot see a pairing"},"1072":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-20","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"Reaching the checkout from a script"},"1073":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-21","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1074":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-22","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Stack-host bootstrap: the one script run straight from a shell"},"1075":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-23","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"The contributor path — the dev container, or `test-in-image` — and where it fits"},"1076":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-24","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"The daily commands, and the Makefile shim over them"},"1077":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-25","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"What Bazel brings over running the scripts directly"},"1078":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-26","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Script targets, runfiles, and why a new `scripts/*.sh` is a target automatically"},"1079":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-27","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"**What this enables**"},"1080":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-28","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Running any operator CLI from a foreign working directory with pinned inputs"},"1081":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-29","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Adding a script without editing a BUILD file"},"1082":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-30","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Getting the same Bazel, Bats, shellcheck and Terraform that CI uses without installing\nany of them"},"1083":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-31","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#building-with-bazel","content":"Bazelisk is how this repo runs tests, lint, and the operator CLIs. The Makefile targets call\nthe same commands. test-with-bazel.md covers the Bats harness;\n../branching.md the branch rules that CI guards;\ndevcontainer.md the container that carries the toolchain."},"1084":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-32","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-contributor-path","content":"The toolchain Bazel drives comes from one Linux golden image, `images/dev/Dockerfile`, and\nthe contributor path is that image rather than a set of tools installed on your machine:"},"1085":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-33","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-contributor-path","content":"Open the checkout in the contributor dev container (`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\nbuilds it) and run the commands below unchanged."},"1086":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-34","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-contributor-path","content":"Or, from a machine that is not in that container, `bazelisk run //scripts:test-in-image --`\ndocker-runs `evo-t1-dev:latest` and runs the gate inside it."},"1087":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-35","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-contributor-path","content":"Both give you the GNU userland the gate runs on, which a macOS laptop cannot promise\nnatively. Neither replaces the bootstrap below — that one is for the stack host."},"1088":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-36","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#stack-host-bootstrap","content":"`scripts/setup-host.sh` is the only script run straight from a shell, and it is the\n**stack host's** bootstrap: the box that runs Coder, LiteLLM, Ollama, Kasm, Homepage and\nHermes, where Compose and Bazel have to live on the host itself. It installs what Bazel\nneeds (Bazelisk, shellcheck, shfmt, buildifier, Terraform), so it necessarily runs before\nBazel exists — that is its whole exemption, not a convenience:"},"1089":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-37","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#recovery-and-dns","content":"`--repair` is the recovery when `bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack` dies creating\nthe runfiles tree (`FileAccessException ... Permission denied` on\n`homepage/assets/icons/evo-t1.svg`). Bazel never reaches the stack script, so the\nrepair has to live in this shell entry point."},"1090":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-38","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#recovery-and-dns","content":"On Linux it also installs public DNS so `github.com` still resolves when Tailscale\nMagicDNS is the only nameserver (`Could not resolve host: github.com` after a compose `up`).\n`--check` reports that lookup and writes nothing."},"1091":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-39","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#recovery-and-dns","content":"Everything else is a Bazel target, including every `scripts/*.sh`."},"1092":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-40","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#ci-repeats-the-gate","content":"CI repeats the gate from a clean runner inside the same golden image:\n`.github/workflows/ci.yml` builds\n`images/dev` with buildx and the Actions layer cache and docker-runs the two suites below in\nit, so the bazel job does not install the pins onto the runner at all — the image already\ncarries them."},"1093":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-41","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#ci-repeats-the-gate","content":"The persistent cache on that path is the buildx GHA layer cache, so a pull\nrequest that leaves `images/dev/**` alone replays the image layers."},"1094":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-42","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target         | What it runs                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//:test-fast` | One `sh_test` per `tests/bats/*.bats` file, plus the shell inventory and docstring gates |","table":"table-0"},"1095":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-43","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target    | What it runs                                       |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//:lint` | ShellCheck, shfmt, buildifier (manual: host tools) |","table":"table-0"},"1096":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-44","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target        | What it runs                                                                                                            |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//:validate` | test-fast, lint, `docker compose config -q`, `.env.sample` vs `.env.example`, terraform fmt when terraform is installed |","table":"table-0"},"1097":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-45","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target   | What it runs                    |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `//:fix` | buildifier and shfmt write mode |","table":"table-0"},"1098":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-46","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target             | What it runs                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//scripts:<stem>` | One operator CLI: `bazelisk run //scripts:<stem> -- <args>`, e.g. `//scripts:dev-stack -- up`, `//scripts:new-workspace -- --dry-run <url>` |","table":"table-0"},"1099":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-47","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target                    | What it runs                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//scripts:test-in-image` | The merge gate inside `evo-t1-dev:latest`, for a machine that is not the contributor container |","table":"table-0"},"1100":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-48","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#daily-commands","content":"| Target                   | What it runs                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//scripts:seed-dev-env` | Materialize a contributor home (Grok config, editor settings, notes, tmux, helpers) from the workspace templates |","table":"table-0"},"1101":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-49","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"`make test`/`bats`/`lint`/`fix`/`validate` and the `stack-*`/`prod-stack-*` shims are the\nsame commands; `make help` lists them."},"1102":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-50","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"`//:test-fast` does not:"},"1103":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-51","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"start Compose"},"1104":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-52","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"pull models"},"1105":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-53","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"SSH to a Spark box"},"1106":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-54","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-makefile-shims","content":"The suites exercise those scripts against `tests/bats/tool_stubs`. `bazelisk run\n//scripts:<stem> -- <args>` is how a human runs one of them for real."},"1107":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-55","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#operator-runs-are-bounded","content":"Those operator runs are bounded: a script's non-interactive `docker exec` closes stdin\n(`</dev/null`), and the docker wrappers go through `timeout(1)` with `--kill-after`, so a\n`bazelisk run //scripts:<stem>` cannot sit forever the way `docker exec -i` did under\n`bazelisk run`, waiting for an EOF that never came."},"1108":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-56","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#operator-runs-are-bounded","content":"`logs --follow` is the intentional long-running exception, and you stop it with Ctrl-C."},"1109":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-57","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"**Hermetic sandbox.** `test --spawn_strategy=local,sandboxed` and `build\n--spawn_strategy=sandboxed`: an action sees its declared inputs and its runfiles tree, not\nthe whole checkout. That is why a suite declares its stubs and payload files as `data` and\nwhy a script resolves its repo root with `resolve_checkout` (`scripts/lib/common.sh`) instead of\ntrusting the cwd."},"1110":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-58","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"**Action cache.** An action's outputs are keyed on its inputs and command line, so an\nunchanged suite replays its cached PASS instead of re-running Bats."},"1111":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-59","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"**Local disk and repository cache.** `.bazelrc` points `--disk_cache` at\n`~/.cache/bazel-disk` and `--repository_cache` at `~/.cache/bazel-repo`. A contributor\ncontainer and a Coder workspace reuse those directories across runs."},"1112":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-60","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"In CI the gate container is `--rm` and runs with `HOME=/tmp` and `USER=$(id -un)`, so a\nplain run keeps neither cache between jobs, and Bazel can name a uid the image passwd\nfile does not list; the cache that survives there is the image's buildx GHA cache."},"1113":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-61","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-bazel-brings","content":"No remote cache is configured — the same two flags would take a `--remote_cache=<uri>`\nendpoint later."},"1114":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-62","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"The repository cache is the one worth persisting in CI, and `EVO_T1_BAZEL_CACHE=<host dir>`\nis the seam: `//scripts:test-in-image` bind-mounts that directory into the gate container and\npoints `--repository_cache` at it, so each external archive downloads once per key."},"1115":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-63","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"Each CI gate step exports it as `${RUNNER_TEMP}/bazel-repo-cache`\nand is wrapped in an `actions/cache`\npair keyed on `MODULE.bazel`, `MODULE.bazel.lock` and `.bazelrc`, with the save under\n`if: always()` — the archives fetched before a red gate are exactly what the next run would\notherwise pay for again."},"1116":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-64","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"That endpoint matters: `github.com/.../releases/download/...` answers 504 for a slice of\nrequests, one such 504 aborts Bazel's analysis, and a refetch-on-every-job job decides its\ncolour by luck."},"1117":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-65","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"The in-container path is passed as an explicit option because the `~` in `.bazelrc` expands\nfrom the Bazel server's own `user.home`, which this container's uid does not appear in: a\nmount placed from that `~` could sit where Bazel never writes and look like a working cache\nfor exactly one run."},"1118":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-66","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#persisting-the-repository-cache-in-ci","content":"With the variable unset the script mounts nothing, which is what a contributor laptop gets."},"1119":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-67","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-generated-launcher","content":"`scripts/BUILD.bazel` declares one `exec_shell` launcher plus one `sh_binary` wrapper per\n`scripts/*.sh`, generated from the directory, so a new CLI is a Bazel target without a second\nedit there. `//:validate` is an alias for `//scripts:validate`; `//:fix` keeps the same\nlauncher pattern at the repo root."},"1120":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-68","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-generated-launcher","content":"`rules_shell` only symlinks an `sh_test` or `sh_binary` source when that file is executable.\n`//tools:exec_shell.bzl` writes a generated launcher and runs the real `.sh` from runfiles\nwith bash, so a checkout whose scripts are mode `100644` still builds."},"1121":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-69","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#declared-libs-and-payload-groups","content":"Each CLI target also declares the repo files that script reads by path: the libs it\nsources (`_SCRIPT_LIBS`) and the payload groups whose files it opens (`_SCRIPT_PAYLOAD`),\nboth keyed by script stem in `scripts/BUILD.bazel`."},"1122":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-70","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#declared-libs-and-payload-groups","content":"Those payload groups live one per payload directory (`//litellm:config`,\n`//searxng:settings`, `//homepage:config`, `//homepage:icons`, `//hermes:seed`,\n`//hermes:skills`, `//proxy:confs`, `//images/dev:dockerfile`, `//images/dev:tool_versions`,\nand a `:payload` in each of `templates/common`, `templates/workspace`,\n`templates/devcontainer`), with the root BUILD.bazel holding the groups that have no\ndirectory of their own (`//:compose_file`, `//:env_sample`, `//:env_example`, `//:license`,\n`//:devcontainer`, `//:githooks`, and the `//:ci_*` groups)."},"1123":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-71","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#declared-libs-and-payload-groups","content":"`//:stack_data` is the explicit aggregate of all of them, and\n`//scripts:doc_sources` (every `scripts/**.sh`, so a sourced `scripts/lib/*.sh` resolves\ntoo) rides along on every CLI."},"1124":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-72","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-real-checkout-fallback","content":"`proxy/certs/` is `.bazelignored` (bootstrap issues those on the host), so a\n`bazelisk run` of a stack runner, of `push-template`, or of the six CLIs that read a file the\ncheckout alone holds (`dashboard-password`, `pull-models`, `coder-agents`, `spark-verify`,\n`spark-configure`, `build-dev-image`) prefers `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the real checkout)\nover the runfiles copy as the compose project directory, the live `.env`, and the template\ntree (runfiles `templates/**` are symlinks that Coder cannot follow after unpack)."},"1125":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-73","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-real-checkout-fallback","content":"Without the committed payloads a sandboxed run would read a partial copy of the repo and fail\nfor the wrong reason."},"1126":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-74","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#a-new-payload-directory","content":"A new top-level payload directory gets its own package with its own `filegroup` targets, joins\n`//:stack_data` by label, and is named in the map of every target that reads it: `test-fast`\nand `lint` only see repo files that travel in runfiles, so an unlisted directory is invisible\nto the harness rather than checked loosely."},"1127":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-75","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"The two maps in `scripts/BUILD.bazel` and the one in `tests/BUILD.bazel` are the\nmachine-readable record of which repo file each target reads:"},"1128":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-76","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"| Map            | Says                                                                           |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `_SCRIPT_LIBS` | the `scripts/lib` closure one CLI sources, executes, or ships to a remote host |","table":"table-1"},"1129":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-77","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"| Map               | Says                                                                |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `_SCRIPT_PAYLOAD` | the payload groups whose files that CLI (or a lib it sources) opens |","table":"table-1"},"1130":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-78","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"| Map              | Says |\n| ---------------- | ---- |\n| `_SUITE_PAYLOAD` |      |","table":"table-1"},"1131":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-79","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#the-dependency-maps-and-their-gate","content":"| Map               | Says                                                                                |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `*_PAYLOAD_ALLOW` | a pairing the source scan cannot see from either side; each entry states its reason |","table":"table-1"},"1132":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-80","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-reports","content":"`tests/bazel_deps.py` re-derives all of them by scanning the shell and Bats sources and\nreports the drift both ways: a script that starts reading a payload its target does not\ndeclare, and a target that still ships a payload nothing opens."},"1133":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-81","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-reports","content":"`//tests:bats_bazel_deps_test` runs it, so the BUILD files stay something an automated\nreader can trust, and a `bazelisk query` of any target names the files a change to which\nshould be reviewed with it."},"1134":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-82","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"The scan treats as prose rather than a dependency, so the maps record reads and not\nmentions:"},"1135":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-83","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"a comment"},"1136":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-84","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"a here-doc body"},"1137":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-85","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"a log message"},"1138":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-86","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#what-the-scan-counts-as-prose","content":"a scratch file a suite writes"},"1139":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-87","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#when-the-scan-cannot-see-a-pairing","content":"When the scan genuinely cannot see a pairing (a lib that builds a path and returns it as a\nstring, a `case` glob over `git diff` output, help text), the entry goes in the `_ALLOW`\nmap with the reason as a comment above the key; the Bats gate fails an `_ALLOW` key that\nhas no reason."},"1140":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-88","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"A script that needs the checkout reaches it the same way:"},"1141":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-89","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"source its libs by absolute path from `SELF_DIR`"},"1142":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-90","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"resolve the root with `resolve_checkout` (`scripts/lib/common.sh`)"},"1143":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-91","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"`cd` into what it prints"},"1144":{"id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel-92","page_id":"/contribute/building-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","build","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/building-with-bazel#reaching-the-checkout-from-a-script","content":"Never `cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"` - under `bazelisk run` the launcher execs the runfiles\ncopy of the script, so that is the runfiles tree, which holds only `//:stack_data` and is\nrecreated on the next build."},"1145":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","type":"page","content":"Contributor environment","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"url":"/contribute/devcontainer"},"1146":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-0","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer","content":"The one Linux golden image behind laptop work, the Coder workspaces and CI: what the contributor dev container builds, how it caches, how it seeds itself, and which path is the merge gate."},"1147":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-1","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Contributor environment"},"1148":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-2","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-