"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"The cache seam: the mounted volumes, the `~/.bazelrc` block, and when to drop them"},"1180":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-34","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"The background warm-up, and the one knob that turns it off"},"1181":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-35","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"What `seed-dev-env` materializes into that home, and what it refuses to touch"},"1182":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-36","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"GitHub auth inside the container, and why `github-auth check` runs SELF there"},"1183":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-37","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"The merge gate (Linux image) versus the convenience path (native Darwin)"},"1184":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-38","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"What CI does, and why this repo's own Coder workspaces stay on `workspace`"},"1185":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-39","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Keeping the container maintained as the project moves"},"1186":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-40","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"**What this enables**"},"1187":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-41","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Reproducing CI's failure on your own machine with the same image CI runs"},"1188":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-42","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Running the Bazel gate on macOS without maintaining a second, BSD-flavoured toolchain"},"1189":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-43","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Recreating the container without paying for a cold Bazel cache again"},"1190":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-44","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Telling the contributor container, the Coder workspace and the stack host apart in one look"},"1191":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-45","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"One image — `images/dev/Dockerfile`, built as `evo-t1-dev:latest` — is the contributor and\ntest runtime on macOS, on Linux, and on GitHub. The same Dockerfile serves three things:"},"1192":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-46","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"the Coder workspaces the stack provisions"},"1193":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-47","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"the contributor dev container on a laptop"},"1194":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-48","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"the container CI docker-runs its checks inside"},"1195":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-49","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#contributor-environment","content":"Every version in it comes from `images/dev/tool-versions.env`;\n../coder-templates.md covers the workspace side, and\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nis the checklist the PR follows."},"1196":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-50","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"`images/dev/tool-versions.env` is the single source of truth for every tool version:\nBazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, shellcheck (apt), bats, Terraform/tflint/terragrunt, the\nCoder CLI, the Docker *client* trio, Node, Python, Go, protoc and the pinned Grok CLI."},"1197":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-51","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"Each `KEY` there is also an `ARG` in `images/dev/Dockerfile`, and the `ARG` default\nmirrors the pin, so a bare `docker build` matches a scripted one."},"1198":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-52","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"`bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image` refuses to build when a pin has no matching\n`ARG`, or when an `ARG` default drifted from the pin. Add both sides of a new pin in the\nsame change."},"1199":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-53","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"`GH_STACK_ENABLED` is the one build-time choice that sits outside that file, because it\nis a flag rather than a pin. The image installs the official `github/gh-stack` GitHub CLI\nextension (stacked pull requests, invoked as `gh stack`) only for a build that passes\n`GH_STACK_ENABLED=true`, so it ships **off by default** and a normal build says nothing\nabout it. Turn it on with `GH_STACK_ENABLED=true bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image`:\nthe script forwards the flag to the guarded `RUN` in `images/dev/Dockerfile`, only an\nexact `true` enables the layer, and what it installs stays pinned by `GH_STACK_VERSION` in\n`tool-versions.env`. Owner: the stack image build (that script and that layer). Expiry:\n2027-02-23, by which point the extension is either on by default or the flag and its\noff-path are deleted in one `chore:`."},"1200":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-54","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"The image ships the Docker client only. The build ends with `test ! -x\n/usr/local/bin/dockerd` (plus `containerd`, `runc`, `docker-proxy`), so the merge-gate\ncontainer drives a daemon it is given rather than owning one."},"1201":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-55","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-one-image-the-one-pin-file","content":"Build it locally when you want the tag in the local store (the Coder docker provider\nresolves `evo-t1-dev:latest` from there and never pulls):"},"1202":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-56","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#reopen-the-repo-in-a-container","content":"Use VS Code, Cursor, or any editor with the Dev Containers extension, and reopen this\nrepository **in a container**."},"1203":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-57","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` is what that reads:"},"1204":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-58","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                                  | Value                          | Why                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build.context` / `build.dockerfile` | `../images/dev` / `Dockerfile` | `ARG` defaults are the pins, so no build args are needed. |","table":"table-0"},"1205":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-59","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key               | Value                                                    | Why                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build.cacheFrom` | `ghcr.io/toxicoder/evo-t1-coder-stack/evo-t1-dev:latest` | Seeds BuildKit's layer cache from the image CI publishes on every merge to `main`, so a fresh clone pulls finished layers. An unreachable registry is a buildx warning, not a failed build. |","table":"table-0"},"1206":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-60","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key          | Value   | Why |\n| ------------ | ------- | --- |\n| `remoteUser` | `coder` |     |","table":"table-0"},"1207":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-61","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                   | Value  | Why                                                                                                                       |\n| --------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `updateRemoteUserUID` | `true` | The container's `coder` uid matches the host user's, so the bind-mounted checkout stays writable without a `chmod` dance. |","table":"table-0"},"1208":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-62","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                          | Value                   | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `containerEnv` / `remoteEnv` | `EVO_T1_DEVCONTAINER=1` | The marker that says *contributor container*, not Coder workspace. Also carries `SEARXNG_URL`, `EVO_T1_BAZEL_CACHE_ROOT`, and the `BAZELISK_HOME` / `NPM_CONFIG_CACHE` / `UV_CACHE_DIR` / `PIP_CACHE_DIR` download dirs. |","table":"table-0"},"1209":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-63","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key      | Value                                       | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mounts` | `/var/run/docker.sock` + four named volumes | The socket is the workstation's own daemon, which is how a `docker run` inside it is a real one. The volumes are Bazel's disk, repository and output caches plus the package-manager download cache; see The cache seam. A host whose daemon is not on that path (a remote or TCP `DOCKER_HOST`, or a Docker Desktop with no `/var/run/docker.sock` compatibility symlink) drops that one entry: the build, the seed and every gate work without it, and only `docker` commands in here lose their daemon. |","table":"table-0"},"1210":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-64","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key       | Value                                                                     | Why                            |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `runArgs` | `--add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway`, `--ulimit nofile=1048576` | `:4000` and SearXNG on `:8181` |","table":"table-0"},"1211":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-65","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key            | Value  | Why                                                        |\n| -------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `forwardPorts` | `3000` | `bazelisk run //docs-site:dev` serves the docs site there. |","table":"table-0"},"1212":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-66","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                | Value               | Why                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hostRequirements` | 4 cpus, 8 GB, 32 GB | Advisory floor for the gate and a Next build (the devcontainer CLI and Codespaces enforce it, an editor warns). |","table":"table-0"},"1213":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-67","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                 | Value                                                    | Why                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `postCreateCommand` | `bash .devcontainer/library-scripts/configure.sh create` | One idempotent script: the cache seam, the seed, the git hooks, the socket ACL, then the background warm-up. |","table":"table-0"},"1214":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-68","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                | Value                                                   | Why                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `postStartCommand` | `bash .devcontainer/library-scripts/configure.sh start` | Runs on every start, not just the first: cheap checks, the socket ACL again (host-side perms change), and a warm-up a previous start skipped or failed. |","table":"table-0"},"1215":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-69","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-devcontainerjson-declares","content":"| Key                                | Value | Why                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `customizations.vscode.extensions` |       | shellcheck and shfmt are the two `//:lint` runners, wired into the editor beside the Terraform, Docker, YAML, Python and Tailwind helpers this tree holds. Nothing else is installed: the list is the languages under `git ls-files`, because every extension is a download at container start. |","table":"table-0"},"1216":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-70","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"`customizations.vscode.settings` carries container-scoped settings only:"},"1217":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-71","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"the two lint-and-format tool pins (`shellcheck.executablePath` with\n`shellcheck.customArgs`, `shellformat.path` with `shellformat.flag`)"},"1218":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-72","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"the `bazel-*` and `node_modules` watcher excludes"},"1219":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-73","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"`git.branchProtection` for `main`"},"1220":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-74","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"Each key belongs to an extension the row above installs, which is what makes the pin do\nsomething."},"1221":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-75","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-container-scoped-editor-settings","content":"Editor taste (theme, minimap, word wrap) still arrives from `seed-dev-env.sh` through\n`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json`, so the two never fight."},"1222":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-76","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-none-of-this-is-in-the-image","content":"Nothing in this table belongs in the image. `images/dev/Dockerfile` is shared with the\nCoder workspaces and the CI gate, so it carries the toolchain and stays unaware that a\ncontributor container exists."},"1223":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-77","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-none-of-this-is-in-the-image","content":"Everything above is container shape, read from the checkout on every start. That is what\nmakes the whole thing editable without a rebuild."},"1224":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-78","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-dies-with-the-container","content":"`.bazelrc` points `--disk_cache` and `--repository_cache` at `~/.cache`, and Bazel's\noutput base lives under `~/.cache/bazel` as well. Inside a container `$HOME` is the\nimage's own filesystem, so all three die with the container, and a recreation - which\nis what every edit to this config or the Dockerfile causes - repays the whole cost:"},"1225":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-79","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-dies-with-the-container","content":"re-fetch every external archive"},"1226":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-80","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-dies-with-the-container","content":"re-analyze the graph"},"1227":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-81","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-dies-with-the-container","content":"re-run every action"},"1228":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-82","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-block-configuresh-writes","content":"The config mounts three named volumes under `/var/cache/evo-t1-bazel`, and\n`.devcontainer/library-scripts/configure.sh` writes this block into `~/.bazelrc`:"},"1229":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-83","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-block-configuresh-writes","content":"`~/.bazelrc` is the seam because Bazel reads it after the repo's `.bazelrc`, and\nbecause it reaches only this container: a Coder workspace booted from the same image\nkeeps using its own `~/.cache`."},"1230":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-84","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-block-configuresh-writes","content":"Everything outside the two marker lines belongs to the developer and survives every run,\nand a re-run replaces the block rather than stacking a second one."},"1231":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-85","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-block-configuresh-writes","content":"`EVO_T1_BAZEL_CACHE_ROOT` is the one value both halves read, so the mount targets and the\nblock move together, and `bazelisk test //tests:bats_contributor_devcontainer_test` fails\nif they drift."},"1232":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-86","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#dropping-the-caches","content":"Docker creates a named volume once and reuses it, so the caches survive recreations\nuntil you deliberately drop them."},"1233":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-87","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#dropping-the-caches","content":"The volumes belong to the host's daemon, so a host shell is the reliable place to run\nthis: from inside the container the same commands work only while the config's socket\nmount is in place."},"1234":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-88","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#dropping-the-caches","content":"Drop them when a Bazel upgrade or a corrupt action cache is the suspect, not as\nroutine cleanup - deleting them costs one cold gate run each."},"1235":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-89","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"`configure.sh` finishes by starting `library-scripts/warmup.sh` detached (`setsid`, so\nthe Dev Containers CLI's teardown of the postCreate process group does not take it\nwith it). It runs two commands, in this order:"},"1236":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-90","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"`bazelisk test //:test-fast`"},"1237":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-91","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"`bazelisk run\n//docs-site:install`"},"1238":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-92","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"That is where a cold container actually spends its time:"},"1239":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-93","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"the Bazelisk download"},"1240":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-94","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"every `MODULE.bazel` fetch"},"1241":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-95","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"the site's `npm ci`"},"1242":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-96","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"The editor is usable the whole time; the first real gate run then reads a warm cache."},"1243":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-97","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"A warm-up that did not finish is not skipped forever: `postStartCommand` re-runs it\nwhenever the status file still says `failed: <step>`, and only an `ok` one is left alone."},"1244":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-98","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"`EVO_T1_WARMUP=off` is the only knob. It reaches the container through\n`containerEnv`'s `${localEnv:EVO_T1_WARMUP}`, so a laptop can opt out permanently from\nits own shell profile without editing the config, and an unset value keeps the default."},"1245":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-99","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-warm-up","content":"A skipped or failed warm-up costs a slow first command and nothing else: every gate\nstill runs, and `//:lint` does not depend on it."},"1246":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-100","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"The container is code in this repository, and it rots the same way a lockfile does.\nThese are the moments that oblige a contributor to touch it, and each has a gate:"},"1247":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-101","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project                                     | What the container owes it                                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A pin moves or is added in `images/dev/tool-versions.env` | The matching `ARG` in `images/dev/Dockerfile`, or `bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image` refuses the build. `build.cacheFrom` keeps the rebuild cheap. |","table":"table-1"},"1248":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-102","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project                                             | What the container owes it                                                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A gate gains a tool (`//:lint`, `//:validate`, a coverage target) | The tool belongs in the image and its pins in `tool-versions.env`; a container-only convenience belongs in `configure.sh`, never in the image. |","table":"table-1"},"1249":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-103","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project                 | What the container owes it                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| A new language or lint runner appears | The extension and its formatter path and flags in `customizations.vscode` (`shellcheck.executablePath` + `shellcheck.customArgs`, `shellformat.path` + `shellformat.flag`), set to the exact binary and flags the gate runs - the Bats suite reads those flags out of `lints/run_shellcheck.sh` and `lints/run_shfmt.sh` rather than repeating them, so a gate change goes red here, and `//lints:runners` stays declared for that suite in `_SUITE_PAYLOAD_ALLOW` (`tests/BUILD.bazel`) or the comparison loses the files it reads. Keys must belong to an extension the config actually installs: `bashIde.*` configures a different shellcheck extension and is inert here. |","table":"table-1"},"1250":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-104","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project                      | What the container owes it                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A new top-level payload directory of shell | `lints/run_shellcheck.sh`, `lints/run_shfmt.sh` and `fix.sh` scan sets, plus the matching entry in `lints/BUILD.bazel`. `.devcontainer` joined all three; a fourth directory is a one-line change to each. |","table":"table-1"},"1251":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-105","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project            | What the container owes it                                                                                            |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| A new contributor-facing env var | `containerEnv` (and `remoteEnv` when a VS Code terminal or task must see it), never a shell profile the image writes. |","table":"table-1"},"1252":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-106","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"| Change in the project                        | What the container owes it |\n| -------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| A new cache worth keeping across recreations | A named volume in `mounts` |","table":"table-1"},"1253":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-107","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"`.devcontainer/library-scripts/*.sh` is first-party shell: it carries\n`# @function` blocks, is linted by `//:lint` (shellcheck `-x --severity=warning`, shfmt\n`-s -i 2 -ci`), and its behaviour is pinned by\n`bazelisk test //tests:bats_contributor_devcontainer_test`."},"1254":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-108","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"That suite reads `devcontainer.json` as data, so each of these is a failing test rather\nthan a surprise on someone's laptop:"},"1255":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-109","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"renaming a mount target"},"1256":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-110","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"dropping the `EVO_T1_DEVCONTAINER` marker from one env layer"},"1257":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-111","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#keeping-it-maintained","content":"pointing the build at something other than `images/dev`"},"1258":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-112","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#how-the-container-seeds-it","content":"`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh` materializes, into a laptop or CI home, the same stack-owned\nfiles a Coder workspace writes at startup — from the same template payloads, with no\nTerraform and no docker."},"1259":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-113","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#how-the-container-seeds-it","content":"The contributor container runs it for you: `postCreateCommand` calls\n`configure.sh create`, which calls this script with `--devcontainer --context7-mcp`\nand nothing else, so a rebuilt container re-materializes every stack-marked file from the\ncurrent seed and leaves anything you own alone."},"1260":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-114","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#how-the-container-seeds-it","content":"Everything below is what that one call does, and what to re-run by hand after a seed\nchange:"},"1261":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-115","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag           | Effect                                                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--home <dir>` | Home tree to shape (default `$HOME`; created when absent; an existing non-directory is an error). |","table":"table-2"},"1262":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-116","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag                  | Effect                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--litellm-url <url>` | Model-transport address rendered into `settings.json` and `~/.grok/config.toml` (default `http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1`). |","table":"table-2"},"1263":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-117","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag             | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--context7-mcp` | Keep the `[mcp_servers.context7]` docs lane in the rendered `~/.grok/config.toml` even with no `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` in the environment. Without it a keyless home renders the context7-free file, so the contributor has no docs lane while their workspaces do. The key is optional: with no value the server sends no `Authorization` header, still handshakes, and answers at the public rate limit (private libraries are the only thing out of reach), so a missing block is the defect this flag prevents, not a key problem. |","table":"table-2"},"1264":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-118","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag             | Effect                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--devcontainer` | After a successful write, run `gh auth setup-git` when `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` is set and `gh` is on PATH. Best effort, and the token is never an argument. |","table":"table-2"},"1265":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-119","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag      | Effect                            |\n| --------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `--force` | Re-materialize files a user owns. |","table":"table-2"},"1266":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-120","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-flags-it-takes","content":"| Flag        | Effect                                                            |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dry-run` | Print the plan; write nothing, create no directory, call no `gh`. |","table":"table-2"},"1267":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-121","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-two-research-lanes","content":"The two research lanes that config can render are split by question type:"},"1268":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-122","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-two-research-lanes","content":"a library, framework, CLI or setup question goes to `context7` (resolve the library id\nfirst, then query docs on that id)"},"1269":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-123","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-two-research-lanes","content":"anything else on the web goes to the `searxng` `search` tool"},"1270":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-124","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-two-research-lanes","content":"a URL already in hand goes to `searxng`'s `fetch_content` - Grok's native `web_search`\nis parked here and native `web_fetch` needs an egress proxy endpoint this stack does not\nrun, so neither is a lane"},"1271":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-125","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-two-research-lanes","content":"Prove what this home declares with:"},"1272":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-126","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#repairing-a-missing-context7-block","content":"A missing `[mcp_servers.context7]` block in that file means the seed ran keyless and\nwithout `--context7-mcp`: re-run the seeder with the flag, adding `--force` when the\nexisting file carries no stack marker and the seeder left it alone."},"1273":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-127","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#repairing-a-missing-context7-block","content":"On a Coder workspace the same repair runs from the stack host:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:refresh-configs -- --container coder-<owner>-<ws>`."},"1274":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-128","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"What it writes:"},"1275":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-129","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"`~/.tmux.conf`"},"1276":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-130","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"the shared `~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` (with the code-server and desktop VS Code\nUser settings symlinked to it)"},"1277":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-131","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"`~/.grok/AGENTS.md`"},"1278":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-132","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"`~/.coder/AGENTS.md`"},"1279":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-133","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"the rendered `~/.grok/config.toml`"},"1280":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-134","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"the two terminal helpers in `~/.grok/bin`"},"1281":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-135","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"`~/.grok/notes-setup.sh` plus this clone's `notes.md`"},"1282":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-136","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-files-it-writes","content":"the `~/.grok/bin` line in `~/.bashrc`"},"1283":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-137","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-notesmd-back-copy","content":"That `notes.md` is `notes_materialize` from the same library: it restores the canonical copy\nunder `~/.grok/notes/<host>/<owner>/<repo>/` over a live file that is empty or still the\nseeded stub, and copies a real live file back there, so a stub never walks over written\nnotes."},"1284":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-138","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#the-notesmd-back-copy","content":"Here that runs once, at seed time - the background watcher that repeats the back-copy\nabout every 30 seconds is a workspace-startup thing (`NOTES_SYNC_INTERVAL`; see\n../grok-build-and-agents.md) - so re-run the\nseeder to push a fresh edit to the canonical copy in this container."},"1285":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-139","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#stack-owned-and-user-owned-files","content":"Two rules decide every write, and they are the same rules the workspace startup applies:"},"1286":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-140","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#stack-owned-and-user-owned-files","content":"A file carrying the stack marker - the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` comment, the\n`\"__evoT1Stack\": true` JSON key, or the `__evoT1Stack = true` TOML key - is\nstack-owned and is reseeded when the seed in this repo drifted. Taking\n`~/.grok/config.toml` over means deleting both its marker lines, since the Grok CLI\ndeletes comments when it rewrites that file:\n../grok-build-and-agents.md."},"1287":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-141","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#stack-owned-and-user-owned-files","content":"A marker-free file is user-owned and stays untouched unless `--force` says otherwise.\nThe terminal helpers and `notes-setup.sh` are the exception: startup rewrites those on\nevery boot, so this script does too."},"1288":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-142","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#stack-owned-and-user-owned-files","content":"It never writes a secret, never writes a GitHub token or a PAT, and never installs the\nGrok CLI — the golden image already carries `/usr/local/bin/grok`."},"1289":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-143","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#stack-owned-and-user-owned-files","content":"Exit `5` means no proven checkout was found (it wants `docker-compose.yml` where it is\nlooking), which is the same repo-root probe every other script in the repo makes."},"1290":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-144","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"The contributor container is its own credential chain, so the doctor runs in SELF mode\nthere — exactly as it does inside a Coder workspace:"},"1291":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-145","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"SELF mode applies when `CODER_WORKSPACE_ID` is set **or** `EVO_T1_DEVCONTAINER=1` is. The\ncontainer sets the latter; a Coder workspace sets the former."},"1292":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-146","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"SELF means no docker at all and no `DOCKER_HOST`: one probe of this environment's own\ncredential chain, printed as one `self:` line per credential. `docker` in here addresses\nthe workstation daemon mounted in, never the stack host's workspace fleet."},"1293":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-147","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"Pass only the repository URL. A named container argument is refused with a pointer to the\nhost shell, because that container lives on a daemon this environment cannot enumerate."},"1294":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-148","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"Credentials still arrive by the one supported path: Coder External Auth mints them, and\nthe gh auth store is what git actually reads."},"1295":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-149","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"That store is the target because `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` are the copy injected when the\ncontainer started and expire about an hour later, and the plain\n`!gh auth git-credential` helper echoes that pair, so git would keep sending a dead token."},"1296":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-150","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"The helper this stack installs clears the pair first, which is why\n`gh auth setup-git` alone is not enough. There is no static token and no PAT in this\nrepo's tooling."},"1297":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-151","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"`push would FAIL` from the check above means one command:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- fix https://github.com/toxicoder/evo-t1-coder-stack.git`.\nIt:"},"1298":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-152","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"mints a live token"},"1299":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-153","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"writes the store"},"1300":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-154","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"installs that helper"},"1301":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-155","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"re-proves the verdict"},"1302":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-156","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#github-auth-in-the-container","content":"For `gh` itself, prefix `env -u GH_TOKEN -u GITHUB_TOKEN`: no process can rewrite another\nprocess's environment."},"1303":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-157","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#running-the-gate-here","content":"The merge gate is the Linux image, so run it in the contributor container:"},"1304":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-158","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"From a machine that is **not** inside the container, ask the image to run them instead of\ninstalling the toolchain onto that machine:"},"1305":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-159","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"That is the host ingress:"},"1306":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-160","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"it `docker run`s `evo-t1-dev:latest` as this process's uid:gid (`$(id -u):$(id -g)`)"},"1307":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-161","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"sets `HOME=/tmp` and `USER=$(id -un)` so Bazel has a writable home and a name for a uid\nthe image passwd file does not list"},"1308":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-162","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"runs the same suites CI runs"},"1309":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-163","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"A macOS laptop gets the Linux result without a Linux box."},"1310":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-164","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#from-the-host-with-test-in-image","content":"Build the tag first with `bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image` if the daemon does not\nhave it."},"1311":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-165","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#typed-inside-the-container","content":"Typed *inside* the contributor container that same target touches no docker:\n`EVO_T1_DEVCONTAINER=1` tells it this environment already is the golden image, so it\nexecs `bazelisk` in place."},"1312":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-166","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#typed-inside-the-container","content":"The command is the same on both sides of the seam, and a container never nests inside\nitself."},"1313":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-167","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#native-macos-runs-are-convenience-only","content":"Native `bazelisk test` on macOS is a convenience, not a merge path. The suites run there,\nbut the BSD userland differs from the GNU one the image ships (`sed`, `date`, `find`,\n`sort`), so a green Darwin run is not the run that gates the merge and a red one is not\nproof of a defect."},"1314":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-168","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#native-macos-runs-are-convenience-only","content":"The container, or `test-in-image`, is the answer\ntest-with-bazel.md and ../branching.md gate on."},"1315":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-169","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"`.github/workflows/ci.yml` builds `images/dev` with `docker buildx build` and the GitHub\nActions layer cache (`type=gha`), then `docker run`s that image and runs the checks inside\nit:"},"1316":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-170","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"`//:test-fast`"},"1317":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-171","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"`//:lint`"},"1318":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-172","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"`//:validate`"},"1319":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-173","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"the `docs-site/` Node checks"},"1320":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-174","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"No Actions `container:` key is involved. The job runs on a plain runner and reaches the\ntoolchain through `docker run --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\"` with `HOME=/tmp` and\n`USER=$(id -un)`, so:"},"1321":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-175","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"what gates the merge is an image tag"},"1322":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-176","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"the bind-mounted checkout stays writable"},"1323":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-177","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"permission tests see a non-root identity"},"1324":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-178","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"Bazel can name a uid the image passwd file does not list"},"1325":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-179","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"The Bazel job no longer installs the pins onto the runner: the image already has them at\nthe pinned versions."},"1326":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-180","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"A pull request that does not touch `images/dev/**` replays the cached layers instead of\nrebuilding them, which is what keeps the gate's wall time flat."},"1327":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-181","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-ci-does","content":"The equivalent run on your own machine is the host ingress above, so a CI-only failure is\nreproducible without a Linux box or a workflow rerun."},"1328":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-182","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-this-repos-own-workspaces-stay-on-workspace","content":"`.devcontainer/contributor-env` is a sentinel, not a config file."},"1329":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-183","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-this-repos-own-workspaces-stay-on-workspace","content":"It is tracked in this repository, and `probe_repo` (in `scripts/lib/workspace.sh`) treats a\nclone that tracks it as a **miss** — exit `3` — even when the same clone also tracks\n`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`."},"1330":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-184","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-this-repos-own-workspaces-stay-on-workspace","content":"The sentinel outranks every other signal, so `new-workspace` answers `workspace` for this\nrepo and a Coder workspace of it never builds the contributor container on its DinD\nsidecar."},"1331":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-185","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-this-repos-own-workspaces-stay-on-workspace","content":"That container is the *laptop and CI* environment: it mounts the host docker socket and\nassumes a workstation daemon, neither of which belongs inside a workspace's nested dev\ncontainer."},"1332":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-186","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#why-this-repos-own-workspaces-stay-on-workspace","content":"Do not copy the sentinel into another repository. An application repo's\n`.devcontainer/` is exactly what `new-workspace` is supposed to find, and the sentinel in\nfront of it silently downgrades that workspace to the plain template."},"1333":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-187","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"**Not the stack host.** The compose host (gmktec) is bootstrapped with\n`bash scripts/setup-host.sh`, and it cannot be this container: it owns the daemon that\nruns Coder, LiteLLM, Ollama, Kasm, Homepage and Hermes. See\n../project-conventions.md for the ingress rule that keeps\nthat script the single documented `bash scripts/…`."},"1334":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-188","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"**Not a template change.** `templates/workspace/startup.sh.tftpl` and\n`templates/devcontainer/startup.sh.tftpl` are untouched by any of this; the contributor\nseed reads them as payloads, it does not rewrite the twins."},"1335":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-189","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"**Not a second toolchain.** Nothing in the contributor path installs pins onto a laptop\nor a runner — that is what the image is for."},"1336":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-190","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"**Not a place for contributor-only behavior in the image.** The image is shared with Coder\nworkspaces and CI, so anything that only a person at a keyboard wants (the Bazel volume\nseam, the warm-up, the git hooks, the socket ACL) lives in\n`.devcontainer/library-scripts/configure.sh`, which only this container runs. An `ENV` or\n`RUN` line added to `images/dev/Dockerfile` for the same purpose changes what a workspace\ngets, which is the mistake this split exists to prevent."},"1337":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-191","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"**Not a credential store.** GitHub auth stays Coder External Auth; no static token and no\nPAT appears in any file this page describes."},"1338":{"id":"/contribute/devcontainer-192","page_id":"/contribute/devcontainer","tags":["contributing","devcontainer","bazel","ci","docker"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/devcontainer#what-this-is-not","content":"When the container itself is the suspect, `bazelisk run //:validate` from inside it is the\nfastest answer, and ../troubleshooting.md covers the stack-side\nfailures it rules in or out."},"1339":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"page","content":"Writing documentation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style"},"1340":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-0","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style","content":"The contract every page in docs/ has to satisfy before the site will render it: frontmatter, the authored H1, the opening scan pair, and the navigation file that decides whether a page is reachable at all."},"1341":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-1","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Writing documentation"},"1342":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-2","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#frontmatter","content":"Frontmatter"},"1343":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-3","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-declared-fields","content":"The declared fields"},"1344":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-4","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-each-field-feeds","content":"What each field feeds"},"1345":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-5","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-page-title","content":"The page title"},"1346":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-6","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-layout-prints","content":"What the layout prints"},"1347":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-7","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#why-the-body-owns-the-title","content":"Why the body owns the title"},"1348":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-8","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-opening-scan-pair","content":"The opening scan pair"},"1349":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-9","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-authored-shape","content":"The authored shape"},"1350":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-10","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"How the match works"},"1351":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-11","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#chrome-that-arrives-on-its-own","content":"Chrome that arrives on its own"},"1352":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-12","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#prose-and-tables","content":"Prose and tables"},"1353":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-13","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#diagrams-and-fenced-code","content":"Diagrams and fenced code"},"1354":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-14","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#navigation","content":"Navigation"},"1355":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-15","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#where-the-sidebar-comes-from","content":"Where the sidebar comes from"},"1356":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-16","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#leaves-and-folders","content":"Leaves and folders"},"1357":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-17","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#regenerating-the-generated-file","content":"Regenerating the generated file"},"1358":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-18","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-checks-refuse","content":"What the checks refuse"},"1359":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-19","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#checks","content":"Checks"},"1360":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-20","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-bazel-targets","content":"The Bazel targets"},"1361":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-21","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","type":"heading","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-operator-cli-twin","content":"The operator CLI twin"},"1362":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-22","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1363":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-23","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"What a page's frontmatter has to carry, and what each field is used for"},"1364":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-24","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Why every page writes its own `# H1` and what the layout prints beside it"},"1365":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-25","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"The two opening lists that become the scan card, and the order they have to sit in"},"1366":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-26","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"How abbreviations, tables and diagrams pick up their chrome without a component call"},"1367":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-27","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Where the sidebar comes from, and which check refuses a page it cannot reach"},"1368":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-28","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"**What this enables**"},"1369":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-29","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Adding a page that shows up in the menu, the search index and the prev/next footer"},"1370":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-30","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Predicting what a reader sees from what you wrote, without opening a browser to find out"},"1371":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-31","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"Fixing a docs failure from the assertion that named it"},"1372":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-32","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#writing-documentation","content":"The site is a Fumadocs app that reads `docs/` straight out of the repository, so the markdown\nhere is the source of record: nothing is copied into `docs-site/`, and the README's links keep\npointing at these files. Most of the chrome is derived from the prose rather than authored in\nit, which is what keeps 20-odd pages consistent."},"1373":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-33","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-declared-fields","content":"Every page declares three fields, and `docs-site/tests/unit/docs-content.test.ts` refuses a\npage that is missing any of them:"},"1374":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-34","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-each-field-feeds","content":"`title` is the sidebar label, the search result title, and the string your `# H1` has to\nmatch character for character."},"1375":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-35","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-each-field-feeds","content":"`description` is printed as the lead paragraph under the title and indexed for search. Quote\nit when it contains a colon, or YAML reads the line as a mapping."},"1376":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-36","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-each-field-feeds","content":"`tags` are indexed, so a reader who searches for the word you filed the page under finds it.\n`pageSchema` strips unknown keys, which is why `tags` is declared explicitly in\n`docs-site/lib/content.ts` — a new field needs the same treatment or it silently never\nreaches the index."},"1377":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-37","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-layout-prints","content":"Each page writes its own `# H1`, once, as the first heading of the body, spelled exactly like\nthe frontmatter `title`."},"1378":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-38","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-layout-prints","content":"That heading is the one the table of contents and every `#anchor` point at, so `DocsH1`\nprints it and then the description beneath it as the lead paragraph."},"1379":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-39","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-layout-prints","content":"A page whose first heading is not its title keeps a plain heading and gets no lead paragraph,\nwhich is the visible sign that the two strings drifted apart."},"1380":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-40","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#why-the-body-owns-the-title","content":"The reason the authored heading is the only title: the page header used to print the frontmatter\ntitle and the body printed its own, so every page opened with the same string twice."},"1381":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-41","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-authored-shape","content":"Immediately after the title, two bold labels each followed by a bullet list:"},"1382":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-42","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"`docs-site/lib/remark-page-brief.ts` recognises that four-node run and rewrites it into one\n`<PageBrief>` — the two-column card with the list and tick icons."},"1383":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-43","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"The match is exact:"},"1384":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-44","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"the label has to be the whole paragraph, bold, and spelled `What's on this page` and\n`What this enables`"},"1385":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-45","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"the lists have to be lists"},"1386":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-46","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"no heading may sit between the title and the pair"},"1387":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-47","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#how-the-match-works","content":"Get any of that wrong and the page renders the lists as plain bullets, which is the only\nsymptom."},"1388":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-48","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#chrome-that-arrives-on-its-own","content":"Nothing below needs a component call in the page."},"1389":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-49","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#prose-and-tables","content":"**Abbreviations.** A term listed in `docs/includes/abbreviations.md` as `*[TERM]: definition`\nis wrapped wherever it appears in prose. Hover or focus shows the definition; click or Enter\nopens it in a dialog. Text inside a link, a heading, inline code, or an existing term is left\nalone. Keep each definition tooltip-sized."},"1390":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-50","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#prose-and-tables","content":"**Tables.** A content table gets its head pinned under the navbar while the table is on\nscreen, and a mirrored scroll bar at the bottom of the viewport when its columns are wider\nthan the page. Both come from `docs-site/components/table-chrome.tsx`; a table that already\ncarries a class is left as authored."},"1391":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-51","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#diagrams-and-fenced-code","content":"**Diagrams.** A ` ```mermaid ` fence renders through `Mermaid`, follows the light/dark switch,\nand shows the chart text beside a parse error rather than leaving a blank box."},"1392":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-52","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#diagrams-and-fenced-code","content":"**Fenced code.** Every fence needs a language, checked by the same contract test, because the\nhighlighter and the copy button both key off it."},"1393":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-53","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#where-the-sidebar-comes-from","content":"The sidebar is not read from the filesystem: most pages sit flat in `docs/` while belonging to\ndifferent sections, and the reading order a prev/next footer needs is an editorial decision."},"1394":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-54","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#where-the-sidebar-comes-from","content":"The tree is declared once in `NAV` inside `docs-site/scripts/gen_nav.py` and generated into\n`docs-site/lib/nav.json`, which the page-tree builder imports and a Zod schema validates."},"1395":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-55","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#leaves-and-folders","content":"A section holds an ordered mix of leaves and collapsible folders:"},"1396":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-56","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#leaves-and-folders","content":"A leaf is `(label, path)` and a folder is `(label, [child, ...])`"},"1397":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-57","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#leaves-and-folders","content":"Folders stay ordinary directories: a section whose first entry is an index page uses that\npage as its clickable label"},"1398":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-58","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#regenerating-the-generated-file","content":"Regenerate after you change either the tree or the file layout:"},"1399":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-59","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#what-the-checks-refuse","content":"`//docs-site:nav_test` and the contract test together refuse a page that exists but is not\ndeclared, and a declaration whose file is gone, so an unlinked page cannot be merged."},"1400":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-60","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-operator-cli-twin","content":"`docs/manage-docs.sh` is the same set as a single operator CLI (`serve`, `build`, `preview`,\n`verify`, `typecheck`, `test`, `nav`, `status`, `clean`) for a host that has Node but not Bazel."},"1401":{"id":"/contribute/docs-style-61","page_id":"/contribute/docs-style","tags":["docs","fumadocs","writing","nav"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/docs-style#the-operator-cli-twin","content":"The gates run through Bazel; see Testing with Bazel for how the npm-backed\ntargets are wired and why they stay out of `//:test-fast`."},"1402":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"page","content":"Navigating the repo with the Bazel graph","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel"},"1403":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-0","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","content":"Answer what-depends-on-this with one bazelisk query instead of a grep sweep: the bazel-map CLI, the raw query predicates behind it, and the empty-result trap."},"1404":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-1","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Navigating the repo with the Bazel graph"},"1405":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-2","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#why-a-query-not-a-grep","content":"Why a query, not a grep"},"1406":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-3","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"What the logs measured"},"1407":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-4","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-not-querying-costs","content":"What not querying costs"},"1408":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-5","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"url":"/contribu