":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Running the suites that cover the files you touched instead of the whole fast gate"},"1443":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-40","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Catching a payload directory no filegroup claims before the gates stay green by accident"},"1444":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-41","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Telling a rule class from a target name without opening a BUILD file"},"1445":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-42","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Stopping the late-gate discovery of a coupling rule the graph already recorded"},"1446":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-43","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"This repo keeps its coupling in BUILD files. Three of them carry the record:"},"1447":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-44","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"`scripts/BUILD.bazel` names the libs and payload groups each CLI reads"},"1448":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-45","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"`tests/BUILD.bazel` names what each Bats suite opens"},"1449":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-46","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"the root `BUILD.bazel` aggregates every payload group into `//:stack_data`"},"1450":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-47","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"`//tests:bats_bazel_deps_test` fails when those maps drift from the sources, so the graph is a\nrecord an automated reader can trust, and \"which suites cover this file\" has a ground truth sitting\nin it. Answering that from `grep` re-derives what one `bazelisk query` prints."},"1451":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-48","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"Three pages this one leans on:"},"1452":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-49","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"building-with-bazel.md explains the maps, runfiles,\nand the daily commands"},"1453":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-50","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#navigating-the-repo-with-the-bazel-graph","content":"test-with-bazel.md explains the suites those queries name\nand the two inventory gates; ../project-conventions.md\nthe CLI vocabulary this tool prints in"},"1454":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-51","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"A sweep of this repo's own agent session logs measured the habits the graph is meant to replace."},"1455":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-52","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"Corpus: the 199 parent sessions recorded for this checkout under `~/.grok/sessions/`\nbefore 2026-11-01"},"1456":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-53","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"Counted with `jq` and `grep -c` over each session's `chat_history.jsonl`"},"1457":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-54","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"Every count is a floor, because a truncated tool result hides a call"},"1458":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-55","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                   | Measured             |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `bazelisk query` at all | 8 sessions, about 4% |","table":"table-0"},"1459":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-56","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                      | Measured                  |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `rdeps()` and `somepath()` | never used in that corpus |","table":"table-0"},"1460":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-57","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                                    | Measured                                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Recursive grep for a structural question | the default instrument: `grep -rn` outnumbered `bazelisk query` by an order of magnitude |","table":"table-0"},"1461":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-58","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                                         | Measured                                          |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//:test-fast` re-run to learn one dependency | 48 sessions ran it; 16 ran it three or more times |","table":"table-0"},"1462":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-59","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                                                       | Measured    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| Reading the checker's own source to learn why a gate failed | 19 sessions |","table":"table-0"},"1463":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-60","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-the-logs-measured","content":"| Habit                                               | Measured                                                      |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Guessing a target name into `ERROR: no such target` | 4 to 7 sessions, depending on how strictly a match is counted |","table":"table-0"},"1464":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-61","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-not-querying-costs","content":"The cost of not querying shows up late. In the sessions that hit a coupling rule, the first\n`FAIL: //` line appeared only after a hundred or more messages of editing: the rule was\ndiscoverable in the graph on message 1, and was instead discovered by running the gate."},"1465":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-62","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-not-querying-costs","content":"One agent audited `//:stack_data` by listing the repo's top-level directories rather than diffing\nthe graph against `git ls-files`, which is the same question asked in a way that cannot answer it."},"1466":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-63","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-not-querying-costs","content":"The verbs below are the shapes of those questions."},"1467":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-64","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-cli-bazel-map","content":"`bazel-map` is a thin shell over `bazelisk query`. It reads nothing and writes nothing; each verb\nis one query, run from the real checkout, with Bazel's stderr kept so a miss is reported instead of\nswallowed."},"1468":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-65","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-cli-bazel-map","content":"Run it through Bazel like every other CLI:"},"1469":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-66","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#flags-and-exit-codes","content":"Flags, accepted anywhere in argv: `--staged`, `--untracked`, `--ref <ref>`, `--all`,\n`--label-kind`, `--json`, `-h|--help`."},"1470":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-67","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#flags-and-exit-codes","content":"Exit codes:"},"1471":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-68","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#flags-and-exit-codes","content":"0 when every named thing resolved"},"1472":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-69","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#flags-and-exit-codes","content":"1 on a query failure"},"1473":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-70","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#flags-and-exit-codes","content":"2 on a usage error (an unknown verb or flag, or a verb invoked without the argument it needs)"},"1474":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-71","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#act-on-the-answer-with---json","content":"**Use `--json` when you want to act on the answer.** Prose (`== section ==`, `ok:`, `note:`,\n`summary:`) rides stderr and stdout carries only labels, one per line, which is the shape\n`bazelisk test` consumes:"},"1475":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-72","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#act-on-the-answer-with---json","content":"Without `--json` the same labels are interleaved with the report lines, so piping them straight into\nanother command feeds it `ok: tests-for` as an argument."},"1476":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-73","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#act-on-the-answer-with---json","content":"Paths are repo-relative, and a batch costs one query: when a batch fails, the verb re-runs it per\npath and names the path the graph does not know instead of hiding every other answer."},"1477":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-74","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-a-large-edit-what-moves-with-this-file","content":"This is the question that costs the most sessions, because the answer is spread over four different\nmechanisms and each one is normally discovered by a failing gate."},"1478":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-75","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-suites-that-read-a-payload","content":"Seven suites, printed in about 60 ms. Change that file and those are the suites that go red; edit one\nof them and the same verb in the other direction tells you what it covers."},"1479":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-76","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-twin-template-copies","content":"Three payload trees are in play:"},"1480":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-77","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-twin-template-copies","content":"`templates/workspace/` and `templates/devcontainer/` keep independent payload copies\nthat must move\ntogether"},"1481":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-78","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-twin-template-copies","content":"`templates/common/` holds the files both consume as one shared copy"},"1482":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-79","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-twin-template-copies","content":"The verb matches basenames over the union of the three payload groups, so the twin set is the\ngraph's answer rather than a convention you have to remember:"},"1483":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-80","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-twin-template-copies","content":"A per-tree file whose sibling tree has no counterpart is a `warning:` naming the group that claims\nit: that asymmetry is the drift worth knowing about before you edit, not after."},"1484":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-81","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"A file the graph does not know is a warning naming that path, and the usual cause is a file you just\ncreated that no filegroup claims yet. `owners` answers \"is this visible to the harness at all\":"},"1485":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-82","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"An empty list is the finding: no filegroup carries the file, so `test-fast` and `lint` never open it."},"1486":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-83","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"The pair verb, `unlisted`, asks it per directory by diffing `git ls-files` against the graph's own\nsource list. It skips Bazel's own declaration files:"},"1487":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-84","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"`BUILD.bazel`"},"1488":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-85","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"`*.bzl`"},"1489":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-86","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"`MODULE.bazel`"},"1490":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-87","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"Bazel reads them implicitly and they only appear in the graph when a package deliberately exports\nthem, so a directory holding nothing but a BUILD file reads as clean."},"1491":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-88","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"A new top-level payload directory, as building-with-bazel.md spells out:"},"1492":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-89","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"belongs in its own package with its own `filegroup` targets"},"1493":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-90","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"joins `//:stack_data` by label"},"1494":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-91","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"is named in the map of every target that reads it"},"1495":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-92","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-filegroup-that-must-claim-a-new-payload-file","content":"`unlisted` is how you find out you have not done that, rather than finding out that the gate never\nnoticed."},"1496":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-93","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"A new `scripts/*.sh` is a Bazel target automatically (the package is generated from the directory),\nbut it is not wired automatically. It needs two keys, both in `scripts/BUILD.bazel`:"},"1497":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-94","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"a `_SCRIPT_LIBS` key (the `scripts/lib` closure it sources)"},"1498":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-95","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"a `_SCRIPT_PAYLOAD` key (the payload groups it opens)"},"1499":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-96","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"Until those keys land the graph does not know the file at all, which is worth saying out loud:\n`rdeps` reads the graph, not the filesystem."},"1500":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-97","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"That warning is the honest version of \"nothing depends on this\", and it is the reason to keep\nstderr with a query. Go to the gate that owns the map instead of guessing its label:"},"1501":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-98","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"A script missing its key outright fails `//scripts` analysis before any test runs, and a script\nwhose declared map disagrees with its sources is what that checker reports, naming the pairing and\nthe direction. Once the keys are in place the same verb resolves the file, and\n`tests-for scripts/bazel-map.sh` lists `//tests:bats_bazel_deps_test` among its consumers."},"1502":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-99","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"Every new function additionally owes:"},"1503":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-100","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"one `# @function` block"},"1504":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-101","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-map-key-a-new-scriptssh-needs-and-the-test-a-new-function-needs","content":"one asserting test in exactly one suite, which test-with-bazel.md\ncovers; `//tests:shell_inventory` and `//tests:doc_coverage` are the two gates, and both are\ntest targets the graph can point you at before the gate does."},"1505":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-102","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"`scope` derives the test list from what this checkout changes, which is the loop that replaces\nre-running the whole fast gate after every edit:"},"1506":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-103","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"Default scope reads `git diff HEAD`. Add:"},"1507":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-104","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"`--staged` for the index"},"1508":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-105","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"`--untracked` to count files git does not track yet (a file you just created is exactly the case\nworth covering)"},"1509":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-106","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"`--ref <ref>` for what this branch adds over a base"},"1510":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-107","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"`--all` also lists the aggregate suites that reach everything (`//:test`, `//:test-fast`,\n`//:test-all` and `//tests:bats`), which is useful when you want the full set named explicitly\nrather than the leaf suites you can invoke."},"1511":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-108","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"The default already includes the lint targets: every test rule here, `//lints:shell` and\n`//lints:shfmt` among them, is an `sh_test`."},"1512":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-109","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"Two things scope tells you that a habit of `bazelisk test //:test-fast` hides:"},"1513":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-110","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"**A Bats file is cheap; a script is not.** `tests-for tests/bats/common.bats` returns five targets.\n`tests-for scripts/lib/common.sh` returns 60 of the 67 test targets on this checkout, because every\nsuite declares `//scripts:doc_sources`, which is every `scripts/**.sh` (66 targets reach that\ngroup). That is the honest graph answer: editing a broadly sourced script genuinely re-runs nearly\nthe whole suite set, and knowing it before you start is what decides whether to run the derived\nlist or the aggregate."},"1514":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-111","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#while-you-iterate-which-tests-and-when-you-still-owe-a-full-pass","content":"**An empty result means run everything.** Nothing changed against HEAD, or the change touches no\nfile the graph tracks, and `scope` says so and points at `//:test-fast`."},"1515":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-112","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#keep-the-uncached-pass","content":"The uncached pass is not replaced."},"1516":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-113","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#keep-the-uncached-pass","content":"`bazelisk test` replays a cached PASS for an action whose inputs did not change, so the derived list\nproves your change against whatever actually rebuilds, and one\n`bazelisk test //:test-fast --nocache_test_results` remains the pass you owe before the PR, per\nbuilding-with-bazel.md."},"1517":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-114","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#keep-the-uncached-pass","content":"Use the derived list for the loop and keep the full uncached pass for the end, instead of paying for\nsixty suites to learn one thing per edit."},"1518":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-115","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#enumerate-targets-instead-of-guessing-them","content":"Seven logged sessions guessed a target name and got `ERROR: no such target`. A target is never\nguessed, it is listed:"},"1519":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-116","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#enumerate-targets-instead-of-guessing-them","content":"The rule class is the part that saves the round trip. `//docs-site:app` looks like the site's test\ntarget and is a `filegroup`, so `bazelisk test` on it fails to start; the real test targets are the\n`sh_test` rows."},"1520":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-117","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#enumerate-targets-instead-of-guessing-them","content":"The same listing filtered by a name fragment is how you find a Bats suite's target without knowing\nthe stem convention:"},"1521":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-118","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#what-a-target-reads-and-why-an-unlisted-directory-is-invisible","content":"`//:test-fast` runs in a sandbox: an action sees its declared inputs and its runfiles tree, not the\ncheckout. So \"what does this target read\" is a real question with a printed answer, and the answer\nhas two depths worth keeping separate."},"1522":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-119","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-direct-inputs","content":"The direct inputs are the `data` the dependency maps write, which is what you edit when a target\nneeds one more payload group:"},"1523":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-120","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-transitive-closure","content":"The files it can actually open are the transitive closure of those groups, which is what the verb\nprints:"},"1524":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-121","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-transitive-closure","content":"That target resolves to 198 source files through 25 declarations: the gap is the `filegroup` and\n`scripts/lib` expansion under each label. `labels(\"data\", ...)` is the narrower question (\"what does\nthe BUILD file say\"), `files` is the wider one (\"what is in the sandbox\"), and the two disagreeing is\nusually the bug."},"1525":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-122","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#why-an-unlisted-directory-stays-invisible","content":"This is why an unlisted payload directory stays invisible rather than being checked loosely: a file\nthat travels in no runfiles tree is a file no sandboxed action can open, so `test-fast` and `lint`\nnever read it and never fail. Nothing prints a warning about that."},"1526":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-123","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#why-an-unlisted-directory-stays-invisible","content":"`owners <path>` and `unlisted <dir>` are the two ways to ask, and they are the difference between a\npayload the harness guards and a payload nobody has ever executed."},"1527":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-124","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#raw-query-recipes-when-a-verb-does-not-fit","content":"Every verb is one of these, so a question outside the verb set needs one predicate, not a grep plan.\nAll of these run warm in about 50 to 70 ms."},"1528":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-125","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate              | Question it answers       |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `rdeps(//..., \"path\")` | what depends on this file |","table":"table-1"},"1529":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-126","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate        | Question it answers                       |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `deps(//target)` | what this target depends on, transitively |","table":"table-1"},"1530":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-127","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate              | Question it answers                |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `kind(\"sh_test\", ...)` | narrow to the rules you can act on |","table":"table-1"},"1531":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-128","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate                   | Question it answers              |\n| --------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `attr(\"name\", \"re\", pkg:*)` | find a target by a name fragment |","table":"table-1"},"1532":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-129","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate                  | Question it answers                        |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `labels(\"data\", //target)` | the groups a target declares as its inputs |","table":"table-1"},"1533":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-130","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate        | Question it answers                            |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `somepath(a, b)` | is there any path from this suite to that file |","table":"table-1"},"1534":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-131","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-predicates","content":"| Predicate                     | Question it answers     |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `A intersect B`, `A except B` | combine two result sets |","table":"table-1"},"1535":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-132","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#narrow-an-rdeps-with-the-kind-filter","content":"The `kind` filter is what makes an `rdeps` usable. A bare `rdeps(//..., \"litellm/config.yaml\")`\nincludes `//:test-fast`, which reaches every file and therefore tells you nothing about this one:"},"1536":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-133","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#excluding-the-aggregates-and-the-lint-targets","content":"Two exclusions earn their place. `except kind(\"test_suite\", //...)` drops the aggregates, which is\nwhat the CLI filters on so `//:test-fast` cannot answer a per-file question, and\n`except kind(\"sh_test\", //lints:*)` drops the two manual lint targets, `//lints:shell` and\n`//lints:shfmt`, that ride on every script:"},"1537":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-134","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#proving-a-gate-sits-on-a-file","content":"A reachability proof, for when you must know that a gate really does sit on top of a file:"},"1538":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-135","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#counting-what-the-gates-can-see","content":"The whole-graph enumeration `unlisted` is built from, which is also the answer to \"how much of the\nrepo do the gates actually see\":"},"1539":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-136","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#counting-what-the-gates-can-see","content":"The `//` half is the honest measure of what the gates can see, and it moves as files are added, so\ntreat any absolute total in a document as a snapshot rather than a fact to assert."},"1540":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-137","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#set-algebra","content":"And set algebra, for \"is this payload covered by the suite I trust with it\":"},"1541":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-138","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#the-empty-result-is-not-an-answer","content":"This is the trap that makes a hand-check unreliable, and it is the reason the CLI keeps Bazel's\nstderr instead of discarding it. A query can print `ERROR: no such target` and leave stdout empty,\nwhich looks exactly like \"nothing depends on this\":"},"1542":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-139","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-you-believe-an-empty-list","content":"One mistyped character, an empty stdout, and a shell that tests only `-z \"$out\"` reports a clean\nresult. So before you believe an empty list:"},"1543":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-140","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-you-believe-an-empty-list","content":"check the exit status (Bazel exits non-zero here)"},"1544":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-141","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-you-believe-an-empty-list","content":"read stderr"},"1545":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-142","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-you-believe-an-empty-list","content":"confirm the operand resolved at all with `bazelisk query '\"litellm/config.yaml\"'`, which prints\nits label back"},"1546":{"id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel-143","page_id":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel","tags":["bazel","contributing","tooling","graph"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/navigate-with-bazel#before-you-believe-an-empty-list","content":"A miss you can see is a finding; a miss you cannot see is a green gate over a file nobody tests."},"1547":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"page","content":"Strong types","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types"},"1548":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-0","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types","content":"The typing rule for every language in this repo: Python under mypy with no Any, TypeScript under the strictest flags it compiles, Terraform variables with a declared constraint, and what bash and awk owe instead."},"1549":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-1","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Strong types"},"1550":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-2","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"The rule"},"1551":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-3","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#python","content":"Python"},"1552":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-4","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-profile","content":"The profile"},"1553":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-5","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#running-it","content":"Running it"},"1554":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-6","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-patterns-the-profile-pushes","content":"The patterns the profile pushes"},"1555":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-7","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-escape-hatches","content":"The escape hatches"},"1556":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-8","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#typescript","content":"TypeScript"},"1557":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-9","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"The compiler switches"},"1558":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-10","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#checked-javascript","content":"Checked JavaScript"},"1559":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-11","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#absent-from-every-tracked-file","content":"Absent from every tracked file"},"1560":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-12","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#terraform","content":"Terraform"},"1561":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-13","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#why-an-undeclared-variable-is-a-runtime-bug","content":"Why an undeclared variable is a runtime bug"},"1562":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-14","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"What the checker reports"},"1563":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-15","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#both-twins-today","content":"Both twins today"},"1564":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-16","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash-awk-and-bats","content":"Bash, awk, and Bats"},"1565":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-17","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"Bash"},"1566":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-18","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#awk-and-bats","content":"awk and Bats"},"1567":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-19","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","type":"heading","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"Adding a file"},"1568":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-20","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1569":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-21","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"The rule in one sentence, and the two gates that hold it"},"1570":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-22","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Python: the mypy profile, the aliases that replace `Any`, and how to add a file"},"1571":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-23","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"TypeScript: the compiler switches, and how the `.mjs` scripts get checked"},"1572":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-24","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Terraform: why a `variable` without a `type` is a runtime bug"},"1573":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-25","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Bash, awk, and Bats: what an untyped language owes instead of annotations"},"1574":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-26","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Adding a new language, or a new file to an existing one"},"1575":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-27","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"**What this enables**"},"1576":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-28","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Making an annotation that a reviewer cannot argue about, because a tool decides it"},"1577":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-29","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Catching a wrong-shaped input at plan time or type-check time rather than in a container"},"1578":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-30","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Adding a `.py`, `.ts`, or `.tf` file without guessing which list it belongs on"},"1579":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-31","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#strong-types","content":"Telling a contributor why `Any` came back from CI"},"1580":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-32","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"Every value has a declared shape at the boundary where it enters a module, and a\nbroad type is a design smell rather than a shortcut."},"1581":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-33","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"Where a language has a type system, the strictest setting that compiles is the setting the\nrepo uses."},"1582":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-34","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"Where it has none, the convention is the gate."},"1583":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-35","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"Two gates carry most of it, and both are members of `//lints:all`, so `//:lint`,\n`//:test-all`, and the `bazel` job of `.github/workflows/ci.yml` run them:"},"1584":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-36","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"| Gate           | Language | What it refuses                                         |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//lints:mypy` | Python   | a missing annotation, an explicit `Any`, a bare generic |","table":"table-0"},"1585":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-37","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"| Gate                    | Language   | What it refuses                                         |\n| ----------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `//docs-site:typecheck` | TypeScript | the same, plus every index access that can be undefined |","table":"table-0"},"1586":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-38","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-rule","content":"`//:validate` adds the Terraform half, and `//tests:bats_mypy_lint_test` and\n`//tests:bats_tf_types_test` are the asserting sides of the two newest gates."},"1587":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-39","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-profile","content":"`mypy.ini` at the repo root is the whole policy. It is `--strict` written out option\nby option, plus the two that make this a rule rather than a preference:"},"1588":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-40","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-profile","content":"`disallow_any_explicit` refuses `Any` typed into a signature by a person."},"1589":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-41","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-profile","content":"`disallow_any_generics` refuses `list` and `dict` written without their element\ntype, which are the same hole reached by a different spelling."},"1590":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-42","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-profile","content":"The binary is the `MYPY_VERSION` pin from `images/dev/tool-versions.env`, baked into\nthe golden image by `images/dev/Dockerfile`, so the gate needs no network and no\n`pip install`."},"1591":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-43","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#running-it","content":"Run it directly when you want the error text without Bazel in the way:"},"1592":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-44","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-patterns-the-profile-pushes","content":"The pattern the profile pushes you toward is a named alias for anything unstructured.\n`scripts/lib/mcp_lane_report.py` reads TOML and JSON, so rather than widen a\nsignature it declares the two document shapes and narrows with `isinstance`:"},"1593":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-45","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-patterns-the-profile-pushes","content":"The same file writes its two fixed vocabularies as `Literal`s, which is what makes a\ntypo in a check name a gate failure rather than a line an operator never sees."},"1594":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-46","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-patterns-the-profile-pushes","content":"A record that travels between functions gets a `NamedTuple`, a `@dataclass`, or a\n`TypedDict` — `tests/bazel_deps.py` names its Starlark map `LabelMap` and its\n`drift()` result `Drift`, and `tests/coverage/py_report.py` types the slice of\n`coverage report --json` it reads with three `total=False` TypedDicts."},"1595":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-47","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-escape-hatches","content":"`# type: ignore` needs a specific error code and a reason that names the real cause.\n`warn_unused_ignores` makes a stale one an error, so an ignore cannot quietly\noutlive the problem it papered over."},"1596":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-48","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-escape-hatches","content":"Where the value is unstructured but an `isinstance` guard already decides what it\nis, a `cast` is the honest instrument: narrowing there would change what happens to\nthe malformed input."},"1597":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-49","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`docs-site/tsconfig.json` starts at `strict: true` and adds the switches that find\nreal defects at no churn cost:"},"1598":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-50","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noUncheckedIndexedAccess`"},"1599":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-51","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noImplicitOverride`"},"1600":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-52","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noImplicitReturns`"},"1601":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-53","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`"},"1602":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-54","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noUnusedLocals`"},"1603":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-55","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noUnusedParameters`"},"1604":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-56","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"Each carries a comment naming the class of bug it catches."},"1605":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-57","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"Two well-known switches are deliberately off:"},"1606":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-58","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`exactOptionalPropertyTypes` collides with React's optional DOM props and with\nfumadocs' `StaticOptions`"},"1607":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-59","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"`noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature` collides with how the unit tests read the\nfumadocs source config"},"1608":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-60","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#the-compiler-switches","content":"Both would be paid for in casts, which is the wrong direction."},"1609":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-61","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#checked-javascript","content":"`allowJs` and `checkJs` are on, which is how the two operator CLIs\n`docs-site/scripts/serve_static.mjs` and `verify_site.mjs` are type-checked: each\nopens with `// @ts-check` and carries JSDoc `@param`/`@returns` on every function,\nwith `@typedef`s for the shapes it reads out of `lib/nav.json`."},"1610":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-62","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#checked-javascript","content":"`zod` already validates the frontmatter at the content boundary in\n`docs-site/lib/content.ts`, so parsed pages arrive as typed `PageNode`s rather than\nas `unknown`."},"1611":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-63","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#absent-from-every-tracked-file","content":"`any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, and `@ts-nocheck` are absent from every\ntracked file. The one exclusion is `docs-site/.source/`, the code fumadocs-mdx\ngenerates, which is gitignored."},"1612":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-64","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#absent-from-every-tracked-file","content":"`docs-site/tests/unit/helpers/fumadocs-stub.ts` is\nwhere a dependency's shape gets stated once when a test needs one."},"1613":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-65","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#why-an-undeclared-variable-is-a-runtime-bug","content":"A `variable` block is the only place a Coder template can declare what an input is,\nand an undeclared one takes whatever HCL guessed. `search_mcp = \"flase\"` then reaches\na `== \"true\"` comparison and reads as false, so the operator gets a workspace that\ncame up wrong and a plan that said nothing."},"1614":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-66","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#why-an-undeclared-variable-is-a-runtime-bug","content":"A declared constraint turns that into a plan-time error."},"1615":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-67","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"`scripts/lib/tf_types.awk` is run by `//:validate` over both template twins and\nreports three findings:"},"1616":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-68","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"`missing-type`"},"1617":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-69","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"`broad-any`"},"1618":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-70","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"`bare-container` (a `list`, `set`, or `map` with no element type, which is `any`\nwearing a different hat)"},"1619":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-71","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#what-the-checker-reports","content":"Only the `type` attribute of a top-level `variable` block is read, so a `type` key inside\na `default` body is never mistaken for the constraint, and `any` is matched as a word\nso `company_mcp` is not a finding."},"1620":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-72","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#both-twins-today","content":"Both twins conform today: every `variable` carries a `type` and a `description`, and\nneither uses `any`, `list(any)`, or a bare container."},"1621":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-73","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#both-twins-today","content":"`//tests:bats_tf_types_test` holds that, with fixtures that prove the gate still\nreports each finding rather than having quietly stopped looking."},"1622":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-74","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"Bash has no type system, and no annotation comment buys one. What the repo does\ninstead is put the checking where the language can actually be checked:"},"1623":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-75","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"`//lints:shell` runs ShellCheck at `--severity=warning` over every first-party\n`.sh`, and the tree is clean at that level today."},"1624":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-76","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"Variables are declared before they are used and carry their shape in the\ndeclaration: `local -a` for an indexed array, `local -A` for an associative one,\n`local -r` or `declare -r` for a constant. Naming the kind is what makes an array\nthat was meant to be empty distinguishable from one that was never set."},"1625":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-77","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"Every function in `scripts/` carries a `# @function` block with `Globals:`,\n`Arguments:`, `Outputs:`, and `Returns:`, and each `Arguments:` line states what\nthe parameter is. `//tests:doc_coverage` enforces the block and\n`//tests:shell_inventory` enforces that a test names the function."},"1626":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-78","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#bash","content":"`set -euo pipefail` is the floor, so an unset parameter is a failure rather than\nan empty string."},"1627":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-79","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#awk-and-bats","content":"awk is POSIX-subset and single-purpose: a program in `scripts/lib/*.awk` takes its\ninput in `ARGV`, its configuration in `ENVIRON`, and prints tab-separated fields the\ncaller reads line by line. The types are that line shape, and they are documented in\nthe program's header block — see `scripts/lib/tf_types.awk` for the shape to copy."},"1628":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-80","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#awk-and-bats","content":"Bats suites are bash and follow the same rules as their shell."},"1629":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-81","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"| Adding                  | You also edit                                                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `scripts/lib/<name>.py` | nothing: `//scripts:py_programs` globs it and `lints/run_mypy.sh` scans the directory; if a CLI runs it, it joins that CLI's `_SCRIPT_LIBS` |","table":"table-1"},"1630":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-82","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"| Adding                | You also edit                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| another `.py` package | `lints/run_mypy.sh` `targets` **and** the data edge of `:mypy` in `lints/BUILD.bazel` — the two are kept equal by hand, and the runner's header says so |","table":"table-1"},"1631":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-83","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"| Adding              | You also edit                                    |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `docs-site/**/*.ts` | nothing: it is already in the `tsconfig` program |","table":"table-1"},"1632":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-84","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"| Adding       | You also edit                                                     |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| a `.mjs` CLI | `// @ts-check` and JSDoc on every function, since `checkJs` is on |","table":"table-1"},"1633":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-85","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"| Adding                     | You also edit                                                                  |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| a `variable` in a template | its `type` and its `description`, in both twins where the template keeps twins |","table":"table-1"},"1634":{"id":"/contribute/strong-types-86","page_id":"/contribute/strong-types","tags":["types","mypy","typescript","terraform","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/strong-types#adding-a-file","content":"A Python file that lands outside the runner's list is unchecked code that looks\ngated, which is the failure `//tests:bats_mypy_lint_test` exists to catch: it\nenumerates the tree and fails on any `.py` the target list does not cover, with\n`tests/bats/fixtures/` the one sanctioned exclusion because that tree is scaffold\npayload typed in the repository it is copied into."},"1635":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"page","content":"Testing with Bazel (the Bats harness)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel"},"1636":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-0","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","content":"Hermetic Bats: how a suite is discovered, what the stub PATH gives you, and the two inventory gates a new function has to satisfy."},"1637":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-1","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Testing with Bazel (the Bats harness)"},"1638":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-2","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"Layout"},"1639":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-3","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#two-gates-one-rule","content":"Two gates, one rule"},"1640":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-4","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-each-gate-checks","content":"What each gate checks"},"1641":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-5","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#where-the-name-has-to-live","content":"Where the name has to live"},"1642":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-6","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#running-a-suite","content":"Running a suite"},"1643":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-7","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#which-runtime-gates","content":"Which runtime gates"},"1644":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-8","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-npm-backed-gates","content":"The npm-backed gates"},"1645":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-9","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#measured-coverage","content":"Measured coverage"},"1646":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-10","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-the-shell-ledger-records","content":"What the shell ledger records"},"1647":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-11","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-not-xtrace","content":"Why not xtrace"},"1648":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-12","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-python-and-docs-site-targets","content":"The Python and docs-site targets"},"1649":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-13","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#traps-that-fail-silently","content":"Traps that fail silently"},"1650":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-14","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-vitest-gate","content":"The vitest gate"},"1651":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-15","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-three-paths-a-suite-may-use","content":"The three paths a suite may use"},"1652":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-16","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-path-recipe","content":"The stub-PATH recipe"},"1653":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-17","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-helpers","content":"The stub helpers"},"1654":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-18","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#how-run-behaves","content":"How run behaves"},"1655":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-19","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#reading-the-stub-log-and-the-assertions","content":"Reading the stub log, and the assertions"},"1656":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-20","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#sandbox-safe-probe-for-the-repo-root-then-say-so","content":"Sandbox-safe: probe for the repo root, then say so"},"1657":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-21","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"Resolve, then prove"},"1658":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-22","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","type":"heading","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-each-part-is-there","content":"Why each part is there"},"1659":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-23","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1660":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-24","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"The layout: suites, helpers, stubs and fixtures"},"1661":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-25","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"The two inventory gates that tie a production function to a test"},"1662":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-26","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Running one suite, from any directory"},"1663":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-27","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Which runtime actually gates a merge, and which one is a convenience"},"1664":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-28","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"The stub-PATH recipe, and the two paths a suite may take"},"1665":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-29","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Sandbox-safe repo-root probing"},"1666":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-30","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"**What this enables**"},"1667":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-31","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Adding a test that passes in the Bazel sandbox and on a laptop"},"1668":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-32","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Making a new function satisfy `//tests:shell_inventory` without guessing"},"1669":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-33","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Reproducing a CI failure locally by running the suites in the image CI runs them in"},"1670":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-34","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#testing-with-bazel-the-bats-harness","content":"Every suite under `tests/` is hermetic Bats: it runs against stubs and a throwaway tree,\nnever against a daemon, a network, or the operator's real `.env`."},"1671":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-35","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"`tests/bats/*.bats` — one suite per module. `tests/bats.bzl` turns each file into one\n`bats_<stem>_test` sh_test (dashes become underscores: `bats_spark_configure_test` for\n`spark-configure.bats`) and adds it to the `bats` suite that `//:test-fast` runs."},"1672":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-36","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"`tests/bats/test_helper.bash` — the shared helpers, pulled in with `load 'test_helper'`."},"1673":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-37","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"`tests/test_helpers.sh` — the assertions, shared with the bash gates."},"1674":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-38","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"`tests/bats/tool_stubs/` — the fake external tools (`docker`, `ssh`, `curl`, `git`,\n`coder`, `psql`, `timeout`, …); `tests/bats/fixtures/` holds a fixture that has to answer\nlike the real client, such as the `psql-token` copies that echo `returning id`."},"1675":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-39","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#layout","content":"`tests/bats_runner.sh` — what Bazel executes: it locates bats-core and this checkout in\nrunfiles, exports `REPO_ROOT`, and execs bats."},"1676":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-40","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-each-gate-checks","content":"`tests/shell_inventory.sh` fails when a function under `scripts/` is not named under\n`tests/`; `tests/doc_coverage.sh` fails when a `# @function` block (or the file header) is\nmissing or incomplete. So every new function needs, in the same change as the function:"},"1677":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-41","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-each-gate-checks","content":"one asserting test in the **one** suite for its module — a `scripts/lib/<mod>.sh` helper\nbelongs to `tests/bats/<mod>.bats`, and a helper that only an entry CLI defines belongs to\n`tests/bats/entry-fns.bats`, which loads single functions with `load_shell_function`;"},"1678":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-42","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-each-gate-checks","content":"the `# @function` block above the definition, with Globals/Arguments/Outputs/Returns."},"1679":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-43","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-each-gate-checks","content":"Name it in exactly one suite. A chain test that happens to mention the name also satisfies\nthe inventory, but the owning suite is the one that asserts its behaviour."},"1680":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-44","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#where-the-name-has-to-live","content":"The inventory strips comment lines before it looks for a name, so a name that only ever\nappears in a `# @function` block or in prose is still untested: it has to sit in a code line\nsomewhere under `tests/`. The usual way to get one there is a unit case that calls the\nhelper directly:"},"1681":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-45","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#running-a-suite","content":"A suite is one cached action. Its `.bats` file, `test_helper.bash`, `test_helpers.sh`,\n`bats_runner.sh` and the `scripts/**.sh` plus stub/fixture files it declares as `data` are\nits inputs, so editing one script re-runs only the suites that read it, and an unchanged\nsuite replays its cached PASS."},"1682":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-46","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#running-a-suite","content":"Beyond that common set each suite names only the payload groups it opens, in\n`_SUITE_PAYLOAD` in `tests/BUILD.bazel`; a suite whose target does not declare a payload it\nreads finds that payload missing under its own target, and `//tests:bats_bazel_deps_test`\nis the gate that keeps the map honest."},"1683":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-47","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#which-runtime-gates","content":"The merge gate is the Linux golden image — the same `images/dev/Dockerfile` the Coder\nworkspaces boot and CI builds:"},"1684":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-48","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#which-runtime-gates","content":"Inside the contributor dev container (devcontainer.md) the commands\nabove are exactly what CI runs."},"1685":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-49","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#which-runtime-gates","content":"On a host that is not that container, `//scripts:test-in-image` docker-runs\n`evo-t1-dev:latest` as this process's uid:gid, with `HOME=/tmp` and `USER` set so\nBazel can name that uid, and runs them there. `EVO_T1_BAZEL_CACHE=<dir>` keeps the\narchives Bazel downloads between runs; both CI jobs set it and wrap it in\n`actions/cache` (building-with-bazel.md)."},"1686":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-50","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#which-runtime-gates","content":"A native `bazelisk test` on macOS is convenience only: the BSD userland differs from the\nGNU one in the image (`sed`, `date`, `find`, `sort`), so a red run there is not proof of a\ndefect and a green one is not the run that unlocks the merge button. CI and branch\nprotection gate on the image result either way."},"1687":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-51","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-npm-backed-gates","content":"The npm-backed gates (`//docs-site:typecheck`, `:unit`, `:unit_coverage`, `:verify`) are\n`manual` for the same reason, and they all run out of `docs-site/node_modules` in the\ncheckout: `run_npm.sh` resolves its own runfiles copy back into it, so a cold checkout\ninstalls once for the whole family, under `docs-site/.npm-ci.lock`."},"1688":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-52","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-npm-backed-gates","content":"Without that lock every test action ran its own `npm ci`, and a gate that started while\nanother was still writing the tree died on a SIGBUS reading a short esbuild binary."},"1689":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-53","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-npm-backed-gates","content":"A box with no `flock` (a macOS laptop) installs unlocked, since nothing else is running\nthere."},"1690":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-54","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#measured-coverage","content":"Three targets answer \"is this code actually executed by a test\" instead of\nassuming it. They are `manual` like the npm gates, so `//:test-fast` stays fast, and\nthey are members of `//:test-all`, which pre-push and CI run:"},"1691":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-55","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-the-shell-ledger-records","content":"`//tests:shell_coverage` is the one to understand before you write a shell test.\nIt builds a mirror of the checkout with `tests/coverage/instrument.py`: every\nproduction `.sh` is copied with one extra statement at the top of each function\nbody that appends `<path>\\t<function>` to `$EVO_COV_LEDGER`, and every other path\nstays a symlink into the real tree."},"1692":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-56","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#what-the-shell-ledger-records","content":"`tests/bats_runner.sh` points `REPO_ROOT` at\nthat mirror when `EVO_COV_MIRROR` is set, so the suites execute the instrumented\ncopies through whichever access pattern they already use — run the CLI, source the\nlib, or `load_shell_function`. Then `tests/coverage/aggregate.py` names every\nfunction whose body never ran."},"1693":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-57","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-not-xtrace","content":"Why a ledger and not `bash -x`: xtrace traces bats-core itself, wrote 3.4 GB of log\nfor one suite, and leaked trace lines into the stderr bats captures per test, which\nturned output-asserting suites red. The ledger measures the narrower thing the gate\nasks and breaks nothing."},"1694":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-58","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-not-xtrace","content":"The consequence for a test author: a function counts when something calls it. A\nname in a comment, a stub, a fixture or a quoted grep pattern satisfies\n`//tests:shell_inventory` and satisfies nothing here."},"1695":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-59","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-python-and-docs-site-targets","content":"`//tests:py_coverage` discovers `tests/python/test_*.py` and\n`docs-site/test_gen_nav.py` under coverage.py 7.17, pinned in\n`images/dev/tool-versions.env` and baked into the golden image; without it the\ntarget fails with a pointer to `//scripts:test-in-image` rather than passing while\nmeasuring nothing. `//docs-site:unit_coverage` is `npm run unit:coverage`\n(vitest v8 provider, thresholds in `docs-site/vitest.config.ts`)."},"1696":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-60","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#traps-that-fail-silently","content":"Three runfiles traps bit this gate, and all fail *silently*, so they are worth\nnaming:"},"1697":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-61","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#traps-that-fail-silently","content":"Under `bazelisk test` every source arrives as a **symlink**. A `find -type f`\nover the tree then sees no regular file and reports an empty suite, which reads\nas \"nothing to test\". `py_cov.sh` uses `find -L`."},"1698":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-62","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#traps-that-fail-silently","content":"coverage.py resolves the symlink and records the **checkout** path, while the\nprocess cwd is the runfiles tree. A relative `--include=scripts/lib/*.py` is\nmatched against the cwd, matches nothing, prints `No data to report`, and exits\n`0`. The gate therefore decides from `tests/coverage/py_report.py`, which lists\nthe `.py` files the tree ships and requires each one to appear in the machine-\nreadable report above the floor. A module nobody imported is a named failure."},"1699":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-63","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#traps-that-fail-silently","content":"The mirror pads every `.sh` it instruments, so a suite that measures a payload's\n**byte size** through `REPO_ROOT` prices the harness instead of the product. This is\nhow `//tests:shell_coverage` failed an execve budget the checkout had already passed:\n`templates/common/notes-setup.sh` weighed 1182 bytes more in the mirror than it\nships. A size gate resolves its tree through `bats_source_repo_root`, and\n`startup-script-size.bats` builds a real instrumented mirror to prove it still\nmeasures what ships."},"1700":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-64","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-vitest-gate","content":"The same \"empty looks like green\" rule applies to the vitest gate: it must measure\nfiles no test imported."},"1701":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-65","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-vitest-gate","content":"Vitest 4 made that the default and removed the `all` key from `CoverageOptions`. To prove\nthe default still holds after a vitest bump, drop a `lib/__cov_probe.ts` exporting one\nuncalled function and confirm the run reports it at 0% and fails; then delete the file."},"1702":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-66","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-three-paths-a-suite-may-use","content":"`REPO_ROOT` — where the checkout is *for this run*. `tests/bats_runner.sh` exports it;\noutside Bazel it is whatever `bats_canonical_repo_root` resolves. Derive it, never\nhardcode a machine path, and treat \"cannot resolve\" as a `skip`, not a failure."},"1703":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-67","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-three-paths-a-suite-may-use","content":"`BATS_TEST_TMPDIR` — per-test scratch, removed after each test. `make_scratch` prints a\nfresh directory under it; `fake_root`-style helpers build a throwaway checkout there."},"1704":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-68","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-three-paths-a-suite-may-use","content":"`bats_source_repo_root` — the checkout whose **bytes** are what the stack ships, which\nunder the coverage mirror is the one the mirror was built from (`EVO_COV_SOURCE_ROOT`)\nwhile `REPO_ROOT` is the mirror. A gate that counts the size of a shipped payload reads\nit there; the production functions it loads still come from `REPO_ROOT`, so measuring\nthe shipping tree costs no coverage mark."},"1705":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-69","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-path-recipe","content":"Copy this shape; it is the convention every suite already uses (`use_stubs` prints nothing\nand shadows PATH for the current test only, and fails when a stub is missing):"},"1706":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-70","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-helpers","content":"`stub_bin <tool…>` copies each stub out of `STUB_BIN_DIR` into `${BATS_TEST_TMPDIR}/bin`\nand `chmod 755`s it; `use_stubs` = `stub_bin` + a fresh `STUB_LOG` + the PATH shadow.\nThe copy-plus-chmod is load-bearing: the Bazel sandbox and some tar extractions strip the\nexec bit, and a per-test copy keeps one test's argv log out of the next test."},"1707":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-71","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-helpers","content":"`with_path <dir…>` prepends directories to PATH when a test needs a hand-written fake\ninstead of a shared stub."},"1708":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-72","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#the-stub-helpers","content":"**Prepend; never replace PATH.** `use_stubs` and `with_path` put the stub directory *in\nfront of* the host PATH. `PATH=\"${BIN}\"` takes `bash`, `grep`, `cut`, `sort` and `wc` away\nfrom the script under test as well, and a script that pipes its answer through\n`grep | wc | tr` then fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the contract the\nsuite means to check."},"1709":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-73","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#how-run-behaves","content":"**`run` keeps stdout in `$output`.** With `run --separate-stderr` there is no `$stdout`:\n`$output` is stdout and `$stderr` is stderr. An assertion written against `$stdout`\ncompares against an empty string and fails, which is how a whole suite of real\nassertions can look like a broken harness."},"1710":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-74","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#how-run-behaves","content":"**`run` can call a helper, and a helper that `exit`s is safe.** `run` forks, so\n`run --separate-stderr usage_error '…'` followed by `[ \"${status}\" -eq 2 ]` works even\nthough `usage_error` ends in `exit 2`. Pass a real command (`bash \"${SCRIPT}\" …`) when\nthe script is what is under test."},"1711":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-75","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#reading-the-stub-log-and-the-assertions","content":"`stub_log <tool>`, `stub_log_last`, `stub_log_count` read back what the stub recorded from\n`$STUB_LOG/<tool>.log`; assert on the argv, not on prose."},"1712":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-76","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#reading-the-stub-log-and-the-assertions","content":"`real_bin <tool>` resolves a tool with the stub directory removed from PATH. That is the\nintegration-tier gate: `if [ -z \"$(real_bin terraform)\" ]; then skip \"terraform not\ninstalled\"; fi` — a test that could talk to a real daemon skips when the tool is absent\ninstead of failing."},"1713":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-77","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#reading-the-stub-log-and-the-assertions","content":"The `docker` stub passes `exec`/`compose exec` through by default (`STUB_DOCKER_EXEC_RUN=1`),\nso a binary the script execs inside a container lands on its own stub; set\n`STUB_DOCKER_EXEC_RUN=0` with `STUB_DOCKER_EXEC_RC`/`STUB_DOCKER_EXEC_OUT` for the\n\"the daemon answered, and it said No\" case."},"1714":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-78","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#reading-the-stub-log-and-the-assertions","content":"Assertions come from `tests/test_helpers.sh`: `fail`, `assert_eq`, `assert_match`,\n`assert_not_match`, `assert_file_exists`, `assert_file_not_exists`, `load_shell_function`.\n`load_shell_function` is the one harness place that expands a function body (it is how a\nsingle entry-CLI function gets unit-tested); production scripts still never use `eval`."},"1715":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-79","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#sandbox-safe-probe-for-the-repo-root-then-say-so","content":"A script must work when the cwd is **not** the checkout. Under `bazel test` the working\ndirectory is an exec root or a runfiles tree that holds *copies* of whatever the target\ndeclares as `data`; under `bazel run` it is wherever the operator typed `bazelisk`, and\n`bazel run` alone sets `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY`. Neither guarantees a working Docker\ndaemon, an `ssh`, or a reachable Spark box — a sandboxed action usually has none of them on\nPATH."},"1716":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-80","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"So resolve the root from the environment first, then prove it, and fail loudly when the\nproof fails. `resolve_checkout` in `scripts/lib/common.sh` is that resolver and every CLI that\nreads a file the checkout alone holds calls it, so do not write a second one. It takes the calling\nscript's own directory as its last candidate and the marker to probe for (`docker-compose.yml` by\ndefault); the call site in every one of those CLIs is this:"},"1717":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-81","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"It tries these candidates in order, and prints the first candidate that proves out:"},"1718":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-82","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"`${REPO_ROOT:-}`"},"1719":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-83","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"`${BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY:-}`"},"1720":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-84","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"`${GITHUB_WORKSPACE:-}`"},"1721":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-85","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"`${PWD}`"},"1722":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-86","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#resolve-then-prove","content":"`${SELF_DIR}/..`"},"1723":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-87","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-each-part-is-there","content":"The `${REPO_ROOT:-}` / `${GITHUB_WORKSPACE:-}` default is not decoration: these scripts run\nunder `set -euo pipefail`, and a bare `${REPO_ROOT?}` aborts with `REPO_ROOT: parameter not\nset` the moment a sandbox or CI runner leaves the variable unset."},"1724":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-88","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-each-part-is-there","content":"The file probe (`-f \"${candidate}/${marker}\"`) says \"this is a repo root\"; refusing a derived\ncandidate whose `pwd -P` lands under `bazel-out/`, `bazel-bin/`, `execroot/`, or a\n`*.runfiles` tree says \"and it is the real checkout, not a copy\", because runfiles carries its\nown copy of the marker. Two probes, because either one alone passes in the wrong case: writing a\nrotated `.env` or a `sparks/<host>.env` through the runfiles copy reports success while the\ncheckout keeps the old bytes. An explicit `${REPO_ROOT}` is exempt from the second probe — it is\na statement about where to work, and this harness points it at the copy of the repo under test."},"1725":{"id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel-89","page_id":"/contribute/test-with-bazel","tags":["bats","tests","bazel","contributing"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute/test-with-bazel#why-each-part-is-there","content":"Exit `5` with one `unresolvable repo root` line beats guessing a cwd and half-running a\nfleet check against a copy of the repo."},"1726":{"id":"/dashboard","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"page","content":"Dashboard and desktops","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard"},"1727":{"id":"/dashboard-0","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard","content":"The Homepage dashboard and Kasm Workspaces: what each card reads, how the password is issued, and how a desktop gets streamed."},"1728":{"id":"/dashboard-1","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"Dashboard and desktops"},"1729":{"id":"/dashboard-2","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#homepage-dashboard","content":"Homepage dashboard"},"1730":{"id":"/dashboard-3","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#what-it-shows","content":"What it shows"},"1731":{"id":"/dashboard-4","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#service-cards","content":"Service cards"},"1732":{"id":"/dashboard-5","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#the-search-box-and-the-searxng-card","content":"The search box and the SearXNG card"},"1733":{"id":"/dashboard-6","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#the-secrets-vault-card","content":"The secrets vault card"},"1734":{"id":"/dashboard-7","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#card-links","content":"Card links"},"1735":{"id":"/dashboard-8","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"The Observability group"},"1736":{"id":"/dashboard-9","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#login","content":"Login"},"1737":{"id":"/dashboard-10","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#config-files","content":"Config files"},"1738":{"id":"/dashboard-11","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#what-the-gate-checks","content":"What the gate checks"},"1739":{"id":"/dashboard-12","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#what-the-check-runs","content":"What the check runs"},"1740":{"id":"/dashboard-13","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#invariants-across-the-configs","content":"Invariants across the configs"},"1741":{"id":"/dashboard-14","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group-card-by-card","content":"The Observability group, card by card"},"1742":{"id":"/dashboard-15","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"Widgets, bookmarks, icons, and search hosts"},"1743":{"id":"/dashboard-16","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#after-a-recreate-revalidate-once","content":"After a recreate: revalidate once"},"1744":{"id":"/dashboard-17","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"Host stats, and the docker socket"},"1745":{"id":"/dashboard-18","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#look","content":"Look"},"1746":{"id":"/dashboard-19","page_id":"/dashboard","type":"heading","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"Kasm Workspaces"},"1747":{"id":"/dashboard-20","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1748":{"id":"/dashboard-21","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"What each dashboard card shows and which API it reads, the search lane included"},"1749":{"id":"/dashboard-22","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"The header tiles: CPU, memory, temperature, disk, interface throughput, clock, search"},"1750":{"id":"/dashboard-23","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"The password gate, the proxy in front of it, and how to rotate the password"},"1751":{"id":"/dashboard-24","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"The payload gate: which dashboard mistakes the build catches before a deploy does"},"1752":{"id":"/dashboard-25","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"Kasm's wizard-and-UI port pair, and what resetting it destroys"},"1753":{"id":"/dashboard-26","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"**What this enables**"},"1754":{"id":"/dashboard-27","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"Reading the box's health from one page without a shell"},"1755":{"id":"/dashboard-28","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"Fixing a card that reports down when the service itself is up"},"1756":{"id":"/dashboard-29","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#dashboard-and-desktops","content":"Two services that read the box rather than serve code: the Homepage dashboard (the\nlanding page) and Kasm Workspaces (streamed desktops)."},"1757":{"id":"/dashboard-30","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#service-cards","content":"A card per service, with status pulled from each service's own API over the compose\nnetwork - `http://coder:3000`, `http://litellm:4000`, `http://ollama:11434`,\n`http://hermes:9119/api/status` - so nothing here needs a daemon credential."},"1758":{"id":"/dashboard-31","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#service-cards","content":"The header carries boxed tiles for host CPU, memory, CPU temperature, disk and `eth0`\nthroughput, beside the clock (date and 24-hour time), local weather (open-meteo,\nkeyless) and a search box."},"1759":{"id":"/dashboard-32","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-search-box-and-the-searxng-card","content":"That box asks the stack's own SearXNG rather than a public engine, so a search from the\ndashboard goes to the same instance the workspace agents and Hermes dial."},"1760":{"id":"/dashboard-33","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-search-box-and-the-searxng-card","content":"The **Host** group carries the matching card: its badge probes `http://searxng:8181/healthz`, which\nanswers from the instance's own state without querying an upstream engine, and its three\nfields come from `GET /config` on the same port - the release tag, and the two switches\nthat decide whether the box is a public instance (`limiter`, `public_instance`)."},"1761":{"id":"/dashboard-34","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-search-box-and-the-searxng-card","content":"The dashboard never asks the instance for result rows: a polled `/search` would park engines\non the rate-limit and CAPTCHA walls, which is why that probe is\n`bazelisk run //scripts:search-check`'s job, run on demand. See\ntroubleshooting.md."},"1762":{"id":"/dashboard-35","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-secrets-vault-card","content":"The **Host** group carries one more card, for the secrets vault: its badge probes\n`http://infisical:8080/` - the container port, not the published `INFISICAL_PORT`,\nbecause this dashboard reaches every service over compose DNS - and `/` is the path the\npinned image's own healthcheck calls live. Its `href` rides\n`{{HOMEPAGE_VAR_INFISICAL_URL}}`, which bootstrap fills from `STACK_INFISICAL_URL` when\nthe public names are set."},"1763":{"id":"/dashboard-36","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-secrets-vault-card","content":"The bundle is one flag, `INFISICAL_ENABLED`, off as shipped:\nwith it off compose starts none of the three containers and the badge reads down with\nthem, so run `bazelisk run //scripts:infisical -- status` before chasing the card."},"1764":{"id":"/dashboard-37","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#card-links","content":"Card `href`s come from `STACK_CODER_URL` / `STACK_KASM_URL` / `STACK_LITELLM_URL` /\n`STACK_HERMES_URL`, which default to LAN URLs built from `STACK_LAN_HOST` and the\nport variables. Change a port or re-detect the LAN IP and the links follow; set `auto`\nin `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` and the cards follow the names bootstrap composes from the\nnaming parts (public-access.md)."},"1765":{"id":"/dashboard-38","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#card-links","content":"The Hermes card\nfollows `STACK_HERMES_URL` when bootstrap sets it, and stays on\n`http://<STACK_LAN_HOST>:9119` when that key is empty. See hermes.md."},"1766":{"id":"/dashboard-39","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#card-links","content":"The search card and the header box share `STACK_SEARCH_URL`. The router composes public\nnames for the dashboard, coder, kasm, litellm and hermes only, so search has no public\nname to fall to: leave the key empty and both stay on the LAN, where the card's status\nstill reports for anyone who can reach the dashboard."},"1767":{"id":"/dashboard-40","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"The **Observability** group is the one group that reports on services publishing no port."},"1768":{"id":"/dashboard-41","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"Its five cards - Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, Mimir - carry a `siteMonitor` on\ncompose DNS (`http://grafana:3000/api/health`, `http://prometheus:9090/-/healthy`,\n`http://loki:3100/ready`, `http://tempo:3200/ready`, `http://mimir:8080/ready`), which is\nwhat proves the bundle is wired up: four of those six containers ship no healthcheck at\nall (distroless image, no shell), so the badge is the only automatic signal they have."},"1769":{"id":"/dashboard-42","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"The bundle's four other services - `node_exporter`, `cadvisor`, `blackbox_exporter` and\n`alertmanager` - carry no card and publish nothing beyond the stack host's loopback, so\ntheir liveness is read there, not here."},"1770":{"id":"/dashboard-43","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"The hrefs go through `HOMEPAGE_VAR_GRAFANA_URL` and `HOMEPAGE_VAR_PROMETHEUS_URL`, which\ndefault to the LAN URLs built from `STACK_LAN_HOST`, `GRAFANA_PORT` and\n`PROMETHEUS_PORT`, and follow `STACK_GRAFANA_URL` once bootstrap composes the public name"},"1771":{"id":"/dashboard-44","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"so the card that opens Grafana Explore for Loki and Tempo opens the same Grafana the\ndatasources point at."},"1772":{"id":"/dashboard-45","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"The Grafana card also carries a `customapi` widget on\n`/api/health` - the one endpoint that needs no session or API key - so the tile shows the\nstorage state and the running version, which is what you compare against the image pin in\n`docker-compose.yml` after a pull."},"1773":{"id":"/dashboard-46","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group","content":"Only Grafana has a URL a browser can resolve; the\nthree backends are reached from inside it. See observability.md."},"1774":{"id":"/dashboard-47","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"`https://<host>/` serves the dashboard behind a self-signed certificate that\n`scripts/bootstrap.sh` issues, so expect a one-time browser warning. Port 80 redirects\nto HTTPS."},"1775":{"id":"/dashboard-48","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"The password gate is homepage v2's built-in one, and it is worth keeping: the page\nlists every service on the box."},"1776":{"id":"/dashboard-49","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"`HOMEPAGE_AUTH_PASSWORD` holds the plaintext, because\nhomepage hashes that env var itself but still needs the value."},"1777":{"id":"/dashboard-50","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"Either form:"},"1778":{"id":"/dashboard-51","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"rewrites `.env`"},"1779":{"id":"/dashboard-52","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"recreates the container"},"1780":{"id":"/dashboard-53","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"verifies the new value landed"},"1781":{"id":"/dashboard-54","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#login","content":"The script's job is keeping the secret out of shell history, `ps` and git, and leaving\n`.env` at mode 600."},"1782":{"id":"/dashboard-55","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#config-files","content":"`homepage/config/*.yaml` plus `custom.css` are bind-mounted read-only, so `git diff`\nstays the record of dashboard changes, and the directory itself has to stay writable\nbecause the app creates `logs/` inside it."},"1783":{"id":"/dashboard-56","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#config-files","content":"A new config file (`kubernetes.yaml`, ...)\nneeds its own mount line in `docker-compose.yml` before the app sees it."},"1784":{"id":"/dashboard-57","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#config-files","content":"`custom.css` lives in `/app/config` and is served by the allow-listed\n`/api/config/custom.css` route. It styles the sign-in page too, so keep internal\nhostnames out of it."},"1785":{"id":"/dashboard-58","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#what-the-check-runs","content":"`//:validate` proves these files parse. `tests/homepage_config_check.py` reads them the\nway the app does and fails on the mistakes that parse happily:"},"1786":{"id":"/dashboard-59","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#invariants-across-the-configs","content":"every `{{HOMEPAGE_VAR_*}}` token has a key in `docker-compose.yml`, and every\n`HOMEPAGE_VAR_*` key is used by some config file"},"1787":{"id":"/dashboard-60","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#invariants-across-the-configs","content":"every service and bookmark group has a `layout` entry, and every `layout` key names a\nreal group; a `style: row` group's `columns` equals the number of cards it holds"},"1788":{"id":"/dashboard-61","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#invariants-across-the-configs","content":"a card `href` is a token or a public URL, never a compose service name: the browser\ncannot resolve `http://coder:3000`, only the dashboard server can"},"1789":{"id":"/dashboard-62","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#invariants-across-the-configs","content":"a `siteMonitor` or widget `url` names a compose service or a token, never a loopback\nor LAN-address literal, which would bake the LAN into git"},"1790":{"id":"/dashboard-63","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group-card-by-card","content":"the **Observability** group, card by card: five cards, one per bundle service, each\nprobing its own health path over compose DNS - `http://grafana:3000/api/health`,\n`http://prometheus:9090/-/healthy`, `http://loki:3100/ready`,\n`http://tempo:3200/ready`, `http://mimir:8080/ready`. Those four distroless containers\nship no in-container healthcheck, so this probe is the only liveness read the stack has\nfor them, and a badge pointed anywhere else is caught here"},"1791":{"id":"/dashboard-64","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group-card-by-card","content":"the same group's links: every href rides a `{{HOMEPAGE_VAR_*}}` token and none carries\na URL literal (Loki, Tempo and Mimir publish no port, so their two hrefs open\n`{{HOMEPAGE_VAR_GRAFANA_URL}}/explore` rather than a store nobody can reach), and no\nprobe bakes a loopback or LAN address"},"1792":{"id":"/dashboard-65","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#the-observability-group-card-by-card","content":"the group's place on the page: `Observability` has its own `layout` entry, renders as\none `style: row` band whose `columns` equals the cards it holds, and sits after the\n**Host** group"},"1793":{"id":"/dashboard-66","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"no `block` customapi widget declares more than four mappings - the shipped bundle\nslices the list, so a fifth row silently never renders"},"1794":{"id":"/dashboard-67","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"a bookmark's value is a list of single-key mappings carrying both `abbr` and `href`;\nwritten as a plain mapping the entry loads with a name and nothing else, because the\napp drops the keys it did not ask for"},"1795":{"id":"/dashboard-68","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"a local `icon:` path is under `/icons/`, the one path the auth middleware exempts from\nthe sign-in redirect"},"1796":{"id":"/dashboard-69","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"a `search` widget with `provider: custom` carries a url ending in `=`, because v2.4.0\nappends the encoded query to whatever `url` says and has no `{{query}}` token"},"1797":{"id":"/dashboard-70","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"a Spark URL in `docker-compose.yml` takes its host from an env var. The boxes are\noff-stack, so compose DNS cannot reach them and a hostname written here names a\nmachine nobody owns: `SPARKn_HOST` in `.env` names each box once and compose\ncomposes the card's probe URL from it (see\nconfig-updates.md)"},"1798":{"id":"/dashboard-71","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#widgets-bookmarks-icons-and-search-hosts","content":"The suite also breaks each invariant in a scratch copy, so a check that has stopped\nfailing fails the build."},"1799":{"id":"/dashboard-72","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#after-a-recreate-revalidate-once","content":"v2.4.0 serves a prerendered page with the settings baked in, so a freshly created\ncontainer shows an empty default layout (`initialSettings {}`) until the config is\nre-read. Click the refresh button in the header, or:"},"1800":{"id":"/dashboard-73","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#after-a-recreate-revalidate-once","content":"A plain `restart` keeps the generated page, so day-to-day YAML edits need nothing.\nNew asset files do need a recreate (`up -d`), since `restart` keeps the old mounts."},"1801":{"id":"/dashboard-74","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"CPU, memory, CPU temperature and disk are host-wide through `/proc`. A network widget\nonly sees the container's own netns (`lo`/`eth0`) - `/sys/class/net` is namespaced, so\nthe host Wi-Fi NIC stays invisible even with `/sys` mounted. That tile reads `eth0`."},"1802":{"id":"/dashboard-75","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"Those numbers are also series now: `node_exporter` reads the same `/proc` and `/sys`\nread-only and `cadvisor` covers the containers, so the tile answers \"what is the box doing\nnow, as the dashboard sees it\" and the Grafana board answers \"and what was it at 03:00\".\nThe tile survives the bundle being off; the board does not."},"1803":{"id":"/dashboard-76","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"Which board, exactly, is catalogued in observability.md under\n`## The dashboards` - four families of them:"},"1804":{"id":"/dashboard-77","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"the stack host (`evo-host-taskmanager`, `evo-containers`)"},"1805":{"id":"/dashboard-78","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"the DGX Sparks (`evo-sparks-overview`, `evo-spark-host`, `evo-sparks-fleet`)"},"1806":{"id":"/dashboard-79","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"the inference backends (`evo-inference-models`, `evo-inference-backends`)"},"1807":{"id":"/dashboard-80","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"the bundle itself (`evo-home`, `evo-stack-overview`, `evo-alerts`, `evo-stack-logs`,\n`evo-stack-traces`, `evo-litellm`)"},"1808":{"id":"/dashboard-81","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"The question-to-page table lives there; this page stays about the dashboard and the\ndesktops."},"1809":{"id":"/dashboard-82","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"The docker socket stays unmounted: service status comes from each service's API, which\navoids handing the dashboard a root-equivalent host credential."},"1810":{"id":"/dashboard-83","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#host-stats-and-the-docker-socket","content":"The Hermes card in the\n**Host** group is the same pattern (`siteMonitor` of `http://hermes:9119/api/status`);\nthe Hermes container itself *does* mount the socket — that credential lives there, not\nhere. See hermes.md."},"1811":{"id":"/dashboard-84","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#look","content":"The layout follows the upstream README example - logo plus greeting top-left, boxed\nresource tiles, clock, weather and search top-right, cards on a wallpaper."},"1812":{"id":"/dashboard-85","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#look","content":"The\nwallpaper (`background.webp`) and the logo (`evo-t1.svg`) live in\n`homepage/assets/icons/`, mounted at `/app/public/icons` and served as `/icons/...`."},"1813":{"id":"/dashboard-86","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#look","content":"Homepage's auth middleware exempts only that path from the sign-in redirect, which is\nwhat lets the same wallpaper render on the login page, and is why `favicon` points at\n`/icons/evo-t1.svg` too: a tab icon from anywhere else 307s to `/auth/signin`."},"1814":{"id":"/dashboard-87","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#look","content":"`disableIndexing: true` is the whole anti-crawler measure: the app then serves\n`/robots.txt` with `User-agent: *` / `Disallow: /`, and writes no robots meta tag into\nthe page."},"1815":{"id":"/dashboard-88","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#look","content":"It matters only when `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` gives the dashboard a public name -\nthe page already sits behind the password, and its paths should not reach a crawler\neither."},"1816":{"id":"/dashboard-89","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"**First boot:** `https://<host>:3000` - run the install wizard once."},"1817":{"id":"/dashboard-90","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"**After install:** the UI is on `https://<host>:4443`. Both ports serve TLS with the\nself-signed certificate Kasm's own installer generates, and plain `http://` reaches\nneither port."},"1818":{"id":"/dashboard-91","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"`KASM_UI_PORT` has to match on **both** sides of the port mapping. The daemon-side\nlistener listens on that number, so the mapping is `4443:4443`."},"1819":{"id":"/dashboard-92","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"The image ships default users (`admin@kasm.local` / `user@kasm.local`); change them\nduring the wizard."},"1820":{"id":"/dashboard-93","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"Kasm is a privileged Docker-in-Docker container, and privileged whether or not the\nobservability bundle is on. The other privileged containers are `cadvisor`, which comes\nup only with the `observability` profile\n(observability.md), and the opt-in workspace DinD sidecar. Keep Kasm\nLAN-only unless you have decided who may reach the public name\n(see SECURITY.md)."},"1821":{"id":"/dashboard-94","page_id":"/dashboard","tags":["homepage","kasm","dashboard","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/dashboard#kasm-workspaces","content":"Losing the wizard after install is expected: use `:4443`. Resetting Kasm means\nremoving the `kasm-data` volume, which destroys all Kasm config."},"1822":{"id":"/getting-started","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started"},"1823":{"id":"/getting-started-0","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started","content":"First boot on a GMKtec EVO-T1, top to bottom — bootstrap the host, bring the stable stack up, register Coder, push the templates, open a workspace."},"1824":{"id":"/getting-started-1","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Getting started"},"1825":{"id":"/getting-started-2","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"1826":{"id":"/getting-started-3","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#first-boot","content":"First boot"},"1827":{"id":"/getting-started-4","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#clone-the-repository","content":"Clone the repository"},"1828":{"id":"/getting-started-5","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#the-secrets-file","content":"The secrets file"},"1829":{"id":"/getting-started-6","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#install-the-toolchain","content":"Install the toolchain"},"1830":{"id":"/getting-started-7","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"Look before you change anything"},"1831":{"id":"/getting-started-8","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#prepare-the-box","content":"Prepare the box"},"1832":{"id":"/getting-started-9","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#start-the-stack-and-pull-the-models","content":"Start the stack and pull the models"},"1833":{"id":"/getting-started-10","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#once-coder-answers","content":"Once Coder answers"},"1834":{"id":"/getting-started-11","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#register-the-first-account","content":"Register the first account"},"1835":{"id":"/getting-started-12","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#push-both-templates","content":"Push both templates"},"1836":{"id":"/getting-started-13","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#wire-the-chat-agent","content":"Wire the chat agent"},"1837":{"id":"/getting-started-14","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#create-the-first-workspace","content":"Create the first workspace"},"1838":{"id":"/getting-started-15","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#finish-in-a-browser","content":"Finish in a browser"},"1839":{"id":"/getting-started-16","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"url":"/getting-started#what-to-read-next","content":"What to read next"},"1840":{"id":"/getting-started-17","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"**What's on this page**"},"1841":{"id":"/getting-started-18","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"The one-time host bootstrap, and why it is the only step run straight from a shell"},"1842":{"id":"/getting-started-19","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Bringing the stable stack up and pulling the models"},"1843":{"id":"/getting-started-20","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Registering the first Coder account, pushing both templates, wiring the chat agent"},"1844":{"id":"/getting-started-21","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Creating the first workspace from a git URL"},"1845":{"id":"/getting-started-22","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"**What this enables**"},"1846":{"id":"/getting-started-23","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"A working stack on a fresh box without reading the whole README first"},"1847":{"id":"/getting-started-24","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Knowing which step to re-run when a later one says a prerequisite is missing"},"1848":{"id":"/getting-started-25","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"The commands are the README's spin-up section\nwith the reasoning attached. Run them on the stack host, not inside a workspace: a\nworkspace's `docker` addresses its own DinD sidecar, and the whole-stack targets reach the\ndaemon that runs Coder."},"1849":{"id":"/getting-started-26","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#before-you-start","content":"A GMKtec EVO-T1 (or any box with the Arc 140T and enough RAM for the model in\n`OLLAMA_MODELS`) with Docker and Compose v2 installed."},"1850":{"id":"/getting-started-27","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#before-you-start","content":"The LAN address you will browse to. `CODER_ACCESS_URL` has to be an `https://` URL that\nis not `localhost`, or a workspace cannot reach LiteLLM."},"1851":{"id":"/getting-started-28","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#the-secrets-file","content":"Create the one file that holds real secrets, and lock it down before anything else reads\nit:"},"1852":{"id":"/getting-started-29","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#install-the-toolchain","content":"Bootstrap the toolchain — the only step that runs before Bazel exists, because it is what\ninstalls Bazelisk:"},"1853":{"id":"/getting-started-30","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"Then look before you change anything. `--check` is read-only:"},"1854":{"id":"/getting-started-31","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"missing tools"},"1855":{"id":"/getting-started-32","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"placeholder secrets"},"1856":{"id":"/getting-started-33","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"certificates"},"1857":{"id":"/getting-started-34","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#look-before-you-change-anything","content":"images"},"1858":{"id":"/getting-started-35","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prepare-the-box","content":"rotate the secrets"},"1859":{"id":"/getting-started-36","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["start","bootstrap","install","coder"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prepare-the-box","content":"set `CODER_ACCESS_URL`"},