ontent":"Understanding a behaviour before trying to change it"},"2895":{"id":"/learn-14","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-stack","content":"Knowing which page owns a concept when two of them seem to"},"2896":{"id":"/learn-15","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#learn-the-stack","content":"> **Not the same as the `/ez-learn` command.** This tab is the concepts index for people\n> reading the docs. `/ez-learn` typed at the Grok Build prompt turns the session you are in\n> into durable memory - flush it into a session log, dream those logs into organized memory,\n> remember one note, or browse and clear the store; it is this stack's copy of the upstream\n> `/flush`, `/dream`, `/remember` and `/memory`.\n>\n> Skill authoring is its siblings:\n>\n> - `/ez-skillify` captures the session that just worked\n> - `/ez-create-skill` scaffolds one from a description\n>\n> `grok inspect` lists the three once their seed has landed. A missing one is the skill-seed\n> entry in troubleshooting.md."},"2897":{"id":"/learn-16","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#what-the-two-templates-build","content":"Two templates turn a git URL into a running container:"},"2898":{"id":"/learn-17","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#what-the-two-templates-build","content":"the plain `workspace` template"},"2899":{"id":"/learn-18","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#what-the-two-templates-build","content":"`devcontainer`, which builds the clone's own `.devcontainer` on a DinD sidecar"},"2900":{"id":"/learn-19","page_id":"/learn","tags":["learn","concepts","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/learn#what-the-two-templates-build","content":"Both are pushed from this checkout, and both seed the agent config the workspace starts with."},"2901":{"id":"/