age_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#litellm-model-routing","content":"how a request picks a backend"},"2998":{"id":"/litellm-routing-85","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#litellm-model-routing","content":"what a pinned conversation does"},"2999":{"id":"/litellm-routing-86","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#litellm-model-routing","content":"what happens when a Spark box goes down"},"3000":{"id":"/litellm-routing-87","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#litellm-model-routing","content":"Short version lives in README.md (\"LiteLLM model aliases\"); this file is\nthe long version behind it. Symptom-first checks live in\ntroubleshooting.md."},"3001":{"id":"/litellm-routing-88","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#litellm-model-routing","content":"Related: coder-templates.md (the templates that render\n`~/.grok/config.toml`), grok-build-and-agents.md (the CLI and\nthe control-plane chat), project-conventions.md."},"3002":{"id":"/litellm-routing-89","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#two-doors-one-key","content":"Workspaces and desktops always talk to one base URL,\n`http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1`, and pick a model alias. That is the\nhost-gateway door."},"3003":{"id":"/litellm-routing-90","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#two-doors-one-key","content":"The control-plane chat agent dials the same proxy at `http://litellm:4000/v1`, over the\ncompose network, from inside the `coder` container. That is the server-side door."},"3004":{"id":"/litellm-routing-91","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#two-doors-one-key","content":"Both doors authenticate with the same `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` value."},"3005":{"id":"/litellm-routing-92","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#two-doors-one-key","content":"Inside a workspace the key travels as the `LITELLM_API_KEY` environment variable, which\n`~/.grok/config.toml` references by `env_key`, so no key byte lands in a file."},"3006":{"id":"/litellm-routing-93","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-an-alias-is","content":"An alias is a `model_name:` entry in `litellm/config.yaml`, not a model."},"3007":{"id":"/litellm-routing-94","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-an-alias-is","content":"Every alias is a stable name. A workspace setting never has to change when a backend\nmoves behind one."},"3008":{"id":"/litellm-routing-95","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-an-alias-is","content":"A rename or deletion is the edit that can reach workspaces: both\n`templates/*/grok-config.toml.tftpl` twins render the alias list into\n`~/.grok/config.toml`, a running workspace keeps the copy it rendered at start, and\nthe next start re-renders it."},"3009":{"id":"/litellm-routing-96","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-top-level-blocks","content":"`model_list:` is the alias list; `router_settings:` is the routing."},"3010":{"id":"/litellm-routing-97","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-top-level-blocks","content":"`routing_strategy: least-busy` is the picker;\n`optional_pre_call_checks: [\"session_affinity\"]` is the pinning layer above it."},"3011":{"id":"/litellm-routing-98","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallbacks-and-the-cooldown-rule","content":"`fallbacks:` carries the degrade path `agent: [\"coder\"]`, repeated for each thinking\nalias, because those groups go down with exactly the same boxes. The four unpinned\nlanes and the two fast-compaction lanes hop one step further, through the lane that\nbakes their own level, so a lane that asked for `low` is not served an `xhigh` answer\nby its fallback."},"3012":{"id":"/litellm-routing-99","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallbacks-and-the-cooldown-rule","content":"`cooldown_time: 60` is how long a box that tripped the rate rule sits out, and it is\nalso the fail window that rule counts over."},"3013":{"id":"/litellm-routing-100","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallbacks-and-the-cooldown-rule","content":"There is no `allowed_fails` key in the config, and the absence is deliberate: naming it\nwith a non-default number selects the counting branch of the cooldown decision instead\nof the rate rule, and that branch counts inside a window of `cooldown_time`."},"3014":{"id":"/litellm-routing-101","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallbacks-and-the-cooldown-rule","content":"The `allowed_fails: 40` and `cooldown_time: 5` this replaced therefore asked for 41\nfailures inside 5 s, which is why it never fired."},"3015":{"id":"/litellm-routing-102","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallbacks-and-the-cooldown-rule","content":"Without the key the vendor's rate rule decides when a box stops being a candidate; see\nwhat `cooldown_time: 60` is for."},"3016":{"id":"/litellm-routing-103","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"`background_health_checks: true` and `enable_health_check_routing: true` do the\nre-probing and then make the result decide routing, so recovery does not wait for\nuser traffic to rediscover it."},"3017":{"id":"/litellm-routing-104","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"They sit beside `health_check_interval: 120`, `health_check_staleness_threshold: 900`\nand `health_check_concurrency: 2`."},"3018":{"id":"/litellm-routing-105","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"Those keys have to sit in `general_settings:`; `health_check_interval` and\n`health_check_concurrency` under `router_settings:` make the proxy raise `ValueError`\nat boot."},"3019":{"id":"/litellm-routing-106","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"The concurrency is deliberately small: a probe is a real generation that carries the\nlane's baked `reasoning_effort`, and on a box whose prompt cache sits full it evicts\na warm conversation to fit itself. See the TensorFold log section of\ntroubleshooting.md."},"3020":{"id":"/litellm-routing-107","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"`health_check_ignore_transient_errors: true` is load-bearing rather than tidy. A box\nthat is merely busy can answer a 16-token probe with a 429 or a 408, and with the\nkey on those endpoints are dropped before the state is written\n(`proxy_server.py:3971-3974`) and again before the cooldown loop takes them\n(`proxy_server.py:4002-4006`). Flipping it off would cost a session-pinned\nconversation its warm box and that box's prompt cache its next prefill, over one\nslow probe."},"3021":{"id":"/litellm-routing-108","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"The four Arc deployments - `coder`, `coder-fast`, `chat`, `compaction-fast` - carry\n`model_info.disable_background_health_check: true`, so the sweep drops them\n(`proxy_server.py:4116-4118`)."},"3022":{"id":"/litellm-routing-109","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"A group's only deployment can never be pulled out by the health filter anyway - dropping\nit empties the candidate list, which is the `router.py:14177` fail-open - so the mark buys\nno routing, and it is not free: the same cycle cools what it marked\n(`proxy_server.py:4013`) and the cooldown list has no fail-open under this config, because\nthe bypass at `router.py:12774` needs a policy the file refuses to set."},"3023":{"id":"/litellm-routing-110","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"`coder` is the terminal hop of every Spark lane, so a 401 or a 404 from a probe would park\nthe fallback for `cooldown_time` with no user request having failed."},"3024":{"id":"/litellm-routing-111","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"Read the two functions in order and the family is exact: that pair clears\n`_is_cooldown_required` on its own named arms (`cooldown_handlers.py:239` and `:243`), and\nthe arm at `:400-401` then cools it on the bare question of whether LiteLLM would retry\nthe status, with no single-deployment guard -- `_should_retry` returns False for\neverything outside 408/409/429/5xx (`utils.py:6854-6880`)."},"3025":{"id":"/litellm-routing-112","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"No other probe reply strands anything: 429 and 408 are skipped at the call site by\n`health_check_ignore_transient_errors` (`proxy_server.py:4001-4004`), any other 4xx is\nrefused at `:248`, and a genuine 5xx clears the catch-all at `:252` only to fall through\nevery base-case arm."},"3026":{"id":"/litellm-routing-113","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"That reading is the source's, not the harness's -- the arm which recorded\n`exception_status` 500 had the Arc unreachable, and `proxy_server.py:3999` derives the\nstatus with `getattr(original_exception,\n\"status_code\", 500)`, so a box answering no HTTP at all arrives pre-labelled retryable, and is\nvetoed at `:223-227` on its `APIConnectionError` text besides."},"3027":{"id":"/litellm-routing-114","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"The consequence that is measured, and which stands without the stranding argument: those\nfour no longer appear in the cached `/health` report at all, and four of the 31 probes a\ncycle stop being paid."},"3028":{"id":"/litellm-routing-115","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-health-sweep-does","content":"`health_check_staleness_threshold` has to be named because the shipped default does\nnot follow the interval: it is `DEFAULT_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL * 2`, 600 s whatever\n`health_check_interval` says (`router.py:993`), and it is the window the health filter\ntrusts before it stops filtering. 900 s is what keeps a slow sweep from opening that\nwindow; see how long it takes, and how it comes\nback."},"3029":{"id":"/litellm-routing-116","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#retries-and-timeouts","content":"`num_retries: 2` covers a transient blip; moving off a busy box is routing's job, not\nthe retry chain's. `request_timeout: 1200` is now the tightest deadline on the chain -\nthe CLI's streaming idle allowance (`inference_idle_timeout_secs`) sits at 1800 s - so\nthe proxy is the end that gives up first, at a full twenty minutes per attempt."},"3030":{"id":"/litellm-routing-117","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#retries-and-timeouts","content":"`model_group_retry_policy:` gives the nine agent lanes their own `RetryPolicy`. The\nreason it exists is narrow enough to be worth its own section below."},"3031":{"id":"/litellm-routing-118","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-router-sees-a-connection-error","content":"TensorFold on the Spark boxes refuses an over-admitted stream with the Zig error value\n`NoRoom`, delivered as an HTTP 500 body."},"3032":{"id":"/litellm-routing-119","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-router-sees-a-connection-error","content":"The OpenAI SDK hands that to LiteLLM with no int\n`status_code`, which at the pinned `v1.102.1` puts it on the status-less branch of\n`exception_mapping_utils`, so the router sees `APIConnectionError`."},"3033":{"id":"/litellm-routing-120","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-router-sees-a-connection-error","content":"`RetryPolicy` in that tag has no `APIConnectionErrorRetries` field."},"3034":{"id":"/litellm-routing-121","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-router-sees-a-connection-error","content":"`DefaultRetries` is the only field that can reach the error,\nwhich is why each agent lane declares one:"},"3035":{"id":"/litellm-routing-122","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-to-read-before-changing-the-block","content":"Read these three facts before changing the block:"},"3036":{"id":"/litellm-routing-123","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-to-read-before-changing-the-block","content":"The nine Spark groups are independent and none inherits `agent`, so each needs its own\nsix keys. The zeros pin the exceptions `DefaultRetries` would otherwise reach; at this\ntag `NotFoundError` has no field of its own, so without a policy a typo'd model id is\nretried on `DefaultRetries`."},"3037":{"id":"/litellm-routing-124","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-to-read-before-changing-the-block","content":"The policy is scoped to the Spark lanes. `coder` (Arc), `chat` and `compaction-fast`\n(the Arc group a summary hops to) keep the plain `num_retries` path."},"3038":{"id":"/litellm-routing-125","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-to-read-before-changing-the-block","content":"These retries are instant and stay on the same box. A status-less exception means\n`_deployment_ids_to_skip_on_retry` excludes nothing and `_time_to_sleep_before_retry`\nreturns 0 while any deployment is healthy, and on the five pinned groups the\nworkspace-wide `x-litellm-session-id` pin sends every subagent of a workspace to one\nbox anyway. The block makes a refusal less likely to surface. Relocation comes from the\nbox and the fan-out."},"3039":{"id":"/litellm-routing-126","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-to-read-before-changing-the-block","content":"The four unpinned lanes - `agent-swarm`, `agent-explore`, `agent-review` and\n`agent-swarm-fast` - are the exception: with no pin to name a box, each of their\nretries is re-placed by `least-busy` and can land on another one."},"3040":{"id":"/litellm-routing-127","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The two levers that actually move load off a shedding box:"},"3041":{"id":"/litellm-routing-128","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The box-side reclaim switch. The recipe measured the same refusal going from\n\"2 of 5 streams refused\" to \"5 of 5 admitted\" once patch 0029 is live with\n`TF_FLASHNEXT_ADMIT_RECLAIM=1`. `//scripts:spark-configure --apply` owns the per-host\noverride file those settings belong in, and `//scripts:spark-verify` already fails a\nbox whose `streams.max` drifts from the fleet's `PARALLEL`. Asserting the\nadmit-reclaim setting itself is still open work: neither script names that key today."},"3042":{"id":"/litellm-routing-129","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"Keep what one workspace puts on one box at or under that box's `PARALLEL` (5). A pinned\nlane sends the whole fan-out to the box its session key resolves to, so the width worth\nasking for there is 4: one box's streams, minus the parent's own request."},"3043":{"id":"/litellm-routing-130","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The unpinned `agent-swarm` lane is what the writers ride by default, and the one that\ncan afford a wider wave - 15 subagents spread by `least-busy` over three boxes fill\neach box's `PARALLEL` exactly, which is the difference between buying wall-clock and\nbuying queue depth."},"3044":{"id":"/litellm-routing-131","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"That default asks every box for all of its streams, and it reserves nothing for the\nparent's own request the way the one-box width of 4 does. That is a deliberate trade\nrather than an oversight: the parent's conversation, the reader waves and the review\npass all arrive on the same three boxes and share those `PARALLEL` streams, so at 15 a\nsingle busy workspace can have the fleet fully subscribed and the last arrivals wait."},"3045":{"id":"/litellm-routing-132","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"What makes that survivable is `limit_behavior = \"queue\"` holding the overflow instead\nof failing the spawn, so the cost of overshoot is a subagent's latency."},"3046":{"id":"/litellm-routing-133","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"That 15 is `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`'s own shipped default, the same on every lane\nwhatever the operator picks there."},"3047":{"id":"/litellm-routing-134","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"`grok_swarm_width` (3 boxes x `PARALLEL` 5) is the fleet's own ceiling, rendered as the\n`# fleet-width:` line beside `max_concurrent`, and the width a workspace gets only when\nit sets `grok_subagent_max_concurrent = null` on purpose. So an operator who shares the\nfleet shrinks it with two knobs, not one: `grok_swarm_width` moves the ceiling and\n`grok_subagent_max_concurrent` moves the width. Drop the first alone and the session\nstill ships 15, and 15 streams over a 10-stream fleet is refused by the box with\n`NoRoom`."},"3048":{"id":"/litellm-routing-135","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The two reader lanes spread the same way, and each group counts its own in-flight\nrequests, but the box's `PARALLEL` streams are one pool that every alias arriving on it\nshares. Past 15 across the fleet the boxes have no streams left to give, whatever the\nlane."},"3049":{"id":"/litellm-routing-136","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The same 15 is the budget of a whole tree, because `max_depth` (rendered from\n`grok_subagent_max_depth`, default 2, validated 1..3) lets a child spawn."},"3050":{"id":"/litellm-routing-137","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"`reviewer`, `security-auditor` and `tester` name `spawn_subagent` in their `tools`,\nand every mapper such a child raises holds a stream the same way its parent does, so\na parent sums the in-flight `1 + spawns` over every task and keeps that total at or\nbelow the fleet's stream count (`fleet:` in the plan, 15 by default,\n`templates/common/ez-micro-plan.plan_check.py:42`)."},"3051":{"id":"/litellm-routing-138","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"That checker refuses a wave whose cost passes the fleet, and the sum is a separate\nfigure from the session cap `[subagents] max_concurrent` sets, because a grandchild\nopens its own session."},"3052":{"id":"/litellm-routing-139","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-two-levers-that-move-load","content":"The box refuses an over-admitted stream the same way it refuses any other, with\n`NoRoom`."},"3053":{"id":"/litellm-routing-140","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#knobs-that-look-right-and-do-nothing","content":"Two knobs that look right and do nothing here:"},"3054":{"id":"/litellm-routing-141","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#knobs-that-look-right-and-do-nothing","content":"`retry_after` is only a `min_timeout` and is never consulted while the group has healthy\ndeployments."},"3055":{"id":"/litellm-routing-142","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#knobs-that-look-right-and-do-nothing","content":"`fallbacks_by_model` does not exist in this tag (the proxy warns and ignores an unknown\n`router_settings` key, so a config that looks correct silently does nothing, which is why\n`//tests:bats_litellm_config_test` rejects it by name)."},"3056":{"id":"/litellm-routing-143","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias   | Model                | Backend                                                                                | Structured tool calls |\n| ------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `agent` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | `SPARK1/2/3_OPENAI_URL` (TensorFold on :8888 - one deployment per Spark box, optional) | yes (measured)        |","table":"table-0"},"3057":{"id":"/litellm-routing-144","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias       | Model                | Backend                                                                          | Structured tool calls                 |\n| ----------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-low` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `low` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3058":{"id":"/litellm-routing-145","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias          | Model                | Backend                                                                             | Structured tool calls                 |\n| -------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-medium` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `medium` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3059":{"id":"/litellm-routing-146","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias         | Model                | Backend                                                                            | Structured tool calls                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-xhigh` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `xhigh` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3060":{"id":"/litellm-routing-147","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias         | Model                | Backend                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Structured tool calls                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-swarm` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `xhigh`, and the first group with no session pin, so each request is placed on the least-busy healthy box; the default `grok_subagents_lane`, so the writer types fan out here | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3061":{"id":"/litellm-routing-148","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias           | Model                | Backend                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Structured tool calls                 |\n| --------------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-explore` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `low`, and no pin here either, so a wave of one-shot read-only children is placed across the fleet rather than queueing behind one box; the default `grok_explore_lane` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3062":{"id":"/litellm-routing-149","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias          | Model                | Backend                                                                                                                                                                                                                | Structured tool calls                 |\n| -------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-review` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent`, as its own group; thinking baked to `xhigh` like `agent`, and the same pin lift as `agent-explore`, so a wave of reviewers spreads the same way; the default `grok_review_lane` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3063":{"id":"/litellm-routing-150","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias              | Model                | Backend                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Structured tool calls                 |\n| ------------------ | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-xhigh-fast` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent-xhigh`, as its own group; the same deployments, the same baked `xhigh`, the same session pin - this lane differs from its parent in one call of the conversation, which the proxy callback moves to `compaction-fast` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3064":{"id":"/litellm-routing-151","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias              | Model                | Backend                                                                                                                                                         | Structured tool calls                 |\n| ------------------ | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-swarm-fast` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` | the same three Spark boxes as `agent-swarm`, as its own group; baked `xhigh`, the same pin lift as `agent-swarm`, and the same summary hop to `compaction-fast` | yes (same model and boxes as `agent`) |","table":"table-0"},"3065":{"id":"/litellm-routing-152","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias   | Model               | Backend | Structured tool calls |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `coder` | `qwen2.5-coder:32b` |         | no (measured)         |","table":"table-0"},"3066":{"id":"/litellm-routing-153","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias        | Model               | Backend | Structured tool calls |\n| ------------ | ------------------- | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `coder-fast` | `qwen2.5-coder:14b` |         | no (measured)         |","table":"table-0"},"3067":{"id":"/litellm-routing-154","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias             | Model               | Backend                                                       | Structured tool calls                              |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `compaction-fast` | `qwen2.5-coder:14b` | `[model.*]` block and no `local.model_choices` entry names it | no (measured on these weights, as on `coder-fast`) |","table":"table-0"},"3068":{"id":"/litellm-routing-155","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-alias-table","content":"| Alias  | Model        | Backend | Structured tool calls |\n| ------ | ------------ | ------- | --------------------- |\n| `chat` | `qwen2.5:7b` |         | yes (measured)        |","table":"table-0"},"3069":{"id":"/litellm-routing-156","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"The `agent` row is ONE model group with three deployments, one per Spark box,\nall equal."},"3070":{"id":"/litellm-routing-157","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"The eight `agent-*` rows are that same lane with a thinking level baked into\n`litellm_params.reasoning_effort`. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next takes `low`, `medium` and `xhigh`\nand nothing else - there is no `high` - so the level is a name to pick rather than a knob\nto turn, and `agent-low` / `agent-medium` / `agent-xhigh` are how the level reaches Coder\nAgents: its model dropdown chooses an alias, not a request parameter."},"3071":{"id":"/litellm-routing-158","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"The `agent-explore` and `agent-review` rows are the same idea aimed at a fleet role rather\nthan at a person in that dropdown - see\nthe fan-out lanes."},"3072":{"id":"/litellm-routing-159","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"`agent` is not the unthinking default. It bakes `reasoning_effort: xhigh`, so a\nCoder Agents chat on the default alias thinks hard, and `agent-xhigh` asks the\nbox for the same level by name. A `reasoning_effort` the client sends in the\nrequest still wins over the baked one."},"3073":{"id":"/litellm-routing-160","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"Those eight groups reuse the same `SPARK1/2/3_OPENAI_URL` / `SPARK_n_API_KEY` pairs as\n`agent`. They are separate model groups on the same hardware, not eight more boxes:\nrouting state is per group, so least-busy's counters and the session pin are computed\ninside a group and two chats on different aliases can land on the same box at once."},"3074":{"id":"/litellm-routing-161","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"What does not change is the box - 5 full 262144-token streams in total, whichever aliases\narrive on it. This is not the \"two deployments on one box\" mistake below, which is about a\nsingle group counting two URLs on one machine as two machines."},"3075":{"id":"/litellm-routing-162","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"The three rows after `agent-xhigh` differ from the four above them in routing state\nonly: same model, same three boxes, the thinking level each row names, and no session\npin. See\nthe swarm lane and\nthe fan-out lanes."},"3076":{"id":"/litellm-routing-163","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-rows","content":"The two rows after those are not new lanes. `agent-xhigh-fast` is `agent-xhigh` and\n`agent-swarm-fast` is `agent-swarm`, deployment for deployment, and what differs is\nwhere one call of the conversation is answered - the CLI's summary request, which a\nproxy callback re-serves from `compaction-fast` on the Arc when the summary fits that\nwindow, and from a Spark group at thinking `low` when it does not. See\nthe fast-compaction lanes."},"3077":{"id":"/litellm-routing-164","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-arc-summary-row","content":"`compaction-fast` is that hop's small-summary target, and a row no template offers a client: no\n`reasoning_effort` line, no tool-calling flags, and `max_input_tokens: 32768` rather\nthan the Spark rows' 262144, because a summary is prose and 32768 is the honest\nwindow of those weights."},"3078":{"id":"/litellm-routing-165","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-backend-has-to-match","content":"The Spark boxes serve TensorFold's OpenAI-compatible `/v1` and nothing else: Ollama\nruns on the Arc, so a Spark box never sees the Ollama protocol."},"3079":{"id":"/litellm-routing-166","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-backend-has-to-match","content":"`model:` is sent to the backend verbatim, so `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` has to match the\nserved id byte-for-byte, case and hyphens included."},"3080":{"id":"/litellm-routing-167","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-backend-has-to-match","content":"The `agent` lane deliberately carries the `openai/` provider prefix. `ollama_chat/`\nwould route those boxes through the Ollama-specific code path, and `api_base` has to\ninclude `/v1`."},"3081":{"id":"/litellm-routing-168","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"The Qwen2.5-Coder weights do not emit structured tool calls on this runtime."},"3082":{"id":"/litellm-routing-169","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"Measured against this box's IPEX-LLM Ollama, whose bundled `ollama` is 0.9.3."},"3083":{"id":"/litellm-routing-170","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"A request carrying `tools` for `qwen2.5-coder:32b` or `:14b` comes back as plain text,\n`finish_reason: \"stop\"`, and no `tool_calls` field at all."},"3084":{"id":"/litellm-routing-171","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"It behaves that way on both `/api/chat` and `/v1/chat/completions`."},"3085":{"id":"/litellm-routing-172","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"The model writes the JSON call into the message body, which no agent driver can consume."},"3086":{"id":"/litellm-routing-173","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"`qwen2.5:7b` on the same runtime does return a real `tool_calls` array."},"3087":{"id":"/litellm-routing-174","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-was-measured","content":"So the limitation tracks the model, not the runtime."},"3088":{"id":"/litellm-routing-175","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-agent-mode-needs","content":"Agent mode therefore needs either the Spark `agent` lane or the small `chat` model."},"3089":{"id":"/litellm-routing-176","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-agent-mode-needs","content":"Grok Build, Cline, Roo and Kilo all default to `agent`."},"3090":{"id":"/litellm-routing-177","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-agent-mode-needs","content":"`scripts/coder-agents.sh` registers `agent` (the default, with `chat` standing in when the\nSpark lane is dark), `agent-low`/`agent-medium`/`agent-xhigh`, `agent-swarm`, and `chat`\nas Coder Agents chat model configs, for the same reason: an agent turn without callable\ntools cannot browse or edit, so registering `coder` or `coder-fast` would only add a\nvisibly broken model to the pickers."},"3091":{"id":"/litellm-routing-178","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-agent-mode-needs","content":"Nine Spark aliases drive tools, so nine could be registered; only the five above are - the\nthinking aliases are there to make the level selectable from that picker, while\n`agent-explore` and `agent-review` answer a parent's dispatch rather than a person at the\ndropdown, so registering them would add two names nobody types."},"3092":{"id":"/litellm-routing-179","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-agent-mode-needs","content":"The two fast-compaction lanes are absent for a mechanical reason of the same kind: the hop\nkeys on the summary instruction the Grok CLI appends, and the aibridge behind this\ndropdown never sends one, so a chat on `agent-xhigh-fast` is a chat on `agent-xhigh`\nwearing a longer name."},"3093":{"id":"/litellm-routing-180","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#one-group-three-deployments","content":"Three deployments, one per Spark box, and no `order:` tier. A tier would make the\nlower boxes unreachable while any tier-1 box stayed healthy."},"3094":{"id":"/litellm-routing-181","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#one-group-three-deployments","content":"Spreading across every reachable box is the point of running three of them, five full\n262144-token streams each. Pinning only narrows the candidate list first."},"3095":{"id":"/litellm-routing-182","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#one-group-three-deployments","content":"One endpoint per box, one box per endpoint. Never point two deployments, or two\naliases, at the same physical machine: the proxy counts deployments, not machines."},"3096":{"id":"/litellm-routing-183","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"`least-busy` picks the deployment carrying the fewest in-flight requests out of a list\nthat some filter already made healthy. It has no health input of its own, and that is\nthe one thing to know before trusting it to spread load."},"3097":{"id":"/litellm-routing-184","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"Its counters are raised before the call (`router_strategy/least_busy.py:120`) and given\nback on the failure hook (`:129`, `:143`), so a box that refuses every request sits at\nzero -- and `_least_busy` (`:83`) returns the FIRST deployment at the minimum. A dead box\nlisted first in a group is therefore the preferred target, not the avoided one:\nunfiltered, `least-busy` prefers it over a healthy box."},"3098":{"id":"/litellm-routing-185","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"What pulls it out is the health filter that runs ahead of the strategy, which is the whole\nsubject of when a Spark box goes down."},"3099":{"id":"/litellm-routing-186","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"Its counters are per deployment and expire after a hardcoded 3600 s; there is no\n`routing_strategy_args` block to set, and `ttl` there would be a paste from newer docs."},"3100":{"id":"/litellm-routing-187","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"It decides only for unpinned traffic: the affinity pin below resolves first, and\n`least-busy` runs when nothing is pinned, when the pinned deployment is unhealthy or in\ncooldown, and for any request with no session id. Every `agent-swarm`,\n`agent-explore`, `agent-review` and `agent-swarm-fast` request is unpinned traffic,\nwhich is the whole of those four lanes."},"3101":{"id":"/litellm-routing-188","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"Health checks, cooldowns and those counters all attribute per deployment through\n`model_info.id`, which is why each box carries a unique id: `agent-spark-1`,\n`agent-spark-2`, `agent-spark-3`."},"3102":{"id":"/litellm-routing-189","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"Each thinking group, the swarm group, the two fan-out groups and the two fast groups carry\ntheir own triple - `agent-low-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-medium-spark-1/2/3`,\n`agent-xhigh-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-swarm-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-explore-spark-1/2/3`,\n`agent-review-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-xhigh-fast-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-swarm-fast-spark-1/2/3`"},"3103":{"id":"/litellm-routing-190","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"so the same physical box is a separate deployment, with its own health state and its own\n  in-flight counter, inside every group it belongs to."},"3104":{"id":"/litellm-routing-191","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"`compaction-fast` needs no triple: the Arc is one box and its single deployment is\n`compaction-fast-arc`."},"3105":{"id":"/litellm-routing-192","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-picker-least-busy","content":"A cooled box therefore stays visibly out of `healthy_deployments` instead of blending\ninto the group's aggregate stats."},"3106":{"id":"/litellm-routing-193","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"`session_affinity` sits above the picker, in `router_settings.optional_pre_call_checks`,\nand it arms the router's `DeploymentAffinityCheck`. Checked on LiteLLM 1.102.1."},"3107":{"id":"/litellm-routing-194","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"One conversation from one client sticks to the box that answered its first turn, for as\nlong as that box stays healthy."},"3108":{"id":"/litellm-routing-195","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"The pin idles out after 1 h (3600 s) without a request, and every request refreshes it.\nIt bounds idle time between requests, not conversation length."},"3109":{"id":"/litellm-routing-196","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"A conversation that goes quiet for longer than the TTL may move."},"3110":{"id":"/litellm-routing-197","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"A busy pinned box sheds its own overflow in its own scheduler instead of queueing\ninside the proxy."},"3111":{"id":"/litellm-routing-198","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-pin-session_affinity","content":"The trade is deliberate: stickiness buys prefix-cache locality and one predictable box\nfor the whole conversation, so one workspace's agent loop can sit on a busy box."},"3112":{"id":"/litellm-routing-199","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-this-lane-carries-no-pin","content":"The fifth Spark group, and the first of the four that carry no pin. Same\n`openai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` on the same three boxes, same baked `xhigh`, same tool-calling\nflags and 262144 window - the\ndifference is routing state only, so no pin resolves and every request goes to the global\n`least-busy` picker, landing on the healthy box with the fewest requests in flight."},"3113":{"id":"/litellm-routing-200","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"One key lifts the pin; apart from that key and the group's own deployment, retry-policy\nand fallback entries, nothing in the config distinguishes it from the five pinned lanes:"},"3114":{"id":"/litellm-routing-201","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"At the pinned `v1.102.1` tag that key is a real `Router.__init__` argument and is not in\n`ROUTER_SETTINGS_MANAGED_OUTSIDE_CONFIG`, so `config.yaml` reaches it, and its valid flags\nare exactly `deployment_affinity`, `responses_api_deployment_check`, `session_affinity`\nand `encrypted_content_affinity`."},"3115":{"id":"/litellm-routing-202","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"An entry REPLACES the global flag list for the group it names rather than adding to it, so\nthe empty list means no affinity check of any kind runs for `agent-swarm`. Every group\nabsent from the map keeps falling back to the global `[\"session_affinity\"]`, which is why\nthe five lanes a conversation rides still pin exactly as they did. Setting the key also\nself-arms the affinity callback, so those groups keep pinning."},"3116":{"id":"/litellm-routing-203","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"This key is the opt-out; a client header is not. An empty or short `x-litellm-session-id`\ndoes not skip the pin at this tag - that header is read verbatim at any length, and only\nthe generic `x-<vendor>-session-id` family is shape-checked - so a caller that tried to\nspread by sending an empty value would collapse every swarm request onto one shared pin."},"3117":{"id":"/litellm-routing-204","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"Two facts not to get wrong:"},"3118":{"id":"/litellm-routing-205","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"It has no pin, and that is what makes it the wrong home for a long single-thread\nconversation. Pinning buys prefix-cache locality; without it the next turn may be\nprefilled on a different box and pay prefill again. A chat, an orchestrator, or\nanything whose turns share a warm prefix belongs on `agent`. The lane is for\nindependent parallel work - subagents, batch edits, one-shot jobs, which is also why\nthe two reader lanes below lift the pin the same way."},"3119":{"id":"/litellm-routing-206","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"The spread is bought by removing a pin, not by adding a proxy queue or a cap. There is\nstill no `rpm`, `tpm` or `max_parallel_requests` anywhere in the config, and\n`queue_class`, `queue_class_config` and `enable_queue` do not exist at this tag. A\nsaturated box keeps shedding load in its own scheduler; the proxy parks nothing behind\nan in-memory semaphore."},"3120":{"id":"/litellm-routing-207","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-key-that-lifts-the-pin","content":"That is the arithmetic the lane exists for: 3 boxes x `PARALLEL` 5 full-length streams is\n15 concurrent streams, and a pinned workspace only ever reaches the 5 of the one box its\nkey resolves to."},"3121":{"id":"/litellm-routing-208","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-a-child-does-not-need-the-pin","content":"The sixth and seventh Spark groups, `agent-explore` and `agent-review`, lift the same pin\nthe swarm lane lifts, and for the same reason taken one step further: both serve a child\nthat answers once. The `explore` type and the seeded `explorer` agent dig for evidence and\nreturn a digest; `reviewer` and `security-auditor` read what landed and return findings."},"3122":{"id":"/litellm-routing-209","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-a-child-does-not-need-the-pin","content":"Neither carries a long warm prefix into a next turn, so the prefix-cache warmth the pin\nprotects is worth nothing here, while its cost is paid in full - the parent loop and every\nchild it spawns carry that workspace's one `x-litellm-session-id`, so a pinned wave of six\nresolves to a single deployment and waits on that box's `PARALLEL` admission slots while\nthe other two boxes sit reachable and under-offered."},"3123":{"id":"/litellm-routing-210","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-review-panel-is-a-wave-too","content":"That check is a panel of three skeptics dispatched in one turn - the requirements angle,\nthe proof angle that re-runs the producers' own `done:` commands, and the adversary angle -\neach riding `agent-review`, each owning no file, and each allowed up to three read-only\nmappers of its own under `max_depth` 2."},"3124":{"id":"/litellm-routing-211","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-review-panel-is-a-wave-too","content":"Three spawners with three mappers each is twelve of\nthe fifteen streams the fleet owns, which fits beside a parent still holding its own\nconversation, and the panel is cheap precisely because the writers have all landed by the\ntime it runs: the fleet is then idle, and both the skeptics and the mappers they spawn are\nunpinned traffic that `least-busy` can place on all three boxes at once."},"3125":{"id":"/litellm-routing-212","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-review-panel-is-a-wave-too","content":"The baked level is the only thing that separates them. An explore child is a lookup, so it\ntakes `low` and answers fast; a review child is the check that a landed claim is actually\ntrue, so it takes the `xhigh` `agent` itself carries. Each names itself with an empty flag\nlist beside the swarm lane's (`litellm/config.yaml:721-729`) and declares its own six-key\n`model_group_retry_policy` block, because a group inherits nothing from its siblings."},"3126":{"id":"/litellm-routing-213","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-lift-costs","content":"What the lift costs is what it costs the swarm lane, said plainly: a second turn of the\nsame conversation is not sticky, so it may be prefilled on a different box and pay prefill\nagain. For a child that answers once there is no second turn to pay for; point a\nconversation at these aliases and there is."},"3127":{"id":"/litellm-routing-214","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-lift-costs","content":"A long single-thread chat, an orchestrator, or anything whose turns share a warm\nprefix belongs on `agent`."},"3128":{"id":"/litellm-routing-215","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#rolling-one-lane-back-alone","content":"Each reader lane is the default for its own role and is set by its own template\nvariable, so either rolls back alone without moving the other or the writers'\n`agent-swarm` default:"},"3129":{"id":"/litellm-routing-216","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#rolling-one-lane-back-alone","content":"| Lane            | Role it carries                                       | Default         | `--var` that puts it back on a pinned lane                                                                 |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-explore` | the built-in `explore` type and the seeded `explorer` | `agent-explore` | `--var grok_explore_lane=agent-low` keeps the level and the pin; `=agent` sends mapping work at full depth |","table":"table-1"},"3130":{"id":"/litellm-routing-217","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#rolling-one-lane-back-alone","content":"| Lane           | Role it carries                                                                                         | Default        | `--var` that puts it back on a pinned lane                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `agent-review` | the seeded `reviewer` and `security-auditor`, which carry the independent review of a multi-file change | `agent-review` | `--var grok_review_lane=agent-xhigh` keeps the level and the pin; `=agent` matches the parent exactly |","table":"table-1"},"3131":{"id":"/litellm-routing-218","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"The variables are declared in `templates/workspace/coder.tf:24-52` and its devcontainer\ntwin, and they are what fills `[subagents.models]` in\n`templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl`. The fan-out width rides a different variable\nand does not follow any of these three: it is `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`'s own\nshipped 15."},"3132":{"id":"/litellm-routing-219","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"`main.tf` renders that through\n`grok_subagent_max_concurrent = var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent != null ? var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent : var.grok_swarm_width`,\nand the `: var.grok_swarm_width` arm of the ternary answers only a caller that passes null\non purpose - the quote is the opt-in, not the source of the width."},"3133":{"id":"/litellm-routing-220","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"`grok_swarm_width` (default 15) is the fleet's own ceiling, rendered as the\n`# fleet-width:` line beside `max_concurrent`."},"3134":{"id":"/litellm-routing-221","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"The lane decides placement, not width - what a pinned lane changes is where those 15\nland, and one box only ever admits `PARALLEL` (5) of them."},"3135":{"id":"/litellm-routing-222","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"The workspace side of that seam is\ngrok-build-and-agents.md."},"3136":{"id":"/litellm-routing-223","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"A contributor home names the same three lanes with `GROK_EXPLORE_LANE`, `GROK_PLAN_LANE`\nand `GROK_REVIEW_LANE` for `//scripts:seed-dev-env`."},"3137":{"id":"/litellm-routing-224","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-lane-variables-live","content":"Neither lane is registered as a Coder Agents chat model, so a pin is the only way onto\neither one."},"3138":{"id":"/litellm-routing-225","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fast-compaction-lanes-agent-xhigh-fast-and-agent-swarm-fast","content":"The eighth and ninth Spark groups, and the only two that ask the proxy to answer one of\ntheir calls somewhere else."},"3139":{"id":"/litellm-routing-226","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fast-compaction-lanes-agent-xhigh-fast-and-agent-swarm-fast","content":"Everything else about each is its parent: `agent-xhigh-fast` is\n`agent-xhigh` - three equal `openai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` deployments, `xhigh` baked, the\nsession pin kept - and `agent-swarm-fast` is `agent-swarm`, the same three boxes with the\npin lifted for it alone among the new lanes."},"3140":{"id":"/litellm-routing-227","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fast-compaction-lanes-agent-xhigh-fast-and-agent-swarm-fast","content":"The nine Spark lane groups are now\n`agent agent-low agent-medium agent-xhigh agent-swarm agent-explore agent-review\nagent-xhigh-fast agent-swarm-fast`, plus the Arc group `compaction-fast`."},"3141":{"id":"/litellm-routing-228","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"What the hop is: on those two aliases only, the proxy recognises the CLI's\nconversation-summary call and re-serves it from somewhere cheaper than the Spark box it\narrived on - `compaction-fast`, the small Ollama-served coding weight on the Arc, when the\nsummary fits that window, and a Spark group thinking at `low` when it does not."},"3142":{"id":"/litellm-routing-229","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"That is where the speed comes from - the Spark lane answers at xhigh thinking and a\nsummary does not need it."},"3143":{"id":"/litellm-routing-230","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"The CLI appends its summary instruction as the last turn of the body - the\nauto-compaction ask, or the `/compact` one wrapped in a `<summary_request>` tag - and the\ncallback matches a stable clause inside whichever one it sees,\n`produce a faithful, concise summary of the conversation so far` and\n`summarize the conversation so far`, in a turn short enough to be the instruction itself."},"3144":{"id":"/litellm-routing-231","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"It reads that ask nowhere else in the body: the system prompt rides every turn of the\nsession, so matching there would move a whole conversation to the summary target the moment\nan operator pasted one of those sentences into a workspace rulebook."},"3145":{"id":"/litellm-routing-232","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"It reads it from whichever key the protocol carries the turns under - `messages` for\nChat Completions and Anthropic Messages, `input` for a model whose `api_backend` is\n`responses` - so the hop does not quietly stop working on a protocol choice."},"3146":{"id":"/litellm-routing-233","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"A recognized ask is\nrewritten to the target model, with `tools`, `tool_choice` and `reasoning_effort` dropped\nfrom it: a summary is prose, the schemas are dead weight to it, and a small model handed a\ntool schema may answer with a call instead of a summary."},"3147":{"id":"/litellm-routing-234","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"Every other call of the same conversation stays on its Spark box, and a session on any\nother alias compacts exactly as it always has."},"3148":{"id":"/litellm-routing-235","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"The hop is a property of the alias, not of the proxy: picking one of these\ntwo aliases is the opt-in, and `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION=0` is the kill switch beside it."},"3149":{"id":"/litellm-routing-236","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-hop-is","content":"One residue is worth naming: a user turn whose entire content is a quoted ask looks like an ask,\nand gets the summary target's answer."},"3150":{"id":"/litellm-routing-237","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#it-is-not-a-client-setting","content":"What it is not: a client setting. The Grok Build CLI has no compaction-model key, so\nthere is nothing in `~/.grok/config.toml` that points that call anywhere, and\n`[models] session_summary` is not the compaction lane either - it serves titles and the\nsession recap."},"3151":{"id":"/litellm-routing-238","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#it-is-not-a-client-setting","content":"The whole remedy therefore lives server-side, and the measurement behind it\nis the `compact failed: exceeded wall-clock budget 300s` section of\ntroubleshooting.md."},"3152":{"id":"/litellm-routing-239","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-extra-config-is-worth-it","content":"Why the extra config is worth it: compactions that did succeed on the Spark lane took 107 s\nto 1915 s, and 18 of the 36 sampled successes ran past the CLI's 300 s wall-clock budget -\nthey are the summaries that budget was discarding."},"3153":{"id":"/litellm-routing-240","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-extra-config-is-worth-it","content":"What the hop changes without a stopwatch\nis who answers: a 14B Arc weight with no thinking level and no schemas in the prompt, rather\nthan a Spark box thinking at xhigh over the same request with its tool schemas attached."},"3154":{"id":"/litellm-routing-241","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#why-the-extra-config-is-worth-it","content":"No timing has been measured on the hop yet, so no speed-up figure is quoted here for either\ntier; `docs/troubleshooting.md` names the one log line that shows it firing, and that line\nis where a measurement starts."},"3155":{"id":"/litellm-routing-242","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-tier-answers-and-what-caps-the-guard","content":"Which tier answers: the guard is `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT` (default 24000), and\nit picks a tier rather than ending the hop."},"3156":{"id":"/litellm-routing-243","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-tier-answers-and-what-caps-the-guard","content":"Below it the summary goes to `compaction-fast`,\nwhich is the right place for it, because those weights answer inside a 32768-token window\nand Ollama clamps an over-long input instead of refusing it - a summary pushed in over that\ncomes back quietly truncated, and a truncated summary is worse than the slower one it would replace."},"3157":{"id":"/litellm-routing-244","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-tier-answers-and-what-caps-the-guard","content":"That window is also the ceiling the guard cannot raise past: the fork happens at the\nsmaller of `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT` and the `max_input_tokens` `config.yaml`\ndeclares for the Arc target group, so `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT=100000` forks at\n32768 and logs one `compaction router: EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT=100000 is above\nthe 32768 tokens config.yaml declares for 'compaction-fast'; forking at the declared window\ninstead` line."},"3158":{"id":"/litellm-routing-245","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-tier-answers-and-what-caps-the-guard","content":"The declared window is a fact about the weights and the pinned LiteLLM has no\ncontext-window check between the hook and Ollama, so a knob cannot reach past it; a target\ngroup that declares no window leaves the guard whole, and prints one\n`compaction router: 'compaction-fast' declares no max_input_tokens in config.yaml; forking at\nEVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT alone` line rather than failing quietly."},"3159":{"id":"/litellm-routing-246","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"Above it the summary goes to `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` (default\n`agent-low`): the same three Spark boxes, the 262144-token window a real summary needs, and\nthe thinking baked to `low` instead of `xhigh`."},"3160":{"id":"/litellm-routing-247","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"Blank that knob, or name the lane the call\narrived on, and an oversized summary stays where it is, which is the pre-hop behaviour."},"3161":{"id":"/litellm-routing-248","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"The estimate is counted over everything the backend prefills - each turn's text, the\npayloads the text flattener cannot see, and every request-level schema key - and it\ncharges three classes of character separately:"},"3162":{"id":"/litellm-routing-249","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"ASCII prose at four characters to a token"},"3163":{"id":"/litellm-routing-250","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"a base64 payload at two"},"3164":{"id":"/litellm-routing-251","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"anything outside ASCII at one"},"3165":{"id":"/litellm-routing-252","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"Reading those denser classes at the prose rate was\nhow a 90,000-character screenshot read as 22,500 tokens and went to a 32768-token model."},"3166":{"id":"/litellm-routing-253","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-spark-tier-and-the-token-estimate","content":"Every one of them errs toward the larger number, and the larger number means the Spark tier."},"3167":{"id":"/litellm-routing-254","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-guard-sits-against-the-client","content":"Where the guard sits against the client: the shipped `[session]` block sets\n`auto_compact_threshold_percent = 70` and both fast aliases declare a `context_window` of\n262144 (`templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl:387`, and `:284` and `:301` for the two\naliases), so a session on either one reaches its auto-compaction at about 183,500 tokens -\nover seven times the guard."},"3168":{"id":"/litellm-routing-255","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-guard-sits-against-the-client","content":"A summary that size cannot be read faithfully by a 32768-token\nmodel, so the Arc tier was never going to serve it and the guard is what stops it trying: on\nthat estimate the call goes to `agent-low`, which keeps the window and drops the baked\n`xhigh` thinking."},"3169":{"id":"/litellm-routing-256","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-the-guard-sits-against-the-client","content":"Pointing `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_TARGET` at `agent-low` is the lever that\ncovers a full-size summary even with the limit left alone, and it is a routing choice with\nits own trade, not a free win: the summary is still a Spark call, holding a stream on a box\nthe writers want, at a thinking level turned down from the one the lane exists to bake."},"3170":{"id":"/litellm-routing-257","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fallback-on-the-spark-tier","content":"The known limit on that tier is its fallback, and it is the stack's standing one: every\nSpark group's last resort is the Arc, so `agent-low: [\"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:862`, and the same shape under `agent-xhigh-fast: [\"agent-xhigh\",\n\"coder\"]` and `agent-swarm-fast: [\"agent-swarm\", \"coder\"]`) means that when all three Sparks\nare cooled an oversized summary lands on `coder` - a 32768-token group - and is answered\nfrom a truncated reading, which is the outcome the fork exists to prevent."},"3171":{"id":"/litellm-routing-258","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fallback-on-the-spark-tier","content":"Nothing here makes that worse: the pair's own chains end at `coder` too, and so does\n`compaction-fast: [\"agent-low\", \"coder\"]`. The fork changes who tries first."},"3172":{"id":"/litellm-routing-259","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fallback-on-the-spark-tier","content":"What an operator holds is the choice of who tries second: blank\n`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` to leave the summary on the lane it arrived on,\npoint it at another Spark group, or edit the fallback list beside it in the same routing\nfile."},"3173":{"id":"/litellm-routing-260","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-fallback-on-the-spark-tier","content":"When the Sparks are unreachable the answer is the\none every agent lane already has - the working degraded mode is `chat`."},"3174":{"id":"/litellm-routing-261","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-has-been-measured-so-far","content":"What has been measured is the old path, not the new one. The 107 s to 1915 s spread and\nthe 18 abandoned successes above are both from the Spark lane before the hop existed,\nswept out of the session logs in troubleshooting.md."},"3175":{"id":"/litellm-routing-262","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-has-been-measured-so-far","content":"Neither tier has a timing of its own yet: the hop has not served a summary on a running\nstack, so no speed-up figure is claimed for either one."},"3176":{"id":"/litellm-routing-263","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-has-been-measured-so-far","content":"`tests/python/test_compaction_router.py` proves which group each\nrequest shape lands on; the operator's own log line is what will prove what it costs."},"3177":{"id":"/litellm-routing-264","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"Everything a caller can tune is one of five environment variables, read in\n`litellm/compaction_router.py` and nowhere else, which makes the litellm service's\n`environment:` block in `docker-compose.yml` the whole policy:"},"3178":{"id":"/litellm-routing-265","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"| Knob                     | Default                            | What flipping it does                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION` | on; `0`, `false`, `off` disable it | the kill switch - off, every call of every lane stays where its alias routes it |","table":"table-2"},"3179":{"id":"/litellm-routing-266","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"| Knob                           | Default                             | What flipping it does                                  |\n| ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_LANES` | `agent-xhigh-fast,agent-swarm-fast` | which groups may hop; name one to narrow the hop to it |","table":"table-2"},"3180":{"id":"/litellm-routing-267","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"| Knob                            | Default           | What flipping it does                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_TARGET` | `compaction-fast` | the model group a summary under the guard is moved to; a name that is no `model_name:` in `config.yaml` is refused and the call stays put |","table":"table-2"},"3181":{"id":"/litellm-routing-268","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"| Knob                                 | Default | What flipping it does                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT` | `24000` | the token estimate that decides which of the two tiers takes the call; a ceiling this module may lower and never raise, because the Arc target group's own `max_input_tokens` caps it and logs one line when it does |","table":"table-2"},"3182":{"id":"/litellm-routing-269","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-five-knobs","content":"| Knob                                  | Default     | What flipping it does                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` | `agent-low` | where a summary above the guard goes, checked against `config.yaml` the same way; blank it, or name the lane it arrived on, and it stays there |","table":"table-2"},"3183":{"id":"/litellm-routing-270","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"Three ways to land this feature and get nothing."},"3184":{"id":"/litellm-routing-271","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"The first is caught for you at the pinned\nLiteLLM and the other two are silent, which is why the silent two are what the gates check:"},"3185":{"id":"/litellm-routing-272","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"`litellm_settings.callbacks` must name the *instance*,\n`compaction_router.proxy_handler_instance`, never the class. `ProxyLogging` dispatches\n`async_pre_call_hook` only to a callback that IS a `CustomLogger` and overrides that hook\nin its own class dict."},"3186":{"id":"/litellm-routing-273","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"At the pinned `v1.102.1` a class entry fails loudly:\n`litellm/proxy/common_utils/callback_utils.py` maps it to a `ValueError` that names\n`proxy_handler_instance` and the config does not load."},"3187":{"id":"/litellm-routing-274","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"That check is recent, so the older wording you may find in a comment - a class boots\nclean, the lanes keep working, the hop never fires - describes what it used to do."},"3188":{"id":"/litellm-routing-275","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"The module is mounted as a single file,\n`./litellm/compaction_router.py:/app/compaction_router.py:ro`. A directory mount over\n`/app` hides `config.yaml` beside it, and it has to sit in the same directory as the\nconfig file because that is the directory the proxy resolves a callback's dotted name\nagainst - the bare module name in\n`callbacks` resolves no other way."},"3189":{"id":"/litellm-routing-276","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#three-ways-to-land-it-and-get-nothing","content":"A new group inherits neither the retry policy nor the affinity lift. Both fast lanes\ndeclare their own six-key `model_group_retry_policy` block, and only `agent-swarm-fast`\njoins `model_group_affinity_config` with `[]`; `agent-xhigh-fast` is absent from that map\non purpose, so it keeps falling back to the global `[\"session_affinity\"]` and stays\npinned like its parent. That one key is the whole difference between the pinned twin and\nthe spread one."},"3190":{"id":"/litellm-routing-277","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-carries-a-session-id","content":"A value has to look like an id to count: alphanumerics, hyphens or underscores, 8\ncharacters or more."},"3191":{"id":"/litellm-routing-278","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-carries-a-session-id","content":"The sources, in order, are `x-litellm-trace-id`, then\n`x-litellm-session-id`, then any `x-<vendor>-session-id`, then\n`session-id`/`session_id`/`thread-id`/`conversation_id` (Codex style), then W3C\ntraceparent and baggage, plus `metadata.session_id` in the body."},"3192":{"id":"/litellm-routing-279","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-carries-a-session-id","content":"The Grok CLI forwards `extra_headers` verbatim."},"3193":{"id":"/litellm-routing-280","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-carries-a-session-id","content":"Both workspace templates render `x-litellm-session-id = \"ws-<workspace-uuid>\"` under\n`[models]` in `~/.grok/config.toml`, so one key covers every conversation of a\nworkspace, subagent calls included."},"3194":{"id":"/litellm-routing-281","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-carries-a-session-id","content":"In `shared` profile mode that is one file per workspace, re-rendered on that workspace's own\nstart, so two workspaces of one owner can carry different renders of that key."},"3195":{"id":"/litellm-routing-282","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-floats-freely","content":"Cline and Roo editor traffic carries no session id: the extension settings have no\ncustom-header field."},"3196":{"id":"/litellm-routing-283","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-floats-freely","content":"Coder Agents chats carry none either. Coder's aibridge forwards model calls with the\nprovider key only and adds no per-conversation session id."},"3197":{"id":"/litellm-routing-284","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-floats-freely","content":"Both float across the healthy boxes by load."},"3198":{"id":"/litellm-routing-285","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#when-a-pinned-box-cools-or-goes-unhealthy","content":"That request routes elsewhere, to whichever box `least-busy` picks."},"3199":{"id":"/litellm-routing-286","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#when-a-pinned-box-cools-or-goes-unhealthy","content":"The pin itself is kept."},"3200":{"id":"/litellm-routing-287","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#when-a-pinned-box-cools-or-goes-unhealthy","content":"The conversation goes back to the box once it is healthy again."},"3201":{"id":"/litellm-routing-288","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"The health filter does, and it is the only mechanism that can."},"3202":{"id":"/litellm-routing-289","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"Selection on the chat-completion path runs `async_get_available_deployment` (`router.py:13041`) ->\n`async_get_healthy_deployments` (`router.py:12700`) ->\n`_async_filter_health_check_unhealthy_deployments` (`router.py:14137`), and that last\ncall is a no-op unless `enable_health_check_routing` is set in `general_settings:`\n(`router.py:14153`)."},"3203":{"id":"/litellm-routing-290","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"That is the key the config turns on for exactly this job."},"3204":{"id":"/litellm-routing-291","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"Cooldown cannot do it, and that is not a tuning question. `_is_cooldown_required`\nreturns False as soon as the exception text contains `APIConnectionError`\n(`litellm/router_utils/cooldown_handlers.py:223`, `ignored_strings`)."},"3205":{"id":"/litellm-routing-292","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"A refused connection, a dead engine, and a TensorFold `NoRoom` refusal all surface as\nthat exception, so the failure that most needs a box pulled is the one the cooldown path\nis written to skip."},"3206":{"id":"/litellm-routing-293","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"The probe loop writes the health state (`proxy_server.py:3981`)\n*before* that veto can reach the same exception: the write sits behind the guard at\n`proxy_server.py:3965` and above the routing-only bail at `proxy_server.py:3988-3989`,\nso the mark is there whether or not the cooldown loop below it ever runs, which is why\nthe filter marks what cooldown never marks."},"3207":{"id":"/litellm-routing-294","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"Three settings switch the filter off, and the config avoids all three:"},"3208":{"id":"/litellm-routing-295","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"`enable_health_check_routing` off"},"3209":{"id":"/litellm-routing-296","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"`health_check_interval` unset or <= 0, which returns from the probe loop before it ever\nstarts (`proxy_server.py:4071`)"},"3210":{"id":"/litellm-routing-297","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"a router-wide `allowed_fails_policy` with `background_health_check_model_groups` unset\n(`router.py:14161`)"},"3211":{"id":"/litellm-routing-298","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-actually-removes-it","content":"That last one is why `router_settings:` carries no\n`allowed_fails_policy` anywhere, and why one added there for an unrelated reason would\nquietly disable the filter that keeps a dead box out of `least-busy`."},"3212":{"id":"/litellm-routing-299","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"With `allowed_fails` gone, cooldown uses the vendor's rate rule\n(`cooldown_handlers.py:392-398`), guarded at `:395`: cool a deployment once it fails\nmore than `DEFAULT_FAILURE_THRESHOLD_PERCENT` (0.5, `constants.py:69`) of at least\n`DEFAULT_FAILURE_THRESHOLD_MINIMUM_REQUESTS` (5, `constants.py:131`) requests in a rolling minute."},"3213":{"id":"/litellm-routing-300","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"The counting branch is the `else` one line below at `:404-405`,\nreached only when a router-wide policy is set or `allowed_fails` carries a\nnon-default number (`:363-366`), and this file names neither."},"3214":{"id":"/litellm-routing-301","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"`SINGLE_DEPLOYMENT_TRAFFIC_FAILURE_THRESHOLD` is 1000, so the \"all\nrequests failed\" arm never fires at this fleet's volume."},"3215":{"id":"/litellm-routing-302","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"That is the rule doing what cooldown was always the right tool for: a box that answers\nbadly - a 500, a timeout, a malformed completion - is parked for `cooldown_time`, 60 s,\nand comes back on its own. The same 60 s is the period the probe loop cools a deployment\nits previous cycle marked unhealthy (`proxy_server.py:4013`,\n`time_to_cooldown=router.cooldown_time`, `:4018`); with routing on, that path runs now,\nwhere it used to return early."},"3216":{"id":"/litellm-routing-303","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"That 60 s is not confined to the probe path."},"3217":{"id":"/litellm-routing-304","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-cooldown_time-60-is-for-now","content":"Both paths read the one `cooldown_time`\nknob, so raising it off the 5 s default (`constants.py:75`) widens every group's\nexclusion, the three-deployment Spark groups included: a box that fails 3 of 5\nrequests in a minute now sits out for a minute\ninstead of 5 s, and a minute without one of three boxes moves a session pin that was\nwarm there."},"3218":{"id":"/litellm-routing-305","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"Detection is one sweep plus the interval, not the interval alone: the probe loop sleeps\n`health_check_interval` *after* a sweep finishes (`proxy_server.py:4234`) rather than\nfiring on a clock."},"3219":{"id":"/litellm-routing-306","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"A sweep is the 27 deployments that did not opt out pushed through\nthe `health_check_concurrency: 2` gate - the sweep drops every deployment carrying\n`model_info.disable_background_health_check` (`proxy_server.py:4116-4118`), which is\nfour of the 31 - so the wait before a box is re-probed is one full sweep plus 120 s."},"3220":{"id":"/litellm-routing-307","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"Recovery needs no operator and no restart."},"3221":{"id":"/litellm-routing-308","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"A green probe overwrites the mark with\n`is_healthy: True` (`health_check.py:683`), so a box is eligible again on the first\nprobe that succeeds after it comes back - no request has to fail first to rediscover it."},"3222":{"id":"/litellm-routing-309","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"That is eligible, not proven serving: the same loop cooled what it marked\n(`proxy_server.py:4013`), and that cooldown entry has to expire on its own clock, so\nthe first turn back can still land on another box."},"3223":{"id":"/litellm-routing-310","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"The bound on that state is `health_check_staleness_threshold: 900`, and the filter fails\nopen: it returns the whole candidate list:"},"3224":{"id":"/litellm-routing-311","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"when the health state is missing"},"3225":{"id":"/litellm-routing-312","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"when it is older than that threshold"},"3226":{"id":"/litellm-routing-313","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"when filtering would leave no candidate at all So a fleet whose probe state has gone\nstale routes to every box rather than to none - a stale sweep costs the filter, never\nthe traffic."},"3227":{"id":"/litellm-routing-314","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"The threshold is set explicitly because the\nshipped default is `DEFAULT_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL * 2` = 600 s whatever\n`health_check_interval` says (`router.py:993`); left at the default it would not track\nthe 120 s interval this config asks for."},"3228":{"id":"/litellm-routing-315","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"A restart of the proxy is itself a fail-open condition, and it is not logged."},"3229":{"id":"/litellm-routing-316","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#how-long-it-takes-and-how-it-comes-back","content":"No Redis is configured for this proxy, so the marks live in one process\n(`router_utils/health_state_cache.py:32-36`) and every restart or redeploy clears\nthem until the first sweep finishes; the filter has no log line on any of its\nfail-open exits, so nothing proves that window happened while it is open."},"3230":{"id":"/litellm-routing-317","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"The filter sits on the chat-completion selection path."},"3231":{"id":"/litellm-routing-318","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"The image, audio, embedding and rerank paths select through\n`_async_get_healthy_deployments` (`router.py:8554`), which applies the cooldown filter\nand the blocked flag only - a dead box stays a candidate there."},"3232":{"id":"/litellm-routing-319","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"This fleet serves chat and streaming completions, so the limit is honest rather\nthan load-bearing, but it is the reason a new modality on these aliases needs its own\nlook before anyone calls it covered."},"3233":{"id":"/litellm-routing-320","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"What covers a request already in flight is unchanged by this work and predates it:"},"3234":{"id":"/litellm-routing-321","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"the two attempts the retry chain allows (`num_retries: 2` in `litellm_settings`, and\n`DefaultRetries: 2` inside each Spark lane's `model_group_retry_policy` block)"},"3235":{"id":"/litellm-routing-322","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"the rest of that per-group policy"},"3236":{"id":"/litellm-routing-323","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"the `fallbacks` chains"},"3237":{"id":"/litellm-routing-324","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#what-the-filter-does-not-cover","content":"The filter changes where a retry lands, not whether the turn is retried."},"3238":{"id":"/litellm-routing-325","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"The `litellm:` service in `docker-compose.yml` carries a `healthcheck:` block beside\nthese router settings, and it is a different check on a different thing: it asks whether\nthe proxy process answers, not whether a Spark box does."},"3239":{"id":"/litellm-routing-326","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"Its `test:` is the JSON-array form invoking the image's own `/app/.venv/bin/python3` -\nthe image ships no `curl` and no `wget` - at a one-line `urllib` request to\n`http://127.0.0.1:4000/health/liveliness` with `timeout=5`, exiting 0 only on a 200,\nwith `interval: 30s`, `timeout: 10s`, `retries: 3`, and `start_period: 60s` to cover the\nboot that imports the config and builds 31 deployments before uvicorn binds."},"3240":{"id":"/litellm-routing-327","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"`/health/liveliness` is the endpoint because it is unprotected and answers `I'm alive!`,\nwhile `/health` sits behind `user_api_key_auth`\n(`health_endpoints/_health_endpoints.py:1938` and `:1110`) and a probe on\nit would need the master key in the container's own command line."},"3241":{"id":"/litellm-routing-328","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"What it does not do: the compose daemon restarts a container that *exits*, not one that\ngoes unhealthy."},"3242":{"id":"/litellm-routing-329","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"`restart: unless-stopped` stays the only thing that recovers a crashed\nproxy, and this probe buys visibility instead - `dev-stack status` and\n`docker compose ps` print (unhealthy), `docker inspect` carries the last three probes,\nand the log tag ships the event to Loki."},"3243":{"id":"/litellm-routing-330","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-containers-own-probe","content":"It also buys a `service_healthy` wait that\nnothing here takes: `hermes` keeps `depends_on: litellm: condition: service_started`\ndeliberately, because compose waits indefinitely for a healthy condition and a probe that\nstopped passing would hold the host assistant down with the proxy."},"3244":{"id":"/litellm-routing-331","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallback-the-spark-lanes-to-coder","content":"When every Spark box is down, `router_settings.fallbacks` degrades `agent` straight to\n`coder`, which is text-only."},"3245":{"id":"/litellm-routing-332","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallback-the-spark-lanes-to-coder","content":"Chat stays usable while agent mode quietly loses its tools. That is the point of the\nhop, not an accident."},"3246":{"id":"/litellm-routing-333","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#fallback-the-spark-lanes-to-coder","content":"Each thinking alias carries the same hop of its own - `agent-low: [\"coder\"]`, and the\nsame for `agent-medium` and `agent-xhigh`. Groups are independent, so none of them\ninherits `agent`'s entry, and the five pinned lanes go down with the same boxes."},"3247":{"id":"/litellm-routing-334","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"`agent-swarm` degrades one step further: `agent-swarm: [\"agent\", \"coder\"]`. Health\nstate, cooldowns and in-flight counters are per group, so its own three deployments can\nall be cooled while the same boxes are still healthy under `agent`; `agent` is tried\nfirst, where `least-busy` may still have a box to pick, and Arc `coder` stays the last\nresort it is for every other Spark lane. The chain is acyclic: agent-swarm -> agent ->\ncoder, and `coder` declares no hop of its own."},"3248":{"id":"/litellm-routing-335","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"The two fan-out lanes degrade the way the swarm lane does, one step further than the\npinned lanes, and each hops through the lane that bakes its own level:"},"3249":{"id":"/litellm-routing-336","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"`agent-explore: [\"agent-low\", \"coder\"]` and `agent-review: [\"agent-xhigh\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:882-883`)."},"3250":{"id":"/litellm-routing-337","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"The extra step is worth taking for the same reason - these groups' own three\ndeployments can all be cooling while the same boxes are healthy under the pinned alias,\nsince health state and cooldowns are kept per group - and the hop is chosen so a parent\nthat dispatched an explore child at `low` gets a `low` answer from the fallback rather\nthan an `xhigh` it did not ask for."},"3251":{"id":"/litellm-routing-338","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"Both chains are acyclic and end at `coder`: agent-explore -> agent-low -> coder,\nagent-review -> agent-xhigh -> coder, and neither fallback lane names a lane that hops\nback here."},"3252":{"id":"/litellm-routing-339","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"Each fast lane hops to the lane it is the twin of:\n`- agent-xhigh-fast: [\"agent-xhigh\", \"coder\"]` and\n`- agent-swarm-fast: [\"agent-swarm\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:887-888`). Same boxes, same baked level, same pin behaviour, so a\nsession that lost its own group keeps everything except that group's routing state. Both\nchains are acyclic and end at `coder` like every other here: agent-xhigh-fast ->\nagent-xhigh -> coder, agent-swarm-fast -> agent-swarm -> coder."},"3253":{"id":"/litellm-routing-340","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"`compaction-fast` degrades to a Spark rather than to another Arc alias -\n`- compaction-fast: [\"agent-low\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:893`) - and that direction is the point."},"3254":{"id":"/litellm-routing-341","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"`coder`, `coder-fast` and `compaction-fast` all answer from the one Ollama container\non the Arc, so a hop between them is a hop to whatever is already down. `agent-low` is\nthe quickest answer the fleet has, which is what a summary was after on this lane in\nthe first place."},"3255":{"id":"/litellm-routing-342","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-per-lane-fallback-chains","content":"Acyclic: compaction-fast -> agent-low -> coder. It is the one chain here that a user\nnever picks: it belongs to the group the callback moves traffic to, not to an alias\nanyone types."},"3256":{"id":"/litellm-routing-343","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#history-caps-and-what-is-deliberately-absent","content":"It used to be a chain, `agent -> agent-fast -> coder`. `agent-fast` was a second alias\nfor the same model on a second box with a lower output ceiling; one group of three equal\ndeployments already covers every reachable box, so the chain collapsed to one acyclic\nhop."},"3257":{"id":"/litellm-routing-344","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#history-caps-and-what-is-deliberately-absent","content":"If a concurrency cap is ever reintroduced, its pairing is `fallbacks` plus\n`context_window_fallbacks`. Both, not one."},"3258":{"id":"/litellm-routing-345","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#history-caps-and-what-is-deliberately-absent","content":"There are no rpm, tpm or `max_parallel_requests` caps anywhere, on purpose. A cap parks\nrequests behind an in-memory semaphore inside the proxy; without one, a fully offered\nbox sheds load in its own scheduler."},"3259":{"id":"/litellm-routing-346","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-agent-backend-card","content":"The dashboard's **Agent backend** card exists to surface exactly that failure."},"3260":{"id":"/litellm-routing-347","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-agent-backend-card","content":"Its per-box widgets go to error state while `agent` still answers, because `agent`\nanswers from the Arc while every Spark is down."},"3261":{"id":"/litellm-routing-348","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-agent-backend-card","content":"The card and its per-box widgets read `AGENT_MODEL_URL` and `SPARKn_HEALTH_URL` from\n`.env`, and compose builds both from the box's `SPARKn_HOST` plus `SPARK_HTTP_PORT`,\nso a card follows the hostname you set once and they answer without a key."},"3262":{"id":"/litellm-routing-349","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-box-answered","content":"The `x-litellm-model-id` response header names the deployment that answered."},"3263":{"id":"/litellm-routing-350","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-box-answered","content":"With a pin, it names the pinned box; without one, whichever box `least-busy` picked."},"3264":{"id":"/litellm-routing-351","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-box-answered","content":"The proxy's own `/health` lists every deployment, so trust it over the absence of\nboot errors."},"3265":{"id":"/litellm-routing-352","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#which-box-answered","content":"A wrong model id does not crash the proxy: 1.102.1 builds the Router with\n`ignore_invalid_deployments` forced to True, so a bad id drops that deployment at boot\nwith one log line and later surfaces as \"No deployments available\"."},"3266":{"id":"/litellm-routing-353","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-measured-burst","content":"Measured on a harness boot of this config against the live Spark boxes, before\n`session_affinity` existed."},"3267":{"id":"/litellm-routing-354","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-measured-burst","content":"That 30-request burst was multi-session, fan-out-style traffic."},"3268":{"id":"/litellm-routing-355","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-measured-burst","content":"It spread 12/10/8 across the three deployments and returned 30x 200."},"3269":{"id":"/litellm-routing-356","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-measured-burst","content":"With no concurrency cap configured, the proxy neither queued nor shed inside itself,\nand a fully offered box absorbed the overflow in its own scheduler."},"3270":{"id":"/litellm-routing-357","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-measured-burst","content":"A single conversation pinned to one box now keeps its streams on that box while it\nstays healthy - that is the behaviour the burst predates."},"3271":{"id":"/litellm-routing-358","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#editing-an-alias","content":"Edit `litellm/config.yaml`."},"3272":{"id":"/litellm-routing-359","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#editing-an-alias","content":"Restart the proxy on the stack you changed, so it re-reads that file."},"3273":{"id":"/litellm-routing-360","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#editing-an-alias","content":"Check that `SPARK_1_API_KEY`, `SPARK_2_API_KEY` and `SPARK_3_API_KEY` are still\nnon-empty. An empty key fails every request inside the proxy, before it ever reaches\nthe box."},"3274":{"id":"/litellm-routing-361","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#restart-the-proxy-first","content":"Order matters when an alias is new rather than changed: the proxy reads\n`litellm/config.yaml` at boot and a workspace renders its catalog from that file when it\nstarts, so restart the proxy first and boot the workspace after it."},"3275":{"id":"/litellm-routing-362","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#restart-the-proxy-first","content":"A workspace older than the proxy asks for an alias the config does not have, and the\nrouter answers \"No deployments available\" rather than falling back."},"3276":{"id":"/litellm-routing-363","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#restart-the-proxy-first","content":"The rollback is one variable per lane, and\nit does not need the proxy at all: `--var grok_subagents_lane=agent` re-pins the writers to\none box, and `--var grok_explore_lane=agent-low` and `--var grok_review_lane=agent` put each\nreader role back on a pinned alias that every config version already carries."},"3277":{"id":"/litellm-routing-364","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#restart-the-proxy-first","content":"Neither stack runner has a `restart` subcommand (`up`, `down`, `status`, `logs`, `reset`\nare the whole set), so the proxy restart stays a direct compose call. Stable stack:"},"3278":{"id":"/litellm-routing-365","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#restart-the-proxy-first","content":"The dev sandbox takes the same restart with its own project name and env file:"},"3279":{"id":"/litellm-routing-366","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"`scripts/coder-agents.sh` registers `agent` (the default, with `chat` standing in when\nthe Spark lane is dark), `agent-low`/`agent-medium`/`agent-xhigh`, `agent-swarm`, and\n`chat` as the Coder Agents chat model configs, through `CODER_AGENTS_PROVIDER_URL`\n(default `http://litellm:4000/v1`). `agent-swarm` is registerable but is never picked\nfor an auxiliary lane pin: the control-plane chat agent is one conversation, and one\nconversation wants the pin."},"3280":{"id":"/litellm-routing-367","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"The two fan-out lanes are absent from that list on purpose. `agent-explore` and\n`agent-review` exist to be pinned by `[subagents.models]`, not chosen from a picker, so\nediting them moves a fleet role's traffic and leaves the Agents dropdowns alone."},"3281":{"id":"/litellm-routing-368","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"The two fast-compaction lanes are absent for a mechanical reason of the same kind: the\nhop keys on the summary instruction the Grok CLI appends, and the aibridge behind those\ndropdowns never sends one, so an Agents chat on `agent-xhigh-fast` is a chat on\n`agent-xhigh` under a longer name. They are a CLI and a workspace-form choice instead."},"3282":{"id":"/litellm-routing-369","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"A new alias is a client catalog entry as well as a proxy entry. Both\n`templates/*/main.tf` twins carry one `{value, name, description}` object per alias in\n`local.model_choices`, which is what the workspace create form offers for\n`grok_default_model`, and both `templates/*/grok-config.toml.tftpl` twins carry its\n`[model.\"<alias>\"]` block. An alias the config has and the twins do not is an alias no\nworkspace ever lists."},"3283":{"id":"/litellm-routing-370","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"The editor roster is the third copy of the name. `__evoT1StackModels` in both\n`templates/*/settings.json.tftpl` twins is the alias list Cline and Roo/Kilo are\noffered, and that seed is copied onto the per-owner `vscode-settings-<owner-id>` volume\nonly while the file is absent - a roster that gains an id never reaches an owner whose\n`settings.json` already exists, so re-seeding means deleting that volume's file."},"3284":{"id":"/litellm-routing-371","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"A routing hook adds two artifacts beyond the alias itself.\n`litellm/compaction_router.py` is a payload file beside the config, bind-mounted\nsingle-file as `./litellm/compaction_router.py:/app/compaction_router.py:ro` - never a\ndirectory mount over `/app`, which would hide `config.yaml` - and it is live only while\n`litellm_settings.callbacks` names `compaction_router.proxy_handler_instance`, the\ninstance rather than the class."},"3285":{"id":"/litellm-routing-372","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"Both of those live in `docker-compose.yml` and `litellm/config.yaml` respectively, so\nthey restart differently: `restart litellm` re-reads the config file, while a new mount\nand the five `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION*` keys need the container recreated with the same\ncompose invocation and `up -d litellm`."},"3286":{"id":"/litellm-routing-373","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#where-an-alias-edit-lands","content":"So an alias edited or deleted in `litellm/config.yaml` moves in the Agents model\ndropdowns exactly as it does in the CLI."},"3287":{"id":"/litellm-routing-374","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#ipex-llm-over-vanilla-ollama","content":"The IPEX-LLM runtime is Intel's XPU path (oneAPI / Level Zero) for the Arc stack."},"3288":{"id":"/litellm-routing-375","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#ipex-llm-over-vanilla-ollama","content":"`OLLAMA_NUM_GPU=999` offloads every layer to the 140T, and the iGPU pulls its weights\nstraight out of the 96 GB DDR5."},"3289":{"id":"/litellm-routing-376","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#ipex-llm-over-vanilla-ollama","content":"Vanilla Ollama on an Intel iGPU is effectively CPU-bound, and several times slower on a\n32B coder model."},"3290":{"id":"/litellm-routing-377","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#ipex-llm-over-vanilla-ollama","content":"`runners=[ipex_llm]` in the ollama logs is that GPU backend confirming itself."},"3291":{"id":"/litellm-routing-378","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#moe-over-dense","content":"`qwen2.5-coder:32b` is treated here as a Mixture-of-Experts model: 32B-class quality\nwith far fewer active parameters per token."},"3292":{"id":"/litellm-routing-379","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#moe-over-dense","content":"On a memory-rich but bandwidth- and latency-constrained iGPU that is the sweet spot,\nbecause an equivalent dense model would move every parameter per token and run much\nslower at the same footprint."},"3293":{"id":"/litellm-routing-380","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-front-door-rule","content":"Workspaces see a stable OpenAI-compatible URL and stable alias names."},"3294":{"id":"/litellm-routing-381","page_id":"/litellm-routing","tags":["litellm","models","routing","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/litellm-routing#the-one-front-door-rule","content":"So you can flip `coder` from the local Arc to a Spark box, or add a new alias, and no\nworkspace setting has to change."},"3295":{"id":"/luks-unlock","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"page","content":"Unlock an encrypted host remotely","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock"},"3296":{"id":"/luks-unlock-0","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock","content":"Configure the stack host so a reboot with an encrypted root can be answered from a laptop, and prove the boot image can do it before you reboot."},"3297":{"id":"/luks-unlock-1","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"Unlock an encrypted host remotely"},"3298":{"id":"/luks-unlock-2","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#the-command-that-matters","content":"The command that matters"},"3299":{"id":"/luks-unlock-3","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#what-install-writes","content":"What install writes"},"3300":{"id":"/luks-unlock-4","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"The files it writes"},"3301":{"id":"/luks-unlock-5","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#why-the-order-is-deliberate","content":"Why the order is deliberate"},"3302":{"id":"/luks-unlock-6","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#unlocking-from-a-laptop","content":"Unlocking from a laptop"},"3303":{"id":"/luks-unlock-7","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"The unlock itself"},"3304":{"id":"/luks-unlock-8","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#if-the-connection-is-refused","content":"If the connection is refused"},"3305":{"id":"/luks-unlock-9","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#what-the-check-catches","content":"What the check catches"},"3306":{"id":"/luks-unlock-10","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"The blocker lines"},"3307":{"id":"/luks-unlock-11","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#the-encrypted-boot-warning","content":"The encrypted /boot warning"},"3308":{"id":"/luks-unlock-12","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#static-networks","content":"Static networks"},"3309":{"id":"/luks-unlock-13","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#two-keys-two-purposes","content":"Two keys, two purposes"},"3310":{"id":"/luks-unlock-14","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#what-this-deliberately-does-not-do","content":"What this deliberately does not do"},"3311":{"id":"/luks-unlock-15","page_id":"/luks-unlock","type":"heading","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"url":"/luks-unlock#where-to-look-next","content":"Where to look next"},"3312":{"id":"/luks-unlock-16","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"**What's on this page**"},"3313":{"id":"/luks-unlock-17","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"Why a reboot is the dangerous moment on an encrypted headless box"},"3314":{"id":"/luks-unlock-18","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"The one command that answers \"can I unlock this from a laptop\""},"3315":{"id":"/luks-unlock-19","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"What `install` writes, and which file each line belongs to"},"3316":{"id":"/luks-unlock-20","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"The unlock itself, step by step, from the operator's own machine"},"3317":{"id":"/luks-unlock-21","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"What the check catches, and what it deliberately leaves alone"},"3318":{"id":"/luks-unlock-22","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"**What this enables**"},"3319":{"id":"/luks-unlock-23","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"Rebooting a server nobody is standing next to"},"3320":{"id":"/luks-unlock-24","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"Catching a config that looks right and boots dead, before the reboot"},"3321":{"id":"/luks-unlock-25","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"Reading the exact ssh command and host key fingerprint to expect"},"3322":{"id":"/luks-unlock-26","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"An Ubuntu server with a LUKS root stops in the initramfs on every reboot and\nwaits for a passphrase. With no keyboard attached, that wait is the outage:"},"3323":{"id":"/luks-unlock-27","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"the machine is up"},"3324":{"id":"/luks-unlock-28","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"the disks are unreadable"},"3325":{"id":"/luks-unlock-29","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"the only fix is a person at the console"},"3326":{"id":"/luks-unlock-30","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"The distro answer is to move an SSH server and cryptsetup's unlock prompt into\nthe initramfs, so the passphrase is typed over SSH from anywhere."},"3327":{"id":"/luks-unlock-31","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"`//scripts:luks-unlock` writes that config and then proves the generated\ninitramfs really contains the unlock path."},"3328":{"id":"/luks-unlock-32","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#unlock-an-encrypted-host-remotely","content":"The proof is the point: every one of the six settings involved fails by staying\nsilent until the boot that needs it."},"3329":{"id":"/luks-unlock-33","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-command-that-matters","content":"That is `check`, the default verb, and it writes nothing."},"3330":{"id":"/luks-unlock-34","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-command-that-matters","content":"It answers one question - if this box rebooted right now, could you decrypt it\nfrom a laptop - and closes with either `ok: this box can be unlocked from a laptop after a\nreboot` or `error: do not reboot yet - N blocker(s)`."},"3331":{"id":"/luks-unlock-35","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-command-that-matters","content":"Run it before every reboot of an encrypted box, and after any kernel or\n`initramfs-tools` update. It exits `1` when something blocks the unlock, so it\nfits in front of a maintenance script as a gate."},"3332":{"id":"/luks-unlock-36","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-install-writes","content":"`install` installs the two packages, writes the config, regenerates the\ninitramfs, and then runs the same check over what it produced."},"3333":{"id":"/luks-unlock-37","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-install-writes","content":"Add `--dry-run` first and every write and command is printed as `would: ...`\ninstead of executed. Nothing reboots."},"3334":{"id":"/luks-unlock-38","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"| File                                  | Line it writes | Why it matters                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/etc/cryptsetup-initramfs/conf-hook` | `CRYPTSETUP=y` | Without it the cryptroot scripts never enter the boot image, so there is nothing to type a passphrase into. |","table":"table-0"},"3335":{"id":"/luks-unlock-39","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"| File                                         | Line it writes                                                          | Why it matters                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/etc/initramfs-tools/conf.d/zz-luks-unlock` | `DROPBEAR=y`, `IP=`, `UMASK=0077`, and `HOOKS=` when a list is in force | One file this CLI owns, named to sort last so it wins over every other drop-in. `IP=` is what gives the boot image an address; `UMASK=0077` keeps the packed key out of unprivileged hands. |","table":"table-0"},"3336":{"id":"/luks-unlock-40","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"| File                                      | Line it writes               | Why it matters                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `/etc/dropbear/initramfs/authorized_keys` | the operator's public key(s) | Password logins are off in the initramfs. No key there means the SSH server refuses everyone, including you. |","table":"table-0"},"3337":{"id":"/luks-unlock-41","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"| File                                    | Line it writes                              | Why it matters                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/etc/dropbear/initramfs/dropbear.conf` | `DROPBEAR_OPTIONS=\"-p 2222 -s -I 60 -j -k\"` | `-s` keeps password logins off, `-I` bounds a session someone walked away from, and the port stays off the installed sshd's so the different host keys do not look like an attack. An existing `DROPBEAR_OPTIONS` is left alone. |","table":"table-0"},"3338":{"id":"/luks-unlock-42","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-files-it-writes","content":"| File                                          | Line it writes                               | Why it matters                                                                                 |\n| --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/etc/dropbear/initramfs/dropbear_*_host_key` | generated with `dropbearkey` when none exist | dropbear refuses to start with no host key, and the package only creates them at install time. |","table":"table-0"},"3339":{"id":"/luks-unlock-43","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#why-the-order-is-deliberate","content":"The order is deliberate: the hook packs the authorized key at generation time,\nso a key written after `update-initramfs` is not in the image. That is why\n`install` ends by reading the image back."},"3340":{"id":"/luks-unlock-44","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"Pin the identity while the box is still up, so a stranger's key cannot be\nmistaken for it later:"},"3341":{"id":"/luks-unlock-45","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"Reboot the box."},"3342":{"id":"/luks-unlock-46","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"Wait a minute, then connect on the initramfs port. The check prints the\ncommand; it keeps its own `known_hosts` on purpose:"},"3343":{"id":"/luks-unlock-47","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"Type the passphrase:"},"3344":{"id":"/luks-unlock-48","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-unlock-itself","content":"The boot continues on its own once the mapping appears - no second reboot."},"3345":{"id":"/luks-unlock-49","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#if-the-connection-is-refused","content":"If the SSH connection is refused, the box is still in the initramfs or before\nit:"},"3346":{"id":"/luks-unlock-50","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#if-the-connection-is-refused","content":"the boot does not proceed past an unmapped root, so waiting is safe"},"3347":{"id":"/luks-unlock-51","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#if-the-connection-is-refused","content":"the console (out-of-band console, IPMI, or the provider's serial console)\nstill shows where it stopped"},"3348":{"id":"/luks-unlock-52","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"Every row below is a `check` line you can get instead of an `ok`, and each one\nhas booted dead in the field."},"3349":{"id":"/luks-unlock-53","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                             | Cause                  | Fix                                                                                               |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `no initramfs address (IP is unset, none, or off)` | nothing ever set `IP=` | `install --ip dhcp`, or `--iface ens3` to pin one NIC, or a raw netboot spec for a static network |","table":"table-1"},"3350":{"id":"/luks-unlock-54","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                          | Cause                                                   | Fix                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `HOOKS leaves out net dropbear` | a hand-written `HOOKS=` list that predates the packages | `install` merges the four names it needs into whatever list is in force |","table":"table-1"},"3351":{"id":"/luks-unlock-55","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                 | Cause                                                       | Fix                                                            |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `the boot image holds no bin/dropbear` | the package was installed after the last `update-initramfs` | re-run `install` so the image is regenerated after the install |","table":"table-1"},"3352":{"id":"/luks-unlock-56","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                             | Cause                                                                              | Fix                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `no authorized key was packed into the boot image` | the key was written after the image, or in a path the installed hook does not read | re-run `install`; the CLI asks the installed hook which path it reads rather than assuming |","table":"table-1"},"3353":{"id":"/luks-unlock-57","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                              | Cause                         | Fix                                          |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `the key body holds characters that are not base64` | a pasted key wrapped mid-body | re-paste on one line; `check` names the line |","table":"table-1"},"3354":{"id":"/luks-unlock-58","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                                          | Cause                                                          | Fix                                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `key file /etc/keys/root.key is not covered by KEYFILE_PATTERN` | the crypttab key lives on disk and never reaches the initramfs | add a `KEYFILE_PATTERN` to `conf-hook`, or move that volume to a passphrase |","table":"table-1"},"3355":{"id":"/luks-unlock-59","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                            | Cause                                                              | Fix                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `MODULES=dep packs only drivers loaded right now` | the NIC driver is not loaded today, so it will be missing tomorrow | name the driver in `/etc/initramfs-tools/modules`, or go back to `MODULES=most` |","table":"table-1"},"3356":{"id":"/luks-unlock-60","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                                                 | Cause                                                 | Fix                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `the initramfs listens on 2222, the same port the installed sshd uses` | the two daemons share a port with different host keys | pick another `--port`, and keep using the separate `UserKnownHostsFile` |","table":"table-1"},"3357":{"id":"/luks-unlock-61","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-blocker-lines","content":"| Report                                             | Cause                                  | Fix                                              |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `an encrypted /boot needs GRUB to read the initrd` | `/boot` is inside the encrypted volume | verify GRUB can read it before trusting a reboot |","table":"table-1"},"3358":{"id":"/luks-unlock-62","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#the-encrypted-boot-warning","content":"The last one is worth dwelling on: `check` can read every config file and still\nbe looking at an image GRUB cannot load, so an encrypted `/boot` is reported as\na warning to verify by hand rather than cleared."},"3359":{"id":"/luks-unlock-63","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#static-networks","content":"A box with no DHCP gets the raw initramfs form, which is passed through\nuntouched because `initramfs-tools` parses it, not this CLI:"},"3360":{"id":"/luks-unlock-64","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#static-networks","content":"`--iface ens3` with `--ip dhcp` produces the same pinned-device shape with\nDHCP kept. A name the kernel never assigned is a blocker, not a typo you\ndiscover after the reboot: `check` compares it against `/sys/class/net`."},"3361":{"id":"/luks-unlock-65","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#two-keys-two-purposes","content":"The unlock key authorizes a root shell on a machine whose disks are still\nsealed, and the initramfs image holding it sits on an unencrypted `/boot`.\nAnyone who can read `/boot` can read that public key."},"3362":{"id":"/luks-unlock-66","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#two-keys-two-purposes","content":"Treat it as a separate credential with its own purpose: a dedicated key whose\nprivate half lives on the laptop you bring to a reboot, not the key you push to\nevery repository."},"3363":{"id":"/luks-unlock-67","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#two-keys-two-purposes","content":"`UMASK=0077` keeps the image itself out of unprivileged hands, and the initramfs\nhost keys stay separate from `/etc/ssh` on purpose - they are generated per boot\nimage, and sharing them would leak which key the sealed machine answers to."},"3364":{"id":"/luks-unlock-68","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-this-deliberately-does-not-do","content":"**Reboot anything.** The reboot is the operator's decision, made after a\ngreen `check`."},"3365":{"id":"/luks-unlock-69","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-this-deliberately-does-not-do","content":"**Edit `/etc/crypttab` or the LUKS headers.** The volumes are read to decide\nwhether the boot can open them. Key slots, passphrases and headers are never\nwritten, so this CLI cannot be the thing that destroys a key."},"3366":{"id":"/luks-unlock-70","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-this-deliberately-does-not-do","content":"**Enroll a TPM.** `systemd-cryptenroll` is a different design with a\ndifferent failure mode - a firmware update that changes the PCR policy seals\nthe box with nobody in the loop - and it belongs in its own change."},"3367":{"id":"/luks-unlock-71","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#what-this-deliberately-does-not-do","content":"**Add an auto-reboot watchdog.** A box sitting in the initramfs with dropbear\nlistening is the recoverable state; rebooting on a timer destroys the\nrecovery window and can turn one bad boot into a loop. `-I` bounds the\nsession, and the listener stays."},"3368":{"id":"/luks-unlock-72","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#where-to-look-next","content":"troubleshooting.md for the symptom-first list once the\nbox is back up."},"3369":{"id":"/luks-unlock-73","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#where-to-look-next","content":"public-access.md for what the box exposes on the network\nafter it boots - the initramfs listener is gone by then."},"3370":{"id":"/luks-unlock-74","page_id":"/luks-unlock","tags":["operate","luks","disk-encryption","boot","headless","ssh"],"type":"text","url":"/luks-unlock#where-to-look-next","content":"operate/index.md for the rest of the day-to-day runbooks."},"3371":{"id":"/new-repo","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"page","content":"New projects from the template","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo"},"3372":{"id":"/new-repo-0","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo","content":"How scripts/new-repo.sh fetches the ezrepo scaffold from GitHub, renders it into a new repository, and what the Coder side adds."},"3373":{"id":"/new-repo-1","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"New projects from the template"},"3374":{"id":"/new-repo-2","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"Two kinds of template"},"3375":{"id":"/new-repo-3","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"What the scaffold ships"},"3376":{"id":"/new-repo-4","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"Lanes"},"3377":{"id":"/new-repo-5","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#rendering-a-repository","content":"Rendering a repository"},"3378":{"id":"/new-repo-6","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#how-the-scaffold-is-fetched","content":"How the scaffold is fetched"},"3379":{"id":"/new-repo-7","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"Flags"},"3380":{"id":"/new-repo-8","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#exit-codes","content":"Exit codes"},"3381":{"id":"/new-repo-9","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"Placeholder tokens"},"3382":{"id":"/new-repo-10","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"Paths removed on the way out"},"3383":{"id":"/new-repo-11","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"What each GitHub step needs"},"3384":{"id":"/new-repo-12","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#coder-side","content":"Coder side"},"3385":{"id":"/new-repo-13","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#the-new-project-preset","content":"The New project preset"},"3386":{"id":"/new-repo-14","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#the-optional-coder-task","content":"The optional Coder Task"},"3387":{"id":"/new-repo-15","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#where-the-hand-off-ends","content":"Where the hand-off ends"},"3388":{"id":"/new-repo-16","page_id":"/new-repo","type":"heading","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"url":"/new-repo#where-this-is-enforced","content":"Where this is enforced"},"3389":{"id":"/new-repo-17","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"**What's on this page**"},"3390":{"id":"/new-repo-18","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Two different things called \"template\", and which one this page is about"},"3391":{"id":"/new-repo-19","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"What the scaffold repository ships, and the account-wide gaps it closes"},"3392":{"id":"/new-repo-20","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Where the scaffold is fetched from, and how to pin or replace it"},"3393":{"id":"/new-repo-21","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Rendering a repository with `new-repo`, its flags, and its lanes"},"3394":{"id":"/new-repo-22","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Which GitHub steps need which App permission, and what the CLI does when one is refused"},"3395":{"id":"/new-repo-23","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"The `New project` workspace preset and the optional Coder Task"},"3396":{"id":"/new-repo-24","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Where all of this is enforced"},"3397":{"id":"/new-repo-25","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"**What this enables**"},"3398":{"id":"/new-repo-26","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Starting a new repository with the quality gate already in place, in one command"},"3399":{"id":"/new-repo-27","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Getting the same scaffold on a laptop, in CI, and from a workspace"},"3400":{"id":"/new-repo-28","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Pinning a scaffold revision, or rendering a local tree with no network at all"},"3401":{"id":"/new-repo-29","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#new-projects-from-the-template","content":"Telling a refused GitHub permission apart from a broken render"},"3402":{"id":"/new-repo-30","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"This repository already uses the word *template* for a **Coder template**: the Terraform tree\nunder `templates/workspace/` and `templates/devcontainer/` that `push-template.sh` registers with\nthe Coder server."},"3403":{"id":"/new-repo-31","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"The other *template* is a **project scaffold**: a tree of files that `scripts/new-repo.sh` copies,\nsubstitutes, and hands to `git init` as the first commit of a brand new repository. It is not\nvendored here."},"3404":{"id":"/new-repo-32","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"It lives in its own repository -- by default `https://github.com/toxicoder/ezrepo` -- and this\nrepo's whole job is to fetch that tree and render it."},"3405":{"id":"/new-repo-33","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"The scaffold is a product with its own CI and its own release rhythm, and a vendored copy drifts\nfrom the day it is committed, so nothing here is kept in step with it."},"3406":{"id":"/new-repo-34","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#two-kinds-of-template","content":"The coupling runs one way: this repo may name the scaffold repository; the scaffold repository\nnever names this one. And the scaffold's quality gate is its own -- the `.self-check/` suite and\nthe CI that runs it in that repository -- so a scaffold change is tested where it is made, and a\nlane or a file the scaffold adds needs no change here."},"3407":{"id":"/new-repo-35","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"These files belong to the scaffold repository. This repo does not ship them, lint them, or keep a\ncopy: it fetches them at run time and renders them."},"3408":{"id":"/new-repo-36","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"The scaffold is language-neutral at the core, with optional per-language lanes. Everything below\nwas chosen from what is measurably missing across the account, not from taste."},"3409":{"id":"/new-repo-37","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"Across a sample of eleven ordinary projects these were each present in none of them, and no\nrepository in the surveyed set had a single release or tag:"},"3410":{"id":"/new-repo-38","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"`SECURITY.md`"},"3411":{"id":"/new-repo-39","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"`CONTRIBUTING.md`"},"3412":{"id":"/new-repo-40","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"issue templates"},"3413":{"id":"/new-repo-41","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"a pull-request template"},"3414":{"id":"/new-repo-42","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"`dependabot.yml`"},"3415":{"id":"/new-repo-43","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"`CODEOWNERS`"},"3416":{"id":"/new-repo-44","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"`.editorconfig`"},"3417":{"id":"/new-repo-45","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area      | What ships                                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Community | `SECURITY.md` with a supported-versions table and private-report route, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` |","table":"table-0"},"3418":{"id":"/new-repo-46","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area   | What ships                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| GitHub | `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `release.yml`, `security.yml`, `dependabot.yml`, `CODEOWNERS`, issue templates with blank issues disabled, a PR template with a Safety/ops-impact section |","table":"table-0"},"3419":{"id":"/new-repo-47","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area    | What ships                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Hygiene | `.editorconfig`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore`, `env.example` (the render writes it out as `.env.example`), `.yamllint.yml`, `.shellcheckrc` |","table":"table-0"},"3420":{"id":"/new-repo-48","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area  | What ships                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Gates | `.pre-commit-config.yaml` whose local hooks **fail** when a tool is missing, plus `tests/run.sh`, a dispatcher that errors rather than skipping when a runner is absent |","table":"table-0"},"3421":{"id":"/new-repo-49","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area | What ships                                                                                       |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Pins | `tool-versions.env`, read by the dev container, `make doctor`, and CI, so the three cannot drift |","table":"table-0"},"3422":{"id":"/new-repo-50","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area           | What ships                                                                              |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Agent contract | `AGENTS.md` with the cost-tiered \"which check first\" table and the path-to-test mapping |","table":"table-0"},"3423":{"id":"/new-repo-51","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area | What ships                                                                                                 |\n| ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/project-conventions.md`, and `docs/adr/` with a template plus one worked ADR |","table":"table-0"},"3424":{"id":"/new-repo-52","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"| Area      | What ships                                                           |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Packaging | a multi-stage non-root `Dockerfile` and a separate `Dockerfile.test` |","table":"table-0"},"3425":{"id":"/new-repo-53","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-the-scaffold-ships","content":"The rule that ties it together: **a check that silently skips is a bug**. Two existing\nrepositories print `tool not found ... Skipping` and then exit zero, and a pre-commit config in\nanother wraps every hook in `command -v ... || exit 0`. Nothing in the scaffold may do that, and\nthe scaffold's own `.self-check/` suite is what holds the line."},"3426":{"id":"/new-repo-54","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"Lane ids are not declared here. `scripts/new-repo.sh` discovers them from the fetched tree's\n`.template-lanes/` directory at run time, so a lane the scaffold repository adds needs no change\nin this repo. The four below are what it ships today:"},"3427":{"id":"/new-repo-55","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"| Lane              | Adds                                                                                |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `shell` (default) | `src/main.sh`, a pure helper under `src/lib/`, Bats suites, `scripts/lint-shell.sh` |","table":"table-1"},"3428":{"id":"/new-repo-56","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"| Lane     | Adds                                                                                                    |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `python` | `pyproject.toml` with Ruff and `fail_under = 100`, `mypy.ini` at strict, a package under `src/`, pytest |","table":"table-1"},"3429":{"id":"/new-repo-57","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"| Lane         | Adds                                                                        |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `typescript` | ESLint 9 flat config, Prettier, Vitest with 100% thresholds, `tsc --noEmit` |","table":"table-1"},"3430":{"id":"/new-repo-58","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"| Lane | Adds                                                                               |\n| ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `go` | `go.mod`, `.golangci.yml`, table-driven tests, `go vet`, `gosec`, a coverage floor |","table":"table-1"},"3431":{"id":"/new-repo-59","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#lanes","content":"Each lane lives at `<scaffold>/.template-lanes/<lane>/`. A file there is copied over the rendered\ntree at the same path, so a lane may add files or replace a core one. `LANE.md` and\n`gitignore.fragment` are lane metadata: the renderer appends the fragment to `.gitignore` and drops\nboth from the output. Ask for a lane the fetched tree does not have and the run dies naming the\nlanes it does offer."},"3432":{"id":"/new-repo-60","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#how-the-scaffold-is-fetched","content":"The scaffold is fetched before anything is rendered: a shallow (`--depth 1`), single-branch clone\nof `--template-ref` into a scratch directory an EXIT trap removes."},"3433":{"id":"/new-repo-61","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#how-the-scaffold-is-fetched","content":"`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` and an empty credential helper keep a scaffold that turned private from\nhanging on a prompt nobody can answer inside a workspace."},"3434":{"id":"/new-repo-62","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#how-the-scaffold-is-fetched","content":"A fetched tree with no `template.yml` at its root is a hard failure -- that manifest belongs to\nthe scaffold repository, so pick a ref that has it."},"3435":{"id":"/new-repo-63","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#how-the-scaffold-is-fetched","content":"The new repository's first commit records what it was built from: `- Scaffold: <url>@<sha>.`, or\n`- Scaffold: local tree <dir>.` for a `--template-dir` render."},"3436":{"id":"/new-repo-64","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag        | Effect                                   |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `--dry-run` | render, report, create nothing on GitHub |","table":"table-2"},"3437":{"id":"/new-repo-65","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag          | Effect                                                                        |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--out <dir>` | parent directory for the rendered repository (default: the current directory) |","table":"table-2"},"3438":{"id":"/new-repo-66","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag        | Effect                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `--no-push` | render and commit locally only |","table":"table-2"},"3439":{"id":"/new-repo-67","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag          | Effect                 |\n| ------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `--no-remote` | skip every GitHub step |","table":"table-2"},"3440":{"id":"/new-repo-68","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag        | Effect                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `--private` | create the repository private |","table":"table-2"},"3441":{"id":"/new-repo-69","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag            | Effect                           |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `--as-template` | mark it as a template repository |","table":"table-2"},"3442":{"id":"/new-repo-70","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag                                             | Effect                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--description`, `--owner`, `--holder`, `--year` | token values; the owner defaults to the authenticated account |","table":"table-2"},"3443":{"id":"/new-repo-71","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag          | Effect                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--lane <id>` | add a lane; repeatable, default `shell`. Ids are discovered from the fetched scaffold, so a lane the scaffold adds needs no change here. `--lane none` clears the lanes named so far and renders the bare core, whose `make test` asks for a lane |","table":"table-2"},"3444":{"id":"/new-repo-72","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag          | Effect                  |\n| ------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `--topic <t>` | extra topic; repeatable |","table":"table-2"},"3445":{"id":"/new-repo-73","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag                   | Effect                                                                                                |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--template-url <url>` | scaffold repository to clone (default: `$EZREPO_URL`, else `https://github.com/toxicoder/ezrepo.git`) |","table":"table-2"},"3446":{"id":"/new-repo-74","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag                   | Effect                                                                                            |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--template-ref <ref>` | branch or tag to fetch (default: `$EZREPO_REF`, else `main`). Pin a tag for a reproducible render |","table":"table-2"},"3447":{"id":"/new-repo-75","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag                   | Effect                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--template-dir <dir>` | render this local tree and fetch nothing (default: `$EZREPO_DIR`); `--template-ref` has no effect on it |","table":"table-2"},"3448":{"id":"/new-repo-76","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag                            | Effect |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ |\n| `--task`, `--task-template <n>` |        |","table":"table-2"},"3449":{"id":"/new-repo-77","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"| Flag              | Effect                            |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `--branch <name>` | default branch, `main` by default |","table":"table-2"},"3450":{"id":"/new-repo-78","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#flags","content":"The three scaffold flags exist so the source can be pointed elsewhere without editing anything:\nthe env pair covers a mirror or a fork for a whole deployment, and `--template-dir` renders a tree\nyou already hold, which is the offline route and the one the hermetic tests use."},"3451":{"id":"/new-repo-79","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#exit-codes","content":"The run exits 0 when the render succeeded -- a refused GitHub step is a `warning:`, not a failure --\nand 1 on a render failure, a bad argument, or a scaffold that cannot be fetched."},"3452":{"id":"/new-repo-80","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"Placeholders are substituted in file contents *and* in file and directory names:"},"3453":{"id":"/new-repo-81","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_NAME__`"},"3454":{"id":"/new-repo-82","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_SLUG__`"},"3455":{"id":"/new-repo-83","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_MODULE__`"},"3456":{"id":"/new-repo-84","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_DESCRIPTION__`"},"3457":{"id":"/new-repo-85","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_OWNER__`"},"3458":{"id":"/new-repo-86","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_LICENSE_HOLDER__`"},"3459":{"id":"/new-repo-87","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"`__PROJECT_YEAR__`"},"3460":{"id":"/new-repo-88","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"Those seven are named once, in `NEW_REPO_TOKENS`, and they are the whole contract between this\nscript and the scaffold -- a ceiling rather than an equality, so the template may use a subset of\nthem. A token that survives is a hard failure, not a warning -- a repository that ships with its\nplaceholders showing is worse than no template at all."},"3461":{"id":"/new-repo-89","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#placeholder-tokens","content":"Markdown carries a token in a second spelling. Prettier reads a bare `__PROJECT_NAME__` as strong\nemphasis and rewrites it to `**PROJECT_NAME**`, so a markdown formatter run over the template turns\nevery prose placeholder into that form; the renderer substitutes both spellings. Which of the seven\nthe scaffold actually uses, in either spelling, is the scaffold's own invariant and its own\n`.self-check/` suite checks it."},"3462":{"id":"/new-repo-90","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"Two kinds of path are removed on the way out:"},"3463":{"id":"/new-repo-91","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"a lane's reserved metadata (`LANE.md`, `gitignore.fragment`, whose contents are consumed rather\nthan copied)"},"3464":{"id":"/new-repo-92","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"the generator-owned paths in `NEW_REPO_TEMPLATE_META`, stripped from every render:"},"3465":{"id":"/new-repo-93","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"`.template-lanes/` (the overlay source this script reads)"},"3466":{"id":"/new-repo-94","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"`.self-check/` (the scaffold's conformance suite, which goes stale the moment a real project\ndiverges from the template it was checked against)"},"3467":{"id":"/new-repo-95","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#paths-removed-on-the-way-out","content":"`.git` (which would hand the new repository the template's history and origin remote)"},"3468":{"id":"/new-repo-96","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"The credential here is the Coder External Auth GitHub App **user-to-server token**; this stack\nnever introduces a static token or PAT. An App can be granted one endpoint and refused another, so\nthe CLI runs the publish side as independent steps, each reporting `ok:` or `warning:` on its own."},"3469":{"id":"/new-repo-97","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"No step is fatal, because aborting on the first refusal would abandon the steps that were allowed."},"3470":{"id":"/new-repo-98","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"| Step   | Endpoint           | App permission                                            |\n| ------ | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Create | `POST /user/repos` | `Administration: write` (or `Repository creation: write`) |","table":"table-3"},"3471":{"id":"/new-repo-99","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"| Step     | Endpoint               | App permission          |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Settings | `PATCH /repos/{o}/{r}` | `Administration: write` |","table":"table-3"},"3472":{"id":"/new-repo-100","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"| Step   | Endpoint                    | App permission          |\n| ------ | --------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Topics | `PUT /repos/{o}/{r}/topics` | `Administration: write` |","table":"table-3"},"3473":{"id":"/new-repo-101","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"| Step   | Endpoint                                  | App permission          |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Alerts | `PUT /repos/{o}/{r}/vulnerability-alerts` | `Administration: write` |","table":"table-3"},"3474":{"id":"/new-repo-102","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"| Step | Endpoint       | App permission       |\n| ---- | -------------- | -------------------- |\n| Push | git over HTTPS | the credential above |","table":"table-3"},"3475":{"id":"/new-repo-103","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"Dependabot **secrets** are a different permission that this App does not currently hold, which is\nwhy the CLI does not attempt them."},"3476":{"id":"/new-repo-104","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"When a step is refused the CLI prints the endpoint, GitHub's message, and the permission to ask\nfor, then re-mints nothing and continues."},"3477":{"id":"/new-repo-105","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#what-each-github-step-needs","content":"Because git and `gh` consult `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` before the stored login, an expired token\npair from an old refresh can shadow a working credential. Every call tries the environment first\nand, on refusal, retries once with the pair cleared and says so in a `warning:`. Re-mint with\n`coder external-auth access-token github`."},"3478":{"id":"/new-repo-106","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#coder-side","content":"Two things, and neither replaces the CLI."},"3479":{"id":"/new-repo-107","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#the-new-project-preset","content":"The **`New project (scaffold ready)` preset** in both templates is a form shortcut. It pins the\ngolden image, turns on the DinD sidecar in the workspace template, and passes this stack as\n`additional_repos`, which is what puts `scripts/new-repo.sh` inside a fresh workspace beside the\nproject being started."},"3480":{"id":"/new-repo-108","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#the-new-project-preset","content":"The scaffold does not ride along: the CLI fetches it from GitHub when it runs. It is a preset, so it\nonly sets parameter values."},"3481":{"id":"/new-repo-109","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#the-optional-coder-task","content":"**`--task`** calls `coder task create` once the repository exists. The Coder server here is v2.36.6\nand does ship `coder task`, but the Terraform provider is pinned to `~> 2.18`, so a task cannot be\ndeclared inside a template. The CLI therefore creates it at run time and, when it cannot reach the\nCoder API -- the usual case outside a logged-in host shell -- prints the exact command and continues\nwith exit 0."},"3482":{"id":"/new-repo-110","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#the-optional-coder-task","content":"That follows `new-workspace.sh`, which treats \"cannot create right now\" as a not-yet rather than an\nerror."},"3483":{"id":"/new-repo-111","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-the-hand-off-ends","content":"The CLI never creates the workspace itself. It prints\n`next: bazelisk run //scripts:new-workspace -- <url>` and stops, because `new-workspace.sh` owns the\ndev-container probe and the template choice, and a second copy of that decision would eventually\ndisagree with the first."},"3484":{"id":"/new-repo-112","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-the-hand-off-ends","content":"That preset/CLI pair is the whole hand-off. It is where this repo hands a new project over, and the\nonly coupling between the two repositories: this repo names the scaffold it clones, the scaffold\nnever names this one."},"3485":{"id":"/new-repo-113","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-this-is-enforced","content":"The split follows the ownership: the scaffold's own invariants are checked in the scaffold\nrepository, and this repo checks only the renderer."},"3486":{"id":"/new-repo-114","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-this-is-enforced","content":"The scaffold's `.self-check/` suite, in that repository and run by its own CI, owns the template's\ninternal invariants: every token the template uses is one this script declares, every lane ships\nits `LANE.md` plus `gitignore.fragment` pair, every tool is pinned rather than `@latest`, the\nworkflows declare `permissions`, the docs links resolve, and the pins cover the lanes present."},"3487":{"id":"/new-repo-115","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-this-is-enforced","content":"`//tests:bats_new_repo_test` owns the renderer: token substitution in file contents and in file\nand directory names, the markdown `**NAME**` alias, the lane overlay and its `gitignore`\nfragments, the generator-owned paths stripped from every render, the argv of the scaffold clone,\nthe credential ladder that retries once with `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` cleared, the GitHub ladder\nstaying advisory (a refused step warns and never fails the run), and the Coder Task being a\nconvenience that cannot fail a render."},"3488":{"id":"/new-repo-116","page_id":"/new-repo","tags":["template","new-repo","scaffold","coder-task","ezrepo"],"type":"text","url":"/new-repo#where-this-is-enforced","content":"`//tests:bats_bazel_deps_test` keeps `_SCRIPT_PAYLOAD[\"new-repo\"]` honest about what the CLI\nactually reads."},"3489":{"id":"/observability","page_id":"/observability","type":"page","content":"Observability bundle","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability"},"3490":{"id":"/observability-0","page_id":"/observability","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"type":"text","url":"/observability","content":"The ten profile-gated monitoring services: what each one does, how metrics, logs and traces reach Grafana, how an alert reaches Alertmanager, where each config file lives, what the data costs on disk, and what is deliberately left out."},"3491":{"id":"/observability-1","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#observability-bundle","content":"Observability bundle"},"3492":{"id":"/observability-2","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#the-ten-services","content":"The ten services"},"3493":{"id":"/observability-3","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#how-the-data-moves","content":"How the data moves"},"3494":{"id":"/observability-4","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#the-path-each-signal-takes","content":"The path each signal takes"},"3495":{"id":"/observability-5","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#four-places-a-panel-goes-empty","content":"Four places a panel goes empty"},"3496":{"id":"/observability-6","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#the-four-fixed-datasource-uids","content":"The four fixed datasource UIDs"},"3497":{"id":"/observability-7","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#alerts-and-rules","content":"Alerts and rules"},"3498":{"id":"/observability-8","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#who-evaluates-and-who-delivers","content":"Who evaluates and who delivers"},"3499":{"id":"/observability-9","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#four-things-to-know-before-editing-the-wiring","content":"Four things to know before editing the wiring"},"3500":{"id":"/observability-10","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#the-webhook-destination-is-empty-as-shipped","content":"The webhook destination is empty as shipped"},"3501":{"id":"/observability-11","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#the-flag","content":"The flag"},"3502":{"id":"/observability-12","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#turning-the-bundle-off","content":"Turning the bundle off"},"3503":{"id":"/observability-13","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","grafana","loki","tempo","mimir","operate"],"url":"/observability#both-flag-paths-are-gated","content":"Both flag paths are gated"},"3504":{"id":"/observability-14","page_id":"/observability","type":"heading","tags":["observability","prometheus","