e","tags":["operate","dashboard","maintain","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/operate#before-you-reach-for-a-hammer","content":"the dev-stack `reset`"},"3784":{"id":"/operate-30","page_id":"/operate","tags":["operate","dashboard","maintain","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/operate#before-you-reach-for-a-hammer","content":"a Kasm reset"},"3785":{"id":"/operate-31","page_id":"/operate","tags":["operate","dashboard","maintain","overview"],"type":"text","url":"/operate#before-you-reach-for-a-hammer","content":"The cost of each is spelled out on the entry in troubleshooting.md —\nread that line first."},"3786":{"id":"/operate/monitoring","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"page","content":"Monitoring and alerts","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Operate the box"],"tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring"},"3787":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-0","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring","content":"Running the observability bundle day to day: where the 30 alerts live, what Alertmanager pages on and off, why its UI stays on loopback, where a silence belongs, and how the three DGX Sparks become Prometheus targets."},"3788":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-1","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Monitoring and alerts"},"3789":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-2","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"Alerts"},"3790":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-3","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"The alerts that cover the blind spots"},"3791":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-4","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-alert-that-closes-the-same-shape","content":"The Spark alert that closes the same shape"},"3792":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-5","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#what-that-means-day-to-day","content":"What that means day to day"},"3793":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-6","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"The three exporters"},"3794":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-7","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-exporters","content":"The Spark exporters"},"3795":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-8","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"The three modes"},"3796":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-9","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#the-targets-file-and-the-walkthrough","content":"The targets file and the walkthrough"},"3797":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-10","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","type":"heading","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"url":"/operate/monitoring#where-to-look-next","content":"Where to look next"},"3798":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-11","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"**What's on this page**"},"3799":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-12","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"The alerts the bundle ships, and the two pages that show them"},"3800":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-13","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"What an empty `ALERTMANAGER_WEBHOOK_URL` means for who gets paged"},"3801":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-14","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Why Alertmanager's UI is loopback-only, and where a silence belongs"},"3802":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-15","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Making the three DGX Sparks Prometheus targets with `//scripts:spark-monitor`"},"3803":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-16","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"**What this enables**"},"3804":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-17","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Telling a firing alert from a missing exporter before you restart anything"},"3805":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-18","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Enrolling the Sparks without hand-editing a Prometheus config"},"3806":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-19","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#monitoring-and-alerts","content":"Every command here is a Bazel target run from a **host** shell. Inside a Coder workspace\nthe `docker` CLI only reaches that workspace's own DinD sidecar, so a check aimed at the\nstack's own containers has to be run where the stack lives."},"3807":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-20","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"Three rule files arrive with Prometheus and need no second registration:"},"3808":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-21","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"`observability/prometheus/rules/stack.rules.yml` carries the twelve host alerts"},"3809":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-22","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"`spark.rules.yml` the eight Spark alerts"},"3810":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-23","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"`inference.rules.yml` the ten inference alerts - 30 in all"},"3811":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-24","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#alerts","content":"Prometheus evaluates them. The bundle now also runs Alertmanager\n(`prom/alertmanager:v0.35.0`) to group them, hold them, and decide who hears about them."},"3812":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-25","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"Three of the host alerts exist because the obvious design has a blind spot:"},"3813":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-26","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"The two single-exporter gap alerts each wait for the *other* exporter to vouch for the\nbox, so both exporters dying at once - a powered-off host, a restarted Docker - was\nsilent; `HostExportersSilent` asks no second opinion and fires on the double absence."},"3814":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-27","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"A dead blackbox prober produces no probe series at all, so nothing it probes can report\nit; `BlackboxProbeGap` reads `up{job=\"blackbox\"}`, which is why Prometheus scrapes the\nprober as a service of its own."},"3815":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-28","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"The same argument one layer up: every rule pages *through* Alertmanager, and an\nAlertmanager that is gone loses no series that any other rule reads, so the bundle keeps\nevaluating and firing into nothing."},"3816":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-29","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-alerts-that-cover-the-blind-spots","content":"`AlertmanagerGap` is critical where those two are warning, and asks both shapes of the\nfault - `absent()` for the service being gone and `up == 0` for a container that runs\nwithout answering."},"3817":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-30","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-alert-that-closes-the-same-shape","content":"One Spark alert closes the same shape on the other side."},"3818":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-31","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-alert-that-closes-the-same-shape","content":"`SparkDown` needs the probe to fail as well as the scrape, so a box that is genuinely up\nand simply not reporting host metrics pages nothing, and `SparkGpuSeriesSilent` asks only\nthe DCGM family."},"3819":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-32","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-alert-that-closes-the-same-shape","content":"`SparkHostMetricsSilent` is the one that reads a box whose health probe succeeds while\n`spark:box_up` has never been 1 - the usual cause being a hand-edited file where the\nstamped `exporter` label lost its exact spelling, which drops that box's group out of\nevery job's keep filter."},"3820":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-33","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#what-that-means-day-to-day","content":"**An empty `ALERTMANAGER_WEBHOOK_URL` is the shipped state, and it pages nobody.**\nThe rules still fire and stay readable on Prometheus's `/alerts` page and on Grafana's\nAlerting page; only the delivery step is silent. Set the key to a webhook URL when you\nwant a person told, and never put a URL that carries a credential in `.env`."},"3821":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-34","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#what-that-means-day-to-day","content":"**Alertmanager's UI is published on loopback only** (`OBS_ALERTMANAGER_PORT`, 9093),\nfor the same reason Coder's `:2112` metrics port is: that UI can silence a firing\nalert, so an unauthenticated silencer on the LAN is a way to make a real fault\ninvisible. Read it from a shell on the stack host."},"3822":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-35","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#what-that-means-day-to-day","content":"**Make silences in Alertmanager, not in Grafana.** Alertmanager owns grouping,\nsilences and the repeat interval, so a silence created anywhere else does not stop the\nroute - and the two views then disagree about why nobody was paged."},"3823":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-36","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"The three exporters feeding those rules sit beside the bundle on the same\n`observability` profile, all published to `127.0.0.1` only:"},"3824":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-37","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"node_exporter (`quay.io/prometheus/node-exporter:v1.12.1`) on `OBS_NODE_EXPORTER_PORT` (9101)"},"3825":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-38","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"cAdvisor (`ghcr.io/google/cadvisor:v0.61.0`) on `OBS_CADVISOR_PORT` (9290)"},"3826":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-39","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"blackbox_exporter (`prom/blackbox-exporter:v0.29.1`) on `OBS_BLACKBOX_PORT` (9115)"},"3827":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-40","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-exporters","content":"The data path behind them, and what each config file costs to change, is\nobservability.md."},"3828":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-41","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-exporters","content":"The three DGX Sparks are not scrape targets until you make them one."},"3829":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-42","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-spark-exporters","content":"Each box needs two containers - node_exporter on `SPARK_NODE_EXPORTER_PORT` (9100) and the\nNVIDIA DCGM exporter on `SPARK_DCGM_EXPORTER_PORT` (9400) - and neither exists on a box\nuntil `--apply` creates it:"},"3830":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-43","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"Plan is the default and opens no ssh session and no docker call, so the first two are\nsafe to run before anything is decided."},"3831":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-44","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"`SPARK_MONITOR_ENABLED` (false as shipped) is the opt-in that decides whether `--targets`\nprints the three boxes or an empty array, and the DCGM image comes from\n`SPARK_DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE`."},"3832":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-45","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"That one tag - `nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:4.4.2-4.7.0-ubuntu22.04` - is the pin\nthis stack could not verify upstream, so `--apply` is what proves it:"},"3833":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-46","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"it surfaces whatever the registry answers when the pull fails"},"3834":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-47","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-three-modes","content":"`--status` prints the tag a box actually runs"},"3835":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-48","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-targets-file-and-the-walkthrough","content":"`--targets` prints the `sparks.json` that Prometheus reads through `file_sd_configs`; the\nredirect that writes it on the host, the refresh interval, and what an absent file mean\nare in `observability/spark-targets/README.md`."},"3836":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-49","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#the-targets-file-and-the-walkthrough","content":"The box-by-box walkthrough, the counter file the DCGM container is handed, and the failure\nmodes are spark-monitoring.md."},"3837":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-50","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#where-to-look-next","content":"Observability bundle - the ten profile-gated services, the path\na metric takes, the retention, and what the bundle costs on disk"},"3838":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-51","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#where-to-look-next","content":"Spark monitoring - enrolling the three DGX Sparks: the two\nexporter containers, the `SPARK_MONITOR_ENABLED` opt-in, and what `--apply` does to a\nbox."},"3839":{"id":"/operate/monitoring-52","page_id":"/operate/monitoring","tags":["operate","observability","prometheus","alertmanager","spark"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/monitoring#where-to-look-next","content":"Rotate a credential - what to re-check after a key the bundle reads moves"},"3840":{"id":"/operate/secrets","page_id":"/operate/secrets","type":"page","content":"Secrets with Infisical","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Operate the box"],"tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"url":"/operate/secrets"},"3841":{"id":"/operate/secrets-0","page_id":"/operate/secrets","tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/secrets","content":"The opt-in secrets vault: the twelve managed keys, the operator CLI verbs and their exit codes, the adoption sequence, what the workspace boot publishes and what it refuses, what happens when the vault is unreachable, and how a rotated credential reaches its service."},"3842":{"id":"/operate/secrets-1","page_id":"/operate/secrets","type":"heading","tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"url":"/operate/secrets#secrets-with-infisical","content":"Secrets with Infisical"},"3843":{"id":"/operate/secrets-2","page_id":"/operate/secrets","type":"heading","tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"url":"/operate/secrets#what-the-integration-is","content":"What the integration is"},"3844":{"id":"/operate/secrets-3","page_id":"/operate/secrets","type":"heading","tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"url":"/operate/secrets#the-flag","content":"The flag"},"3845":{"id":"/operate/secrets-4","page_id":"/operate/secrets","type":"heading","tags":["secrets","infisical","operate","credentials"],"url":"/operate/secrets#the-truthiness-rule","content":"The truthiness rule"}