for the four reference repos"},"5342":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-33","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"The safety lines that never move"},"5343":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-34","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"**What this enables**"},"5344":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-35","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"Deleting the `development` branch without losing a commit that was only ever on it"},"5345":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-36","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"Deploying dev, staging and production from one commit instead of three builds"},"5346":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-37","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"Shipping work that is not finished, on the trunk, without exposing it"},"5347":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-38","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"Running the same procedure in any of this fleet's repositories with `/trunk-refactor`"},"5348":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-39","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#trunk-based--flags-refactor","content":"This is the human-readable twin of the `trunk-refactor` skill\n(`skills/trunk-refactor/SKILL.md`). The skill is what an agent session follows; this page is\nwhat a person reads, with the examples the skill leaves out to stay short. The branch rules\nthemselves live in Branching - this page is about getting a repository *onto*\nthose rules."},"5349":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-40","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"One long-lived branch. It is normally `main`, it is always deployable, and it is what every\nenvironment is built from."},"5350":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-41","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"An environment is a set of values, a set of secrets, and a place to run. It is a GitHub\nEnvironment, a compose project, a namespace, an inventory group. It is not a git branch."},"5351":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-42","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"Work happens on short-lived branches cut from the tip of the trunk and merged by pull\nrequest within days: `feat/`, `fix/`, `refactor/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `ci/`."},"5352":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-43","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"Incomplete or experimental work lands on the trunk behind a flag that defaults off."},"5353":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-44","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"Promotion is the same commit or tag applied to a different environment. Nothing is rebuilt\nper environment, because a per-environment build is a per-environment bug surface."},"5354":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-45","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-model-in-six-statements","content":"Branch cleanup is part of the work, not a chore someone does later."},"5355":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-46","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#what-the-model-rules-out","content":"long-lived `development`/`staging`/`production` branches"},"5356":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-47","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#what-the-model-rules-out","content":"\"merge to development first\""},"5357":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-48","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#what-the-model-rules-out","content":"a release branch that has to be kept forever"},"5358":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-49","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#what-the-model-rules-out","content":"cherry-picking a fix from one environment branch to another"},"5359":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-50","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#what-the-model-rules-out","content":"a flag platform nobody asked for"},"5360":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-51","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-failure-this-prevents","content":"The failure that motivates all of this is the merge that goes the wrong way."},"5361":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-52","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-failure-this-prevents","content":"A `development` branch that is 134 commits ahead of `main` (a real number from a real repository\nin this fleet) is not a staging area, it is a second product whose differences nobody is\nreconciling, and the day someone finally merges it, the review is unreviewable."},"5362":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-53","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"The skill's twelve binary criteria, in prose. Each needs a command's output as proof."},"5363":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-54","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                          | How you prove it               |\n| --- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| 1   | One trunk, no environment branches | `git ls-remote --heads origin` |","table":"table-0"},"5364":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-55","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                               | How you prove it                                           |\n| --- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2   | No branch holds commits the trunk lacks | `git rev-list --count origin/main..origin/<branch>` is `0` |","table":"table-0"},"5365":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-56","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion      | How you prove it                                                                     |\n| --- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 3   | Trunk is gated | the CI file names a job that runs the full gate on pull request and on push to trunk |","table":"table-0"},"5366":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-57","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                           | How you prove it                              |\n| --- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| 4   | Branch names and ages obey the rule | `git for-each-ref` over `refs/remotes/origin` |","table":"table-0"},"5367":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-58","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                                     | How you prove it                                             |\n| --- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 5   | Every environment has one home for its values | the file or overlay exists and no branch is needed to deploy |","table":"table-0"},"5368":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-59","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                  | How you prove it                                |\n| --- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| 6   | One artifact, many targets | the promotion command block, pasted and working |","table":"table-0"},"5369":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-60","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                         | How you prove it                                                     |\n| --- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 7   | Unfinished work is off by default | the flag's default reads as false in the sample dotenv or flags file |","table":"table-0"},"5370":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-61","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                                | How you prove it                                                                            |\n| --- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 8   | The flag inventory is complete both ways | `grep -rn \"<FLAG>\" .` finds a reader for every declaration and a declaration for every read |","table":"table-0"},"5371":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-62","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion            | How you prove it                              |\n| --- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| 9   | No committed secrets | `git ls-files` shows only sample dotenv names |","table":"table-0"},"5372":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-63","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                    | How you prove it                                                |\n| --- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 10  | The docs agree with the tree | branching doc, contributing, and agent rules say the same thing |","table":"table-0"},"5373":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-64","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion                      | How you prove it                       |\n| --- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| 11  | The repo's own gates are green | the gate command with its summary line |","table":"table-0"},"5374":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-65","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ideal-state-checklist","content":"| #   | Criterion             | How you prove it                                                                         |\n| --- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 12  | Nothing was destroyed | no force-push, no unconfirmed remote delete, every proposed deletion carries its tip SHA |","table":"table-0"},"5375":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-66","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#inventory-first","content":"Before any edit, answer five questions and keep the answers in a scratch file:"},"5376":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-67","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"**Which branches exist, how old are they, who owns them?**"},"5377":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-68","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"**What does each non-trunk branch hold that the trunk does not?**"},"5378":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-69","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`git cherry` marks a commit `-` when an equivalent patch is already upstream. A branch that\nis `ahead=0` behind trunk is done, and its row reads \"delete\" without further argument."},"5379":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-70","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"**How is anything deployed here?** Look, do not assume:"},"5380":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-71","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`compose*.yml`"},"5381":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-72","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`docker-compose*.yml`"},"5382":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-73","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`kustomization.yaml`"},"5383":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-74","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`values.yaml`"},"5384":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-75","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`inventories/`"},"5385":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-76","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`*.tf`"},"5386":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-77","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`argocd/`"},"5387":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-78","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`manage.sh`"},"5388":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-79","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`Makefile`"},"5389":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-80","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`MODULE.bazel`"},"5390":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-81","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`.github/workflows/`"},"5391":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-82","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"`templates/*/main.tf`"},"5392":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-83","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"**What flags already exist?** `grep -rnE 'FEATURE_|_ENABLED|^\\s*profiles:'` over the compose\nfiles, dotenv samples, Terraform variables and scripts."},"5393":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-84","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-five-inventory-questions","content":"**What is the gate you must not break?** `bazelisk test //:test-fast`, `npm test`,\n`make test`, `./manage.sh <check>`, `pytest`, `go test ./...`. Run it before you start so a\nlater red is attributable."},"5394":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-85","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#environments-without-environment-branches","content":"An environment may differ from its neighbour in values, secrets, and where it runs. If a branch\ndiffers in *code*, that code belongs on the trunk behind a flag."},"5395":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-86","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#docker-compose","content":"Name the deployment, not the branch:"},"5396":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-87","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#docker-compose","content":"The project name (`-p`) is what isolates networks, volumes and container names, which is how two\nenvironments share a host. Every published port has to be a value for that to work:\n`\"${APP_PORT:-3000}:3000\"`. Optional services go behind a profile:"},"5397":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-88","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#docker-compose","content":"so `docker compose up` stays clean and `--profile experimental` opts in."},"5398":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-89","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#docker-compose","content":"This fleet's own dev-versus-stable split is the reference implementation: separate project\nnames, separate dotenv files, and a subdomain composed from parts rather than from a branch\nname, driven by `bazelisk run //scripts:dev-stack -- up`,\n`bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack -- up`, and `bazelisk run //scripts:update-stack` for the\npull-and-deploy pair."},"5399":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-90","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#docker-compose","content":"In that repository the environment branches were still sitting on the\nremote (`dev`, `development`, `staging`, `uat`, `prod`) while every one of them reported\n`ahead=0` against `main`: five branches, zero unique commits, waiting for someone to confirm the\ndelete."},"5400":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-91","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#k3s--kubernetes","content":"One namespace per environment, one overlay per environment, one image reference:"},"5401":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-92","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#k3s--kubernetes","content":"Promotion edits the tag, not a branch:"},"5402":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-93","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#k3s--kubernetes","content":"With Helm the same shape is `values/dev.yaml`, `values/staging.yaml`, and\n`helm upgrade --install app ./chart -n lab-staging -f values/staging.yaml --set image.tag=...`.\nSecrets come from the cluster's own store or an external secret, never from the overlay."},"5403":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-94","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ansible","content":"The playbook is the trunk; the environment is inventory:"},"5404":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-95","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#ansible","content":"Promotion is the same playbook revision and role versions against a different inventory. A\nbranch that carries playbook changes is a pull request; a branch that carries only variable\nchanges is a file under `group_vars/`."},"5405":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-96","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#terraform--opentofu-with-argocd","content":"Environment is a workspace or an `envs/<env>/` directory that instantiates one shared module;\n`terraform plan` against `envs/staging` and `envs/production` is the same module revision twice.\nArgoCD gets one `Application` per environment, all pointing at the same Kustomize or chart path,\nand promotion is a commit that bumps the image tag (by hand, or by the Image Updater)."},"5406":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-97","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#terraform--opentofu-with-argocd","content":"A per-environment ArgoCD branch is a sync-drift generator and a rollback trap."},"5407":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-98","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#coder-and-template-parameters","content":"Where the switch selects infrastructure rather than behaviour, use the platform's own parameter\nsurface: a `variable` in the workspace template plus the values each workspace supplies, which is\nhow this stack already separates a development workspace from a stable one. Bump the template\nrevision; do not fork a template per environment."},"5408":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-99","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-flag-ladder","content":"Climb as far as you need and stop."},"5409":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-100","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-flag-ladder","content":"**One env var, read at one seam**, documented in the dotenv sample with its off default. This\ncarries most needs: `FEATURE_AGENT_TUNNEL_V2=0`."},"5410":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-101","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-flag-ladder","content":"**Compose `profiles:`** when what you are hiding is a whole service."},"5411":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-102","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-flag-ladder","content":"**A checked-in `config/flags.yaml`** once there are enough switches that a reviewer cannot\nhold them, or when one tree runs in several environments with different settings. Copy\n`config/flags.yaml.example` from this repository. Keep the schema - `default`, `owner`,\n`description`, `expires`, `environments`, optional `stacks` overrides - and keep the real\nprocess environment winning, so CI and an operator can still force a value."},"5412":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-103","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-flag-ladder","content":"**The platform's parameters** (Terraform variables, Helm values, Ansible vars, Coder template\nvariables) when the flag selects infrastructure."},"5413":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-104","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#a-flag-service-is-an-operator-decision","content":"A flag service, an SDK, or a database-backed flag table is a decision an operator makes\nexplicitly. It is not the default for a home lab or a single-node host, and it is never what a\nfirst pass should add."},"5414":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-105","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"Rules that keep flags alive long enough to be removed:"},"5415":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-106","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"One naming convention. `FEATURE_<THING>` for behaviour, a plain value for a setting. The name\nin the inventory is exactly the name the process reads, so `grep` is a complete audit."},"5416":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-107","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"Off by default on the trunk. An on-by-default flag is an unfinished feature that became\nload-bearing on the day it shipped."},"5417":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-108","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"Owner and expiry on every flag, and one `chore:` pull request that deletes the flag, its\noff-path, and any branch still carrying it."},"5418":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-109","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"Read once, branch there. A flag checked in nine modules is nine edits when it retires."},"5419":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-110","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#rules-that-keep-flags-removable","content":"The gate runs with it off; at least one test or documented smoke command runs with it on."},"5420":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-111","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"One verdict per branch, with the evidence beside it."},"5421":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-112","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict | Test                                                            | What you do       |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| merged  | `rev-list --count` is 0, or `git cherry` marks every commit `-` | list for deletion |","table":"table-1"},"5422":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-113","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict    | Test                                     | What you do                                  |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| superseded | its files exist on trunk in another form | list for deletion, citing what superseded it |","table":"table-1"},"5423":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-114","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict | Test                          | What you do                                                 |\n| ------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| port    | small, complete, still wanted | re-adapt onto a new short-lived branch, open a pull request |","table":"table-1"},"5424":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-115","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict  | Test                    | What you do                          |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| preserve | valuable and incomplete | port behind a flag that defaults off |","table":"table-1"},"5425":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-116","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict | Test                              | What you do                       |\n| ------- | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| dead    | no value, or explicitly abandoned | list for deletion with the reason |","table":"table-1"},"5426":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-117","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#the-verdict-table","content":"| Verdict         | Test                        | What you do                                     |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| release-bearing | carries an untagged version | tag the tip, push the tag, then list the branch |","table":"table-1"},"5427":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-118","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#port-a-branch-by-re-adapting-it","content":"Porting is re-adaptation. Take the files, then fix them against today's trunk:"},"5428":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-119","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#cherry-pick-a-coherent-run","content":"Cherry-picking is for a coherent run of commits you want verbatim, and `-x` keeps the source SHA\nin the message so the provenance survives:"},"5429":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-120","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#cherry-pick-a-coherent-run","content":"A port that also reformats is two pull requests. A port of a whole branch at once is a review\nnobody does properly."},"5430":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-121","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#hand-the-deletions-to-a-human","content":"Then hand the deletions to a human:"},"5431":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-122","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#hand-the-deletions-to-a-human","content":"| Branch      | Age        | Author  | Unique commits | Verdict | Recovery SHA |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ------- | -------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| development | 2026-11-02 | someone | 0              | delete  | `a1b2c3d`    |","table":"table-2"},"5432":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-123","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#hand-the-deletions-to-a-human","content":"| Branch  | Age        | Author  | Unique commits | Verdict | Recovery SHA |\n| ------- | ---------- | ------- | -------------- | ------- | ------------ |\n| staging | 2026-08-14 | someone | 0              | delete  | `e4f5g6h`    |","table":"table-2"},"5433":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-124","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#hand-the-deletions-to-a-human","content":"with the commands they will run:"},"5434":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-125","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#record-the-tip-sha-first","content":"Record the tip SHA of every branch in that table before anything goes. A recorded SHA is\nrecoverable until garbage collection; an unrecorded one is not."},"5435":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-126","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"Verified against the remotes on 2026-11-08. Repositories move: re-run the Phase 0 inventory\nrather than trusting this table."},"5436":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-127","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"| Repository                     | Default | Environment-shaped branches                                    | Deployment mechanism | First move                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toxicoder/evo-t1-coder-stack` | `main`  | `dev`, `development`, `staging`, `uat`, `prod` - all `ahead=0` |                      | Confirm deletion of the five merged branches; the model is already documented |","table":"table-3"},"5437":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-128","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"| Repository                       | Default | Environment-shaped branches                                  | Deployment mechanism                                               | First move                                                                                          |\n| -------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toxicoder/nvidia-dgx-spark-lab` | `main`  | `development` (+ `dev`), `development` 134 ahead / 27 behind | `k8s/` with a `k8s/dev/` overlay, Compose for dashboard and hermes | Port the 134 commits in slices onto `main`, flag-off the unfinished ones, then retire `development` |","table":"table-3"},"5438":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-129","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"| Repository                 | Default | Environment-shaped branches                                                                                      | Deployment mechanism                                                                            | First move                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toxicoder/ez-comfy-stack` | `main`  | `development` (+ `dev`), `development` 523 ahead / 19 behind, plus `feat/`, `fix/`, `feature/`, `docs/` families | Compose (`docker/docker-compose.yml`), `scripts/manage.sh`, Makefile, an image-publish workflow | Port in themed slices; the published image tag is the promotion lever, so land the tag story first and normalise the `feature/` prefix to `feat/` |","table":"table-3"},"5439":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-130","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"| Repository               | Default | Environment-shaped branches                               | Deployment mechanism                           | First move                                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toxicoder/inkorporated` | `main`  | `development` (+ `dev`), `development` 0 ahead / 2 behind | `infrastructure/`, CI plus presubmit workflows | `development` is already merged: list it for deletion, then fix the naming families |","table":"table-3"},"5440":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-131","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"Two patterns worth reading across those rows."},"5441":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-132","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"A branch family that is `ahead=0` (this repo, `inkorporated`) is a cleanup with no risk once a\nhuman confirms it."},"5442":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-133","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"A branch family that is hundreds of commits ahead (`nvidia-dgx-spark-lab`, `ez-comfy-stack`) is\na porting programme: slice by area, land each slice green, and let the flags hold what is not\nfinished."},"5443":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-134","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#per-repository-notes","content":"Both begin with the same inventory, and both end with a table a person signs off on."},"5444":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-135","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"No force-push, no rewritten shared history, no merging your own pull request."},"5445":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-136","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"No remote branch deleted without explicit confirmation, and never a trunk ref."},"5446":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-137","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"No secret in a committed file, including the flags file and per-environment value files.\nSamples hold key names and inert defaults; secrets go to the GitHub Environment or the\ncluster's secret store."},"5447":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-138","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"Keep the existing gates green and extend what exists. No new CI system, no Kubernetes, no\nflag platform, no new dependency."},"5448":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-139","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"One logical change per branch and per pull request, with docs and tests in the same change."},"5449":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-140","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments","refactor"],"type":"text","url":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor#safety-lines","content":"A default-branch rename is its own confirmed step, done after the content has converged,\nbecause GitHub rewrites links, protections and open pull requests when it happens."},"5450":{"id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor-141","page_id":"/workflows/trunk-feature-flags-refactor","tags":["git","branching","ci","feature-flags","environments",