real tree."],[5278,"`/api/v1` on its own is the write-side namespace and answers 404 to a `query_range`, so a\ndatasource pointed there still reads green in the UI and returns nothing in a panel. That\nURL is the single most common cause of this symptom."],[2291,"`/bug-hunt <symptom-or-issue> [--bisect <good-ref>] [--no-fix]` reproduces before\ntouching anything, localises with explorers and a real bisect, tests competing hypotheses\nwith a fleet, and ships the test that fails before the fix and passes after it."],[257,"`/create-skill` is real, but only as a *bundled* platform skill whose catalog is\nfetched per identity/team behind an x.ai sign-in this stack does not have;"],[2297,"`/debugger <symptom|failing-test|issue-number> [--no-fix]` is the gate against the\nguess-and-patch pass: no fix is written until a read-only `agent-explore` child has quoted the\nfailing command and its real output, and the skeptic re-runs both the red and the green run."],[2295,"`/documenter <commit-ish|path|PR-number> [--surface docs|readme|rulebook|comments]` documents\na change that already exists: read the diff, fan read-only mappers over every documentation\nsurface on `agent-explore` to find the text the change made wrong, write one file per writer,\nthen put the result past an independent skeptic on `agent-review` that runs every command the\nnew prose names."],[263,"`/ez-bazel-first` puts every tracked file behind a target and budgets the `glob()`s"],[919,"`/ez-bazel-first`, `/ez-strong-types` and `/ez-trunk-based-repo`, which convert\nwhatever repository the workspace is sitting in"],[2299,"`/ez-code-index [repo-path]` writes the local map described below."],[254,"`/ez-create-skill` scaffolds one from what the operator describes."],[2508,"`/ez-create-skill` stands in for the bundled platform skill\n`create-skill`, which arrives only in the skills\nbundle behind an x.ai sign-in this stack does not have; `/ez-skillify` has no published\nupstream counterpart at all; and the memory family `/ez-learn` copies is upstream\n*built-ins*: `/flush`, `/dream` and `/memory` are gated behind cross-session memory,\nwhich is off by default, while `/remember` is a pager command with no such gate. Either\nway the seed is what makes the three commands exist."],[917,"`/ez-create-skill`, which scaffolds one from a description"],[648,"`/ez-learn` is seeded on the same absent-only contract because nothing here supplies the\ncommand: no published source ships an upstream `/learn` at all, and the built-in memory\nfamily it copies is gated behind a memory store that is off by default, so those names\nstay hidden."],[2118,"`/ez-learn` writes memory files - it reproduces the upstream `/flush`, `/dream`,\n  `/remember` and `/memory`; the other two write skill files."],[252,"`/ez-learn` writes memory files, reproducing the upstream memory family `/flush`,\n`/dream`, `/remember` and `/memory`;"],[915,"`/ez-learn`, which turns a session into durable memory (this stack's copy of the\nupstream `/flush`, `/dream`, `/remember` and `/memory` - the CLI's own commands, not\nskills: flush the conversation into a session log, dream those logs into organized\nmemory, save one note, browse or manage the store. Three of the four are gated on a\nmemory store that is off by default, so they stay hidden until one is configured)"],[920,"`/ez-micro-plan`, which cuts one change into micro tasks for a fleet of subagents\nand checks the cut before wave 1"],[253,"`/ez-skillify` captures the session that just worked into a skill;"],[916,"`/ez-skillify`, which captures the session that just worked"],[264,"`/ez-strong-types` pins a strict checker profile per language and ratchets the\nbroad-type census"],[265,"`/ez-trunk-based-repo` turns environment branches into environments and unfinished\nwork into flags."],[2288,"`/feature-implementation <request-or-issue> [--slots N] [--dry-run]` takes one request\nfrom Plan Mode to a verified change: map with read-only explorers, hand the split to\n`/ez-micro-plan`, fan the writers out, close with an independent tester and reviewer."],[3240,"`/health/liveliness` is the endpoint because it is unprotected and answers `I'm alive!`,\nwhile `/health` sits behind `user_api_key_auth`\n(`health_endpoints/_health_endpoints.py:1938` and `:1110`) and a probe on\nit would need the master key in the container's own command line."],[2453,"`/health` is read without `?check_deployments=true` because that form fires a live\n  completion per deployment and evicts the Spark prompt caches the health-check notes\n  in `litellm/config.yaml` warn about."],[2787,"`/home` is **not** mounted in v1. Hermes cannot see your dotfiles, your SSH keys or\nyour shell history, and it should not need to."],[2298,"`/migrator <dep>@<version>|<api-change>` pins where a version actually lives by `path:line`,\nreads the upstream delta from a research lane rather than from memory, writes the plan and the\nrollback before touching anything, then fans the edits out and answers to a skeptic."],[2733,"`/model <alias>` inside a session"],[2769,"`/opt/data` is a **named volume on purpose**. Hermes keeps a SQLite database there in\nWAL mode, and WAL on a virtiofs bind mount is not safe. Bind-mounting that path is how\nyou corrupt the assistant's own memory."],[2296,"`/performance-optimizer <path|command> [--metric <name>] [--no-change]` takes a baseline with\nan instrument that is already local (`time`, `rg --stats`, Bazel `--profile`), hunts the cost\nwith read-only mappers, ranks proposals by measured cost rather than how bad the code looks,\nlands at most one change, re-measures, and ends its skeptical pass on `agent-review`."],[2531,"`/reflect-and-evolve-repo` is its sibling against a different subject: where\n`/reflect-and-evolve` improves the agent setup, this one reviews past work in *this\nrepository* and turns what it finds into planned improvements to code, project\nconventions, scripts, docs and configs."],[2530,"`/reflect-and-evolve` reviews past Grok Build sessions and turns what it finds into planned changes.\nIt reads the per-session `signals.json` under `~/.grok/sessions/<escaped-cwd>/`, ranked by the bundled\n`skills/reflect-and-evolve/scripts/session_signals.py`, plus the `/ez-learn` session logs and the notes file.\nIt changes the seeds in this repo, never the copies a workspace booted with. Repo-scoped like `/trunk-refactor`\nand not seeded into a workspace home: canonical at `skills/reflect-and-evolve/SKILL.md`, discovered through\nthe `.grok/skills/reflect-and-evolve/SKILL.md` symlink, pinned by `tests/bats/reflect-and-evolve-skill.bats`."],[2290,"`/security-audit <path-or-diff> [--scope secrets|injection|authz|egress] [--json]`\ninventories sources and sinks separately, traces each source to a sink with read-only\ntracers, and ranks findings by severity with one checkable line of proof each."],[2289,"`/skeptical-review <diff-spec|pr-number> [--focus <risk>] [--json]` takes the author's\nclaim as unverified, re-runs the exact commands the producer said proved it, attacks the\nchange from several independent angles, and reports each requirement kept or broken with\nthe line that decides it."],[4840,"`/tmp/coder-startup-script.log` holds exactly one `curl: (28)` line when the\nstart-time download was what failed."],[4703,"`/v1/models` is not the read people try first: it lists the 13 model *aliases*, not the\ndeployments under them, so a box that has been filtered out is invisible there and the\nalias still appears."],[4936,"`# fleet-width:` is the fleet's own ceiling, `max_concurrent` this session's cap\n(`templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl:427-428`, devcontainer twin\n`templates/devcontainer/grok-config.toml.tftpl:428-429`). They stay two lines rather\nthan one number because they answer to two variables: `max_concurrent` is the variable's\nown shipped 15, which an explicit `--var` owns and never moves the ceiling. `15` over `4`\nis this entry; `15` over `15` is\nthe pinned-lane entry above."],[1595,"`# type: ignore` needs a specific error code and a reason that names the real cause.\n`warn_unused_ignores` makes a stale one an error, so an ignore cannot quietly\noutlive the problem it papered over."],[2799,"`<mount>` is the host directory of the Hermes data volume (what compose mounts at\n`/opt/data`). `--force` is how an existing volume picks up the seeded\n`dashboard.trusted_proxies`, and `--cwd /absolute/path/to/checkout` is how a host re-seed\nnames the working directory when the shell running it carries no `STACK_HOST_PATH`."],[4599,"`<wsid>` is a workspace id and `<ws>` a workspace name."],[2477,"`~/.agents/INSTRUCTIONS.md`"],[2490,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-bazel-first/scripts/glob_budget.py`"],[2488,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-bazel-first/scripts/owned_files_check.py`"],[2486,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-bazel-first/SKILL.md`"],[2484,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-create-skill/SKILL.md`"],[2480,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-learn/SKILL.md`"],[2500,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-micro-plan/scripts/plan_check.py`"],[2498,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-micro-plan/SKILL.md`"],[2482,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-skillify/SKILL.md`"],[2494,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-strong-types/scripts/type_baseline.py`"],[2492,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-strong-types/SKILL.md`"],[2496,"`~/.agents/skills/ez-trunk-based-repo/SKILL.md`"],[2478,"`~/.agents/skills/grok-build-delegation/SKILL.md`"],[1229,"`~/.bazelrc` is the seam because Bazel reads it after the repo's `.bazelrc`, and\nbecause it reaches only this container: a Coder workspace booted from the same image\nkeeps using its own `~/.cache`."],[1278,"`~/.coder/AGENTS.md`"],[2475,"`~/.coder/AGENTS.md`"],[2489,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-bazel-first/scripts/glob_budget.py`"],[2487,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-bazel-first/scripts/owned_files_check.py`"],[2485,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-bazel-first/SKILL.md`"],[2483,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-create-skill/SKILL.md`"],[2479,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-learn/SKILL.md`"],[2499,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-micro-plan/scripts/plan_check.py`"],[2497,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-micro-plan/SKILL.md`"],[2481,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-skillify/SKILL.md`"],[2493,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-strong-types/scripts/type_baseline.py`"],[2491,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-strong-types/SKILL.md`"],[2495,"`~/.coder/skills/ez-trunk-based-repo/SKILL.md`"],[2476,"`~/.coder/skills/grok-build-delegation/SKILL.md`"],[1277,"`~/.grok/AGENTS.md`"],[886,"`~/.grok/config.toml` and the code-server `~/.local/share/code-server/User/settings.json`\nare the two rendered files: each is that workspace's own, written from the template on every\nstart, so a temporary hand-edit there survives until that workspace restarts and reaches no\nother workspace, while a re-push plus a restart re-renders it from the latest template."],[4906,"`~/.grok/config.toml` is a real file on this workspace's own home volume, so a swap\nfile outlives a stop of that workspace and nothing else."],[683,"`~/.grok/config.toml` is emitted from a quoted heredoc for the same reason: a\n`Bearer $${GH_TOKEN}` line the config template emits travels through as literal text\ninstead of being expanded there, and the CLI expands it from the agent environment. The\nsame holds for the `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` reference."],[590,"`~/.grok/config.toml` is re-rendered when it is absent, when\n`GROK_FRESH_INSTALL` is set, or while *either* marker is present: the `managed-by`\ncomment or the top-level `__evoT1Stack = true` key."],[2345,"`~/.grok/hooks/` is **marker-aware** on the same rule, with two spellings because its two\nkinds of file have two readers: the `\"__evoT1Stack\": true` key, which is the only marker\nspelling that leaves the manifest parseable JSON, and the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack`\ncomment in the four scripts and the deny list. A guard that drifted from the seed is a\nbehaviour change nobody sees, so this family gets the refresh rather than the first-write\nrule. See Hooks."],[602,"`~/.grok/notes-setup.sh` is the exception to the absent-only rule: it is stack-owned code\nand the copy in this workspace has to be the one this template shipped, so it\nis rewritten every start."],[1281,"`~/.grok/notes-setup.sh` plus this clone's `notes.md`"],[715,"`~/.infisical/agent.env` is what a successful fetch produces: mode `0600` inside a `0700`\n`~/.infisical` (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:37-40`, `:92`, `:244-246`), written by nobody\nelse, staged as `~/.infisical/.agent.env.XXXXXX` in that same directory and `mv`'d in, so\na reader never sees a half-written file - the same write-then-rename discipline\n`~/.grok/notes-setup.sh` uses above."],[3929,"`~/.infisical` rides no per-owner mount at all, so `agent.env` sits on this workspace's own\nhome and only this workspace reads it."],[909,"`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json`"],[951,"`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` is the one rendered target it does reseed, and\nit re-*renders* rather than copies: `${litellm_url}` and the `$${...}`\ndollar-brace unfoldings are rewritten, and that workspace's own `cline.apiKey`\nand `roo.openaiApiKey` are carried forward."],[1275,"`~/.tmux.conf`"],[586,"`~/.tmux.conf` and `~/.grok/AGENTS.md` are rewritten while the\n`managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` line is present; editing the file away from the marker\nhands it to the user for good, and each prints one warning line when it is marker-free."],[567,"`~/.tmux.conf` is seeded *before* the two terminal helpers, which their own\n`coder_script` writes after this body returns. `tmux` reads that file once\nat server start and every terminal (plus an SSH client that reattaches) shares that one\nserver, so seeding after the first `tmux new-session -A` could run would leave that\nsession unconfigured for the whole boot."],[906,"`~/.tmux.conf`, `~/.grok/AGENTS.md`, `~/.coder/AGENTS.md`,\n`~/.agents/INSTRUCTIONS.md`, the two `grok-build-delegation/SKILL.md` copies"],[1719,"`${BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY:-}`"],[1720,"`${GITHUB_WORKSPACE:-}`"],[2797,"`${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY}` stays a token on purpose - Hermes expands it at boot, and a\nbyte of the key in a volume copy is what\nMounts and \"be the host\" argues against."],[1721,"`${PWD}`"],[1718,"`${REPO_ROOT:-}`"],[1722,"`${SELF_DIR}/..`"],[881,"`${VAR}` inside `expose` expands during the shell phase, so compose never sees those\nvariables and a changed value needs a rebuild"],[4172,"`$$((` is two dollars, and Coder runs `coder_script` bodies as `bash -c`, which\nexpands `$$` to the PID. Do not wrap `templatefile()` in `chomp()`."],[4820,"`000` on the first probe means nothing listened on 4000. A `200 application/json`\nmeans LiteLLM answered, so the model lane is healthy and the app lane failed\nsomewhere else."],[4821,"`000` on the second probe means the private lane is down as well, so the public\nfailure is not a cloud-side one. `421` means the Host header matched no\n`server_name` here, which is what a rewritten Host looks like. `STACK_ROUTER_CONF`\nin `.env` names the conf those `server_name` lines live in; the vhost side of it is\nin UI and logins."],[4919,"`15` over `15` is this entry -\nthe number is right and the placement is not. `15` over `4` is a different fault, where\nthe width itself was set, and\nthe rendered-width entry\nis the one that answers it."],[5234,"`421` means this box has no vhost for that Host. `STACK_ROUTER_CONF` in `.env` is\nwhat tells you which conf compose actually mounted, so read that file's\n`server_name` lines first, then recreate `router` so it picks up the one that\nlists `server_name hermes-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io`."],[4177,"`additional_repos` — the `--additional-repos` flag on the new-workspace CLI, and the\n`coder_parameter` of the same name that receives its value in both templates\n(`mutable = true`, default empty): extra git URLs for the workspace's clone folders,\ngiven as `url1,url2` or one URL per line. The flag exists on\n`bazelisk run //scripts:new-workspace` only - the stack runners (`dev-stack`,\n`prod-stack`) have no `--additional-repos` (their flags are `-p`, `-f`, `-e`,\n`--tail`, `--follow`, `--json`, `-y`, `-h`)."],[532,"`additional_repos=<list>` whenever `--additional-repos` named at least one extra URL"],[1027,"`AGENT_MODEL_URL` is the single `/v1/models` URL the \"Agent backend\" card uses\nfor both its browser link and its status probe. It defaults to box 2 - same\n`SPARK2_HOST`, same `SPARK_HTTP_PORT` - and all three boxes serve the same\nmodel id, so point it at any reachable one when you want the card to follow a\nparticular box."],[3249,"`agent-explore: [\"agent-low\", \"coder\"]` and `agent-review: [\"agent-xhigh\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:882-883`)."],[2711,"`agent-explore` bakes `low` for a wave of read-only mappers"],[1048,"`agent-low` is what makes that work cheaper\nthan its parent: the 262144-token window stays and the baked `xhigh` thinking goes, which is\nthe cost the hop exists to stop paying. That is a routing choice with its own trade, not a\nfree win - the summary still runs on a Spark box, at a thinking level turned down."],[2712,"`agent-review` bakes `xhigh` for the skeptics that check what that fleet wrote"],[2713,"`agent-swarm-fast` is `agent-swarm` again for a wave of writers"],[3247,"`agent-swarm` degrades one step further: `agent-swarm: [\"agent\", \"coder\"]`. Health\nstate, cooldowns and in-flight counters are per group, so its own three deployments can\nall be cooled while the same boxes are still healthy under `agent`; `agent` is tried\nfirst, where `least-busy` may still have a box to pick, and Arc `coder` stays the last\nresort it is for every other Spark lane. The chain is acyclic: agent-swarm -> agent ->\ncoder, and `coder` declares no hop of its own."],[2212,"`agent-swarm` is one of four Spark groups with no session pin -\n`agent-explore`, `agent-review` and `agent-swarm-fast` lift it the same way, and\nlitellm-routing.md\nis where what each lane buys is worked out - so each child lands on whichever reachable\nbox has the fewest requests in flight and the ceiling\nbecomes `PARALLEL` per box: 3 boxes x 5 = 15, which is every stream the fleet has and\ntherefore a one-workspace-at-a-time number."],[2691,"`agent-verbs` (whether the assistant can still reach `scripts/coder-sessions.sh`\nand the socket those verbs read)"],[2706,"`agent` also thinks hard by default: it bakes `reasoning_effort: xhigh`.\n**`agent-low`**, **`agent-medium`** and **`agent-xhigh`** are the thinking variants of\nit - the same Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on the same three Spark boxes, with real\n`tool_calls` and that level baked into the alias instead."],[2137,"`agent` carries three `[[model.\"agent\".reasoning_efforts]]` tables (`xhigh` is\nthe default). The `agent-low` / `agent-medium` / `agent-xhigh` / `agent-swarm` /\n`agent-explore` / `agent-review` / `agent-xhigh-fast` / `agent-swarm-fast` aliases\nset `supports_reasoning_effort = false` because LiteLLM bakes the level for\ncallers that have no reasoning-effort field."],[3072,"`agent` is not the unthinking default. It bakes `reasoning_effort: xhigh`, so a\nCoder Agents chat on the default alias thinks hard, and `agent-xhigh` asks the\nbox for the same level by name. A `reasoning_effort` the client sends in the\nrequest still wins over the baked one."],[261,"`agents-seed.sh.tftpl` is the `coder_script \"agents_seed\"` body that writes\n`~/.grok/AGENTS.md` from `GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md`. Marker-aware rather than absent-only: a\ncopy still carrying the stack marker is rewritten on every start, and one whose marker\nlines a person deleted stays theirs. `scripts/lib/config_seed.sh` names the same file and\ntarget for the host-side reseed."],[3816,"`AlertmanagerGap` is critical where those two are warning, and asks both shapes of the\nfault - `absent()` for the service being gone and `up == 0` for a container that runs\nwithout answering."],[927,"`all` runs `env` and then `workspace`."],[2172,"`allow` also carries the verbs the branch-first, commit-per-unit policy needs:\n`Bash(git switch *)`, `Bash(git checkout -b *)` and `-B`, `Bash(git add *)`,\n`Bash(git commit *)`."],[1609,"`allowJs` and `checkJs` 