a LAN IP, or the public coder name in\npublic mode. Never `localhost` and never `127.0.0.1`."],[379,"`coder_agent_url` exists so agents keep dialing the local plain listener when\n`CODER_ACCESS_URL` is a public name."],[2052,"`coder_agent.dir` stays unset: the agent would chdir there before `startup.sh`, and\na missing clone folder would fail the agent. With the sample `REPO_URL` that folder\nis `/home/coder/workspace/evo-t1-coder-stack`."],[746,"`coder_app` resources are not gated on `start_count`. `coder/preview` warns\n`Unexpanded count argument on block coder_app.*` when they are: that value is\nnot expanded at workspace-create preview. Scripts, metadata and the container\nstay gated."],[386,"`CODER_CONTAINER_SERVICE` (default `coder`), `CODER_DB_SERVICE` (default `db`),\n`CODER_CONTAINER_API_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:3000`), `CODER_PUSH_USER`,\n`CODER_PUSH_TOKEN_MINUTES`, `DOCKER_BIN`, `PROBE_TIMEOUT` (20s) and `VERIFY_TIMEOUT`\n(60s) are the overrides."],[4029,"`CODER_DEFAULT_TOKEN_LIFETIME` - a duration, not a secret."],[748,"`coder_devcontainer.repo` is also gated on `start_count`, so the stop / template-import\nephemeral plan has an empty tuple even with the toggle on (the default), and that\nternary then fails with `Invalid index` / `empty\ntuple`."],[2434,"`CODER_EXPERIMENTS` in `.env` (empty by default since 2026-10-08) has never gated\nanything about it: the old `agents` default was not a recognized experiment name,\nand the server logged `ignoring unknown experiment` and ignored it on every boot."],[977,"`CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_REGEX` is only for telling providers or hosts apart;\nomitted, it matches every `github.com` remote."],[733,"`coder_metadata.workspace_info` shows the image, the cloned repository (in `workspace`,\nor `none` when the Git repository field is empty), the LiteLLM URL, the default Grok\nmodel, whether DinD is `on (tcp://dind:2375)` or `off`, and - redacted - which key is\nwired in."],[512,"`coder_script.dind_bootstrap` is an ordering guard, not a starter: it waits up to 120s\n(180s cap) for the sidecar to answer `docker version`, because the agent runs its\n`run_on_start` scripts before it creates the dev containers."],[4165,"`coder_script` bodies are sibling `.tftpl` files next to each `main.tf` (`code-server.sh.tftpl`,\nand on `devcontainer` also `dind-bootstrap.sh.tftpl`) rendered with `templatefile()`."],[4161,"`coder-agents.md`"],[4616,"`coder-agents` provisioning the compose placeholder `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` instead of the\ncheckout's"],[2804,"`coder-workspace` (workspaces and their GitHub auth)"],[2719,"`coder` / `coder-fast` - the Qwen2.5-Coder weights on the Arc. Chat is good, but\nthose weights write the tool call into the message body as plain text, so agent\nturns silently lose their tools. See\nlitellm-routing.md."],[2449,"`coder` and `coder-fast` stay out on purpose: on this stack's IPEX-LLM runtime those\n  weights return tool calls as plain text with no `tool_calls`, and an agent turn without\n  callable tools cannot browse or edit, so registering them would only add a silently\n  broken model to the pickers."],[3023,"`coder` is the terminal hop of every Spark lane, so a 401 or a 404 from a probe would park\nthe fallback for `cooldown_time` with no user request having failed."],[3254,"`coder`, `coder-fast` and `compaction-fast` all answer from the one Ollama container\non the Arc, so a hop between them is a hop to whatever is already down. `agent-low` is\nthe quickest answer the fleet has, which is what a summary was after on this lane in\nthe first place."],[2805,"`coding-agents` (what the coding agents in those workspaces are doing right now,\nand how to answer, start, or stop one — the `//scripts:coder-sessions` verbs)"],[4864,"`command -v grok` answering `~/.grok/bin/grok` is the normal answer, not a leftover\ninstaller copy: the workspace `PATH` lists `~/.grok/bin` before `/usr/local/bin`, and\nthat entry is a symlink into `~/.grok/downloads/`, which holds one file per downloaded\nrelease and is where `grok update` installs - so moving it aside does not outlast the\nnext self-update."],[4748,"`compaction router: moved a summary call from agent-xhigh-fast to compaction-fast` is the\nhop firing, once per summary, onto the tier it landed on: `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_TARGET`\nfor a summary within the guard (default `compaction-fast`, which degrades to `agent-low`\nthen `coder`) or `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` for one above it (default\n`agent-low`)."],[3253,"`compaction-fast` degrades to a Spark rather than to another Arc alias -\n`- compaction-fast: [\"agent-low\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:893`) - and that direction is the point."],[3077,"`compaction-fast` is that hop's small-summary target, and a row no template offers a client: no\n`reasoning_effort` line, no tool-calling flags, and `max_input_tokens: 32768` rather\nthan the Spark rows' 262144, because a summary is prose and 32768 is the honest\nwindow of those weights."],[3104,"`compaction-fast` needs no triple: the Arc is one box and its single deployment is\n`compaction-fast-arc`."],[5380,"`compose*.yml`"],[995,"`config.toml` is not\npart of the share: each workspace renders its own on every start, so this\nworkspace's model, theme and extras are its own and no sibling's boot overwrites\nthem."],[410,"`config.toml` is that workspace's own file in both modes, and switching needs a\nrebuild."],[1235,"`configure.sh` finishes by starting `library-scripts/warmup.sh` detached (`setsid`, so\nthe Dev Containers CLI's teardown of the postCreate process group does not take it\nwith it). It runs two commands, in this order:"],[550,"`connection_timeout = 300`."],[2450,"`context_limit` is the agent's own compaction budget (a 70 per cent default\n  compaction threshold applies), which is why it is pinned per alias. The\n  two fast-compaction lanes are absent too, for a mechanical reason rather than a measured\n  one: the hop keys on the summary instruction the Grok CLI appends, the aibridge behind\n  these pickers never sends one, and `compaction-fast` is no client alias at all, so an\n  Agents chat on `agent-xhigh-fast` would be a chat on `agent-xhigh` under a longer name."],[4033,"`CONTEXT7_API_KEY` - the optional Context7 MCP lane's upstream key, forwarded as\n`context7_api_key` by `scripts/push-template.sh:573-577` and seeded into\n`~/.grok/config.toml` by `//scripts:seed-dev-env`. Most operators never set it, and\n`pull` prints one `warning:` per inventory key the vault does not carry, so shipping\nit in the inventory would make the default state a warning on every fetch."],[2408,"`CONTEXT7_API_KEY` is optional and the lane does not\n  depend on it: an empty value sends no `Authorization` header at all, so the server\n  handshakes and answers at the public rate limit, with private libraries the only\n  thing out of reach. A key in `.env` plus a re-push fills the env."],[2161,"`context7_mcp` (default `true`, parked the same way with `CONTEXT7_MCP=false`) adds\nthe cached `context7` stdio MCP server."],[3411,"`CONTRIBUTING.md`"],[4932,"`contributor` means\n  `bazelisk run //scripts:seed-dev-env` did, and that path takes the lane from the\n  `GROK_SUBAGENTS_LANE` environment variable (`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh`), defaulting to\n  `agent-swarm`, the width from `GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT`\n  (`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh:193`, the variable's own shipped `15`), and the ceiling from\n  `GROK_SWARM_WIDTH` (`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh:185`), so a contributor home carries the same\n  two numbers."],[3012,"`cooldown_time: 60` is how long a box that tripped the rate rule sits out, and it is\nalso the fail window that rule counts over."],[4421,"`Could not resolve host: github.com` -> Tailscale MagicDNS is the only nameserver"],[3669,"`CPU`"],[2237,"`ctx/L0.md` is frozen before wave 1, because children already running read the copy that\nwas there when\nthey started - editing it mid-run is a re-dispatch, not an edit."],[1784,"`custom.css` lives in `/app/config` and is served by the allow-listed\n`/api/config/custom.css` route. It styles the sign-in page too, so keep internal\nhostnames out of it."],[1216,"`customizations.vscode.settings` carries container-scoped settings only:"],[4621,"`DASHBOARD_ENV_FILE` points the rotation at another file and exists for test harnesses;\nthere is deliberately no flag for it, because a flag that names a file this CLI\noverwrites is one mistype away."],[5274,"`DashboardScenePage.tsx:171 skipping rendering` is a leftover `console.log` in\nGrafana's own bundle (`public/app/features/dashboard-scene/pages/DashboardScenePage.tsx`,\nread out of the pinned image's source map). It prints when the page declines to render\nfor one pass because the route's dashboard uid changed under it, which is the normal\npath for any navigation between dashboards and for a trip to or from Home."],[3963,"`DB_CONNECTION_URI` and the db service's `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` both interpolate\n`INFISICAL_DB_PASSWORD`, which is the only thing keeping the role and its pointer in step\nacross a rotation."],[2307,"`debug-fix` (`{ symptom, issue, bisect }`) is the defect shape: evidence on `agent-explore`\nbefore any edit, because **Reproduce** quotes the failing command with the output it really\nproduced and no reproduction means no fix; two read-only explorers then localise on disjoint\nhypotheses (one bisecting when a known-good ref is given), one writer on `agent-swarm` lands\nthe fix with the test that is red before the change and green after, and a skeptic on\n`agent-review` re-runs both runs."],[416,"`default` (the CLI's own policy, which does prompt)"],[4734,"`DefaultRetries: 2` is untouched on purpose - TensorFold's `NoRoom` refusal arrives as\n`APIConnectionError`, which is absent from `_RETRIES_BY_EXCEPTION_TYPE`, so that walk\nfalls through to `DefaultRetries` and keeps its two attempts. The proxy reads the file\nat boot:"],[3034,"`DefaultRetries` is the only field that can reach the error,\nwhich is why each agent lane declares one:"],[3414,"`dependabot.yml`"],[2810,"`deploy-from-github` (a named repository to running, with the read-first,\npin-the-ref, isolate, preflight, health-check, keep-a-rollback order)"],[1375,"`description` is printed as the lead paragraph under the title and indexed for search. Quote\nit when it contains a colon, or YAML reads the line as a mapping."],[4583,"`dev-stack status` says `running`, never `healthy` -> those four images have no shell"],[3605,"`dev-stack.sh` and `prod-stack.sh` in their `compose_prefix()` and `run_compose()`"],[3768,"`dev-stack` does the same for the dev one"],[4174,"`devcontainer.json` — a file the *application repository* carries, and the one thing the\n`devcontainer` template builds. `coder_devcontainer.repo` in\n`templates/devcontainer/main.tf` sets no `config_path`, so `@devcontainers/cli` on the\nDinD sidecar searches the clone for `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` (or a\n`devcontainer.json` anywhere inside it)."],[4173,"`devcontainer` — the dev-container template (directory `templates/devcontainer`, Coder\ntemplate name `devcontainer`), always backed by its own DinD sidecar. Its sibling is\n`workspace`: directory `templates/workspace`, template name `workspace`, the plain\ndev container with the optional `dind` parameter."],[238,"`devcontainer` (`templates/devcontainer/`) is the DinD-backed one."],[2513,"`devcontainer` and `workspace` both seed it, so the seed is *not* fetched from\nGitHub any more: no `web_search`/`web_fetch` call is needed to inspect this repo,\nand the instruction text tells the agent so."],[424,"`devcontainer` asks two questions instead: **Git repository** and **Build repo's dev\ncontainer** (`use_devcontainer`, Yes/No, immutable), plus the same Grok and theme fields."],[2048,"`devcontainer` has no persistent prefix to reuse, so it installs the pinned release\n  fresh under `/tmp/code-server` on every start."],[240,"`devcontainer` reuses `workspace`'s variables. `repo_url` exists in both; `dind` does\nnot exist in `devcontainer`."],[2899,"`devcontainer`, which builds the clone's own `.devcontainer` on a DinD sidecar"],[286,"`devcontainer`: **Devcontainer default** (the template default) and **Plain clone**."],[4514,"`did not find docker image 'docker:29.8.1-dind'` -> plan-time failure, not runtime"],[494,"`dind` is not a variable here. A devcontainer workspace without a daemon is nothing,\nand the plain-clone fallback still wants a daemon its `docker` commands can reach."],[531,"`dind=true` on `--dind`"],[1814,"`disableIndexing: true` is the whole anti-crawler measure: the app then serves\n`/robots.txt` with `User-agent: *` / `Disallow: /`, and writes no robots meta tag into\nthe page."],[1588,"`disallow_any_explicit` refuses `Any` typed into a signature by a person."],[1589,"`disallow_any_generics` refuses `list` and `dict` written without their element\ntype, which are the same hole reached by a different spelling."],[2745,"`discover_models: false` on the `litellm` row is what keeps it out of the list - left\non, Hermes probes the proxy's `/v1/models` and adopts whatever it advertises."],[2045,"`display_apps.web_terminal` stays **off**: it would open a shell on the agent's\nworking dir (`/home/coder`). A custom command-type `coder_app` named **Web\nTerminal** (`order = 6`, after **VS Code Web** at `order = 5`, before **GitHub\nreauth** at `order = 7` and **Install GitHub App** at `order = 8`) takes that slot,\n`cd`s to the clone folder - an empty `repo_url` keeps it on `/home/coder` - and\nexecs a login shell. Like the built-in, it reads no `terminal.integrated.*`\nsettings."],[724,"`display_apps` gives: the **VS Code Desktop** helper (a locally installed VS Code /\nCursor / Windsurf plus the `coder.coder-remote` extension), port forwarding, and the\nSSH helper."],[480,"`docker build`, `docker run` and `docker compose` then work inside the workspace. The\n*AI workspace + DinD* preset is the usual way to get this shape, since the client\nbinaries