et as a single operator CLI (`serve`, `build`, `preview`,\n`verify`, `typecheck`, `test`, `nav`, `status`, `clean`) for a host that has Node but not Bazel."],[271,"`documenter.SKILL.md`, `performance-optimizer.SKILL.md`, `debugger.SKILL.md` and\n`migrator.SKILL.md` are the stack's four advisor commands (`/documenter`,\n`/performance-optimizer`, `/debugger`, `/migrator`), `ez-code-index.SKILL.md` is the fifth\nand ships its helper `ez-code-index.code_index.py` in a `scripts/` subdir of the same skill\ndirectory, and `documenter.AGENT.md` is the one role definition the `/documenter` skill\ndispatches. What each does and which lane each phase rides is\ngrok-build-and-agents.md."],[4240,"`domain.sh` reads no flag for either of them, so both names still compose and still\nreach `HOMEPAGE_ALLOWED_HOSTS`, which is the safer half of that trade."],[4491,"`E325: ATTENTION / Found a swap file by the name \"~/.grok/.config.toml.swp\"` -> a vim the last workspace stop killed"],[4684,"`enable_health_check_routing: true` in `general_settings`. Without it,\n`_async_filter_health_check_unhealthy_deployments` (`router.py:14137`) is a no-op at\n`router.py:14153`, and `async_get_available_deployment` (`router.py:13041`) hands\nleast-busy the whole list."],[3208,"`enable_health_check_routing` off"],[5147,"`env -u GH_TOKEN -u GITHUB_TOKEN <command>` makes git or gh use that slot\nfor one command; `fix` makes it permanent for git. See\nthe Bad credentials entry."],[889,"`env` reconciles one env file with its twin. It:"],[4420,"`error: .../.env not found` from `bazelisk run //scripts:dashboard-password` -> the runfiles copy has no working `.env`"],[4518,"`Error: No configuration files` from `push-template` -> runfiles symlinks in the tar"],[5190,"`error: the Infisical export failed; <file> is\n  untouched` when the CLI could not reach the vault"],[1231,"`EVO_T1_BAZEL_CACHE_ROOT` is the one value both halves read, so the mount targets and the\nblock move together, and `bazelisk test //tests:bats_contributor_devcontainer_test` fails\nif they drift."],[1042,"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT` (default `24000`) is the guard, and it\npicks a tier rather than ending the hop."],[1040,"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_LANES` (default `agent-xhigh-fast,agent-swarm-fast`)\nnames the model groups that may hop - name one of them to narrow the hop to\nthat lane alone."],[1045,"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_SPARK_TARGET` (default `agent-low`) is where a summary\nabove the guard goes instead: a Spark group, so it carries the 262144-token\nwindow a full-size summary needs, at thinking baked `low` rather than `xhigh`."],[1041,"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_TARGET` (default `compaction-fast`) is the tier a\nsummary under the guard is moved to."],[1039,"`EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION` (default on) is the kill switch: `0`, `false`, `off` or\n`no` stop the hop outright, and a value that is none of those nor `1`, `true`,\n`on`, `yes` leaves it off too, with one warning line naming what was read."],[1244,"`EVO_T1_WARMUP=off` is the only knob. It reaches the container through\n`containerEnv`'s `${localEnv:EVO_T1_WARMUP}`, so a laptop can opt out permanently from\nits own shell profile without editing the config, and an unset value keeps the default."],[3672,"`evo-sparks-fleet` declares no variable at all, because it aggregates across every box by\ndesign."],[3662,"`evo-sparks-overview` and `evo-spark-host` each declare a `host` templating variable, both\nof them a `query` variable whose query is `label_values(spark:box_up, hostname)`, so the\ndropdown lists the boxes Prometheus actually sees and nothing else. On `evo-spark-host` the\nvariable is labelled `Spark` and every panel on the page filters to whatever it holds."],[2803,"`evo-stack-ops` (pull, status, restart, logs for this stack)"],[1606,"`exactOptionalPropertyTypes` collides with React's optional DOM props and with\nfumadocs' `StaticOptions`"],[2215,"`explore` and the seeded `explorer` from `grok_explore_lane` (default `agent-explore`)"],[2276,"`explorer` is the one definition here that inherits the MCP catalog, because it is the one\nwhose tools name\n`search_tool` and `use_tool`; the other five set `mcpInheritance: none`,\nthe frontmatter key the guide documents for that choice\n(`~/.grok/docs/user-guide/16-subagents.md:228`), on the seeds' own reasoning that an\ninherited catalog with no MCP tool in `tools:` would be empty anyway."],[673,"`ez_learn_skill`, `ez_skillify_skill` and `ez_create_skill_skill` belong to the\n`coder_script.stack_skills` map"],[4154,"`ez-bazel-first.glob_budget.py`"],[4153,"`ez-bazel-first.owned_files_check.py`"],[4152,"`ez-bazel-first.SKILL.md`"],[262,"`ez-bazel-first.SKILL.md`, `ez-strong-types.SKILL.md` and `ez-trunk-based-repo.SKILL.md`\nare the stack's three repository-conversion commands, and they stand in for nothing\nupstream:"],[4150,"`ez-create-skill.SKILL.md`"],[4148,"`ez-learn.SKILL.md`"],[251,"`ez-learn.SKILL.md`, `ez-skillify.SKILL.md` and `ez-create-skill.SKILL.md` are the\nstack's three skill commands:"],[4159,"`ez-micro-plan.plan_check.py`"],[4158,"`ez-micro-plan.SKILL.md`"],[4149,"`ez-skillify.SKILL.md`"],[4155,"`ez-strong-types.SKILL.md`"],[4156,"`ez-strong-types.type_baseline.py`"],[4157,"`ez-trunk-based-repo.SKILL.md`"],[3055,"`fallbacks_by_model` does not exist in this tag (the proxy warns and ignores an unknown\n`router_settings` key, so a config that looks correct silently does nothing, which is why\n`//tests:bats_litellm_config_test` rejects it by name)."],[3011,"`fallbacks:` carries the degrade path `agent: [\"coder\"]`, repeated for each thinking\nalias, because those groups go down with exactly the same boxes. The four unpinned\nlanes and the two fast-compaction lanes hop one step further, through the lane that\nbakes their own level, so a lane that asked for `low` is not served an `xhigh` answer\nby its fallback."],[5136,"`fatal:\n  Authentication failed for 'https://github.com/...'`"],[5137,"`fatal: could not read Username\n  for 'https://github.com'`"],[4419,"`FileAccessException` / `Permission denied` on `homepage/assets/icons/evo-t1.svg` -> leftover runfiles bind-mount"],[56,"`fix/…` means a defect that is already on `main`."],[5168,"`fix` is idempotent, keeps every token off\nargv and out of any file it creates, and repairs the helper plus the store it reads."],[562,"`flock -n` keeps it to one loop per leaf across repeated starts."],[5098,"`focus-events` is what gives tmux a focused client to work with at\nall. `aggressive-resize` stays at its default on purpose: its own entry in\n`options-table.c` scopes it to the `smallest` and `manual` `window-size` modes,\nthe shipped default is `latest`, and tmux(1) calls it \"poor for interactive\nprograms such as shells\"."],[3666,"`Framebuffer fill`"],[2214,"`general-purpose` and the seeded `implementer` and `tester` from `grok_subagents_lane`"],[5269,"`GET /apis/quotas.grafana.app/v0alpha1/namespaces/default/usage?group=dashboard.grafana.app&resource=dashboards`\nanswering `501 (Not Implemented)` is upstream grafana/grafana#136271: with\n`unified_storage.overrides_path` unset the resource server's quota service is nil and\nrefuses the call, while the browse-dashboards view fires it on every page load."],[3632,"`GF_LOG_FILTERS: search-manifest-watcher:error` drops that one logger to `error` and\nleaves every other logger at its default."],[3635,"`GF_UNIFIED_STORAGE_OVERRIDES_PATH: /etc/grafana/stack-overrides.yml`\npoints the unified-storage resource server at the file the table names: without it the\nquota lookup the browse view fires on every dashboard page answers 501, since that\nserver's quota service is nil with nothing pointed at it (grafana/grafana#136271), and the\nbox prints one error line per page load while the browser console fills with 501s; with it\nthe same call answers 200."],[5129,"`gh refused the token, so the\n  store is unchanged` means the credential is revoked or the account disconnected, so run\n  `check` to see what github.com says about it, then take the clicks from\n  the reauth entry."],[1199,"`GH_STACK_ENABLED` is the one build-time choice that sits outside that file, because it\nis a flag rather than a pin. The image installs the official `github/gh-stack` GitHub CLI\nextension (stacked pull requests, invoked as `gh stack`) only for a build that passes\n`GH_STACK_ENABLED=true`, so it ships **off by default** and a normal build says nothing\nabout it. Turn it on with `GH_STACK_ENABLED=true bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image`:\nthe script forwards the flag to the guarded `RUN` in `images/dev/Dockerfile`, only an\nexact `true` enables the layer, and what it installs stays pinned by `GH_STACK_VERSION` in\n`tool-versions.env`. Owner: the stack image build (that script and that layer). Expiry:\n2027-02-23, by which point the extension is either on by default or the flag and its\noff-path are deleted in one `chore:`."],[4163,"`gh-token-refresh.sh.tftpl`"],[279,"`gh-token-refresh.sh.tftpl` is the shared GitHub-token refresh `coder_script`,\nrendered with `templatefile()` so `${github_auth_id}` and\n`${coder_github_app_install_url}` interpolate."],[4166,"`gh-token-refresh.sh.tftpl`, `stack-skills.sh.tftpl` (the body that seeds the\n`ez-learn` / `ez-skillify` / `ez-create-skill` trio) and `stack-repo-skills.sh.tftpl` (the\nbody that seeds the four-command repository family `ez-bazel-first` / `ez-strong-types` /\n`ez-trunk-based-repo` / `ez-micro-plan`, each python helper into a `scripts/` subdir\nbeside its `SKILL.md`)\nare the three that live in\n`templates/common/` instead, so both twins share one copy of them."],[4551,"`gh: command not found` inside a workspace -> the helper needs gh"],[809,"`gh`\nconsults the same pair before its own store, so inside that workspace `gh` needs\n`env -u GH_TOKEN -u GITHUB_TOKEN gh <args>` for the whole of its life; `git` needs no\nprefix once the helper is the env-proof form above, which is what `fix` installs."],[4550,"`gh` answers `Bad credentials` -> the stale env pair, not the store"],[826,"`gh` refusing a healthy store is its own entry there, at\n`gh` answers `Bad credentials`,\nand a workspace with no `gh` binary at\n`gh: command not found`."],[71,"`git add -A`, `git add .`, and `git commit -a` are how a scratch file, a build artifact, or\nsomeone else's edit walks into a commit - and the secret hygiene rule above depends on the\nagent being able to say what is in each one."],[5378,"`git cherry` marks a commit `-` when an equivalent patch is already upstream. A branch that\nis `ahead=0` behind trunk is done, and its row reads \"delete\" without further argument."],[76,"`git diff --stat main...HEAD` matches what was meant"],[2174,"`git push` is absent on purpose - the one step that leaves the machine keeps a human in\nit - and so is\nanything that can lose work (`git branch -D`, `git restore`,\n`git reset --hard`). The deny side closes the two ways a commit could land with\nno gate having seen it:"],[801,"`GIT_ASKPASS`, when no helper answers. Where the staged binary is alive it mints on\ndemand; where it answers `unrecognized subcommand` git gets no answer at all and falls\nthrough to prompting, which is where `could not read Username` comes from."],[3433,"`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` and an empty credential helper keep a scaffold that turned private from\nhanging on a prompt nobody can answer inside a workspace."],[1219,"`git.branchProtection` for `main`"],[5179,"`git` needs no prefix once `fix` has run, because the helper it installs clears the pair\nitself:"],[2160,"`github_mcp` (default `true`, so the block renders unless you park it with\n`GITHUB_MCP=false` and re-push) adds the `github` HTTP MCP server\n(`https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/`), whose `Authorization` header references\n`${GH_TOKEN}` **by name**, so no token value is ever part of a template variable.\nThe agent environment fills it from the Coder External Auth provider (id `github` by default); a\nworkspace whose owner connected no GitHub account renders the block anyway and pays\none failed handshake per session."],[374,"`GITHUB_MCP`, `CONTEXT7_MCP` and `SEARCH_MCP` share one polarity: all three MCP blocks\nship from the template default (`true`), so the only value worth setting is `false`,\nand `true`/unset/empty pushes nothing at all."],[3665,"`GPU util`"],[2093,"`grok doctor` checks terminal, clipboard and microphone support without starting a\nsession, and `/doctor` inside a session adds the checks that need a live one. Each\nitem in the **Findings** list carries its own fix, and `--json` prints the same\nreport for a script. What the report should read here:"],[1895,"`grok doctor` findings in a workspace"],[4480,"`grok doctor` flags `voice.no-input-device` or `terminal.limited-color` -> a headless container, and where you ran the command"],[4790,"`grok mcp doctor searxng` inside the workspace probes the MCP hop. A healthy\nsearch-check plus a failed handshake points at the server, the URL or the port."],[4799,"`grok mcp doctor` inside the workspace lists the declared servers and their handshake."],[4141,"`GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md`"],[243,"`GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md` is the orchestration-protocol seed text that becomes every\nworkspace's `~/.grok/AGENTS.md` (read with `file()`, chomped). It rides\n`coder_script.agents_seed` rather than the startup script, for the reason that section\ngives: it is the largest payload the twins inline."],[674,"`grok_build_agents` to `coder_script.agents_seed`"],[2164,"`grok_config_extra` appends whatever the create form's **Grok config extras** field\nholds, verbatim under its own comment header."],[684,"`grok_config` arrives already rendered from `grok-config.toml.tftpl`. Its boolean keys\n`github_mcp`, `search_mcp` and `context7_mcp` only decide whether their\n`[mcp_servers.*]` block appears, and no credential byte is part of that decision;\n`search_url` supplies the URL the searxng block dials, and the workspace affinity key is\na per-workspace routing hint (a workspace UUID, not a secret)."],[957,"`GROK_EXPLORE_LANE`, `GROK_PLAN_LANE` and `GROK_REVIEW_LANE` the aliases the\nreader, the planner and the skeptic ride"],[583,"`GROK_FRESH_INSTALL` records that an install *completed* this boot - the second\n`command -v` probe inside the install branch is what sets it, so a failed download leaves\nthe flag at `0`."],[959,"`GROK_PERMISSION_MODE` (default `always-approve`) the `[ui]` approval mode - the\nsame choice the create form makes with `grok_permission_mode`, over the same accepted\nset (`default`, `ask`, `auto`, `always-approve`)"],[992,"`GROK_PROFILE_MODE` in the twin is the default for the template variable\n`grok_profile_mode`, which the create form also shows per workspace as the **Grok\nprofile** dropdown."],[955,"`GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT` the width"],[956,"`GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_DEPTH` the nesting depth (the `grok_subagent_max_depth` template\nvariable)"],[954,"`GROK_SUBAGENTS_LANE` names the lane the writers ride"],[2227,"`GROK_SUBAGENTS_LANE` names the writers' lane and `GROK_SUBAGENT_MAX_CONCURRENT` the width,\nwhich defaults to the same `default = 15` the variable ships in both twins' `coder.tf`, so\nthe seeder and the template agree on the width without a second knob."],[4927,"`GROK_SUBAGENTS_MAX_DEPTH` in the agent environment outranks what `config.toml` says, so\na workspace that nests differently from its rendered config is carrying that key;\n`env | grep GROK_SUBAGENTS` names it."],[2228,"`GROK_SWARM_WIDTH`\n(default 15) now feeds only the `# fleet-width:` line the seed writes directly above the\nwidth, `scripts/seed-dev-env.sh:286`, so a contributor home carries the same pair a\nworkspace renders; `GROK_EXPLORE_LANE` (default `agent-explore`),\n`GROK_PLAN_LANE` (default `agent`) and `GROK_REVIEW_LANE` (default `agent-review`) name the\nthree role lanes the same way."],[3047,"`grok_swarm_width` (3 boxes x `PARALLEL` 5) is the fleet's own ceiling, rendered as the\n`# fleet-width:` line beside `max_concurrent`, and the width a workspace gets only when\nit sets `grok_subagent_max_concurrent = null` on purpose. So an operator who shares the\nfleet shrinks it with two knobs, not one: `grok_swarm_width` moves the ceiling and\n`grok_subagent_max_concurrent` moves the width. Drop the first alone and the session\nstill ships 15, and 15 streams over a 10-stream fleet is refused by the box with\n`NoRoom`."],[3133,"`grok_swarm_width` (default 15) is the fleet's own ceiling, rendered as the\n`# fleet-width:` line beside `max_concurrent`."],[962,"`GROK_SWARM_WIDTH` is the fleet's own ceiling, and here it feeds only the\n`# fleet-width:` line the seeder renders beside `max_concurrent` - the same line\nthe templates render from `grok_swarm_width`, so the two agree because each one\nships 15, not because the seeder falls back to the fleet."],[958,"`GROK_THEME` (default `grokbuild`) the `[ui]` theme name"],[4147,"`grok-build-delegation.SKILL.md`"],[250,"`grok-build-delegation.SKILL.md` and `coder-agents.md` are the Coder Agents\nskill and instruction seeds (chomped `file()`)."],[315,"`grok-build-delegation.SKILL.md` still rides the startup argument - it predates the\n  split, it fits, and its own tests pin it there."],[4145,"`grok-build-terminal.sh`"],[770,"`grok-build-terminal` keeps its own session, `grok-build-<folder>-<hash>`, keyed off\nthe repository root found with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (or the terminal's own\n`$PWD` outside a clone) and runs `grok --cwd <that root>` inside it."],[4473,"`grok` -> `command not found` inside a workspace -> the CLI was never installed"],[2784,"`group_add: ${DOCKER_GID}` plus the socket is the same credential the `coder` service\nalready holds: root-equivalent on the host."],[5131,"`HANDOFF` means there is no credential anywhere in reach: click **GitHub reauth**,\nfinish device-code login, install the Coder GitHub App if the reauth page says to, and\nrestart."],[3020,"`health_check_ignore_transient_errors: true` is load-bearing rather than tidy. A box\nthat is merely busy can answer a 16-token probe with a 429 or a 408, and with the\nkey on those endpoints are dropped before the state is written\n(`proxy_server.py:3971-3974`) and again before the cooldown loop takes them\n(`proxy_server.py:4002-4006`). Flipping it off would cost a session-pinned\nconversation its warm box and that box's prompt cache its next prefill, over one\nslow probe."],[3209,"`health_check_interval` unset or <= 0, which returns from the probe loop before it ever\nstarts (`proxy_server.py:4071`)"],[3028,"`health_check_staleness_threshold` has to be named because the shipped default does\nnot follow the interval: it is `DEFAULT_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL * 2`, 600 s whatever\n`health_check_interval` says (`router.py:993`), and it is the window the health filter\ntrusts before it stops filtering. 900 s is what keeps a slow sweep from opening that\nwindow; see how long it takes, and how it comes\nback."],[2742,"`hermes --provider arc-chat` does not need the model named beside it - it sends\n`chat` on its own, and `-m <alias>` is there only to send something else through\nthat row. A run that names no flag is untouched by any of this, so the default stays\n`agent` and a healthy Spark box behaves exactly as before."],[2775,"`hermes config get terminal.cwd` still prints the token because the config *loader*\ndoes expand `${VAR}`"],[2735,"`hermes config set model.default <alias>` to persist it in the live config under\n`/opt/data`"],[5245,"`hermes config set` on `dashboard.trusted_proxies` is the in-container\nalternative. `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL` does not need that reseed."],[2664,"`HERMES_API_BIND` if something off this host should reach it"],[2817,"`HERMES_DASHBOARD_INSECURE` does not remove that requirement. Leave\n`approvals.mode` on `manual`."],[2701,"`HERMES_DASHBOARD_INSECURE` is a deprecated no-op. Setting it changes nothing and buys\nnothing, and it is not how the public name is opened."],[5227,"`HERMES_DASHBOARD_INSECURE` is a no-op. Logs:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack -- logs hermes`."],[5243,"`HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL` has to be the public origin. Bootstrap writes\n`STACK_HERMES_URL` from a `hermes-*` or `hermes.*` entry, and compose copies\nthat into `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL`. The variable is environment: recreate\nthe container after bootstrap."],[2634,"`HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL` is environment and applies when the container is\nrecreated."],[2786,"`HERMES_UID` / `HERMES_GID` are set to the host operator, so a file Hermes writes into\n`$STACK_HOST_PATH` is yours to commit and not owned by uid 10000."],[2777,"`hermes-bootstrap` renders the placeholder in the seeded `config.yaml` at seed time\n(`--cwd DIR` overrides what it renders), which is the part that fixes a long-lived box."],[2683,"`hermes-doctor` answers the second question. It is read-only and prints key names with\nno value."],[2682,"`hermes-shell -- check` answers \"can I open the assistant\". It cannot answer \"is this\nstill the assistant this repo describes\", and the two come apart on a long-lived box:\nan operator edits the config inside the volume, a recreate reads a stale `.env`, a\nmerge changes the seed and a seed-only-when-absent copy never takes it."],[2780,"`hermes/skills/` is tracked in git. Add a skill by editing the repo, never by editing\nthe volume; the volume copy is not the record."],[3579,"`hermes`"],[5076,"`history-limit` reads 100000 but a pane still forgets old output: tmux applies\nthe option when the pane is created, so that pane keeps the limit it was born\nwith. Open a new pane, or restart the server with `tmux kill-server`."],[688,"`HOME` is passed explicitly through `env` because\n`runuser` keeps the invoker's environment; a root agent would otherwise hand git `/root`\nand miss those files entirely. An empty prefix means \"run git directly\", which is correct\nfor a non-root agent and for a root agent with no derivable workspace user."],[1776,"`HOMEPAGE_AUTH_PASSWORD` holds the plaintext, because\nhomepage hashes that env var itself but still needs the value."],[1782,"`homepage/config/*.yaml` plus `custom.css` are bind-mounted read-only, so `git diff`\nstays the record of dashboard changes, and the directory itself has to stay writable\nbecause the app creates `logs/` inside it."],[3577,"`homepage`"],[273,"`hooks.evo-t1-hooks.json` is the hook manifest Grok Build reads at\n`~/.grok/hooks/evo-t1-hooks.json`, and five more files land under `hooks/bin/` beside it:\nthe four handlers it names (`hooks.secret-guard.sh`, `hooks.dangerous-command-guard.sh`,\n`hooks.post-edit-format.sh`, `hooks.selective-test-runner.sh`) plus the\n`hooks.deny-patterns.txt` the command guard reads one ERE per line. The manifest has to stay\nparseable JSON, so its stack marker is the `\"__evoT1Stack\": true` key rather than a comment\nline."],[2808,"`host-diagnostics` (read-only triage for a slow, hot, full or failing box)"],[2807,"`host-linux-ops` (the right Linux command, what each flag does, and the blast\nradius before it runs)"],[548,"`host.docker.internal` mapped to `host-gateway`, so workspaces reach the Coder server\nand LiteLLM."],[2626,"`http://hermes:9119`, with the original Host preserved"],[1774,"`https://<host>/` serves the dashboard behind a self-signed certificate that\n`scripts/bootstrap.sh` issues, so expect a one-time browser warning. Port 80 redirects\nto HTTPS."],[4281,"`https://gmktecbeast.overeazy.io/`, `coder-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io`,\n`kasm-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io`, `hermes-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io`,\n`grafana-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io` and `infisical-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io` 302 to\n`https://authelia.overeazy.io/`. Homepage, Coder, Kasm, Hermes, Grafana and Infisical\nare interactive sessions, and the Hermes policy is already in place."],[1196,"`images/dev/tool-versions.env` is the single source of truth for every tool version:\nBazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, shellcheck (apt), bats, Terraform/tflint/terragrunt, the\nCoder CLI, the Docker *client* trio, Node, Python, Go, protoc and the pinned Grok CLI."],[2306,"`implement-reviewed` (`{ goal, question, verify }`) is `fleet-verify` with the repair round\nadded: map on `agent-explore`, fan the change out on `agent-swarm`, close on `agent-review`,\nthen one bounded fix round for the findings the skeptic marked `broken` and one more skeptic\npass. Without `verify` the writer names the proof and the skeptic challenges that choice."],[3810,"`inference.rules.yml` the ten inference alerts - 30 in all"],[4031,"`INFISICAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD` - the login `bootstrap` uses to create the project and the\nmachine identity (`scripts/lib/infisical.sh:1216`), minted by\n`scripts/bootstrap.sh:119`. It is spent before the project exists, so there is no\nvault to read it from yet."],[4054,"`INFISICAL_DB_PASSWORD` has the same first-init behaviour and no reconciler beside it - the\ncompose block says so at its own comment - so rotating it needs the `infisical-db-data`\nvolume reset, not a recreate."],[4028,"`INFISICAL_DB_PASSWORD`, `INFISICAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `INFISICAL_AUTH_SECRET` - the\nvault's own bootstrap credentials. By definition they cannot come from the vault: it\nneeds them to start. They live in `.env`, and you set them."],[4032,"`INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` - the machine identity's Universal Auth\nsecret, which is the credential every fetch authenticates with\n(`scripts/lib/infisical.sh:803`). Storing it in the project it unlocks would make the\nvault a precondition of reading the vault."],[280,"`infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl` is the `coder_script \"infisical_secrets\"` body that fetches\nthat workspace's own copy of the stack's credentials from the self-hosted vault on start\n(`templates/workspace/main.tf:771-786`)."],[670,"`infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl` is the sparsest body: its map is the single `boot_log_lib`\n  key (`templates/workspace/main.tf:783-785`), so apart from the one line that takes it every\n  braced expansion in it is shell text, none of it interpolates, and the rendered bytes are\n  the same for every workspace."],[4559,"`infisical: pull-on-start is off (INFISICAL_PULL_ON_START)` -> this boot never dials the vault, which is the shipped state"],[4561,"`infisical: refused to publish <home>/.infisical/agent.env; the staged file names a shell-control variable` -> the belt fired, not the filter"],[4562,"`infisical: skipped a secret whose value spans more than one line` -> the vault holds a multi-line secret"],[4555,"`infisical: vault not configured for this stack` -> the boot fetch ran with an empty name on the agent environment"],[1869,"`infisical/`"],[4661,"`info: prompt cache: 80693 tokens, resumed at 79747, kept 1; 12 states, 6289 MiB and\n0 MiB spare of 6465 MiB (hits ..., evicted ...)`: the box is out of prompt-cache room.\n`resumed at N` is how much of the prompt it did not have to recompute, so a healthy\nconversation logs a number just under `tokens`. `resumed at 0` means it recomputed the\nwhole prompt: something evicted that conversation's state. Watch `evicted` and the\nstate count rather than any one line."],[3332,"`install` installs the two packages, writes the config, regenerates the\ninitramfs, and then runs the same check over what it produced."],[4522,"`installed terraform version newer than expected` -> harmless"],[5384,"`inventories/`"],[4901,"`jq` and\n`python` then fail because the file was never created."],[4133,"`JSON_MODE` set sends prose to stderr. CLIs without `--json` unset `JSON_MODE` after source.\nKeep prefixes `warning:` / `note:` / `error:`."],[1818,"`KASM_UI_PORT` has to match on **both** sides of the port mapping. The daemon-side\nlistener listens on that number, so the mapping is `4443:4443`."],[3576,"`kasm`"],[5382,"`kustomization.yaml`"],[3096,"`least-busy` picks the deployment carrying the fewest in-flight requests out of a list\nthat some filter already made healthy. It has no health input of its own, and that is\nthe one thing to know before trusting it to spread load."],[3185,"`litellm_settings.callbacks` must name the *instance*,\n`compaction_router.proxy_handler_instance`, never the class. `ProxyLogging` dispatches\n`async_pre_call_hook` only to a callback that IS a `CustomLogger` and overrides that hook\nin its own class dict."],[1867,"`litellm/config.yaml`"],[2723,"`litellm/config.yaml` owns the set, so an alias is added there and a row follows; the\ngate fails when the two drift apart, or when one alias ends up on two rows."],[749,"`local.code_server_agent_id` is\n`concat(coder_devcontainer.repo[*].subagent_id, [coder_agent.main.id])[0]`: the\nsub-agent when that resource exists, the parent agent on the stopped page."],[1108,"`logs --follow` is the intentional long-running exception, and you stop it with Ctrl-C."],[4516,"`lookup registry.terraform.io on 127.0.0.11:53: server misbehaving` from `push-template` -> coder cannot reach the Terraform registry"],[4860,"`ls ~/.grok/bundled/skills` printing nothing is the expected answer, not a symptom:\nwithout the sign-in there is no bundled cache at all, on any version."],[3132,"`main.tf` renders that through\n`grok_subagent_max_concurrent = var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent != null ? var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent : var.grok_swarm_width`,\nand the `: var.grok_swarm_width` arm of the ternary answers only a caller that passes null\non purpose - the quote is the opt-in, not the source of the width."],[501,"`main.tf` therefore spells the editor's `folder` per hosting environment\n(`local.editor_folder`): `/workspaces/<repo-name>` inside the dev container,\n`/srv/coder-devcontainers/<workspace-id>/<repo-name>` on the plain container, and\n`/home/coder` when no repository was named."],[63,"`main` is not a place to work: an agent edits it only when the operator asked for that in\nwords."],[40,"`main` is the only long-lived branch. It stays green and deployable: `main` is what a\nmachine is built from, so a merge to `main` is by definition deployable to the stack host."],[1101,"`make test`/`bats`/`lint`/`fix`/`validate` and the `stack-*`/`prod-stack-*` shims are the\nsame commands; `make help` lists them."],[4117,"`make` only delegates. An operator CLI runs as `bazelisk run //scripts:<stem> -- <args>`\n(`<stem>` = the file name under `scripts/`); `make help` lists the shims."],[5388,"`Makefile`"],[5387,"`manage.sh`"],[4921,"`max_concurrent` is how many a session may have in flight. `[subagents.models]` is\nwhere each type's traffic goes, and a writer pinned to `agent` carries the workspace's\nown `x-litellm-session-id`, so the whole fan-out lands on the one Spark box that key\nresolves to. That box admits `PARALLEL` (5 by default, `scripts/spark-configure.sh`)\nfull-length streams and the parent session holds one of them, which is why the useful\nwidth there is about 4 no matter what the number above it says."],[2153,"`max_depth = 1` is the rollback to no nesting, and it restores the behaviour the fleet\nshipped with before a child could spawn."],[2201,"`max_depth = 1` is the rollback: no child spawns, and one parent's slot count again\ndescribes the whole tree."],[2151,"`max_depth` rides beside them, rendered from `grok_subagent_max_depth` and shipped\nat 2, and at 2 a child may spawn: `reviewer`, `security-auditor` and `tester` name\n`spawn_subagent` in their `tools` (`templates/common/reviewer.AGENT.md:5`), so a skeptic\nor a tester can fan read-only mappers out one level under itself."],[4162,"`mcp-cache-proxy.json`"],[278,"`mcp-cache-proxy.json` is the context7 MCP cache-proxy blob the startup script\nwrites, into `~/.grok/mcp-cache-proxy/config.json` and only while that file is absent\n(that path is per workspace, so each workspace warms its own SQLite cache). It\nnames no secret: the empty `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` value is what tells `mcp-cache-proxy` to\ninherit `process.env`."],[3670,"`Memory`"],[1616,"`missing-type`"],[4371,"`mode`, `host_source`, `monitor_enabled`, both images, both ports, `ssh_port`"],[3030,"`model_group_retry_policy:` gives the nine agent lanes their