bazel` and `.bzl` - plus `ruff format --quiet` for `.py`. It refuses:"],[2322,"`PostToolUse`, matcher `Edit|Write|search_replace|write` -> `bin/selective-test-runner.sh`:\n**off unless `EVO_T1_HOOK_TESTS=1`**. When it is on, the hook derives one Bazel label -\n`//tests:bats_<stem>_test` straight from a `tests/bats/<stem>.bats` path, otherwise the first\nlabel `bazelisk run //scripts:bazel-map -- tests-for <path>` prints - and starts\n`bazelisk test <label>` detached with `nohup`, logging to\n`${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/evo-t1-hook-tests/<sanitized-label>.log`."],[3668,"`Power`"],[4517,"`pq: value too long for type character varying(256)` from `push-template` -> editor icon data URL"],[5071,"`Prefix m` is the wheel switch, not a copy route: one press hands the wheel to tmux\nfor a long scroll, the next hands it back."],[2316,"`PreToolUse`, matcher `Bash|run_terminal_command` -> `bin/dangerous-command-guard.sh`: tests\n`toolInput.command` against the list beside itself and denies, naming the file, the line\nnumber and the pattern that matched."],[2311,"`PreToolUse`, matcher `Edit|Write|search_replace|write` -> `bin/secret-guard.sh`: denies a\nwrite whose text carries an AWS access-key id, a GitHub token, a Slack token, a Google API\nkey, a `-----BEGIN ... PRIVATE KEY-----` block, a URL that carries both a user and a\npassword, or a credential-keyword assignment (`api_key`, `secret`, `token`, `password`, and\ntheir upper-case SDK spellings) whose value carries a digit."],[611,"`private` mounts no per-owner volume at all: the three state directories then live on\nthis workspace's own home volume too, so they are its own and die with it."],[409,"`private` mounts no per-owner volume, so all three live on that workspace's own\nhome volume and die with it"],[996,"`private`: no per-owner volume at all. Notes, memory and sessions then live on that\nworkspace's own home volume, differ per workspace, and die with the workspace;\n`config.toml` is per workspace either way."],[2352,"`private`: no per-owner volume at all. The notes, the memory and the sessions live\non that workspace's own home volume, differ from its siblings, and die with the\nworkspace. `config.toml` is per workspace either way."],[3767,"`prod-stack` addresses the stable project by name from any directory"],[98,"`production` stays restricted to `main` — or to tags — with required reviewers. See the\nheader comment in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`."],[1870,"`proxy/*.conf`"],[1124,"`proxy/certs/` is `.bazelignored` (bootstrap issues those on the host), so a\n`bazelisk run` of a stack runner, of `push-template`, or of the six CLIs that read a file the\ncheckout alone holds (`dashboard-password`, `pull-models`, `coder-agents`, `spark-verify`,\n`spark-configure`, `build-dev-image`) prefers `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the real checkout)\nover the runfiles copy as the compose project directory, the live `.env`, and the template\ntree (runfiles `templates/**` are symlinks that Coder cannot follow after unpack)."],[3939,"`PS4` and `IFS` (how the sourcing shell parses itself), `PATH` and `HOME` (which binary\nand which config the next command reads)"],[94,"`pull_request.branches` filters on the base rather than the head, so naming only `main` left a\nstacked pull request - a dependent branch that names its parent as its base, the shape the agent\nguidance in `templates/common/GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md` tells you to open - with no gate at all: it\ncollected just the docs deploy its branch push earned from `deploy-docs`. Gate a stack the same\nway as any other pull request."],[4615,"`pull-models` pulling its default list instead of the checkout's `OLLAMA_MODELS`"],[3905,"`pull` writes the managed keys into `.env` and compose reads that file exactly as it\nalways has. The vault is an editor for `.env`, not a dependency of the project."],[1297,"`push would FAIL` from the check above means one command:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- fix https://github.com/toxicoder/evo-t1-coder-stack.git`.\nIt:"],[5152,"`push would WORK (the credential git consults writes <repo>)` and `push would FAIL` are\nthe lines to gate on, keyed to the credential git would really send; `check` exits\nnon-zero on FAIL so a script or an agent can refuse to push on it."],[5153,"`PUSH-READY` (200 advertising refs): a push would negotiate. If the push still fails,\nthe credential is not the failing thing."],[5110,"`PUSH-READY` means the credential is fine and you want\n  the push-denied entry\n  instead."],[469,"`push-template.sh` re-sends both after every push, and `new-workspace.sh` names no\n`--stop-after`, so a script-made workspace gets no autostop deadline either."],[978,"`push-template.sh` reads `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_ID` from `coder.env` and\nforwards it as `--var github_auth_id=` so the templates declare the same id.\nChanging the id orphans existing GitHub account links."],[4126,"`python3 -m webbrowser`"],[3291,"`qwen2.5-coder:32b` is treated here as a Mixture-of-Experts model: 32B-class quality\nwith far fewer active parameters per token."],[3086,"`qwen2.5:7b` on the same runtime does return a real `tool_calls` array."],[1712,"`real_bin <tool>` resolves a tool with the stub directory removed from PATH. That is the\nintegration-tier gate: `if [ -z \"$(real_bin terraform)\" ]; then skip \"terraform not\ninstalled\"; fi` — a test that could talk to a real daemon skips when the tool is absent\ninstead of failing."],[2131,"`refresh-configs`, `storage-clean` and `seed-dev-env` retire the same two paths on\nreseed."],[89,"`Refs #<n>` is the keyword for a pull request that is one step of the work, or lands before\nthe fix."],[5154,"`REFUSED-GRANT` (403): that credential authenticates and every write to the repo is\ndenied, which is the push 403."],[4564,"`Refusing to bind dashboard to 0.0.0.0` -> empty Hermes basic-auth env"],[5156,"`REJECTED` (401): github.com refused the credential itself, as it refuses an expired or\nrevoked token - the fate of the injected pair about an hour after start. `fix` re-mints."],[5108,"`REJECTED` beside `env token (GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN)` is an\n  expired mint (401 refuses the credential itself, which is what an hour-old injected\n  copy is)"],[5134,"`remote: Invalid username or token. Password authentication is\n  not supported for Git operations.`"],[5135,"`remote: Repository not found.`"],[4519,"`REPO_ROOT: unbound variable` from `push-template` -> the size guard read an ambient root"],[1702,"`REPO_ROOT` — where the checkout is *for this run*. `tests/bats_runner.sh` exports it;\noutside Bazel it is whatever `bats_canonical_repo_root` resolves. Derive it, never\nhardcode a machine path, and treat \"cannot resolve\" as a `skip`, not a failure."],[377,"`repo_url` prefills the Git repository field on both create forms. The Terraform\ndefault is still no clone (`workspace`) or the coder/coder demo (`devcontainer`).\n`.env.sample` sets `REPO_URL` to this stack's GitHub URL, so a normal push prefills\n`https://github.com/toxicoder/evo-t1-coder-stack.git` and **VS Code Web** opens\n`~/workspace/evo-t1-coder-stack`. A blank `REPO_URL=` line stays unpassed."],[529,"`repo_url=<url>` always"],[4052,"`restart_coder_if_pg_auth_failed`, sourced by both stack runners, bounces `coder` when\nits logs show `password authentication failed` - which is the failure mode a stale\npassword produces when the two halves land in the wrong order."],[3242,"`restart: unless-stopped` stays the only thing that recovers a crashed\nproxy, and this probe buys visibility instead - `dev-stack status` and\n`docker compose ps` print (unhealthy), `docker inspect` carries the last three probes,\nand the log tag ships the event to Loki."],[3054,"`retry_after` is only a `min_timeout` and is never consulted while the group has healthy\ndeployments."],[3033,"`RetryPolicy` in that tag has no `APIConnectionErrorRetries` field."],[3050,"`reviewer`, `security-auditor` and `tester` name `spawn_subagent` in their `tools`,\nand every mapper such a child raises holds