                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_machine_identity_id` | `\"\"`    | → `INFISICAL_MACHINE_IDENTITY_ID`. The machine identity the boot authenticates as - the id, never the token. It has no slot in any CLI argv, since the client id/secret are the credential, so it gates the fetch and records which identity the stack means (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:10-13`). |"],[436,"| Variable                       | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------ | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_subagent_max_concurrent` | `15`    | `[subagents] max_concurrent`: how many subagents one session may have in flight. The variable ships its own 15 outright - the fleet ceiling, 3 Spark boxes x `PARALLEL` 5 (`scripts/spark-configure.sh`) - so the width is this variable's own number and tracks no other knob, and the cap is 15 on every lane. `null` is the opt-in that hands the width to `grok_swarm_width` above: `main.tf` renders it as exactly `grok_subagent_max_concurrent = var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent != null ? var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent : var.grok_swarm_width` (`templates/workspace/main.tf:553`), with no lane test anywhere in that expression, so that `:` arm answers only a caller that passes null on purpose. An explicit `--var` still overrides the shipped 15, and a validation keeps any explicit value between 1 and 32 (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:64-72`); past the fleet's 15 streams a number deepens LiteLLM's queue rather than buying capacity. An explicit value persists in two places - on the template, from a raw `coder templates push --var`, and on the workspace, from `coder start --parameter` / `coder update --parameter` or the Variables tab (`--var` is a `coder templates push` flag alone; on Coder v2.36.6 `coder start --help` has no `--var`) - so a workspace's own value outlives every template version, while a value carried as a template version's default is replaced by the next push - `//scripts:push-template` sends no fan-out width of its own, so a re-push takes that parameter back to the `coder.tf` default, which is the literal 15 rather than a sentinel that resolves through another variable. Which of the two holds the number is not visible from inside the container: both live in the Coder database, on the host, and neither answers the agent token. The check that reads the pair asks to be run again after the restart, because the number moving is the only proof either remedy had an effect. The render keeps the pair legible from in there - `# fleet-width: 15` sits directly above `max_concurrent` in `[subagents]`, and `bazelisk run //scripts:subagent-check` compares them and prints what it found - and stage 6 of `templates/workspace/startup.sh.tftpl` prints the same mismatch on the startup log as it re-renders the file (Marker ownership of the seeded files). This is also the knob a pinned lane narrows: `agent` only ever reaches the one box its session key resolves to, whose `PARALLEL` (5 by default, `scripts/spark-configure.sh`) is the useful width, so setting it near 4 there keeps the session inside that box's streams instead of queueing behind them - an operator's choice, never the shipped default. Overflow is held, not failed (`limit_behavior = \"queue\"`), so overshoot costs a subagent latency rather than its life, and `sampling_limit` is left unset because it defaults to `max_concurrent`. |"],[453,"| Variable                  | Default           | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_client_secret` | `\"\"`, `sensitive` | → `INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`, and only when non-empty: it keeps its own conditional so an empty secret omits the key rather than handing the boot script a credential it would try to authenticate with (`templates/workspace/main.tf:654-657`). Never printed, and never interpolated into the body, which only names the variable (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:244-252`). |"],[437,"| Variable                  | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `grok_subagent_max_depth` | `2`     | `[subagents] max_depth`: how deep the subagent tree may go. `1` keeps nesting off - only the top-level session spawns - and that is the rollback. `2` is the shipped default: a child may spawn read-only mappers of its own, so a skeptic scopes out its own evidence and the parent skips a round trip. `3` is the operator's experiment ceiling. Nesting is bounded by the role definitions: only `reviewer`, `security-auditor` and `tester` name `spawn_subagent` in `tools`, so a depth-2 wave is read-only work and a mapper has no spawner to recurse with. Every in-flight child holds one of the fleet's 15 streams (3 Spark boxes x `PARALLEL` 5, `scripts/spark-configure.sh`), so a parent sums `1 + spawns` over its in-flight tasks and keeps that total at or below the fleet's stream count - the `fleet:` figure a micro-plan states, which is a separate figure from the session's `slots`. An over-admitted stream is refused by the box. `--var grok_subagent_max_depth=N` sets it for one workspace; same bounded-knob shape as the width above, and the same rendering pass (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:74-82`). |"],[455,"| Variable                  | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_pull_on_start` | `false` | The second gate, under `infisical_enabled`, and it decides only whether a start *waits* on the vault. Forwarded only when both `.env` keys are truthy (`scripts/push-template.sh:636`, `:668-671`). Off leaves the script present but idle: one log line naming the gate and exit 0 (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:27-30`). Handed over as the string `\"true\"`/`\"false\"`, because a `coder_agent` env value has to be a string and the body compares it against a literal (`templates/workspace/main.tf:649-652`). |"],[454,"| Variable                | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ----------------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_environment` | `prod`  | → `INFISICAL_ENVIRONMENT`. Which Infisical environment the export reads; the CLI takes `--env` on every read, so a fork that keeps another environment slug has no default that fits it (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:254-261`). |"],[450,"| Variable               | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_project_id` | `\"\"`    | → `INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID`. The project the export reads. Not a credential, but no read works without it, so an empty value disables the fetch the way an empty URL does (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:221-227`). |"],[431,"| Variable              | Default       | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| --------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_subagents_lane` | `agent-swarm` | The Grok catalog key the **writers** run on, rendered into `[subagents.models]` for `general-purpose` (the type a spawn gets when it names none, so every writer in a fan-out) and for the seeded `implementer` and `tester` definitions. It used to carry all three built-in types, which made the swarm lane a lie: the writers inherited the parent's pinned model and queued behind one box anyway. Each other role has a knob of its own now, so this one no longer moves the whole fleet by itself. A `--var` knob only, and the default ships the writers on the unpinned fleet lane, where the least-busy picker places a fan-out across all three boxes; `--var grok_subagents_lane=agent` is the rollback that puts them back on the same pinned lane as the parent session. It chooses placement only; the fan-out width below comes from `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`, and no lane knob moves it. |"],[452,"| Variable              | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_client_id` | `\"\"`    | → `INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_ID`. The Universal Auth client id; **not** sensitive, because it identifies the identity but cannot authenticate alone. `.env` spells this key the way the Infisical CLI reads it, which is the one name pair here that differs (`scripts/push-template.sh:709-714`). |"],[430,"| Variable             | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `grok_default_model` | `agent` | `agent` is the tool-capable Spark lane (thinking `xhigh` by default, picker `low` / `medium` / `xhigh`); `agent-low` / `agent-medium` / `agent-xhigh` bake the level into the alias. |"],[432,"| Variable            | Default         | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_explore_lane` | `agent-explore` | The Grok catalog key the read-only mappers run on: `[subagents.models]` for the built-in `explore` type and for the seeded `explorer` definition. `agent-explore` is the second Spark group with no LiteLLM session pin, thinking baked to `low`, so a wave of one-shot mappers is placed across all three boxes instead of queueing behind one box's streams - and the pin was never protecting anything here, because a mapper gets one turn and never re-reads its own prompt, which is what a warm prefix would have paid for. `--var grok_explore_lane=agent-low` keeps `low` with the pin back on; `=agent` sends mapping work at the parent's full depth. A validation block keeps the value one bare catalog key (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:28-31`). |"],[443,"| Variable            | Default  | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_profile_mode` | `shared` | `shared` mounts the owner's three Grok state volumes (`grok-notes-<owner-id>`, `grok-memory-<owner-id>`, `grok-sessions-<owner-id>`) at `~/.grok/notes`, `~/.grok/memory` and `~/.grok/sessions`, inside that workspace's own home volume; `private` mounts none of them and the workspace starts with an empty `~/.grok`. Also the default behind the per-workspace **Grok profile** dropdown; switching a live workspace between the two modes needs a rebuild. |"],[448,"| Variable            | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `infisical_enabled` | `false` | The vault's switch, and the first of two gates. Off means the workspace cannot tell Infisical exists: no `INFISICAL_*` key in the agent env, no `coder_script.infisical_secrets` at all (`templates/workspace/main.tf:720-721`), no boot log line. Forwarded only as `--var infisical_enabled=true` for a truthy `.env` `INFISICAL_ENABLED` (`scripts/push-template.sh:636-638`), which is the deliberate inverse of `OBSERVABILITY_ENABLED` - that bundle ships on, so here an absent key is off (`scripts/push-template.sh:623-630`). All eight `infisical_*` variables exist in both twins (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:207-274`, `templates/devcontainer/coder.tf:194-261`). |"],[447,"| Variable            | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_config_extra` | `\"\"`    | The **Grok config extras** textarea: free-form TOML appended verbatim, under a comment header, to that workspace's rendered `~/.grok/config.toml`. |"],[446,"| Variable           | Default           | Notes                                                                                |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `context7_api_key` | `\"\"`, `sensitive` | Handed to the workspace as `CONTEXT7_API_KEY`. The rendered file names the variable. |"],[434,"| Variable           | Default        | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_review_lane` | `agent-review` | The Grok catalog key the skeptics run on: `[subagents.models]` for `reviewer` and `security-auditor`, the two seeded definitions the mandatory independent-review phase of a multi-file change runs as. `agent-review` bakes thinking to `xhigh` and lifts the session pin the way `agent-swarm` does, so a wave of reviewers spreads over the fleet and each one thinks as hard as the parent session it reports to. It is also the single seam for the cost of that phase: `--var grok_review_lane=agent-medium`, with the alias in `litellm/config.yaml` moved with it, makes every review cheaper without touching the writers, the mappers or the planner. Same bare-key validation (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:48-51`). |"],[435,"| Variable           | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_swarm_width` | `15`    | The fleet's own ceiling, and the width a workspace gets only when it sets `grok_subagent_max_concurrent = null` on purpose; the width itself is the other variable's own shipped 15, so the cap is 15 on every lane, pinned or unpinned. That 15 is fleet arithmetic, not taste: 3 Spark boxes x `PARALLEL` 5 full-length streams (`scripts/spark-configure.sh`) is everything the fleet can hold at once. It is a plain default rather than a lane-conditional number because `agent-swarm` is always selectable - the `[model.\"agent-swarm\"]` block ships ungated in `grok-config.toml.tftpl`, so a session whose default lane is pinned can still name it on any subagent - and a config sized at one box's `PARALLEL` would cap a swarm the operator had only to ask for. Same 1..32 validation, and above the fleet's 15 streams a number deepens LiteLLM's queue rather than buying capacity (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:54-62`). It also travels into the rendered profile on its own, as the `# fleet-width: 15` line directly above `max_concurrent` inside `[subagents]` (`templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl:427`, fed by `grok_subagent_fleet_width = var.grok_swarm_width` at `templates/workspace/main.tf:558`), so a profile that a `--var` narrowed still shows the count the fleet was sized at. Shrinking a shared fleet is two knobs now: dropping this one moves that ceiling line alone, so set `grok_subagent_max_concurrent` with it, or 15 streams over a fleet sized at 10 are refused by the box with `NoRoom`. |"],[442,"| Variable           | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `additional_repos` | `\"\"`    | The **Git repositories (additional)** textarea under the repository field. Extra URLs cloned into their own folder beside `repo_url`. |"],[439,"| Variable          | Default                            | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `coder_agent_url` | `http://host.docker.internal:3002` | The URL the agent dials. Kept on the local plain listener so a public `CODER_ACCESS_URL` does not hairpin agent traffic through the reverse proxy. Empty keeps the provider-rendered access URL. |"],[433,"| Variable         | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `grok_plan_lane` | `agent` | The Grok catalog key the planner runs on: `[subagents.models]` for the built-in `plan` type and for the seeded `architect` definition. The one role lane that ships **pinned**, deliberately - a planner is a single conversation that re-reads what it just read and whose answer steers every wave after it, so stickiness and depth both pay where spreading would only re-prefill the same history. `--var grok_plan_lane=agent-medium` trades depth for turnaround on a busy fleet; `agent-xhigh` is the other way. Same bare-key validation (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:38-41`). |"],[449,"| Variable        | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `infisical_url` | `\"\"`    | Handed to the boot fetch as `INFISICAL_DOMAIN`: the base URL of the self-hosted instance, e.g. `http://host.docker.internal:8182`. The CLI dials Infisical Cloud when handed no domain, so an empty value disables the fetch rather than guessing one, and a self-hosted vault nobody names is a wrong-server bug (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:215-219`). `//scripts:push-template` composes the value as `http://host.docker.internal:<INFISICAL_PORT>` rather than forwarding `.env`'s `INFISICAL_URL`, because that key is the address the stack host dials and a workspace has to reach the host gateway instead (`scripts/push-template.sh:652-661`). |"],[438,"| Variable        | Default | Notes                                                         |\n| --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `docker_socket` | `\"\"`    | Optional Docker socket URI; empty means the provider default. |"],[445,"| Variable       | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `context7_mcp` | `true`  | Wires the cached `context7` MCP stdio server into Grok's rendered `config.toml`. The key is optional, so it ships without one. Set `CONTEXT7_MCP=false` and re-push to drop the block. |"],[428,"| Variable      | Default                               | Notes                                    |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `litellm_url` | `http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1` | Reached through the Docker host gateway. |"],[429,"| Variable      | Default           | Notes                                        |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `litellm_key` | `\"\"`, `sensitive` | Handed to the workspace as `LITELLM_API_KEY` |"],[444,"| Variable     | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `github_mcp` | `true`  | Wires the `github` MCP HTTP server into Grok's rendered `config.toml`. Its `Authorization` header names `$GH_TOKEN` and nothing else, so no token value is ever part of a template variable. Set `GITHUB_MCP=false` and re-push to drop the block. |"],[441,"| Variable   | Default                                                                                                                                                 | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `repo_url` | `\"\"` in `workspace`, `https://github.com/coder/coder` in `devcontainer` (Terraform); `.env.sample` `REPO_URL` overrides both to this stack's GitHub URL | Prefills the **Git repository** field. Both templates clone that URL on the first start; a later start leaves a folder that already holds a `.git` alone. `REPO_URL` in `.env` overrides the default. The sample value is this stack's own repo so **VS Code Web** opens `~/workspace/evo-t1-coder-stack`. |"],[427,"| Variable | Default             | Notes                                                                                                                       |\n| -------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `image`  | `evo-t1-dev:latest` | Seeds the **Workspace image** dropdown default. In `devcontainer` it decides nothing about the toolchain inside the editor. |"],[440,"| Variable | Default | Notes                                                                                           |\n| -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dind`   | `false` | Turns on the per-workspace privileged daemon described below. Does not exist in `devcontainer`. |"],[3968,"| Verb          | What it does                                                                                                    | Writes     |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| `install-cli` | Fetch the pinned release (`INFISICAL_CLI_VERSION`) and install the binary. Never pipes a download into a shell. | the binary |"],[3972,"| Verb         | What it does                          