ists so you can read a metric off the box itself. None reaches the LAN, which matters most for blackbox: it is a general-purpose outbound HTTP prober. |"],[3717,"| What         | Where                                             | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Alertmanager | `http://127.0.0.1:9093` (`OBS_ALERTMANAGER_PORT`) | Loopback on purpose. Its UI silences alerts and the service ships no auth, so an Alertmanager reachable by the whole LAN is not something to hand a network. Read silences here from a shell on the stack host, or through Grafana's Alerting pages. |"],[3712,"| What       | Where                                       | Notes                                                                        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Prometheus | `http://127.0.0.1:9090` (`PROMETHEUS_PORT`) | `:2112` metrics port. Reading a graph there needs a shell on the stack host. |"],[3711,"| What    | Where                                                                                                  | Notes                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Grafana | `http://<lan>:3005` (`GRAFANA_PORT`), and `grafana-<suffix>.<base>` when `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` names it | The only published name in the bundle. Login is `GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER` / `GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD` from `.env`; anonymous access and analytics reporting are off. |"],[3715,"| What  | Where                                                     | Notes                             |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Tempo | nothing published - `tempo:3200` query, `tempo:4317` OTLP | Reach it through Grafana Explore. |"],[3713,"| What  | Where                                                   | Notes                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Mimir | nothing published - `mimir:8080` on the compose network | Reach it through Grafana's `mimir` datasource. |"],[3716,"| What  | Where                             | Notes                                                                              |\n| ----- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Alloy | nothing published - `alloy:12345` | The component graph UI stays inside the network; read the container's log instead. |"],[3714,"| What | Where                           | Notes                             |\n| ---- | ------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Loki | nothing published - `loki:3100` | Reach it through Grafana Explore. |"],[1471,"0 when every named thing resolved"],[2501,"1 and 2 are the Coder agent's *default* discovery paths."],[1472,"1 on a query failure"],[2503,"1-4 are written by `startup.sh.tftpl`. 5-10 are the stack's three skill commands and are\nwritten by `coder_script.stack_skills`, whose own `execve` carries the three payloads;\nthey ride their own script body rather than the startup argument because that argument\nhas a single-argument ceiling of its own\n(coder-templates.md). Each `.agents`\ncopy is a `cp` of the managed `.coder` copy, never a second inline body, so the pair\ncannot drift."],[4121,"1–3 line awk"],[2504,"11-26 are the four commands of that second family - the three repository conversions\nplus the `/ez-micro-plan` dispatcher - and are written by\n`coder_script.stack_repo_skills`, a second body with its own ceiling, for the same\nreason and because this family also ships the python helpers 13-14, 16, 19-20 and 25-26\nthat three of its four bodies invoke by `~/.agents` path. Same absent-only contract and\nthe same `cp` twin rule; the helper directories are made by the body, so a workspace that\nalready has the `SKILL.md` but lost a helper still gets the helper back."],[4665,"120 s is the floor the measurement allows, not a taste: at 30 s across five\ndeployments a round was putting more probes on a box than user requests, and each one\ntook a prompt-cache state from a conversation."],[4884,"127 is the shell saying the file it was told to exec is not there. Both editor terminal\nprofiles exec a launcher under `~/.grok/bin`, and `coder_script \"terminal_launchers\"`\n(`templates/common/terminal-launchers.sh.tftpl`) is what writes those two files."],[1473,"2 on a usage error (an unknown verb or flag, or a verb invoked without the argument it needs)"],[2502,"3 and 4 are the same text under the Grok Build CLI's convention, and the CLI is\nwhat `execute`-lane delegation drives. The chat agent dedupes skills by name,\nfirst match wins, home scope before a working-dir path, so one agent never loads a\nskill twice: the twins exist for the CLI, not as a second source for chat."],[5096,"3.4 holds back any Escape it reads for 500 ms to decide whether a sequence\nfollows, so Alt and the arrow keys feel like dropped input and a focus-in can\nwait that long - twice, with `set-timing` - before tmux repaints."],[2505,"5 and 6 are `/ez-learn`: this stack's copy of the upstream memory commands `/flush`,\n`/dream`, `/remember` and `/memory`. It turns the current session into durable facts -\nflush the conversation into a session log under the workspace's `~/.grok/memory/`\ndirectory, dream those logs into an organized `MEMORY.md`, save one note, or browse and\nclear what was stored. Reaching past those logs into the raw transcripts under\n`~/.grok/sessions/` is opt-in depth, done only when the operator asks for it. Its\ndefault mode is report-only, and it writes memory files, never a skill."],[2506,"7 and 8 are `/ez-skillify`, which turns the session that just worked into a skill from its\nown transcript, and 9 and 10 are `/ez-create-skill`, which scaffolds one from what the\noperator describes."],[620,"A\n`config.toml` that still carries the marker is one every start replaces from\n`grok-config.toml.tftpl`, whichever of the two runs first, so what an orphaned swap holds\nis doomed either way."],[727,"A **GitHub reauth** external app (`order = 7`, `/icon/github.svg`) opens Coder's\n`/external-auth/<id>` page in a slim window on the user's Coder session: connect, or\n**Reauthenticate** when the account is already linked."],[950,"A **start/restart** re-renders it from this checkout, which is the only way a\nper-workspace value gets in, and the pass says so after it reseeds."],[4800,"A *park* is deliberate and looks like this: `GITHUB_MCP=false` / `CONTEXT7_MCP=false` /\n`SEARCH_MCP=false` in `.env` (relayed by `push-template.sh`) or\n`--var github_mcp=false` / `--var context7_mcp=false` / `--var search_mcp=false` on a\ntemplate push. With none of those set, a missing block is a defect, not a park."],[1497,"a `_SCRIPT_LIBS` key (the `scripts/lib` closure it sources)"],[1498,"a `_SCRIPT_PAYLOAD` key (the payload groups it opens)"],[631,"a `/proc` with nothing to scan"],[4806,"A `~/.grok/config.toml` carrying neither the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` line\nnor the `__evoT1Stack = true` key is a file the stack stopped managing, so neither\nthe startup script nor the seed writes it again and its default lanes never arrive.\nThe usual cause is not a hand edit: `grok mcp add` persists its own settings by\nrewriting that file and deletes every comment line, which used to revoke stack\nownership by itself."],[2774,"a `${VAR}` left in the file is reported as `does not exist` and the agent works\nsomewhere else"],[4822,"A `404` is what this stack answers for an unknown app slug or an agent that is not\nConnected; the agent is the text after the first `.` in `<ws>.<agent>`."],[4372,"a `boxes` array with one object per box (`probed`, `docker`, `node_exporter`, `dcgm`,\n`dcgm_counter_count`, `gpu_count`, `gpu_names`, `probe_version`, `verdict`, `detail`)"],[2241,"a `calls:` budget of 15 or fewer counting the reads a child needs to get oriented"],[2253,"a `calls` budget over 25 (over 15 is a warning - 15 is the bar for a micro task, 25 is\nwhere the plan is wrong)"],[460,"A `context7_mcp` of `true` with an empty `context7_api_key` is *not* the same shape:\nthe key is optional, the block renders either way, and the server handshakes and\nanswers without one - no `Authorization` header goes out, so the lane runs at the\npublic rate limit and private libraries are the only thing out of reach."],[389,"A `DEV_IMAGE` that is not in the local image store is a note, not a stop: build it\nfirst with `bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image`."],[5361,"A `development` branch that is 134 commits ahead of `main` (a real number from a real repository\nin this fleet) is not a staging area, it is a second product whose differences nobody is\nreconciling, and the day someone finally merges it, the review is unreviewable."],[629,"a `find` or `basename` that is missing or errors"],[116,"A `fix/…` branch that also has to rename a template directory, retarget a `.bats` suite, and\nupdate `docs/`