s a workspace that\ncame up wrong and a plan that said nothing."],[4770,"A `warning:` that a stored model config is disabled, is not the default, or compacts\nagainst the wrong window names a row this script found already in place. It reads\nbefore it writes and this surface has no PATCH, so the correction is the one click in\nAdmin -> Experiments -> Agent Chat the line names."],[2697,"a `web` block that stopped pinning `searxng` or flipped a keyless switch back on,\nwhich routes a search to a vendor's free tier while the config still looks local"],[4931,"A `ws-...` value means Terraform rendered it;"],[467,"A 0 default TTL leaves the checkbox unchecked and leaves `coder create` with nothing to\ninherit, so a workspace runs until its owner stops it."],[841,"A bare target is a container"],[3163,"a base64 payload at two"],[3627,"A bind follows the *path*, so an edit made in the checkout is already inside the\nrunning container, and the only question left is when the process reads it again"],[2812,"A bind-mounted skill needs no recreate when the agent reloads skills from disk; start a\n**new session** - a fresh Chat tab, or a new `hermes-shell` run - and the new skill is\noffered. Recreate only if it still does not show up, since `restart` keeps the old\nmounts."],[3674,"A board you build from scratch is not thrown away - it lands in Grafana's own database on\n`grafana-data` - but it is invisible to git and to the gate below, which is the same drift\nthe `:ro` mounts above exist to prevent."],[655,"A body takes the library as one bare line under its `set -u`. Terraform does not\nre-interpolate a map value, so the library's own dollar-brace shell text lands verbatim -\nno here-doc, no temp file, no second copy to drift. That is also why the escape rule below\nis absolute rather than a style preference: Terraform reads an interpolation token wherever\nit sits, a `.tftpl` comment included, so no comment in one of these files may spell one."],[1794,"a bookmark's value is a