t keeps working; in public mode the browser never sees it, since\nTraefik presents real ones;"],[1003,"A comma-separated list is the hand-pin: those names are used verbatim."],[4247,"a comma-separated list is used verbatim, which is how you pin a name by hand (leave\n`STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS_MODE` empty, or that key keeps re-deriving)."],[1135,"a comment"],[4407,"A container that *is* listed but does not serve still counts as running for\nnode_exporter, and shows up one line later on the DCGM side: the probe counts counters\nfrom a live local scrape of `:<port>/metrics` and only falls back to the field list baked\ninto the image when that scrape returns nothing\n(`scripts/lib/probes/spark-monitor.sh:196-206`), so a `note:` whose counter count matches\nthe image's default list rather than this repo's file means the exporter is up and not\nserving your field list."],[4406,"A container that `docker ps` does not list (exited, restarting) comes back\n`absent`, so the CLI says `node_exporter is absent -- Prometheus scrapes <host>:9100 and\ngets nothing` and points at `--apply --box <n>`\n(`scripts/spark-monitor.sh:616-624`)."],[2226,"A contributor home gets the same seam from the environment of the seed, so a laptop\nmatches what a template `--var` renders:"],[3136,"A contributor home names the same three lanes with `GROK_EXPLORE_LANE`, `GROK_PLAN_LANE`\nand `GROK_REVIEW_LANE` for `//scripts:seed-dev-env`."],[3109,"A conversation that goes quiet for longer than the TTL may move."],[3105,"A cooled box therefore stays visibly out of `healthy_deployments` instead of blending\ninto the group's aggregate stats."],[4529,"A copy from an app inside a tmux pane never reaches the laptop clipboard in VS Code Web -> the browser build drops OSC 52"],[4880,"A create or attach that still fails lands the tab in a plain login\n  shell rather than in VS Code's terminated-process message."],[4912,"A current workspace clears these at boot by itself. `grok_sweep_config_swaps` in the\n`agents-seed.sh.tftpl` body moves a swap of that name into `~/.grok/stale-swaps/` once\nnothing in the container holds it open and it is over an hour old. The boot log prints\nthe archived name, and `vim -r` on that path gets the bytes back for a month."],[726,"A custom **Web Terminal** command-app at `order = 6` takes the terminal slot. Custom\napps are ordered among themselves; static helper buttons have no `order` or `icon` knob\nin this Coder release and are not reorderable."],[974,"A custom GitHub App belongs in `coder.env`\nfully filled, including\n`APP_INSTALL_URL=https://github.com/apps/<slug>/installations/new`."],[851,"A custom GitHub OAuth app"],[788,"A custom OAuth app lives in `coder.env` (beside `docker-compose.yml`);\n`push-template.sh` forwards `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_ID` so the templates declare\nthe same id. Link that provider to **both** templates."],[3514,"A dashboard is a committed file"],[3814,"A dead blackbox prober produces no probe series at all, so nothing it probes can report\nit; `BlackboxProbeGap` reads `up{job=\"blackbox\"}`, which is why Prometheus scrapes the\nprober as a service of its own."],[4677,"a dead engine process"],[1614,"A declared constraint turns that into a plan-time error."],[4809,"A declared context7 server: an empty `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` is the shipped default and\ndoes *not* fail the handshake. With no value the server sends no `Authorization`\nheader, so it handshakes and answers at the public rate limit, and only private\nlibraries are out of reach. A key in `.env` plus a re-push fills the env. When a\ncontext7 handshake really fails the key is not the cause: run\n`bazelisk run //scripts:mcp-check` and it says which of the block, the binary, the\ncache config or the handshake is not OK."],[4808,"A declared github server that fails handshake: the owner has not connected\nGitHub External Auth, so `$GH_TOKEN` is empty. Use the **GitHub reauth** app,\nthen start a new Grok session."],[4804,"A declared server whose `command=` the box cannot find is image drift: the\ntemplates declare a binary the running image never got, because it predates the\nnpm bake in `images/dev/Dockerfile`."],[5449,"A default-branch rename is its own confirmed step, done after the content has converged,\nbecause GitHub rewrites links, protections and open pull requests when it happens."],[4859,"A deletion is undone - the workspace boot writes the file again whenever it is absent,\n  and `refresh-configs` re-seeds an absent target, so the next boot restores the\n  stack's copy. Copy the payload back from `templates/common/<name>.SKILL.md` to give\n  the file back to the stack."],[923,"A deletion is undone - the workspace boot writes the file again whenever it is absent, and\n`refresh-configs` re-seeds an absent target, so the next boot restores the stack's\ncopy."],[2254,"a dependency cycle or an unknown dependency id"],[968,"a depth that is not a count or sits past 3"],[4265,"A dev name is a different `Host` rule and a different backend port: add a router per\ndev name to the file above aimed at `http://<this-box-lan-ip>:18080`, and the DNS\nrecords for those names have to exist too, or the browser fails before this box is\never asked."],[376,"A dev stack that moved the search port needs its own template push: `searxng_url`\nis derived from `STACK_SEARCH_PORT` as read from `.env`, so a push made while\n`dev-stack.env` carries `18181` still names `8181` unless the key is set in `.env`\ntoo. A workspace dials the host gateway, where the compose network does not help,\nso the port in the rendered `SEARXNG_URL` has to be the one actually published."],[2072,"A drag while `Prefix m` has the pointer on selects nothing, since the copy bindings\nstay unbound either way."],[82,"A duplicate becomes a link to the original"],[4607,"A failed bind from an older runfiles compose file can also leave a **directory**\n(or a root-owned file) at `homepage/assets/icons/evo-t1.svg` inside\n`bazel-out/.../prod-stack.runfiles`. The next `bazelisk r