rwrites the mark with\n`is_healthy: True` (`health_check.py:683`), so a box is eligible again on the first\nprobe that succeeds after it comes back - no request has to fail first to rediscover it."],[2468,"A Grok Build session logging `compact failed: exceeded wall-clock budget 300s\n(runaway generation)` is the session-model summary hanging before its first token on\nthe lane that also serves the whole agent loop. Its only live bounds are\n`GROK_COMPACTION_WALL_CLOCK_SECS`, rendered into the agent `env` because no TOML table\ntakes it, and the proxy's `request_timeout`; troubleshooting.md\nowns the measurement and the retry split that stops one hang being bought three times."],[3022,"A group's only deployment can never be pulled out by the health filter anyway - dropping\nit empties the candidate list, which is the `router.py:14177` fail-open - so the mark buys\nno routing, and it is not free: the same cycle cools what it marked\n(`proxy_server.py:4013`) and the cooldown list has no fail-open under this config, because\nthe bypass at `router.py:12774` needs a policy the file refuses to set."],[4039,"a half-seeded project must not lock every service out of its own credential."],[2190,"A hand-edited config is left alone only\n  while it carries one of them, so takeover means deleting **both** lines; delete the\n  file and restart to hand it back."],[5305,"A hand-typed `docker compose ... up -d` selects no profile at all, flag or not -\nprofiles are per command, which is exactly what the runners add. A service the profile\ndid create also keeps running after the flag goes off until you stop it."],[803,"A helper that does not\nclear the pair therefore answers with the injected copy and never asks the store: that\nis the shadow, and it is why a hand-edited helper or a hand-rolled askpass script is the\nwrong instrument (see\nthe push-denied entry)."],[1136,"a here-doc body"],[4814,"A hit in the first means Coder tried the upstream and gave up, so the fault sits on\nthis