ve` (and `--dry-run`) list those keys and write no answers. A\n`summary:` line closes the pass."],[3730,"A missing row means the profile was not selected - see the\ntroubleshooting entry on which env file the dev project actually reads."],[2251,"a missing task key"],[4910,"A name that is this workspace's own is the ordinary case: the home volume outlives\n  every stop and recreate."],[1686,"A native `bazelisk test` on macOS is convenience only: the BSD userland differs from the\nGNU one in the image (`sed`, `date`, `find`, `sort`), so a red run there is not proof of a\ndefect and a green one is not the run that unlocks the merge button. CI and branch\nprotection gate on the image result either way."],[1496,"A new `scripts/*.sh` is a Bazel target automatically (the package is generated from the directory),\nbut it is not wired automatically. It needs two keys, both in `scripts/BUILD.bazel`:"],[3282,"A new alias is a client catalog entry as well as a proxy entry. Both\n`templates/*/main.tf` twins carry one `{value, name, description}` object per alias in\n`local.model_choices`, which is what the workspace create form offers for\n`grok_default_model`, and both `templates/*/grok-config.toml.tftpl` twins carry its\n`[model.\"<alias>\"]` block. An alias the config has and the twins do not is an alias no\nworkspace ever lists."],[1783,"A new config file (`kubernetes.yaml`, ...)\nneeds its own mount line in `docker-compose.yml` before the app sees it."],[3189,"A new group inherits neither the retry policy nor the affinity lift. Both fast lanes\ndeclare their own six-key `model_group_retry_policy` block, and only `agent-swarm-fast`\njoins `model_group_affinity_config` with `[]`; `agent-xhigh-fast` is absent from that map\non purpose, so it keeps falling back to the global `[\"session_affinity\"]` and stays\npinned like its parent. That one key is the whole difference between the pinned twin and\nthe spread one."],[1067,"A new payload directory"],[3696,"A new recording rule therefore needs no test edit, and a metric nothing here records fails\nthe build instead of rendering an empty tile."],[2020,"A new terminal walks into one of that folder's sessions only while no client is\nattached to it, oldest first - that is the closed-tab rejoin, so a tab you closed\nor reloaded leaves its session unattached and the next terminal finds it with its\nhistory intact, and `ssh` + `tmux attach -t <session>` lands there too."],[1126,"A new top-level payload directory gets its own package with its own `filegroup` targets, joins\n`//:stack_data` by label, and is named in the map of every target that reads it: `test-fast`\nand `lint` only see repo files that travel in runfiles, so an unlisted directory is invisible\nto the harness rather than checked loosely."],[1491,"A new top-level payload directory, as building-with-bazel.md spells out:"],[1379,"A page whose first heading is not its title keeps a plain heading and gets no lead paragraph,\nwhich is the visible sign that the two strings drifted apart."],[4309,"A panel stays empty"],[3741,"A panel that is not well-formed JSON, a dashboard whose `title` is blank, and the generated\nSpark file-SD document are gate failures now rather than an empty tile someone notices in\nthe browser."],[2211,"A parent and every child it spawns carry the same `x-litellm-session-id`, so a pinned lane\nplaces the whole fan-out on one box and the useful width is that box's `PARALLEL` - 5 by\ndefault, from `scripts/spark-configure.sh` - minus the parent's own stream; past that, extra\nslots are LiteLLM queue depth."],[2148,"A parent session and every subagent it spawns\ncarry the same `x-litellm-session-id`, so on a pinned lane the whole fan-out resolves\nto one deployment and competes for that box's `PARALLEL` streams - 5 by default, set in\n`scripts/spark-configure.sh` - so the width that is useful on one box is about 4: that\nbox's `PARALLEL` minus the parent's own stream, which is why an operator who pins\neverything to on