h compose."],[3918,"A profile selects services; it does not delete what is already running, so flipping the\nkey back off needs a `down` (or deleting the three by name) before the containers actually\ngo away. Their named volumes survive that, and `reset` is the verb that destroys them."],[4950,"A profile that answers `warning: no '# fleet-width:'\n  line above max_concurrent - this profile predates it; restart the workspace to\n  re-materialize` has no ceiling to compare against yet, so that one is a restart\n  too."],[4948,"A profile whose `[subagents]` table\n  is simply absent answers `warning: no 'max_concurrent' line - this profile has no\n  [subagents] table; restart the workspace to re-materialize`, and a restart is the\n  right order there."],[1326,"A pull request that does not touch `images/dev/**` replays the cached layers instead of\nrebuilding them, which is what keeps the gate's wall time flat."],[884,"A pull that renames, adds or retires a key silently changes what the stack runs on."],[3413,"a pull-request template"],[2825,"A push channel is an inbound door even when you only use it to listen. Every\npublisher to an ntfy topic is one identity to the gateway, so the push-only\nposture - `NTFY_TOPIC` and `NTFY_PUBLISH_TOPIC` set, `NTFY_ALLOWED_USERS` not -\nis the one this doc recommends, and the topic name is the secret."],[348,"A push is also the only thing that *registers* a template: Coder stores the source as a\nFilestore row, not as files it scans on disk."],[1634,"A Python file that lands outside the runner's list is unchecked code that looks\ngated, which is the failure `//tests:bats_mypy_lint_test` exists to catch: it\nenumerates the tree and fails on any `.py` the target list does not cover, with\n`tests/bats/fixtures/` the one sanctioned exclusion because that tree is scaffold\npayload typed in the repository it is copied into."],[888,"A re-pushed template only reaches workspaces\nthat have been **start**ed or **restart**ed since the push - 