al Host, the same as the other names - not `:9119` and not\n`:3005`. A router aimed at a container port skips this\nbox's vhost. The file in Traefik configuration is that\nconfig; diff what the box runs against it."],[4687,"A router-wide `allowed_fails_policy` with `background_health_check_model_groups`\nunset switches the filter off a third time (`router.py:14161`), which is why no such\npolicy sits in this config."],[3210,"a router-wide `allowed_fails_policy` with `background_health_check_model_groups` unset\n(`router.py:14161`)"],[3284,"A routing hook adds two artifacts beyond the alias itself.\n`litellm/compaction_router.py` is a payload file beside the config, bind-mounted\nsingle-file as `./litellm/compaction_router.py:/app/compaction_router.py:ro` - never a\ndirectory mount over `/app`, which would hide `config.yaml` - and it is live only while\n`litellm_settings.callbacks` names `compaction_router.proxy_handler_instance`, the\ninstance rather than the class."],[4506,"A row the sweep cannot use"],[4967,"A row the sweep cannot use says so at the foot of the report instead of vanishing out of\nit. Nothing is printed for the row itself - no `->` phase line, no exec, no verdict,\nnothing counted in the summary - but the sweep counts what the daemon named and what it\njudged out of that same one `docker ps` answer, and prints the difference when there is\none (`scripts/subagent-check.sh:990-991`):"],[2731,"A run with no flags sends the `model:` block's value (`agent`) whatever rows exist,\nand `hermes config set model.provider <row>` changes the route and leaves that value\nalone - the `default_model` pickup is gated on the CLI flag, not on the config key."],[4977,"A running container that carries no `coder.owner` label is the other case where the sweep\n  hands you the command: `coder update /<workspace> --parameter ...` is not a target, and a\n  command that cannot run is worse than none, so it prints the flag it knows and leaves the\n  target to you, and the JS