was\nwarm there."],[4053,"Both run as part of `up`, so the operator's job is one `up` after the rotate. Read the\n`db` and `coder` logs if Coder takes longer than a recreate to come back:"],[2130,"Both startup scripts delete `~/.coder/skills/learn/SKILL.md` and\n`~/.agents/skills/learn/SKILL.md` and prune the directory each leaves, but only while\nthe file still carries the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker; a marker-free\n`learn/SKILL.md` is user-owned and stays."],[713,"Both temp files die in the `EXIT` trap whatever happens between the `mktemp` and the\n`mv` (`:45-52`)."],[301,"Both the preset descriptions and the two routing hints fit the same 128-byte ceiling.\n`coder_parameter` descriptions are **not** capped (some run past 450 characters) and are\nnot checked."],[1620,"Both twins conform today: every `variable` carries a `type` and a `description`, and\nneither uses `any`, `list(any)`, or a bare container."],[736,"Both twins pin the editor release in one `code_server_version` local in their own\n`main.tf`, and the script hands that value to the upstream installer as\n`--version`. Without the flag `https://code-server.dev/install.sh` follows\n`latest`, so a release nobody reviewed would reach every new workspace with no\ncommit in this repo - the same reason the Registry module was forked out. The two\nlocals carry the same value and `//tests:bats_coder_apps_test` fails a drift."],[1563,"Both twins today"],[745,"Both twins' `coder_app` opens on `http://localhost:13337/?folder=<urlencoded>`. The\n`coder_app` resource in `coder/coder` `~> 2.18` has no `folder` argument, so the\nfolder rides in the URL, in the Web Terminal's `command`, and as a positional\nargument to the code-server binary with `--ignore-last-opened` (path-based apps\ndrop the query string, and without that flag the last restored workspace wins)."],[5167,"Both were wrong the same way: they fought the credential-helper precedence that\n`fix` repairs, and they put a live token where `ps` could read it, while the line that\nnames the real cause was one `check` away."],[3193,"Both workspace templates render `x-litellm-session-id = \"ws-<workspace-uuid>\"` under\n`[models]` in `~/.grok/config.toml`, so one key covers every conversation of a\nworkspace, subagent calls included."],[1608,"Both would be paid for in casts, which is the wrong direction."],[5326,"Branch cleanup cookbook"],[5354,"Branch cleanup is part of the work, not a chore someone does later."],[20,"Branch protection"],[96,"Branch protection on `main` should require a pull request before pushing, and the two\nBazel checks before merging — `//:test-fast` and `//:lint`, run inside the golden image\nthe workflow builds, so a green check means the suite passed on the Linux toolchain the\nstack actually ships rather than on whatever the runner image carried that day."],[4105,"Branch rules live in branching.md; the Bazel harness lives in\ncontribute/building-with-bazel.md and\ncontribute/test-with-bazel.md."],[1,"Branching"],[3,"Branching"],[2910,"branching.md is how it gets to `main`"],[4653,"Bring the TensorFold server up on the box. `<host>` is what `.env` names, and `--apply`\nwrites the per-host override file that server runs:"],[875,"Bringing an old checkout back to a runnable state with one command"],[1842,"Bringing the stable stack up and pulling the models"],[4528,"Browser editor (code-server) stays unhealthy -> check these three, in order"],[1861,"build `evo-t1-dev:latest`"],[1201,"Build it locally when you want the tag in the local store (the Coder docker provider\nresolves `evo-t1-dev:latest` from there and never pulls):"],[1310,"Build the tag first with `bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image` if the daemon does not\nhave it."],[1051,"Building with Bazel"],[1053,"Building with Bazel"],[1452,"building-with-bazel.md explains the maps, runfiles,\nand the daily commands"],[5043,"Builds still succeed, so verify with a workspace build before acting on it. Nothing\nin this repo's compose file