VABILITY_ENABLED` is read from the environment the compose command runs\nwith, and each project reads a different file. `dev-stack` passes `--env-file\ndev-stack.env` when that file sits beside the compose file, so a dev run never sees\n`.env`; `prod-stack` names no env file unless `-e` does, and compose then reads `.env`\nbeside the compose file. Setting the key in the wrong one changes nothing."],[5030,"Cause: `startup_size_guard` looks up a payload the twin does not keep beside its\nown `main.tf` under `templates/common/`, and it did that by reading an ambient\n`REPO_ROOT`. Nothing in `scripts/` ever sets that variable: the checkout is the\n`root` the script resolved and `cd`'d into at startup."],[5051,"Cause: `templatefile()` reads a single-dollar brace reference anywhere in a\n`coder_script` body as an interpolation - inside a shell comment or a `for` loop\nas readily as in a command - and the plan then asks the caller's map for a key\n`main.tf` never declares. Both twins fail at once, because both render the same\nbody from `templates/common/`:"],[4835,"Cause: a pinned download returned an error. The layer prints `curl: (22)` and stops\nrather than shipping a partial image."],[5214,"Cause: after the publish loop the body reads the staged file once more against one\nalternation built from its own deny list, and a match deletes the staged file, prints\nthat, and exits `0` - it refuses rather than correcting, and the `agent.env` an earlier\nboot wrote stays exactly as it was."],[5063,"Cause: an app inside the pane - vim's `+` register, anything that emits OSC 52 -\npushes its copy out through the pane, `set-clipboard on` with\n`allow-passthrough on` forwards it, and code-server's terminal hands the escape to\nnobody."],[4608,"Cause: an older `bazelisk run` used the runfiles copy of `docker-compose.yml`, so\ncompose mounted `./homepage/assets/icons` from `bazel-out`. Docker then created a\ndirectory where `evo-t1.svg` belongs, or the homepage container chowned those\nfiles to root."],[4612,"Cause: an older target ran the runfiles copy of the script, so `$(dirname \"$0\")/..`\nwas the runfiles tree, and that tree ships only `//:stack_data`. The working `.env`\nis untracked, so it exists only in the checkout, and the rotation reported a missing\nfile on a host that had one."],[5041,"Cause: an upstream pin. The Coder image ships its own provisioner binary at\n`/usr/local/bin/terraform` (1.15.5 in `coder:v2.36.6`) and Coder caps the version it\nwas tested against."],[4869,"Cause: both are properties of the environment. Neither points at a workspace that\nneeds repair, and neither is fixable from inside the container."],[5268,"Cause: both show up in the browser console on every dashboard page, and only one of\nthem means anything."],[5022,"Cause: both templates inline `templates/common/vscode-alt.svg` as a\n`data:image/svg+xml;base64` URL on `coder_app.code_server`. Coder v2.36 stores\n`workspace_apps.icon` as `varchar(256)`. A multi-kilobyte SVG produces a data\nURL thousands of characters long, and the insert fails."],[5300,"Cause: by design. Only `prometheus` and `grafana` declare a healthcheck, because\n`grafana/mimir`, `grafana/loki`, `grafana/tempo` and `grafana/alloy` are distroless -\nno shell, no `wget`, no `curl` - so any command a healthcheck ran would fail in the image\nrather than on the service. `running` is the best state those four can report, and adding\na healthcheck to one of them is not the fix for an anxious operator."],[5175,"Cause: Coder injects `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` into the agent environment when the\nworkspace starts."],[5048,"Cause: Coder runs every `coder_script` as `bash -c`. HCL heredocs in `main.tf` only\nescape `$${name}` to `${name}`; `$$((` is two literal dollars. The editor wait loop\nthen becomes `waited=<pid>((waited + 1))`, which is the syntax error. The echo\nbefore the loop still prints."],[4900,"Cause: Docker creates an empty named volume as `root:root` 755. The\n`vscode-settings-<owner-id>` volume is empty on first use (the image has no\nfiles there to copy in), so `coder` cannot write `settings.json`."],[5083,"Cause: each client attached to a tmux session is a full xterm.js in its own\nChrome tab re-parsing the same stream, each holding a line-slot array sized\nfrom `terminal.integrated.scrollback`, and each taking its own copy of the\nrendered stream out of the server - 16 mirrors of one pane pulled 78.7 MB\nthrough an 8 s window in which a single mirror pulled 4.9 MB."],[5224,"Cause: Hermes v0.22.5 refuses a non-loopback bind when no\n`DashboardAuthProvider` is registered. The bundled basic-auth plugin skips\nregistration when the password is empty. Compose interpolation\n`${HERMES_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD:-}` (empty default) did that after a pull that\nadded the Hermes keys: `.env` never gained them, so `prod-stack up` without\n`bootstrap` / `update-configs` crash-looped the gateway. The logs repeat\n\"no auth providers are registered\" and do not mention `plugins.disabled`."],[4846,"Cause: no published source names an upstream `/learn`, so there is none to miss. The\n`xai-org/grok-build` built-in command table, all 240 pages of docs.x.ai, every\nfirst-party changelog under `x.ai/cli/changelogs/`, and the public\n`xai-org/plugin-marketplace` catalog all carry zero occurrences of it, so there is no\npublished copy to vendor in."],[4644,"Cause: no Spark box was reachable, so the Arc answered, and the Arc path returns tool\ncalls as plain text."],[5054,"Cause: path-based Coder apps drop the `?folder=` query before the browser sees\nit, and code-server restores the last opened workspace (often `/home/coder`).\nThe clone itself is fine (`already cloned, skipping` is not a failure)."],[5013,"Cause: provisionerd runs `terraform init` inside the `coder` container.\nDocker's embedded DNS (`127.0.0.11`) forwards names it does not know to\nthe host resolver."],[5291,"Cause: Tempo's metrics_generator does not expose span-metrics for Prometheus to scrape.\nIt computes them and `remote_write`s them to `http://prometheus:9090/api/v1/write`, and\nPrometheus answers that with `404 remote write receiver needs to be enabled with\n--web.enable-remote-write-receiver` until the flag is on. The service is healthy either\nway, so the only visible symptom is a tracing dashboard with no series and a Tempo log\nthat repeats `msg=\"non-recoverable error\" ... failedSampleCount` once a flush interval."],[4765,"Cause: that chat has no model config on this deployment, so there is nothing to route to."],[4837,"Cause: that container started before the CLI was baked into the image, or its\nstart-time download failed."],[4898,"Cause: that container was built from an image predating the Docker client toolchain,\nor from the bare-Ubuntu *Minimal shell* preset."],[5008,"Cause: that image is not in the host's local image store, and Terraform never pulls\nit. The `docker_image` data source only inspects the store."],[5188,"Cause: that refresh is best-effort on purpose. With the flag on, `up` pulls the managed\nkeys into the very file compose is about to interpolate\n(`scripts/dev-stack.sh:677-683`), and a vault that cannot be reached must not hold the\nstack down - so a failed pull costs one warning and the bring-up continues on the\ncredentials the file already held."],[4634,"Cause: that target used to read `.env` with `. ./.env`, so the shell parsed the\noperator's file as code. An unquoted value that holds a space is a variable\nprefix followed by a COMMAND, and `set -e` ended the run on that line before a\nsingle pull:"],[5277,"Cause: the `mimir` datasource is `http://mimir:8080/prometheus`, and that suffix is\nMimir's Prometheus-compatible query namespace - not its root and not its write endpoint."],[4716,"Cause: the auto-compaction summary hung before its first token and nothing abandoned it."],[5220,"Cause: the body publishes single-line values only\n(`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:190-209`). A value that opens a single\nquote without closing it on the same line is a multi-line secret - a PEM, say - and its\ncontinuation lines would be republished as keys of their own, which corrupts the value\nand puts secret bytes into key names."],[5200,"Cause: the body's first gate, `templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:14-20` - any\none of those six empty on the agent environment prints this and exits `0`, so the\nworkspace boots with no vault secrets and nothing else complains."],[5208,"Cause: the body's second gate, `templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:27-30`."],[5077,"Cause: the browser exposes `navigator.clipboard` to a secure context only, and\nCoder's LAN door is plain HTTP by default (`CODER_ACCESS_URL` is the LAN\naddress)."],[5253,"Cause: the card's `siteMonitor` is a specific path (`/api/health`, `/-/healthy`,\n`/ready`), and \"the container exists\" says nothing about that path answering. Four of the\nsix containers are distroless, so nothing inside them can be asked; the log is the only\ninterrogation available."],[5242,"Cause: the Chat tab is a WebSocket on `/api/pty` and `/api/ws`. Hermes sends a\nkeepalive every 20 seconds. Close code `4403` is the Host / Origin / peer guard."],[5037,"Cause: the CLI is talking to a public subdomain, and Authelia answers its API calls\nwith the sign-in page."],[4674,"Cause: the exclusion people reach for for this is the one that cannot fire on the failure\na down box actually raises. `_is_cooldown_required` returns False the moment the exception\ntext contains `APIConnectionError` (`litellm/router_utils/cooldown_handlers.py:223`,\n`ignored_strings`)."],[4744,"Cause: the hop is a proxy behaviour, not a client one, and it needs four things true in the\nsame moment. With any one of them false the summary rides a Spark box exactly as it did\nbefore these two aliases existed - the 107 s to 1915 s measured above - and that is the slow\npath, not a fault."],[4772,"Cause: the LiteLLM alias behind that model has no deployment the router will use. The\nArc aliases (`chat`, `coder`, `coder-fast`) go unhealthy the moment their weights are\nnot in the IPEX-LLM container, which answers `model \"...\" not found, try pulling it\nfirst`, and the Spark `agent` aliases go unhealthy when no box answers."],[5287,"Cause: the only host path in the bundle is\n`${STACK_DOCKER_LOG_DIR:-/var/lib/docker/containers}`, mounted read-only into Alloy. If\nthe daemon writes its json-file logs somewhere else, Alloy tails an empty directory and\nLoki's badge stays green, because `/ready` reports the store, not the supply."],[4874,"Cause: the profile asks tmux questions before it hands the tab to anything, and tmux\nexits 1 whenever it refuses."],[5123,"Cause: the refresh script inherits `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` from the agent, and\n`gh auth login --with-token` refuses stdin while those names are set (`The value of the\nGH_TOKEN environment variable is being used for authentication`)."],[5294,"Cause: the same `421` the Hermes entry above describes - this box's `router` answers it\nwhen the Host matches no `server_name` - with one extra way to reach it that the other\nfive names do not have. `scripts/lib/domain.sh` composes the Grafana name from the naming\nparts and reads no flag, so `bootstrap` writes the vhost and `STACK_GRAFANA_URL` even when\n`OBSERVABILITY_ENABLED=false`. The router then has a correct `server_name` with nothing\nbehind it, and the browser gets a `502` from Traefik or a `421` if the Host was rewritten\nbefore it arrived."],[5003,"Cause: the sidecar is unhealthy, its image was never pulled, or the workspace was\ncreated with DinD off."],[4887,"Cause: the three per-owner Grok volumes mount *under* `~/.grok` - `grok-notes-<owner-id>`\nat `~/.grok/notes`, with the memory and sessions pair beside it - and the Docker daemon\ncreates a bind mount's target path as `root:root` 755. Whenever those mount points are\nnew, `~/.grok` arrives owned by root and the workspace user cannot create anything in\nit."],[5230,"Cause: th