ILD.bazel`."],[4691,"Each entry carries `model_id`, which is the per-box deployment id the config names\n(`agent-spark-1`, `agent-swarm-spark-2`, ...), plus `api_base` and\n`exception_status`, and the payload totals them as `healthy_count` /\n`unhealthy_count`."],[3252,"Each fast lane hops to the lane it is the twin of:\n`- agent-xhigh-fast: [\"agent-xhigh\", \"coder\"]` and\n`- agent-swarm-fast: [\"agent-swarm\", \"coder\"]`\n(`litellm/config.yaml:887-888`). Same boxes, same baked level, same pin behaviour, so a\nsession that lost its own group keeps everything except that group's routing state. Both\nchains are acyclic and end at `coder` like every other here: agent-xhigh-fast ->\nagent-xhigh -> coder, agent-swarm-fast -> agent-swarm -> coder."],[4597,"Each fence below is one copy-paste action. A heading quotes the error string where there\nis one, so start with `grep -n` on the text you saw."],[644,"Each file also gets a twin in the `~/.agents` tree, because the `execute`-lane delegation\nthis stack teaches starts `grok -p` inside the workspace and that CLI reads the\n`~/.agents` convention. The chat agent would only ever take the `~/.coder` copies - skill\ndedupe is first-match-wins, home scope before working-dir paths - so one agent never\nloads a skill twice; the twins exist for the CLI, not as a second source for chat."],[2200,"Each grandchild is its own session, so it is not charged to the slot count above; what it\ndoes cost is a model stream, which is why a tree is counted by summing the in-flight\n`1 + spawns` over every task and keeping that total at or below the fleet's stream count\n(`fleet:` in the plan, 15 by default)."],[2268,"Each is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter whose body is the child's system prompt; the\nseeds are `templates/common/<name>.AGENT.md` and they land at\n`~/.grok/agents/<name>.md`. A definition is what fixes a role's model, tools and prompt\nmode, which a persona deliberately does not (`~/.grok/docs/user-guide/16-subagents.md:77`)."],[3680,"each is pure ASCII, LF-only, one trailing newline"],[1220,"Each key belongs to an extension the row above installs, which is what makes the pin do\nsomething."],[3431,"Each lane lives at `<scaffold>/.template-lanes/<lane>/`. A file there is copied over the rendered\ntree at the same path, so a lane may add files or replace a core one. `LANE.md` and\n`gitignore.fragment` are lane metadata: the renderer appends the fragment to `.gitignore` and drops\nboth from the output. Ask for a lane the fetched tree does not have and the run dies naming the\nlanes it does offer."],[102,"Each layer names the branch below it as its base, and only the bottom layer names `main`.\nA reviewer then reads that layer's own commits rather than the change as a whole, which is\nthe reason to stack at all."],[4722,"Each link in the chain, measured:"],[2224,"Each may fan out up to three read-only mappers of its own under the depth above."],[678,"Each of those `chomp(file())` calls sits inside its own block\nrather than behind a `local.`, because a size reader credits a payload by the\n`chomp(file(\"${path.module}/name\"))` literal it can see in the body's own block, and\nfollows a `local.` exactly one hop (`scripts/lib/startup_size.awk`, invariants)."],[2152,"Each of those grandchildren is its own session with its own `max_concurrent`, and what\nit costs the\nfleet is one model stream, so a tree is budgeted by summing the in-flight `1 + spawns`\nover every task and keeping that total at or below the fleet's stream count (`fleet:` in\nthe plan, 15 by default, `templates/common/ez-micro-plan.plan_check.py:42`). That total\nis a separate number from the session cap above, which counts one parent's own children."],[2613,"Each one runs with a plan first and an approval card before the mutating command."],[1377,"Each page writes its own `# H1`, once, as the first heading of the body, spelled exactly like\nthe frontmatter `title`."],[2342,"Each panelist re-runs the producers'\n`done:`