eme and\nits config extras are its own, and a hand edit there lasts until that one workspace\nrestarts."],[2879,"Each subject has exactly one page, and the README links to that page rather than\nrepeating it."],[538,"Each template creates one Docker container per workspace."],[241,"Each template dir keeps its own independent copy of the `.tftpl` payloads\n(`startup.sh.tftpl`, `settings.json.tftpl`, `grok-config.toml.tftpl`). Change one twin,\nchange the other."],[2107,"Each template's startup script probes `command -v grok` on every start and\nre-downloads from `https://x.ai/cli/install.sh` - bounded, with retries - only\nwhile `grok` is missing from PATH. That installer follows the `stable` pointer, not\nthis pin. It deliberately does **not** fetch on every boot: the bake-in under\n`/usr/local/bin` is the upgrade path, so shipping a new CLI means bumping the pin,\nrebuilding the image (`bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image`) and re-pushing the templates."],[3246,"Each thinking alias carries the same hop of its own - `agent-low: [\"coder\"]`, and the\nsame for `agent-medium` and `agent-xhigh`. Groups are independent, so none of them\ninherits `agent`'s entry, and the five pinned lanes go down with the same boxes."],[3102,"Each thinking group, the swarm group, the two fan-out groups and the two fast groups carry\ntheir own triple - `agent-low-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-medium-spark-1/2/3`,\n`agent-xhigh-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-swarm-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-explore-spark-1/2/3`,\n`agent-review-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-xhigh-fast-spark-1/2/3`, `agent-swarm-fast-spark-1/2/3`"],[5209,"Each twin declares `infisical_pull_on_start` with `default = false`\n(`templates/workspace/coder.tf:270-274`, `templates/devcontainer/coder.tf:257-261`), and\nthe push forwards\n`--var infisical_pull_on_start=true` only when `.env` carries a truthy\n`INFISICAL_PULL_ON_START` *under* a truthy `INFISICAL_ENABLED`\n(`scripts/push-template.sh:636`, `:668-671`), so an adopted vault still ships a boot that never\nwaits on the network."],[422,"Each workspace keeps its own and a change applies on the next start."],[794,"Each workspace's agent injects a `GIT_ASKPASS` helper pointing at the `coder` binary it\nstages, alongside the `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` pair in the agent environment. Some\nbuilds of that binary answer every prompt with `unrecognized subcommand`, so the stack\ndepends on the helper below rather than on askpass, and `check` prints a note line when\nthat askpass answers nothing."],[3271,"Edit `litellm/config.yaml`."],[2976,"Editing an alias"],[4333,"Editing that CSV and re-running `--apply` reports `updated`, and the CLI then tells you to\n`--restart` so the running exporter rereads it (`scripts/spark-monitor.sh:696-697`)."],[283,"Editing the common copy changes both templates; the staged copy overwrites any\nsame-named file the template dir still carries."],[2795,"Editing the copy in the volume is how an operator ends up with a config no one can\nreproduce."],[5238,"Editing the rendered\n  `proxy/router.gen.conf` instead only survives until the next bootstrap, which\n  re-renders it from the parts."],[211,"Editor settings seed"],[1221,"Editor taste (theme, minimap, word wrap) still arrives from `seed-dev-env.sh` through\n`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json`, so the two never fight."],[4523,"Editor, credentials, the clone"],[4590,"Editor, credentials, the clone, UI logins, and the public names (`421`, Chat `4403`, Traefik)"],[205,"Editor, terminal, and the metadata tiles"],[2430,"Edits inside a built dev container therefore survive neither a rebuild nor a look at\nthe shared file. Everywhere else no settings map is passed at all, because a merge\nwould replace the symlink."],[2428,"Edits to the overlay stick, and every workspace that owner has gets them layered over its\nown render; delete it to copy the template in again. From the\nhost it is the volume's `settings.json`:"],[921,"Eight of those sixteen are the python helpers three of them run, under a `scripts/`\nsubdirectory of the same skill directory; a reseed recreates that directory when\na workspace lost it."],[1777,"Either form:"],[510,"Either way `folder` is the clone, so code-server and its terminal profiles land on the\nrepository, and the **Web Terminal** button `cd`s there too."],[4655,"Either way keep `SPARK_n_API_KEY` non-empty: `SPARK_1_API_KEY`, `SPARK_2_API_KEY`,\n`SPARK_3_API_KEY`. An empty key fails every request inside the proxy before it ever\nreaches the box."],[3733,"Either way the fix is the file and a recreate of `prometheus` so Compose renders it again;\nthe metrics stay authenticated."],[2348,"Either way the fix is the seed under `templates/common/` and a re-materialize, never a patch\nto the copy that is running - the same rule the two skill families above live by\n(the three stack-seeded skill commands)."],[2518,"Either way the marker never reaches the model: the agent strips HTML comments from\ninjected instruction text."],[4713,"Eligible is the precise word: the\ncooldown entry that same loop wrote for the box has to expire on its own\n(`cooldown_time`), and every failing cycle re-arms it, so the first turn back can\nstill land on another box."],[2771,"Empty (CI `compose config`) falls back to `.:/opt/stack`."],[4245,"empty is LAN-only;"],[1024,"Empty is not a working value - LiteLLM v1.102.1 fails every request at\nclient construction (`AuthenticationError`, before reaching the box) and `agent`\nfalls back to `coder`."],[1001,"Empty keeps everything below LAN-only and every derived `STACK_*_URL` stays empty."],[25,"Enabling it, and the two CLIs"],[4320,"Enrolling or un-enrolling the fleet with one key, without editing a compose file"],[3805,"Enrolling the Sparks without hand-editing a Prometheus config"],[4290,"Enrolling the three DGX Sparks into the Prometheus stack: the two exporter containers a box needs, the one opt-in key, the plan/prove/install commands, how the boxes reach Prometheus through file_sd, and what this change leaves unproven."],[552,"Ensures the **Grok Build CLI** is on PATH. The golden image ships it, so the\n`https://x.ai/cli/install.sh` download runs only where `grok` is missing from PATH -\nthe `ubuntu:24.04` image option, or a home volume that never received the CLI."],[940,"Enter keeps a reusable value already set in a sibling env file, or the example default."],[896,"Enter keeps a sibling's value or the example default."],[1004,"Entries are DNS names, not URLs: no scheme, no port, no path. The entry with no\nprefix is the dashboard."],[1418,"Enumerate targets instead of guessing them"],[1437,"Enumerating real target names instead of guessing them"],[4963,"Enumeration is one `docker ps -a` on that label, cut into four\ntab-separated columns - workspace, owner, container, state - and a row is judged only when\nit is exactly those four columns, the workspace, container and state each say something,\nand no one of the four runs past 255 characters (`scripts/subagent-check.sh:894-896`). A\nfield that long is no Coder name, and a container whose state nobody read is neither the\nrunning one nor the stopped one, so exec-ing into it would print a verdict built on\nnothing."],[5405,"Environment is a workspace or an `envs/<env>/` directory that instantiates one shared module;\n`terraform plan` against `envs/staging` and `envs/production` is the same module revision twice.\nArgoCD gets one `Application` per environment, all pointing at the same Kustomize or chart path,\nand promotion is a commit that bumps the image tag (by hand, or by the Image Updater)."],[21,"Environments"],[97,"Environments are where future protection rules and secrets go, per environment:\n`development`, `staging`, `production`."],[5317,"Environments without environment branches"],[2203,"Equal numbers mean the session is sized for the fleet: every slot it holds is a stream a\nbox can actually serve."],[136,"Escape hatches when a body outgrows the bound"],[691,"Every `[mcp_servers.*]` block the render writes names its binary by the absolute path the\ngolden image bakes (`/opt/npm-global/bin/...`), so the config and the image are two\nartifacts that have to agree - and they do not always. A workspace running an image built\nbefore that binary was added boots with a lane that can never start, and the CLI only\nsays so in its own MCP log."],[1786,"every `{{HOMEPAGE_VAR_*}}` token has a key in `docker-compose.yml`, and every\n`HOMEPAGE_VAR_*` key is used by some config file"],[718,"Every `INFISICAL_` name is filtered out of that file, and that filter is the load-bearing\nline (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:180`): the vault's own address and\nUniversal Auth pair are plausible keys in the very project being exported, and they must\nnot be republished as workspace environment through a file, when the agent environment is\nthe place Coder renders them per start (`:86-87`)."],[4220,"Every `location` adds `X-Evo-Proxy` with the upstream name, and `always` is what\nmakes it survive a 502. Read it beside `X-Coder-Request-Id`, which Coder's own proxy\nsets on an answered request: neither header means the request stopped at Traefik or\nCloudflare, and `421` means the Host header matched no server block here."],[1240,"every `MODULE.bazel` fetch"],[4106,"Every `scripts/**/*.sh` file starts with a `# ## ` header that names the file and says whether it is an entry point or a sourced library."],[3007,"Every alias is a stable name. A workspace setting never has to change when a backend\nmoves behind one."],[4826,"Every body speaks the same shapes (`templates/common/boot-log.lib.sh`, handed to each body\nas the `boot_log_lib` key of its `templatefile()` map):"],[669,"Every braced shell expansion in one has to be written `$${name}`; the one-dollar braced\n  form is swallowed as an interpolation, in a comment or a `for` loop as readily as in a\n  command. The unbraced form (`$name`) needs no escape."],[113,"Every call goes through `env -u GH_TOKEN -u GITHUB_TOKEN gh api`, for the reason in\ntroubleshooting.md."],[79,"Every change answers something, and the tracker is where the answer gets recorded. This is the\nsame etiquette `templates/common/GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md` teaches every workspace, so a bug an agent\nfixes and a bug a human fixes leave the tracker in the same state."],[3806,"Every command here is a Bazel target run from a **host** shell. Inside a Coder workspace\nthe `docker` CLI only reaches that workspace's own DinD sidecar, so a check aimed at the\nstack's own containers has to be run where the stack lives."],[2686,"Every container-level fact comes from `docker inspect` or `docker compose ps`; nothing\nwrites, restarts, recreates, or execs."],[4879,"Every control call is bounded\n  by `timeout`."],[2065,"Every copy that used to end a selection is unbound - Enter, `C-j`, `D`, `A`, the\nword and line copies a double- or triple-click fires, the copy a drag release ran,\nand the `y` the earlier seed bound itself - along with the prefix paste `]` and the\nbuffer picker `=`."],[1457,"Every count is a floor, because a truncated tool result hides a call"],[226,"Every create-form field and template variable, with its default"],[702,"Every credential rides the **agent environment** rather than the script body, for the\nreason every credential in `main.tf` rides it: Coder stores a rendered\n`coder_script.script` as text on the server, so a value interpolated into one would sit in\nCoder's database in plain sight, while an agent-env value is rendered per start and never\nwritten to disk (`templates/workspace/main.tf:687-691`)."],[3687,"every datasource is one of the four provisioned UIDs"],[652,"Every exec'd body narrates itself, so a workspace start reads as a staged run rather than a\nwall of file copies. The verbs are `scripts/lib/common.sh`'s own words - `== section ==`,\n`-> phase`, `ok:`, `warning:`, `note:`, `error:`, and a closing `summary:` - so one\nvocabulary covers the host CLIs and the workspace boot."],[935,"Every flag goes **after*