r` the mounts are on the workspace container only. A dev container the repo\nbuilds on the sidecar keeps its own home and its own `~/.grok`, which is why the live\n`notes-setup.sh` there is a regular file reached through the clone bind rather than a\nlink into `~/.grok`, and why a built dev container sees neither the settings volume nor\nthe shared editor overlay."],[646,"In `devcontainer`, working-dir resolution has a second case: with the dev-container\ntoggle off the agent's working dir is `/home/coder`, exactly as in `workspace`; with it\non, the dev container's own working dir is the cloned folder under\n`/srv/coder-devcontainers/...`, and that folder ships no skill tree, so the `~/.coder`\ncopies remain the live source either way."],[605,"In `shared` mode (the default `grok_profile_mode`) the container mounts three of the\nowner's Docker volumes read-write, nested inside that workspace's own `/home/coder`\nvolume: `grok-notes-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/notes`, `grok-memory-<owner-id>` at\n`~/.grok/memory` and `grok-sessions-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/sessions`."],[2355,"In `shared` mode, three directories: `notes/` (the canonical copy of each\nrepository's private scratch `notes.md`), `memory/`, and `sessions/` - one volume\neach, mounted at `~/.grok/notes`, `~/.grok/memory` and `~/.grok/sessions`. Nothing\nelse under `~/.grok` is shared: `config.toml`, `skills/`, the MCP warm caches and a CLI\nyou installed yourself under `~/.grok/bin` are regular files on this workspace's own\nhome volume, and those die with the workspace."],[3194,"In `shared` profile mode that is one file per workspace, re-rendered on that workspace's own\nstart, so two workspaces of one owner can carry different renders of that key."],[647,"In a `SKILL.md` the marker sits *after* the `---` frontmatter: the skill parser needs\n`---` on line 1 and silently drops a skill whose first line is anything else. In an\ninjected instruction file the marker is pure provenance, because injected content has its\nHTML comments stripped anyway. The stage is best-effort: a read-only or missing `$HOME`\nchanges nothing observable."],[1112,"In CI the gate container is `--rm` and runs with `HOME=/tmp` and `USER=$(id -un)`, so a\nplain run keeps neither cache between jobs, and Bazel can name a uid the image passwd\nfile does not list; the cache that survives there is the image's buildx GHA cache."],[4725,"In every one of the 79 wall-clock failures no first token ever arrived. Successful\ncompactions do stream: their `elapsed_ms` spans 107 s to 1915 s, and 18 of the 36 ran\npast 300 s, which is the summary the budget was discarding."],[541,"in shared mode the three state volumes `grok-notes-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/notes`,\n`grok-memory-<owner-id>` at `~/.grok/memory` and `grok-sessions-<owner-id>` at\n`~/.grok/sessions`"],[5399,"In that repository the environment branches were still sitting on the\nremote (`dev`, `development`, `staging`, `uat`, `prod`) while every one of them reported\n`ahead=0` against `main`: five branches, zero unique commits, waiting for someone to confirm the\ndelete."],[5352,"Incomplete or experimental work lands on the trunk behind a flag that defaults off."],[4079,"Ingress"],[4098,"Ingress rules: what runs from a shell and what is a Bazel target"],[500,"Inside a built dev container the same folder appears under `/workspaces/<repo-name>`,\nthe devcontainer CLI's default mount target and where the dev-container editor opens."],[952,"Inside a running container the same targets are `refresh-configs`'s job too: same reseed set, same marker rule, `--json` for a machine-readable\nanswer, and `--litellm-url <url>` for a stack environment that publishes\nLiteLLM on a port other than 4000 (the reseeded `settings.json` then still\nnames that stack's own model transport)."],[2089,"Inside a tmux pane the client's wheel has nothing to walk - tmux paints in the\nalternate screen, so that buffer holds no pane history - and the 100000 lines live\nbehind `Prefix-[`, paid for in the server and not in the tab."],[5112,"Inside a workspace it repairs that workspace; on the stack host `fix <container>\n[repo-url]` names the one workspace it repairs, and a host run with no container is\nrefused for exactly that reason."],[3005,"Inside a workspace the key travels as the `LITELLM_API_KEY` environment variable, which\n`~/.grok/config.toml` references by `env_key`, so no key byte lands in a file."],[4995,"inside a workspace, or in the contributor container, where `CODER_WORKSPACE_ID` or\n`EVO_T1_DEVCONTAINER` is set: `error: subagent-check --all is a stack-host run: this\nshell's docker addresses its own sidecar`;"],[2760,"inside the container,\n`curl -s -H 'Accept: application/json' \"$SEARXNG_URL/search?q=hermes&format=json\"`\nis the exact request the provider makes"],[1684,"Inside the contributor dev container (devcontainer.md) the commands\nabove are exactly what CI runs."],[168,"Inside the workspace container"],[4297,"Install (`--apply`)"],[5162,"Install Coder's App from the\nworkspace **Install GitHub App** button, or at\ngithub.com/apps/coder/installations/new,\ngrant the repo, then restart. A private repository is never visible to a credential\nthat was never granted it."],[5183,"Install gh, then run `fix` again. The golden image ships a pinned copy (`gh 2.101.0`,\nfrom the release tarball, at `/usr/local/bin/gh`); apt's `gh` is 2.45 and predates\nsubcommands the agent experience uses, so the durable fix is the image, not the distro\npackage."],[3864,"Install the CLI and start the services"],[3990,"Install the CLI binary on the host."],[1829,"Install the toolchain"],[4549,"Install your own credential, if the report earned it"],[222,"Installing a pasted PAT, and the full usage"],[2431,"Installing Cline, Roo, the Red Hat YAML extension and Material Icon Theme is a\nmanual step in the Extensions panel (Open VSX by default). If an extension build\nnames its settings differently, set the OpenAI-compatible endpoint and key in its\nUI."],