istant can plan a change, show the plan, and wait for you to approve it before it\ntouches anything."],[3243,"It also buys a `service_healthy` wait that\nnothing here takes: `hermes` keeps `depends_on: litellm: condition: service_started`\ndeliberately, because compose waits indefinitely for a healthy condition and a probe that\nstopped passing would hold the host assistant down with the proxy."],[2391,"It also names every engine the instance has parked and\n  the reason its backend gave (`parked by its backend: google: access denied`),\n  read out of the reply body whether or not that reply found results - an instance\n  running on half its engines is visible there before it starts answering empty."],[2250,"It also refuses:"],[618,"It also runs there because\nthat body is already where a stack-owned file under `~/.grok` is refreshed against its\nmarker."],[2421,"It also states that native `web_search` is parked so nobody spends a turn rediscovering\nthe 400.\n**Tool output stays out of the parent context** makes that\ntool use delegated work: the child returns a digest - numbered findings, each one\nclaim, one source URL and at most two lines of support, no raw result dumps,\nconfidence stated - and keeps the raw pages to itself."],[3330,"It answers one question - if this box rebooted right now, could you decrypt it\nfrom a laptop - and closes with either `ok: this box can be unlocked from a laptop after a\nreboot` or `error: do not reboot yet - N blocker(s)`."],[3084,"It behaves that way on both `/api/chat` and `/v1/chat/completions`."],[4940,"It can sit in two places, and they clear differently:"],[5275,"It carries\nno diagnostic value, shares no cause with the `501`, and keeps printing after that one\nis fixed. Nothing in this stack can silence it, and nothing needs to."],[2231,"It carries `## Goal` with numbered acceptance checks, `## Dispatch` (lane, `slots:`, where the slot\ncount came from, `parent keeps:` for the hotspots the parent merges itself), `## Lanes`,\n`## Tasks`, `## Ledger`, and `## Not doing`. Beside it sit the context briefs and the\nchild reports:"],[514,"It carries its own copies of `startup.sh.tftpl`, `settings.json.tftpl` and\n`grok-config.toml.tftpl`, so the tmux-default terminal and LiteLLM wiring above apply\nto it too."],[2389,"It carries nine tools - `search`, `image_search`, `news_search`,\n`video_search`, `music_search`, `paper_search`, `fetch_content`, `autocomplete`,\n`list_engines` - and an agent's two workhorses are the first and the seventh:\n`search` for anything that is not a library question, `fetch_content` for a URL\nalready in hand. Measure the self-hosted lane with:"],[295,"It confirms an **active** version."],[4986,"It counts as the row's one warning and both JSON fields come back `null`, because there is\nno number left to report."],[3100,"It decides only for unpinned traffic: the affinity pin below resolves first, and\n`least-busy` runs when nothing is pinned, when the pinned deployment is unhealthy or in\ncooldown, and for any request with no session id. Every `agent-swarm`,\n`agent-explore`, `agent-review` and `agent-swarm-fast` request is unpinned traffic,\nwhich is the whole of those four lanes."],[5140,"It does not ask \"is there a credential\" and it does not trust the environment: it runs\ngit's own configured helper the way git runs it, takes the password that would go on the\nwire, and probes THAT credential against the endpoint `git push` negotiates through -\none GET of `<repo>.git/info/refs?service=git-receive-pack`."],[619,"It does not lean on running after\nthe `startup_script`: a `coder_script` runs in no promised order with it\n(`templates/workspace/coder.tf:272`), so the argument is the marker itself."],[4740,"It does not stop the upstream from hanging. It stops the hang being bought three times,\nand stops a finished summary being thrown away."],[948,"It does not touch `~/.grok/config.toml`. That file is rendered *inside* the\nworkspace, and it is a per-workspace file on that workspace's own home volume:"],[534,"It either runs the command (`--no-wait`; watch with `coder ls` / `coder logs <name>`)\nor, with no usable `coder` login, prints the same command to run by hand and exits 0."],[4962,"It enumerates every container labelled `coder.workspace_id` on the daemon (the DinD\nsidecar carries that label as well and is left out), reads each container's rendered\nprofile, and prints the width verdict for it beside the one `coder update` line that\nclears the stored value."],[2315,"It fails open on an event it cannot parse, and denies when\n  the runner reports `toolInputTruncated`, because that is text the scan never saw\n  (`templates/common/hooks.secret-guard.sh`)."],[3118,"It has no pin, and that is what makes it the wrong home for a long single-thread\nconversation. Pinning buys prefix-cache locality; without it the next turn may be\nprefilled on a different box and pay prefill again. A chat, an orchestrator, or\nanything whose turns share a warm prefix belongs on `agent`. The lane is for\nindependent parallel work - subagents, batch edits, one-shot jobs, which is also why\nthe two reader lanes below lift the pin the same way."],[5170,"It installs that credential into that one workspace's gh auth store and then\nre-installs the env-proof helper that `gh auth setup-git` would otherwise leave behind,\nsince that helper goes straight back to echoing a stale env pair over the token just\npasted."],[2384,"It is **not** a model transport, and the native tool is parked: both twins render\n`disable_web_search = true` at top level, so a session starts with no `web_search`\ntool at all. Measured 2026-10-25: no model transport this box ships serves that\ntool type."],[693,"It is advisory only: one warning line per missing path, never a failed start, so the call\nswallows whatever status the function returns."],[335,"It is also the manual path after you register an account, and the retry path for one\ntemplate."],[1972,"It is always on