ry tab of the clone watches the one agent run.\nThe session is created detached and attached in a second call, so the tab that\nbrings the server up never takes a running agent down with it, and it makes the same\nstale-client sweep its sibling does."],[3724,"It is the check that catches the two failures a `running` state hides: an Alloy pointed at\nan empty log root, and a Prometheus that scraped everything for a day and never wrote a\nsample to Mimir."],[2070,"It is the escape hatch for a long scroll, because tmux paints in the alternate\nscreen - it sends `ESC[?1049h` either way - so the client holds no scrollback of its\nown and a wheel over a pane has nothing to walk."],[2709,"It is the lane for a parallel fan-out, not for one long Hermes session - a single\nthread would give up the pin's prefix-cache locality and could be prefilled on a\ndifferent box each turn. Hermes keeps `agent` as its default."],[1329,"It is tracked in this repository, and `probe_repo` (in `scripts/lib/workspace.sh`) treats a\nclone that tracks it as a **miss** — exit `3` — even when the same clone also tracks\n`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`."],[603,"It is written beside its target and `mv`'d in - and `chmod\n0644`'d first, because `mktemp` makes 0600 and `mv` keeps that mode - so the rename is the\nfirst moment the file exists for anyone to source, and a process that starts seconds\nlater never reads a half-written library."],[778,"It joins the list into one `additional_repos`\nparameter, so `\"a , b\"` and `\"a\\nb\"` both arrive in the template as `a,b`."],[2313,"It leaves the read-side `old_string`/`old_text` alone, so a secret an older commit wrote\n  cannot convict every later edit beside it."],[53,"it lists every branch the trunk already contains, every unmerged branch past the branch\nlifetime, and every branch that carries an environment in its name, each printed with its\ntip SHA because that is the record a deletion has to leave behind."],[3404,"It lives in its own repository -- by default `https://github.com/toxicoder/ezrepo` -- and this\nrepo's whole job is to fetch that tree and render it."],[522,"It looks for a dev container in `.devcontainer/`, `.github/devcontainers/`, or a\n`devcontainer.json`/`devcontainer.yml` anywhere in the tree."],[1815,"It matters only when `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` gives the dashboard a public name -\nthe page already sits behind the password, and its paths should not reach a crawler\neither."],[5113,"It mints a live token through Coder external-auth (the\ninjected pair is never trusted, because it is the frozen copy that expired), writes the\ngh auth store, points git's `github.com` and `gist.github.com` credential helper at that\nstore through a form that clears the env pair first, then re-runs the write probe and\nprints the verdict again, so it proves itself."],[533,"It names no `--stop-after`, so a script-made workspace gets no autostop deadline."],[3999,"It needs `python3` on PATH to parse the response, and the CLI from step 3. The\nmachine identity's own token is checked for presence and deliberately not stored: it stays\ninside Infisical and every later run exchanges the pair below for a fresh one."],[947,"It never drops a key your env file still sets; retired keys are commented out\nin place."],[537,"It never mints, reads, or stores a token - unlike `push-template.sh`, which mints its\nown because a template push has no other credential path. With `CODER_SESSION_TOKEN`\nset but `CODER_URL` unset it refuses to guess, and an empty token is a *not yet* state\nrather than an error."],[946,"It never prints an env value that looks like a credential."],[2464,"It never reaches a Grok Build CLI: the CLI reads no Coder table, and its compaction\nsummary is an **in-session call on the session model** - the `[models] default` alias,\n`agent` here - which is why the summary inherits that lane's output ceiling (measured\non the wire at `max_tokens: 32768`) instead of a cheap helper lane's."],[1288,"It never writes 