n."],[5172,"It REPLACES the per-start\nminted credential for that workspace, and while the account stays connected the next\n`gh_token_refresh` run rewrites the store, so treat a pasted PAT as a stand-in and\nrotate or remove it in GitHub -> Applications when the work ends."],[822,"It REPLACES the per-start minted\ncredential, the next `gh_token_refresh` rewrites the store while an account is connected,\nand `gh auth logout` or a rebuild clears it - treat it as a stand-in and rotate or remove\nit in GitHub -> Settings -> Applications when the work ends."],[54,"It reports and never deletes - `--plan` prints the commands, and deleting stays the\noperator's call."],[289,"It resolves the repo root from `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the real checkout\n`bazelisk run` names) ahead of the runfiles copy, so `.env` and the template\nfiles are regular files rather than execroot symlinks."],[290,"It resolves the running stack on the Docker **daemon** by container label, never\nthrough a cwd-resolved compose project."],[660,"It returns 1 and prints\n  `error:` when the directory stays unwritable, which is what lets a body refuse its own\n  `ok:`."],[2323,"It returns one context line naming the label and that log; it never runs a test inline, so the\nedit turn does not wait on the suite."],[694,"It runs after the clone because it is about what the clone holds, and it also runs on a\nre-start that cloned nothing, because the devcontainer build re-runs then too."],[4994,"It runs on the stack host and refuses everywhere else, because a workspace's `docker`\naddresses its own sidecar (see the preamble at the top of this page):"],[341,"It runs the image's own `coder` binary, so client and server are the same build."],[617,"It runs there rather than in `startup.sh.tftpl`\nbecause the startup argument sits under a byte gate that holds the composed body to 110592\nbytes (12288 of room under the 122880 budget this repo sets for itself, which is itself\n8 KiB under the kernel's measured 131072 one-argument ceiling; see\nThe one-argument ceiling), and the `devcontainer` twin already\ncomposes 110242 of those, leaving 350 bytes for everything else."],[4787,"It separates engines that\n  answered, engines that were unresponsive, and an empty result page, and it names\n  each engine the instance has parked together with the reason the backend gave\n  (`parked by its backend: google: access denied`."],[521,"It shallow-clones (`--depth 1 --no-checkout --single-branch`) into a temporary\ndirectory, from the host, and lists the tracked files."],[2126,"It shares the body because that body exists to stay under the one-argument ceiling\n(coder-templates.md), not because the\nfour commands do the same job; three of the four carry a python helper next to their\n`SKILL.md` and `ez-trunk-based-repo` carries none."],[2661,"It ships off and the published mapping binds **loopback**, because this server\n\"adds full access to the toolset, including terminal commands\" per upstream, on a\ncontainer that holds the docker socket."],[4768,"It skips while the coder or db container is down, or nobody has registered yet, and\nre-running it repairs a provider that drifted and moves a model pin whose alias has\nsince gone unhealthy."],[3268,"It spread 12/10/8 across the three deployments and returned 30x 200."],[728,"It stays on the main agent so\na failed clone (or a `devcontainer` subagent that never starts) still leaves the\nbutton on the workspace page. Device-flow login is not the App install: with the\ninjected App (id `github`) that page prints \"You must install the GitHub App to\nclone private repositories\" as unlinked plaintext, because Coder omits\n`AppInstallURL` on the default provider."],[294,"It streams the source as a tar on stdin, with symlinks dereferenced into regular\nfiles. Coder's provisioner unpacks that archive into an empty workdir and does\nnot follow host paths, so a stored runfiles symlink plans as \"No configuration\nfiles\"."],[3833,"it surfaces whatever the registry answers when the pull fails"],[2312,"It sweeps the fields a write puts text into - the flat `new_string`, `content`, `contents`,\n  `command` and `text`, and\n  `new_string`, `new_text`, `content`, `contents` and `text` inside each entry of a batched\n  `edits` array - one level deep and no deeper, so an unknown nesting is not swept and the\n  truncation check is what covers it."],[528,"It then assembles `coder create` with the template's parameters:"],[2512,"It travels as\n`templates/common/GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md`, staged beside the staged `main.tf` and\nread back with `file()` / `filebase64()`; `templates/common/` keeps one copy for\nboth templates, and the push stages it into each template's pushed copy."],[1717,"It tries these candidates in order, and prints the first candidate that proves out:"],[3256,"It used to be a chain, `agent -> agent-fast -> coder`. `agent-fast` was a second alias\nfor the same model on a second box with a lower output ceiling; one group of three equal\ndeployments already covers every reachable box, so the chain collapsed to one acyclic\nhop."],[3723,"It walks the bundle outward from the dotenv - the operator keys, the host's log\ndirectory, the profile render, each container's state, each endpoint, whether data is\nactually moving - and prints the stack's usual `summary: N ok, W warnings, F failed`."],[2302,"It writes `code-index.json` for a program and `code-index.md` for a person under\n`~/.grok/notes/<host>/<owner>/<repo>/` - the same notes directory `ez-learn` owns, outside the\nclone, carried by the owner's `grok-notes-<owner-id>` volume, so nothing new runs and\nnothing is committed."],[267,"It writes the dispatch plan to `.grok/plans/<slug>/plan.md` (Goal, Dispatch, Lanes,\n  Tasks, Ledger, Not doing) with `ctx/` briefs and `results/` reports beside it, in the\n  same shape the rulebook at `~/.grok/AGENTS.md` tells the parent to expect, and the plan\n  tree is git-ignored by `templates/common/notes-setup.sh` beside the two scratch note\n  names."],[3239,"Its `test:` is the JSON-array form invoking the image's own `/app/.venv/bin/python3` -\nthe image ships no `curl` and no `wget` - at a one-line `urllib` request to\n`http://127.0.0.1:4000/health/liveliness` with `timeout=5`, exiting 0 only on a 200,\nwith `interval: 30s`, `timeout: 10s`, `retries: 3`, and `start_period: 60s` to cover the\nboot that imports the config and builds 31 deployments before uvicorn binds."],[3099,"Its counters are per deployment and expire after a hardcoded 3600 s; there is no\n`routing_strategy_args` block to set, and `ttl` there would be a paste from newer docs."],[3097,"Its counters are raised before the call (`router_strategy/least_busy.py:120`) and given\nback on the failure hook (`:129`, `:143`), so a box that refuses every request sits at\nzero -- and `_least_busy` (`:83`) returns the FIRST deployment at the minimum. A dead box\nlisted first in a group is therefore the preferred target, not the avoided one:\nunfiltered, `least-busy` prefers it over a healthy box."],[339,"Its first unauthenticated call (the first-user check) gets the HTML sign-in page back,\nand the CLI reports that as `unexpected non-JSON response \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`."],[1768,"Its five cards - Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, Mimir - carry a `siteMonitor` on\ncompose DNS (`http://grafana:3000/api/health`, `http://prometheus:9090/-/healthy`,\n`http://loki:3100/ready`, `http://tempo:3200/ready`, `http://mimir:8080/ready`), which is\nwhat proves the bundle is wired up: four of those six containers ship no healthcheck at\nall (distroless image, no shell), so the badge is the only automatic signal they have."],[4648,"Its host list comes from `SPARK_HOSTS` in the process environment, then the\n`SPARKn_HOST` keys in `.env`, then the host part of `SPARKn_OPENAI_URL` - in that\norder, which is why the default run needs no arguments. With none of them set it\nfalls back to the placeholders `.env.sample` ships, `spark-1.lan