or swap\nand load average."],[109,"Merge bottom-up, and only through the asynchronous merge endpoint: `PUT` on\n`/repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{n}/merge-async`, then poll the matching\n`GET .../pulls/{n}/merge-async/{uuid}` until it reports the result. Each merge hands the\nlayer above a new base, so the stack unwinds one layer at a time from the bottom. The\nrule is GitHub's own words: \"a stack cannot be merged with the legacy synchronous merge\nendpoints **or mutations**\". The async merge merges every PR in the stack up to and\nincluding the one requested, runs in the background, is atomic, and reports a\nbranch-protection failure as a failed polling result rather than a submit-time error\n(https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/reference/stacked-pull-requests-apis-and-webhooks)."],[5104,"microsoft/vscode#327437\n  is open (a heap snapshot showed ~38 live terminals holding ~80 MB of a 484 MB\n  renderer heap) and\n  coder/code-server#6413\n  reports browser-tab RAM reaching several GB with a continuous-output terminal\n  left running after the tab is closed; neither has a maintainer mitigation."],[3560,"Mimir is the same PromQL over longer retention"],[1298,"mints a live token"],[1854,"missing tools"],[4422,"Model lane: Spark, LiteLLM, the agent backends"],[1973,"Model wiring"],[2568,"Models"],[2981,"MoE over dense"],[3786,"Monitoring and alerts"],[3788,"Monitoring and alerts"],[5090,"More clients than you have visible terminals means the tabs are mirrors, and a\nclient whose `#{client_written}` stands still while its pane is busy is a tab\nwhose browser side is already gone."],[585,"Most seeded files are written only while absent, so a hand-edited copy is user-owned and\nthe stage re-runs harmlessly. Three of them are re-written on every start, and ownership is\ndecided by a marker - never by mtime and never by first boot:"],[2578,"Mounts and \"be the host\""],[4404,"Move the port with `SPARK_NODE_EXPORTER_PORT` / `SPARK_DCGM_EXPORTER_PORT` - the target\ndocument and 