d run it.\nAnything that deploys, pushes or resets belongs behind that key."],[2757,"Set `web.extract_backend` yourself when you decide a fetch is worth a third-party\nextractor; nothing reaches one by default."],[393,"Set a token first. `CODER_SESSION_TOKEN` is any token from the Coder **Tokens** page or\nfrom `coder tokens create`."],[1429,"Set algebra"],[2353,"Set in two places: the template variable `grok_profile_mode`\n(`GROK_PROFILE_MODE=shared|private` in `.env`, forwarded by `push-template.sh` as\n`--var grok_profile_mode`), and the create form's per-workspace **Grok profile**\nfield, which defaults to the variable. One workspace can therefore sit outside the\nshared state while its siblings stay inside it."],[4259,"Set the naming parts in `.env` and put `auto` in `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` (`.env.sample`\ndocuments every part and shows the explicit-list shape beside it), and in\n`dev-stack.env` too when a dev stack runs beside the stable one."],[1012,"Set the parts in `.env`, and in `dev-stack.env` too when a dev stack runs beside\nthe stable one, then re-run `bazelisk run //scripts:bootstrap` and recreate the\nstack you switched."],[1307,"sets `HOME=/tmp` and `USER=$(id -un)` so Bazel has a writable home and a name for a uid\nthe image passwd file does not list"],[2800,"Setting that key with `hermes config set` is the\nin-container alternative. `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PUBLIC_URL` is not in the volume;\nrecreate the container and the env applies."],[1518,"Seven logged sessions guessed a target name and got `ERROR: no such target`. A target is never\nguessed, it is listed:"],[1478,"Seven suites, printed in about 60 ms. Change that file and those are the suites that go red; edit one\nof them and the same verb in the other direction tells you what it covers."],[161,"Shape"],[4104,"Shell follows the Google Shell Style Guide."],[5346,"Shipping work that is not finished, on the trunk, without exposing it"],[3000,"Short version lives in README.md (\"LiteLLM model aliases\"); this file is\nthe long version behind it. Symptom-first checks live in\ntroubleshooting.md."],[5226,"Sign-in is `HERMES_DASHBOARD_USER` / `HERMES_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD` from `.env`\n(default `admin` / `change-me-hermes` until bootstrap rotates the\nplaceholders). To fill missing keys and replace those placeholders:"],[2628,"Sign-in is HTTP basic auth from `.env`: `HERMES_DASHBOARD_USER` (default `admin`) and\n`HERMES_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD`. Bootstrap generates the password; it is **not** the\nHomepage password, and `bazelisk run //scripts:dashboard-password` does not rotate it."],[2598,"Sign-in: HTTP basic auth, with Authelia in front of the public name"],[4823,"Signed into Authelia with the link still failing puts the fault behind Authelia: the\napp path is gated by the same policy as the rest of the coder name."],[2549,"Signing in"],[2308,"Six payloads in `templates/common/` become one manifest and five files under `~/.grok/hooks/`:\n`evo-t1-hooks.json` plus, under `hooks/bin/`, the four guards and the deny list the command\nguard reads."],[255,"Skill authoring is those last two - `/ez-learn` stores facts, not procedures. They ride\n`coder_script.stack_skills` rather than the startup argument (see\n\"The one-argument ceiling\"), which writes each absent skill into\n`~/.coder/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and twin-copies it to\n`~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, each only while absent."],[78,"Small commits cost nothing at the gate: `.githooks/pre-commit` runs the hermetic half on every\ncommit and `.githooks/pre-push` runs the full set before anything leaves the machine, so a stream\nof focused commits is held to the same bar as one large one. See `main` for installing\nthem."],[5397,"so `docker compose up` stays clean and `--profile experimental` opts in."],[2387,"So `web_search = \"agent\"` and `supports_backend_search = false` stay as\n  they are - the role stays filled so re-enabling is a one-key flip - but while the\n  key reads `true` nothing dials it."],[659,"So a body