ance_optimizer_skill`, `debugger_skill`, `migrator_skill`,\n`ez_code_index_skill`, `ez_code_index_py`) to `coder_script.stack_advisors`"],[2973,"The Agent backend card"],[5150,"The agent env\nexports `GIT_ASKPASS` pointing at the `coder` binary the agent staged under\n`/tmp/coder.<rand>/`, and in a measured workspace that binary answered every prompt, and\n`coder gitaskpass` itself, with `unrecognized subcommand` and no output, so git got no\nanswer at all and fell through to prompting."],[305,"the agent logs `fork/exec /bin/bash: argument list too long` with `exit_code=255` a few\nmilliseconds in"],[304,"The agent runs `coder_agent.startup_script`, and every `coder_script.script`, as\n`bash -c <body>`. The whole body therefore travels as **one** argument to `execve(2)`,\nand Linux caps a single argument at `MAX_ARG_STRLEN`, 32 pages = 131072 bytes. Measured\non this host: an argument of 131071 bytes execs and one of 131072 fails with `E2BIG`.\nPast the wall:"],[667,"The agent-side constant\nis not read from the environment either - its own comment records the number as \"taken from\ndump.sql `max_logs_length` constraint\". Where to read the log and what a truncated one\nmeans is\ntroubleshooting.md."],[664,"The agent's uploader\n  holds the same number as a constant\n  (`codersdk/agentsdk/logs.go`,\n  `maxBytesQueued = 1048576`) and counts it across every log source at once, returning before\n  it appends when the queue is full: the lines you lose are the NEWEST ones, and once the\n  server answers `LogLimitExceeded: true` the uploader drops everything still queued."],[1982,"The AI Gateway stays off"],[3601,"The Alertmanager UI is loopback-bound for the same reason it has no auth - it can silence\nalerts - so read it from a shell on the stack host, or use Grafana's Alerting pages,\nwhich need no extra port."],[3790,"The alerts that cover the blind spots"],[3799,"The alerts the bundle ships, and the two pages that show them"],[1905,"The alias set and the reasoning levels"],[2928,"The alias table"],[2985,"The alias table, and which backend each alias resolves to"],[2996,"the aliases in `litellm/config.yaml`"],[838,"The all pass"],[5177,"The answer for every `gh` call, for as long as that workspace lives:"],[4970,"The answer the counters\nread is the daemon's stdout and nothing more: its stderr goes straight to the terminal,\nso the reason a daemon refused is heard while a CLI or `sudo docker` notice is never\ntallied as a container this sweep failed to judge."],[2559,"The API server door"],[2823,"The API server is the widest door here and ships closed. It carries the same\ntoolset as the dashboard, terminal included, and its only gate is the bearer key,\nso it is off in compose and its host mapping binds loopback until an operator\nnames both."],[4278,"The app path is behind that policy like the rest of its name, so an expired session\nsurfaces there too."],[1917,"The approval default is a stack decision"],[2904,"the Arc 140T through IPEX-LLM"],[1033,"the Arc group `compaction-fast` for a summary small enough for that window"],[2574,"The Arc rows and the picker"],[2931,"The Arc summary row"],[1043,"The Arc weights are a 32768-token\nmodel and Ollama clamps an over-long input instead of refusing it, so a\nsummary above that estimate is never handed over to be quietly truncated."],[2738,"The Arc's own weights also ship as named rows beside that catalogue - `arc-chat`,\n`arc-coder` and `arc-coder-fast` - each pointing at the same LiteLLM door."],[543,"The archive volume sits outside `~/.grok` on purpose and is read by nothing in the\nworkspace: see\nthe out-of-band session archive."],[5229,"The assistant also opens in your own terminal with\n`bazelisk run //scripts:hermes-shell`. When you cannot tell whether the agent,\nits volume, or the model lane is the broken part, start with the readiness\nreport — it launches nothing and names each blocker (daemon, container state,\nseeded volume, model key set or still a placeholder, LiteLLM\n`/health/liveliness`):"],[2751,"The assistant can look things up, and the query leaves through your own SearXNG."],[2887,"The assistant on the host"],[1349,"The authored shape"],[1980,"The auxiliary pins"],[1180,"The background warm-up, and the one knob that turns it off"],[3125,"The baked level is the only thing that separates them. An explore child is a lookup, so it\ntakes `low` and answers fast; a review child is the check that a landed claim is actually\ntrue, so it takes the `xhigh` `agent` itself carries. Each names itself with an empty flag\nlist beside the swarm lane's (`litellm/config.yaml:721-729`) and declares its own six-key\n`model_group_retry_policy` block, because a group inherits nothing from its siblings."],[2248,"The bare ids after the summary are the wave to spawn - `--ready` prints the tasks whose\n`needs:` are all satisfied, capped at `slots`, and the parent takes that set rather than\nthe plan's order and spawns the whole wave in one turn."],[23,"The base chain"],[2911,"The Bazel harness they both assume is in the Contribute\ntab."],[1325,"The Bazel job no longer installs the pins onto the runner: the image already has them at\nthe pinned versions."],[4081,"The Bazel target form"],[1360,"The Bazel targets"],[1239,"the Bazelisk download"],[1590,"The binary is the `MYPY_VERSION` pin from `images/dev/tool-versions.env`, baked into\nthe golden image by `images/dev/Dockerfile`, so the gate needs no network and no\n`pip install`."],[2394,"The binary it launches\n  (`/opt/npm-global/bin/searxng-mcp-server`) is baked into the golden image, so a\n  probe that answers with results plus a failed handshake is a server, URL or port\n  problem, not a missing package."],[1322,"the bind-mounted checkout stays writable"],[799,"The blank first value is git's reset marker: it drops any helper inherited from a\nlower-precedence config file, and git takes the **last** value it finds for that host."],[182,"The blind spot the design accepts"],[638,"The blind spot the design accepts is a holder this process cannot see in `/proc` at all: a\nsibling container's vim, which the PID namespace hides, or a process whose `/proc/<pid>/fd`\nis unreadable from here. Its buffer and the archived bytes both survive, and the move is\nreversible for a month; what goes missing is the E325 prompt that would have warned the\nnext person to open the file."],[1156,"The block configure.sh writes"],[3306,"The blocker lines"],[192,"The bodies and their braced escapes"],[269,"The bodies name the `~/.agents` spelling of those helpers, which is why the twin copy is\n  not optional."],[703,"The body accordingly declares no\nTerraform variable of its own - its `templatefile()` map is the single `boot_log_lib` key"],[3931,"The body gates itself twice before it dials anything. First the **six configured names**:\n`INFISICAL_DOMAIN`, `INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID`, `INFISICAL_MACHINE_IDENTITY_ID`,\n`INFISICAL_ENVIRONMENT`, `INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_ID` and\n`INFISICAL_UNIVERSAL_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`."],[705,"The body runs in this order, and every step that cannot proceed prints what it needs and\nexits 0:"],[2267,"The body that writes them is\n`templates/common/stack-fleet.sh.tftpl`, its own body for the same one-argument reason the\ntwo skill families have theirs\n(coder-templates.md). Thirteen is six agent\ndefinitions, three persona overlays, and four parent-side skills."],[200,"The body's steps, in order"],[4862,"the boot and the reseed\n  retire a marker-carrying `skills/learn/SKILL.md` that predates the rename rather\n  than relying on you to delete it, since deleting a seeded copy would not retire the\n  old command name anyway - the boot and the reseed write it again."],[2510,"The boot and the reseed delete a leftover\nmarker-carrying `skills/learn/SKILL.md` from before the rename. See the CLI section\nabove."],[616,"The boot clears them, from `grok_sweep_config_swaps` in\n`templates/common/agents-seed.sh.tftpl`."],[3344,"The boot continues on its own