vault reads and\nprints exactly what it did before."],[5340,"The branch-cleanup cookbook: classify, port, preserve, list for deletion"],[572,"The browser build of VS\n  Code drops that escape as well\n  (microsoft/vscode#318254), so a\n  pane app's OSC 52 copy is silent in the tab and lands over ssh from a real terminal\n  app, while the operator's own copy in the tab is the plain drag."],[1969,"The built dev container bakes the seed"],[649,"The bundle is a separate thing, and a real one: the CLI extracts\n  platform skills such as `create-skill` into `~/.grok/bundled/`, read back with\n  `SkillScope::Bundled`, and that catalog is fetched per identity/team behind an x.ai\n  sign-in this stack deliberately does not have - LiteLLM is the only transport - so the\n  directory is never created and none of those skills ever lands."],[1763,"The bundle is one flag, `INFISICAL_ENABLED`, off as shipped:\nwith it off compose starts none of the three containers and the badge reads down with\nthem, so run `bazelisk run //scripts:infisical -- status` before chasing the card."],[1807,"the bundle itself (`evo-home`, `evo-stack-overview`, `evo-alerts`, `evo-stack-logs`,\n`evo-stack-traces`, `evo-litellm`)"],[3654,"The bundle itself:"],[1769,"The bundle's four other services - `node_exporter`, `cadvisor`, `blackbox_exporter` and\n`alertmanager` - carry no card and publish nothing beyond the stack host's loopback, so\ntheir liveness is read there, not here."],[3611,"The bundle's payloads are one directory of their own, bind-mounted read-only, so\n`git diff` is the record of every monitoring change and nothing is edited in the running\ncontainer:"],[2110,"The bundled platform skills are a separate set, enumerated by\n  `FORMER_PLATFORM_SKILL_HASHES` in `crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/builtin.rs`\n  (help, imagine, create-skill, check-work, check, xlsx, pptx, docx, code-review,\n  best-of-n, create-workflow), and neither `learn` nor `skillify` is among them."],[1154,"The cache seam"],[1179,"The cache seam: the mounted volumes, the `~/.bazelrc` block, and when to drop them"],[980,"The callback URL on the GitHub side is\n`<CODER_ACCESS_URL>/external-auth/<id>/callback` - `github` for the injected\nApp, `primary-github` for the sample app above."],[4667,"The cap itself is 60 s (`HEALTH_CHECK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, `constants.py:1557`), read per\ndeployment (`health_check.py:530`), so the queue in front of the probe is the plain\nreading of the gap between that cap and the 81 s the log shows - the drop time is what\nwas seen, the queue is inference."],[3261,"The card and its per-box widgets read `AGENT_MODEL_URL` and `SPARKn_HEALTH_URL` from\n`.env`, and compose builds both from the box's `SPARKn_HOST` plus `SPARK_HTTP_PORT`,\nso a card follows the hostname you set once and they answer without a key."],[3874,"The case that corrupts state"],[2286,"The caveat worth knowing before you wire one in: Grok Build applies personas through subagent\nresolution and roles, not through a `spawn_subagent` parameter - the parent does not pass a\npersona name when it spawns a child (`~/.grok/docs/user-guide/16-subagents.md:97`). A persona\nis therefore configured, not handed over: it attaches through a role or through\n`[subagents.personas]`, and `/personas` is where the catalog is read."],[1924,"The ceiling and the fleet width"],[4938,"The ceiling beside it is that same `grok_swarm_width`,\non its own line (`templates/workspace/main.tf:558`). Measured:\n`terraform apply` with the shipped defaults prints `15`, and the same run with\n`-var grok_subagent_max_concurrent=4` prints `4`."],[2086,"The cell data lands one `BufferLine` at a time as output arrives, at 3\n`Uint32` words per column per line\n(BufferLine.ts),\nagainst a VS Code default of 1000\n(terminalConfiguration.ts)."],[642,"The chat agent discovers its context through its *default* paths (verified against the\nv2.36.6 agent binary and its `agentcontextconfig` source): the instruction file\n`AGENTS.md` under `