SE_URL`, `cli-chat-proxy.grok.com`)\nand that route needs an x.ai sign-in: from a workspace `api.x.ai` answers 404 and\n`cli-chat-proxy.grok.com`\nanswers 401 anonymously, and a session started with `--sandbox off` still leaves\n`~/.grok/bundled/` uncreated. LiteLLM is the sole model transport here, there is no\nx.ai credential, and the fetch never runs."],[4331,"the CLI ferries `observability/dcgm/custom-counters.csv` to\n`/opt/evo-t1/dcgm/custom-counters.csv` on the box"],[3483,"The CLI never creates the workspace itself. It prints\n`next: bazelisk run //scripts:new-workspace -- <url>` and stops, because `new-workspace.sh` owns the\ndev-container probe and the template choice, and a second copy of that decision would eventually\ndisagree with the first."],[4736,"The CLI reads that budget\n  from the environment only (resolver\n  `crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/util/config/resolve/compaction.rs`, remote-settings\n  key `compaction_wall_clock_budget_secs`); no TOML table accepts it, so a line pasted\n  into `grok-config.toml` is silently ignored, the same trap `[mcp] max_output_bytes`\n  already documents."],[1408,"The CLI: bazel-map"],[4717,"The CLI's 300 s wall-clock budget does not abort a call in flight - it is evaluated only\nafter the response returns - so at 300 s its entire effect was to reject a summary that\nhad already streamed in and make the session generate it again."],[2356,"The CLI's own skill directories,\n`skills/` and `bundled/`, are never created here without an x.ai sign-in; the stack's\nskill seeds live under `~/.coder/skills` and `~/.agents/skills`, outside this tree."],[4532,"The clients that are no longer being read"],[142,"The clone and the agent URL"],[573,"The clone folder is created before git runs, and before the `coder_script.code_server`\nscript's own `mkdir`: the editor starts in parallel with the startup script, and an\nempty tree is a folder VS Code can open while the clone is still writing."],[527,"The clone is a plain `git clone` from the host, so it consults the host's own git\ncredentials. A private repository therefore needs a grant covering it **on the machine\nyou run this from**."],[172,"The clone, the chown, and the best-effort tail"],[2442,"The closing summary counts how many of the four auxiliary lanes carry a pin, and a lane\nleft without one prints a `warning:` that names the lane."],[4769,"The closing summary counts the auxiliary lanes that carry a pin. A `warning:` naming a\nlane means that lane falls back to Coder's own pick, and `title_generation` and\n`compaction` are the two an operator notices first: conversations stop getting titles,\nthen a long one stops at the compaction threshold. Re-run `--apply` once the alias\nbehind that lane answers."],[3517,"The coarser gate"],[2301,"The code index is a file, not a service:"],[1892,"The code-server install and its pinned release"],[761,"The code-server module is deliberately given no settings map in plain mode: its merge\nruns on every start and would `mv` over the file the boot just layered, dropping the\noverlay's keys. (`devcontainer` passes the seed to the module only in the mode where\nthe merge is wanted, and bakes it as `settings_b64` for the built container.)"],[184,"The Coder Agents seeds and their agents-tree twins"],[613,"The Coder Agents seeds under `~/.coder` and `~/.agents` are not on those mounts: they live\non the workspace's own home volume, and that stage neither needs nor disturbs it."],[1192,"the Coder workspaces the stack provisions"],[1939,"The command guard"],[2333,"The command guard matches the whole command string, case-sensitively and byte-wise, so a\ncommand that *quotes* a denied form is refused the same way a real one is: `awk '/dd if=/'\nnotes.txt` denies, and so does a commit message that names `rm -rf` followed by a space."],[1312,"The command is the same on both sides of the seam, and a container never nests inside\nitself."],[3298,"The command that matters"],[2563,"The commands"],[4294,"The commands"],[1848,"The commands are the README's spin-up section\nwith the reasoning attached. Run them on the stack host, not inside a workspace: a\nworkspace's `docker` addresses its own DinD sidecar, and the whole-stack targets reach the\ndaemon that runs Coder."],[1557,"The compiler switches"],[4188,"The composed names"],[2881,"The concepts behind the box — what the templates build, how a model request is routed, what the agents file seeds, and the rules a change follows."],[3019,"The concurrency is deliberately small: a probe is a real generation that carries the\nlane's baked `reasoning_effort`, and on a box whose prompt cache sits full it evicts\na warm conversation to fit itself. See the TensorFold log section of\ntroubleshooting.md."],[595,"The config file usually already exists, because an earlier start of this workspace\nwrote it, so the marker rather than first boot is what decides."],[1228,"The config mounts three named volumes under `/var/cache/evo-t1-bazel`, and\n`.devcontainer/library-scripts/configure.sh` writes this block into `~/.bazelrc`:"],[176,"The config render and its two markers"],[3572,"The config's `content:` interpolates the very same\n`${LITELLM_MASTER_KEY:-change-me-litellm}` the proxy boots with\n(`docker-compose.yml:1459`), so with no dotenv both ends land on the shipped\nplaceholder and the scrape works, and the fault an operator actually meets is the two\nends disagreeing: rotate the key without recreating `prometheus` and the file still\nholds the old one."],[1694,"The consequence for a test author: a function counts when something calls it. A\nname in a comment, a stub, a fixture or a quoted grep pattern satisfies\n`//tests:shell_inventory` and satisfies nothing here."],[4389,"The consequence of the empty document above: **an unenrolled fleet reads as zero Sparks.**"],[3027,"The consequence that is measured, and which stands without the stranding argument: those\nfour no longer appear in the cached `/health` report at all, and four of the 31 probes a\ncycle stop being paid."],[3347,"the console (out-of-band console, IPMI, or the provider's serial console)\nstill shows where it stopped"],[1194,"the container CI docker-runs its checks inside"],[1246,"The container is code in this repository, and it rots the same way a lockfile does.\nThese are the moments that oblige a contributor to touch it, and each has a gate:"],[1152,"The container-scoped editor settings"],[1314,"The container, or `test-in-image`, is the answer\ntest-with-bazel.md and ../branching.md gate on."],[2968,"The container's own probe"],[4403,"The containers are idempotent by name, so this is a *different* process on the port, not\nthis CLI double-booking itself."],[1964,"The context7 server and its cache"],[1340,"The contract every page in docs/ has to satisfy before the site will render it: frontmatter, the authored H1, the opening scan pair, and the navigation file that decides whether a page is reachable at all."],[1290,"The contributor container is its own credential chain, so the doctor runs in SELF mode\nthere — exactly as it does inside a Coder workspace:"],[1259,"The contributor container runs it for you: `postCreateCommand` calls\n`configure.sh create`, which calls this script with `--devcontainer --context7-mcp`\nand nothing else, so a rebuilt container re-materializes every stack-marked file from the\ncurrent seed and leaves anything you own alone."],[1193,"the contributor dev container on a laptop"],[1054,"The contributor path"],[1075,"The contributor path — the dev container, or `test-in-image` — and where it fits"],[3003,"The control-plane chat agent dials the same proxy at `http://litellm:4000/v1`, over the\ncompose network, from inside the `coder` container. That is the server-side door."],[3200,"The conversation goes back to the box once it is healthy again."],[2371,"The copy is made by a background `rsync` that stage 9 of `startup.sh.tftpl` starts\nand leaves running for the life of the container: every 180 seconds it mirrors\n`~/.grok/sessions/` into `workspaces/<leaf>/`, skipping `*.tmp` and `*.lock`. It\nruns without `--delete`, so a session pruned from the live tree keeps its archived\ncopy. `flock -n` on a per-leaf lock file in the volume root is what keeps the stage\nidempotent: Coder re-runs the startup body on every start, and a second loop over the\nsame leaf would only double the write rate."],[2359,"The copy runs both ways, and not only at boot."],[3785,"The cost of each is spelled out on the entry in troubleshooting.md —\nread that line first."],[1464,"The cost of not querying shows up late. In the sessions that hit a coupling rule, the first\n`FAIL: //` line appeared only after a hundred or more messages of editing: the rule was\ndiscoverable in the graph on message 1, and was instead discovered by running the gate."],[2329,"The cost runs in both directions: `api_key = XyZaBcDeFgHiJk` (a name the list\ncarries, no digit) walks through, and so does\n`github_token_string = Abcd1234EFGH5678` (a digit, a name the list does not carry)."],[4011,"The count is asserted - `check` warns when the inventory is not exactly twelve, because a\nsilently-short list would leave a credential outside the vault while still reporting a clean\nsync."],[3213,"The counting branch is the `else` one line below at `:404-405`,\nreached only when a router-wide policy is set or `allowed_fails` carries a\nnon-default number (`:363-366`), and this file names neither."],[3406,"The coupling runs one way: this repo may name the scaffold repository; the scaffold repository\nnever names this one. And the scaffold's quality gate is its own -- the `.self-check/` suite and\nthe CI that runs it in that repository -- so a scaffold change is tested where it is made, and a\nlane or a file the scaffold adds needs no change here."],[2685,"The created environment is the fact and the `.env` beside the compose file is the\nintention: compose interpolated the former at create time, so a key can be right in\nthe