and. See\ntroubleshooting.md."],[3259,"The dashboard's **Agent backend** card exists to surface exactly that failure."],[3511,"The dashboards"],[3827,"The data path behind them, and what each config file costs to change, is\nobservability.md."],[2579,"The data volume and the checkout"],[4353,"the DCGM counter count"],[4330,"The DCGM exporter is not run on the image's own field list:"],[4377,"the DCGM exporter on `SPARK_DCGM_EXPORTER_PORT`"],[4746,"The decision lives in `litellm/compaction_router.py`, and the five `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION*`\nknobs named below are read there and nowhere else."],[1343,"The declared fields"],[3158,"The declared window is a fact about the weights and the pinned LiteLLM has no\ncontext-window check between the hook and Ollama, so a knob cannot reach past it; a target\ngroup that declares no window leaves the guard whole, and prints one\n`compaction router: 'compaction-fast' declares no max_input_tokens in config.yaml; forking at\nEVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION_INPUT_LIMIT alone` line rather than failing quietly."],[1511,"The default already includes the lint targets: every test rule here, `//lints:shell` and\n`//lints:shfmt` among them, is an `sh_test`."],[5045,"The default is then\nassumed to be 1."],[4211,"The default shape is LAN-only."],[1985,"The delegation sketch"],[2336,"The deny list is a floor, not a fence. It catches the forms this repo has actually measured,\nand a novel destructive command walks straight through it. Nothing in a hook reads the state\nthe command will act on, which is why \"confirm before an action that is hard to undo\" stays a\nrulebook rule that no pattern can replace."],[2324,"The deny list is the extension point. `~/.grok/hooks/bin/deny-patterns.txt` holds one extended\nregex per line, `#` starts a comment and blank lines are ignored, so an operator forbids one\nmore command by appending one line - and because there is no allow list, deleting a line is the\nonly way to permit something again."],[1068,"The dependency maps and their gate"],[2582,"The deploy workspace"],[2826,"The deploy workspace is writable by the assistant's file tools only when you say so\nwith `--writable`, and the file tools refuse anything outside the image's\n`HERMES_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT` (the official default is `/opt/data`) with no prompt at all.\nName the narrowest directory that finishes the job."],[19,"The deploy-docs workflow"],[2440,"The deployment default follows the health gate. `agent` is registered as the default,\nand when LiteLLM reports no healthy deployment behind the Spark alias the Arc `chat`\nconfig takes the default in its place. That matters because a chat opened without an\nexplicit model pick has only the default to resolve to, so a stack that comes up while\nthe Spark lane is dark still gets an Agents chat that answers."],[964,"The depth default is 2, which\nlets a child spawn read-only mappers of its own, and the seeder holds the value to 1..3,\nwith 1 putting nesting back off (`scripts/seed-dev-env.sh:187-197`)."],[4495,"The depth, and what it costs"],[5060,"The dev container must build first, and that needs `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\nin the cloned repository."],[4230,"The dev row is what `bazelisk run //scripts:dev-stack -- up` composes for the\n`evo-t1-dev` project: that command applies `STACK_ENV_LABEL=dev` when neither the shell\nnor the env file already sets a label, and only for that project, so\n`--project-name evo-t1-review` gets none."],[3278,"The dev sandbox takes the same restart with its own project name and env file:"],[3783,"the dev-stack `reset`"],[496,"The devcontainer CLI always bind-mounts the workspace folder into the dev container it\ncreates, and a bind source is resolved by the daemon that *runs* that container - here\nthe sidecar, not the workspace's."],[209,"The devcontainer fork, and the app URL"],[3647,"The DGX Sparks - the off-stack boxes Prometheus probes through blackbox:"],[1805,"the DGX Sparks (`evo-sparks-overview`, `evo-spark-host`, `evo-sparks