2949,"The fast-compaction lanes: `agent-xhigh-fast` and `agent-swarm-fast`"],[721,"The fetch is best-effort and cannot fail a workspace start. `timeout = 120`\n(`templates/workspace/main.tf:730`) bounds the realistic slow case, a vault container\nstill coming up, and every failure path - a refused login, an export that came back empty,\nan `mv` that did not land - prints one line, exits 0, and leaves the boot running on\nwhatever `agent.env` the previous start wrote\n(`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:62-65`, `:68-77`, `:252-254`)."],[3112,"The fifth Spark group, and the first of the four that carry no pin. Same\n`openai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next` on the same three boxes, same baked `xhigh`, same tool-calling\nflags and 262144 window - the\ndifference is routing state only, so no pin resolves and every request goes to the global\n`least-busy` picker, landing on the healthy box with the fewest requests in flight."],[4097,"The file header and the function docstring block both gates require"],[3955,"The file itself is written mode 600 inside a mode 700 `~/.infisical`, staged beside its\ndestination and moved into place in one step rather than appended, so a reader never sees a\nhalf-written file."],[4382,"The file lives at `observability/spark-targets/sparks.json` on the **stack host**, and that\npath is gitignored (`.gitignore:76`) precisely because it names your boxes - three\naddresses are not something this repo commits."],[1724,"The file probe (`-f \"${candidate}/${marker}\"`) says \"this is a repo root\"; refusing a derived\ncandidate whose `pwd -P` lands under `bazel-out/`, `bazel-bin/`, `execroot/`, or a\n`*.runfiles` tree says \"and it is the real checkout, not a copy\", because runfiles carries its\nown copy of the marker. Two probes, because either one alone passes in the wrong case: writing a\nrotated `.env` or a `sparks/<host>.env` through the runfiles copy reports success while the\ncheckout keeps the old bytes. An explicit `${REPO_ROOT}` is exempt from the second probe — it is\na statement about where to work, and this harness points it at the copy of the repo under test."],[4194,"The file to drop in"],[3856,"The file's own mode"],[1414,"The filegroup that must claim a new payload file"],[4913,"The files\n  in there are named `sweep-...orphan...` and only those names are ever pruned, so a file\n  you put in that directory yourself stays."],[1523,"The files it can actually open are the transitive closure of those groups, which is what the verb\nprints:"],[1165,"The files it writes"],[3300,"The files it writes"],[3237,"The filter changes where a retry lands, not whether the turn is retried."],[3634,"The filter is a workaround for that defect, not a preference: it comes out when the pin\nmoves to a release carrying the fix, and the pin today is `grafana/grafana:13.3.1`\n(`docker-compose.yml:976`)."],[3230,"The filter sits on the chat-completion selection path."],[2566,"The findings it exists to catch"],[2794,"The first `compose up` runs `hermes-init`, which is the in-container equivalent of\n`bazelisk run //scripts:hermes-bootstrap`: it runs\n`scripts/hermes-bootstrap.sh --in-container` and copies `hermes/config.yaml` and\n`hermes/SOUL.md` into `/opt/data` **only when those files are missing**."],[4025,"The first eight are the list `scripts/bootstrap.sh` used to carry twice; that duplication\nis what this inventory replaced."],[3184,"The first is caught for you at the pinned\nLiteLLM and the other two are silent, which is why the silent two are what the gates check:"],[5095,"The first is the freeze:"],[5250,"The first registered account is the site admin."],[4047,"The first version piped the reader into `grep -qx` instead, and under the CLI's\n`set -euo pipefail` that lost: `grep -q` exits on its first match, the reader then died of\nSIGPIPE, the pipeline reported 141, and the verb called a genuinely managed key unmanaged\non 195 of 200 attempts."],[1934,"The five advisor commands"],[5316,"The five inventory questions"],[865,"The five keys"],[2958,"The five knobs"],[546,"The five offline MCP servers ship in the image, but the rendered config declares none\nof them by default, so a workspace needs no network to start a session."],[2404,"The five offline stdio servers (`filesystem`, `memory`, `sequential-thinking`,\n`git` and `time`) stay pre-installed in the image (`npm -g` for the first\nthree, `uv tool` for the Python two), but the rendered `config.toml` names\nnone of them: the session traces collected on this machine called none of\ntheir tools, and a declared-but-unused server still costs every session its\nhandshake time and tool schemas. Declare one by hand and check a stubborn\nserver with `grok mcp doctor <name>` inside a workspace."],[219,"The five slots, in order"],[380,"The five values the boot reads the vault with are forwarded **whether or not the flag is\non** (`scripts/push-template.sh:696-730`), so adopting the vault later is a re-push of one\nword rather than a re-config of five, and a stack that never adopted Infisical pushes none\nof them."],[4533,"The fix: one pane per visible terminal"],[2663,"the flag"],[3501,"The flag"],[3844,"The flag"],[4293,"The flag"],[5292,"The flag is on the Prometheus command in `docker-compose.yml`. Confirm it survived, then\nconfirm the series arrived:"],[5323,"The flag ladder"],[5339,"The flag ladder, from one env var up to a checked-in `config/flags.yaml`"],[3889,"The flag that decides whether the bundle exists, and the second gate on the workspace side"],[1162,"The flags it takes"],[2258,"The flags:"],[4344,"The fleet itself comes from `SPARK_HOSTS` or the `SPARKn_HOST` keys and is resolved by\n`derive_spark_hosts` (`scripts/lib/spark.sh:67`); this CLI derives no hostname, and every\nbox line it prints names the host, because three Sparks of which one is quiet is otherwise\nindistinguishable from three Sparks of which one is down."],[4960,"The fleet still has to hold the wave: past its streams\n  the box refuses the spawn with `NoRoom`\n  (litellm-routing.md), so the two knobs\n  move together and the width is the half that keeps a fan-out inside the fleet."],[2344,"The fleet's six `~/.grok/agents/*.md` definitions and its three\n`~/.grok/personas/*.toml` overlays are **marker-aware**, the way\n`~/.grok/AGENTS.md` is: a copy that still carries `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` is\nstack-owned and gets the current seed text on every start, so a stale role definition\ncannot silently change how every child in every workspace behaves. Delete the marker line\nand the file is the person's - the boot leaves a marker-free copy alone."],[675,"the fleet's thirteen to `coder_script.stack_fleet`"],[3679,"the folder is non-empty and each file parses with the repo's own parser"],[3677,"The folder is source, so it is tested as source:"],[4068,"The follow-up that would change that is a compose-secrets rewrite of every service block,\nand it would make every bring-up wait on a server nothing here waits on today."],[276,"The four `.sh` files are written executable, with the payload's `#!` line kept on row 1,\nbecause the runner starts a relative command out of the manifest directly; the manifest\nand the deny list are data and carry no executable bit."],[426,"The four `grok_*_lane` knobs below are `--var` only, and each moves one role, so a single\nrole can be put back on the parent's pinned lane without moving the others - the rollback\nan operator needs when a workspace is older than the LiteLLM config that registers its\nalias (`templates/workspace/coder.tf:19-22`)."],[3021,"The four Arc deployments - `coder`, `coder-fast`, `chat`, `compaction-fast` - carry\n`model_info.disable_background_health_check: true`, so the sweep drops them\n(`proxy_server.py:4116-4118`)."],[220,"The four commands"],[3871,"The four compose-interpolated keys"],[2558,"The four doors"],[3707,"The four exporters keep nothing between runs: what they hold is a scrape interval deep, so\nrecreating one costs no history and needs no