e CI workflow for why the workflow\nhas to match the work-branch prefixes rather than `main` alone."],[5419,"The gate runs with it off; at least one test or documented smoke command runs with it on."],[1401,"The gates run through Bazel; see Testing with Bazel for how the npm-backed\ntargets are wired and why they stay out of `//:test-fast`."],[2670,"the gateway registers the adapter from the *presence* of `NTFY_TOPIC`, so an empty\n`NTFY_TOPIC=` in compose would hand it a half-configured platform"],[1064,"The generated launcher"],[3464,"the generator-owned paths in `NEW_REPO_TEMPLATE_META`, stripped from every render:"],[804,"The gh auth store (`~/.config/gh`, 0600): the one copy on disk, maintained by\n`gh_token_refresh`. Reachable only past a helper that clears the pair."],[1919,"The git verbs the branch-first policy needs"],[1963,"The github server"],[3934,"The golden image bakes the pinned CLI (`images/dev/Dockerfile`, `INFISICAL_CLI_VERSION` in\n`images/dev/tool-versions.env`), so the missing-binary path is what an image older than that pin\nhits. A vault outage has never once stopped a workspace."],[4354,"the GPU count and models"],[1772,"The Grafana card also carries a `customapi` widget on\n`/api/health` - the one endpoint that needs no session or API key - so the tile shows the\nstorage state and the running version, which is what you compare against the image pin in\n`docker-compose.yml` after a pull."],[5160,"The grant behind the credential - the GitHub App installation that the External Auth\nprovider (id `github` by default) minted its token from - has to include the repository\nthe workspace clones or pushes: GitHub -> Settings -> Applications -> `<app>` ->\n**Configure** -> Repository access."],[982,"The grant must include the repos you clone, or a connected credential authenticates\nand is still 403."],[1036,"The Grok Build CLI has no compaction-model\nsetting, so nothing in a client config points that call anywhere and the hop can\nonly live in the 