uard_sh`,\n`dangerous_command_guard_sh`, `post_edit_format_sh`, `selective_test_runner_sh`,\n`deny_patterns_txt`) to `coder_script.stack_hooks`."],[4681,"The half that is: with\n`enable_health_check_routing: true` a box that answered HTTP 500 to client traffic\nreceived zero client requests in the sample window, against several with the flag\nremoved and `allowed_fails: 40` / `cooldown_time: 5` restored - zero against\nseveral, from a throwaway three-box harness that a reviewer re-ran with its own\ncontainers."],[1758,"The header carries boxed tiles for host CPU, memory, CPU temperature, disk and `eth0`\nthroughput, beside the clock (date and 24-hour time), local weather (open-meteo,\nkeyless) and a search box."],[1749,"The header tiles: CPU, memory, temperature, disk, interface throughput, clock, search"],[3201,"The health filter does, and it is the only mechanism that can."],[4434,"The health filter needs both halves running"],[1296,"The helper this stack installs clears the pair first, which is why\n`gh auth setup-git` alone is not enough. There is no static token and no PAT in this\nrepo's tooling."],[1765,"The Hermes card\nfollows `STACK_HERMES_URL` when bootstrap sets it, and stays on\n`http://<STACK_LAN_HOST>:9119` when that key is empty. See hermes.md."],[1810,"The Hermes card in the\n**Host** group is the same pattern (`siteMonitor` of `http://hermes:9119/api/status`);\nthe Hermes container itself *does* mount the socket — that credential lives there, not\nhere. See hermes.md."],[306,"the home directory never seeds"],[2551,"The Homepage card"],[2636,"The Homepage card in the **Host** group links to `STACK_HERMES_URL` (the public\norigin when set, otherwise the LAN URL). Its `siteMonitor` is\n`http://hermes:9119/api/status`, which resolves over compose DNS, so the card stays\ncorrect whatever the browser link is. See dashboard.md."],[1727,"The Homepage dashboard and Kasm Workspaces: what each card reads, how the password is issued, and how a desktop gets streamed."],[175,"The hooks family, and why it is stricter"],[3148,"The hop is a property of the alias, not of the proxy: picking one of these\ntwo aliases is the opt-in, and `EVO_T1_FAST_COMPACTION=0` is the kill switch beside it."],[5015,"The host CLI is fine; only the\nprovisioner job dies."],[4342,"The host-side exporters this bundle adds live beside them - `OBS_NODE_EXPORTER_PORT`\n(583), `OBS_CADVISOR_PORT` (590), `OBS_BLACKBOX_PORT` (596), `OBS_ALERTMANAGER_PORT`\n(601) - and `ALERTMANAGER_WEBHOOK_URL` (635) is empty by default; nothing requires it."],[542,"the host-wide `grok-session-archive` at `/var/lib/grok-session-archive`"],[1770,"The hrefs go through `HOMEPAGE_VAR_GRAFANA_URL` and `HOMEPAGE_VAR_PROMETHEUS_URL`, which\ndefault to the LAN URLs built from `STACK_LAN_HOST`, `GRAFANA_PORT` and\n`PROMETHEUS_PORT`, and follow `STACK_GRAFANA_URL` once bootstrap composes the public name"],[210,"The icon and its 256-byte column"],[2053,"The icon travels as a `data:image/svg+xml;base64` data URL read from\n`templates/common/vscode-alt.svg`: Coder serves icons only from its bundled\n`/icon/*` set or a full `https`/`data` URL, and that icon is not bundled.\n`workspace_apps.icon` is `varchar(256)` on Coder v2.36, so the SVG is a compact\nribbon whose data URL fits that column; a larger file fails `templates push`\nwith `pq: value too long for type character varying(256)`."],[5337,"The ideal-state checklist a refactor has to satisfy before it is called done"],[2589,"The identity file"],[1819,"The image ships default users (`admin@kasm.local` / `user@kasm.local`); change them\nduring the wizard."],[1200,"The image ships the Docker client only. The build ends with `test ! -x\n/usr/local/bin/dockerd` (plus `containerd`, `runc`, `docker-proxy`), so the merge-gate\ncontainer drives a daemon it is given rather than owning one."],[3231,"The image, audio, embedding and rerank paths select through\n`_async_get_healthy_deployments` (`router.py:8554`), which applies the cooldown filter\nand the blocked flag only - a dead box stays a candidate there."],[150,"The image, the daemon, and the repositories"],[1117,"The in-container path is passed as an explicit option because the `~` in `.bazelrc` expands\nfrom the Bazel server's own `user.home`, which this container's uid does not appear in: a\nmount placed from that `~` could sit where Bazel never writes and look like a working cache\nfor exactly one run."],[3651,"The inference backends - the software that serves the models, not the machines it runs\non, which are two rows above:"],[1806,"the inference backends (`evo-inference-models`, `evo-inference-backends`)"],[198,"The Infisical boot fetch"],[229,"The Infisical boot fetch: its two gates, its eight agent-env keys, and `~/.infisical/agent.env`"],[206,"The inlined code-server fork"],[581,"The install check is `command -v grok`, not `[ -x ~/.grok/bin/grok ]`: the golden image\nbakes the CLI into `/usr/local/bin`, so on a golden-image boot the probe answers yes and\nnothing downloads. The download exists for the **Minimal shell** (`ubuntu:24.04`) preset\nand for a home volume that never received a CLI."],[584,"The installer writes its own `~/.grok/config.toml` (a\n`[cli] installer = ...` stub) that is indistinguishable from a user's config, so the\nconfig stage may treat that stub as stack-owned only on a completed install: a download\nthat failed must never wipe a user-owned config in its place. Without that flag a\nbrand-new workspace would be left with an unconfigured CLI, because the stub carries\nneither stack marker and the file already exists."],[5206,"The instance\nURL is the one vault value the log does print, because the push composes it rather than\nforwarding it: a workspace is handed `http://host.docker.internal:<INFISICAL_PORT>`\n(`scripts/push-template.sh:652-661`), never the host's own `INFISICAL_URL`."],[2761,"The instance only answers JSON because `searxng/settings.yml` adds `json` to\n`search.formats`; without it the request is