var:queryparam}`: the tile under the box you\nare reading opens that box's page with `host` already set. That is the path from a red tile\non the overview to the GPU rows for that machine, and it is the only link between the two\nboards."],[679,"The list above is checked, not trusted: `//tests:bats_tftpl_interpolation_test` pulls the\nkeys of the `workspace` `startup_script` map out of the checker's own reading of\n`main.tf` and diffs them against the names this page lists."],[1385,"the lists have to be lists"],[3510,"The LiteLLM board is the credential-dependent one"],[3641,"The LiteLLM board is the one that depends on a credential: its metrics sit behind\n`LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` like every other LiteLLM route, and the bearer Prometheus presents is\nthe file Compose rendered from that key, so anything that puts the two ends out of step -\na key rotated in the env file with `prometheus` never recreated, a token file that is\nmissing or wrong - leaves every panel on that board reading empty while the others stay\nfull."],[2168,"the live `.env` and the populated suffixed shapes (`.env.local`, `.env.*.local`,\n`.env.production` / `.env.prod`, `.env.staging` / `.env.stage`, `.env.development` /\n`.env.dev`, `.env.test` / `.env.testing`, `.env.ci`, `.env.override`) are denied for\n`Read` and `Edit`"],[1935,"The local code index"],[5016,"The lockfile reuse lines (`Reusing previous version\nfrom the dependency lock file`) do not skip the registry: Terraform still\nfetches the discovery document."],[75,"the log above reads as one commit per unit with imperative prefixed subjects"],[4084,"The log contract"],[719,"The log line that follows reports a key\n*count*, never a value, and counts what the publish loop actually wrote (`:249-251`)."],[3752,"the log root Alloy was given"],[872,"The long form of the `.env.sample` comments: GitHub external auth, Grok profile mode, public hosts, the Spark `agent` group"],[3323,"the machine is up"],[1059,"The Makefile shims"],[588,"The manifest and the five files under `hooks/bin/` are rewritten on every start while they carry\nthe marker - the `\"__evoT1Stack\": true` key in the JSON, the only spelling that leaves it\nparseable, and the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` comment in the four scripts and the deny\nlist."],[1415,"The map key a new `scripts/*.sh` needs, and the test a new function needs"],[1922,"The marker that keeps the config stack-owned"],[1383,"The match is exact:"],[1959,"The MCP search lane and its probe"],[2975,"The measured burst"],[2380,"The memory and index files are SQLite, opened live by every workspace holding the\nmount, so two workspaces writing memory at once can race. *Roughly in sync* is the\nbar, not transactional sharing."],[1989,"The memory and skill trio"],[4847,"The memory family\n`/ez-learn` copies (`/flush`, `/dream`, `/remember`, `/memory`) is a different case:\nthose are upstream commands the CLI ships itself - `/flush`, `/dream` and `/memory` are\n*built-in* registry entries gated behind cross-session memory, which is off by default\nhere, and `/remember` is a pager command with no such gate."],[258,"the memory family `/ez-learn` copies is no skill at all but the CLI's own `/flush`,\n`/dream` and `/memory` registry entries plus the pager's `/remember`, with the\nregistry three gated on a memory store, which is off by default and never configured\nhere."],[1183,"The merge gate (Linux image) versus the convenience path (native Darwin)"],[1683,"The merge gate is the Linux golden image — the same `images/dev/Dockerfile` the Coder\nworkspaces boot and CI builds:"],[1303,"The merge gate is the Linux image, so run it in the contributor container:"],[5052,"The message names the body and the position, which is the whole diagnosis: line\n32 there is `if [ -L \"${evo_t1_root}\" ]; then`, a shell loop variable."],[3516,"The metric allow-list"],[1699,"The mirror pads every `.sh` it instruments, so a suite that measures a payload's\n**byte size** through `REPO_ROOT` prices the harness instead of the product. This is\nhow `//tests:shell_coverage` failed an execve budget the checkout had already passed:\n`templates/common/notes-setup.sh` weighed 1182 bytes more in the mirror than it\nships. A size gate resolves its tree through `bats_source_repo_root`, and\n`startup-script-size.bats` builds a real instrumented mirror to prove it still\nmeasures what ships."],[1904,"The model aliases and their lanes"],[1979,"The model config rows"],[5336,"The model in six statements, and what each one rules out"],[2886,"The model lane"],[4587,"The model lane: Spark boxes, LiteLLM, and the agent backends"],[2913,"The model lane: the aliases in `litellm/config.yaml`, how a request picks a backend, and what happens when a Spark box goes down."],[949,"the model list, the session-affinity key, the `[ui]` theme and the `[ui]`\napproval mode belong to one workspace, so a copy pushed from the host would\nstamp this checkout's defaults over what that workspace's own create-form\nanswers rendered - the approval mode is one of those answers\n(`grok_permission_mode`, default `always-approve`)"],[3085,"The model writes the JSON call into the message body, which no agent driver can consume."],[5311,"The model, in six statements"],[2720,"The models come from a `providers:` block in `hermes/config.yaml`. Its `litellm` row\ndeclares the shared catalogue - the aliases that are not one of the Arc's own three\nweights - and each Arc row declares its weight with its `default_model`."],[2599,"The models it calls through LiteLLM"],[3188,"The module is mounted as a single file,\n`./litellm/compaction_router.py:/app/compaction_router.py:ro`. A directory mount over\n`/app` hides `config.yaml` beside it, and it has to sit in the same directory as the\nconfig file because that is the directory the proxy resolves a callback's dotted name\nagainst - the bare module name in\n`callbacks` resolves no other way."],[4544,"The most misread line"],[513,"The mount covers the workspace container o