e lines a pane actually emits - which is why a busy build log is\nwhere a large value is felt, and an idle prompt is not."],[2058,"the setting names, values and defaults were read out of the shipped code-server\n4.145.0's own config registry (VS Code base 1.145.0)"],[5094,"The settings seed drops\n`terminal.integrated.scrollback` to 2000 - the browser keeps a short viewport\nand tmux's `history-limit 100000` behind `Prefix-[` holds the deep history - and\nturns `cursorBlinking` off, and `templates/common/tmux.conf` sets\n`set -s escape-time 10` and `set -g focus-events on`."],[5068,"the settings seed's `terminal.integrated.copyOnSelection: true` puts\nthat highlight on the machine clipboard with no chord (the headless harness on\n4.145.0 recorded `navigator.clipboard.writeText` firing on a client selection,\nbefore this switch)."],[4262,"The shape below is the one Traefik v2 and v3 both read; the entryPoint name, the\ncertificate and the middleware name have to match what that box already defines, so treat\nthose three as the values to align, not as new requirements."],[4243,"The shape is load-bearing: each name is **one label under the zone**, and each service\nprefix joins it with a **hyphen**. A wildcard certificate covers exactly one label, so\nthe dotted two-label form (`coder.gmktecbeast.`) has no certificate at the public edge:\nthe browser aborts with `ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH` and Traefik never sees the\nrequest. Measured on this box - `coder-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io` completes the handshake\nwith the zone's `*.overeazy.io` cert, while the dotted form fails with a TLS alert 40\nand presents no certificate at all."],[4469,"The shapes every body prints"],[2179,"The shapes that are never denied are per-path deletions - `find <dir> -type f -delete`, or\n`rm -f` naming each path - so clean scratch that way."],[4459,"The shapes, one by one"],[656,"The shapes, verbatim from `templates/common/boot-log.lib.sh:22-63`:"],[1276,"the shared `~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` (with the code-server and desktop VS Code\nUser settings symlinked to it)"],[887,"The shared overlay `~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` is a rendered file too, but\nthe boot writes it only while absent, so the API keys an operator put there\nsurvive every restart."],[2185,"the shell forms that signal a whole process group (`kill 0`, `kill -- -<pgid>`,\n`kill -9 -1`)"],[4074,"The shell, function, script, template and naming rules this repo holds itself to, and the gates that enforce them."],[5286,"The shipped datasources carry fixed UIDs (`prometheus`, `mimir`, `loki`, `tempo`) that\nevery shipped dashboard references, so a datasource you rebuilt by hand in the UI is a\ndatasource no panel will ever query. Diff anything suspicious against\n`observability/grafana/provisioning/datasources/stack.yaml`: that file is the record of\nwhat the working config is."],[4928,"The shipped default puts the writers on the unpinned `agent-swarm` lane, where the\nleast-busy picker spreads them over every box and the 15 is the fleet's real width\n(3 boxes x `PARALLEL` 5). Four keys come from that one variable: `general-purpose`,\n`implementer`, `documenter`, `tester`."],[3533,"The shipped payload checks"],[1018,"The shipped placeholders do not resolve on purpose: leave a box you\ndo not run empty and its alias and its card both report down."],[1393,"The sidebar is not read from the filesystem: most pages sit flat in `docs/` while belonging to\ndifferent sections, and the reading order a prev/next footer needs is an editorial decision."],[2843,"The sidebar tabs"],[2875,"The sidebar tabs divide the rest:"],[4277,"The sidecar forwards what it receives and authenticates nothing, so a name whose\nrouter skips the auth middleware reaches its container the same way the LAN does."],[1177,"The single golden image, and the file that pins it"],[4088,"The single-copy payloads"],[1372,"The site is a Fumadocs app that reads `docs/` straight out of the repository, so the markdown\nhere is 