k, where nothing\nlistens."],[309,"The size that matters is not `startup.sh.tftpl`. `main.tf` composes the body from that\ntemplate plus every `templates/common/` payload it inlines, so any edit to the rulebook,\nthe skills, the tmux config, the notes seeder, or the Grok config moves the number."],[124,"The skill command seeds and the body that writes them"],[2346,"The skill copies are **absent-only**, like the `ez-` families: a `SKILL.md` that\nalready exists belongs to the user and is never rewritten - the fleet's eight, and the\nadvisor family's twelve, which are five `SKILL.md`s plus `code_index.py` in each of the two\nhomes. The advisor family's `~/.grok/agents/documenter.md` rides that absent-only contract\nwith the skill it serves rather than the refresh the fleet's six keep, on the body's own\nreasoning that a stale piece of advice misleads one run while a stale guard decides what a\nsession may do."],[5450,"The skill is `skills/trunk-refactor/SKILL.md`. A session in this repository reaches it through\n`AGENTS.md`; any other repository gets it by installing it into the two skill homes the agents\nread:"],[5362,"The skill's twelve binary criteria, in prose. Each needs a command's output as proof."],[2581,"The skills directory"],[4577,"The skipping rendering console line"],[3191,"The sources, in order, are `x-litellm-trace-id`, then\n`x-litellm-session-id`, then any `x-<vendor>-session-id`, then\n`session-id`/`session_id`/`thread-id`/`conversation_id` (Codex style), then W3C\ntraceparent and baggage, plus `metadata.session_id` in the body."],[3791,"The Spark alert that closes the same shape"],[3078,"The Spark boxes serve TensorFold's OpenAI-compatible `/v1` and nothing else: Ollama\nruns on the Arc, so a Spark box never sees the Ollama protocol."],[3794,"The Spark exporters"],[1034,"the Spark group `agent-low` for one too big for it"],[3568,"the Spark jobs that reach `blackbox_exporter:9115` as their prober"],[2930,"The Spark rows"],[2954,"The Spark tier and the token estimate"],[1930,"The spawn ceiling"],[3485,"The split follows the ownership: the scaffold's own invariants are checked in the scaffold\nrepository, and this repo checks only the renderer."],[3558,"The split is upstream's own:"],[3119,"The spread is bought by removing a pin, not by adding a proxy queue or a cap. There is\nstill no `rpm`, `tpm` or `max_parallel_requests` anywhere in the config, and\n`queue_class`, `queue_class_config` and `enable_queue` do not exist at this tag. A\nsaturated box keeps shedding load in its own scheduler; the proxy parks nothing behind\nan in-memory semaphore."],[3644,"The stack host - the box the bundle itself runs on:"],[1804,"the stack host (`evo-host-taskmanager`, `evo-containers`)"],[3566,"the stack host through `node_exporter:9101` and `cadvisor:8080`"],[4043,"The stack is the one with state to corrupt, and the way it breaks is the opposite of an\noutage - the refresh succeeds by writing, so a vault that answers but holds a value nothing\nauthenticates with is what brings `coder`, `litellm`, `homepage`, `hermes`, `grafana` or\n`searxng` up unable to log in."],[2832,"The stack runners take `up`, `down`, `status`, `logs`, `reset`; `status` and `logs` are\nwhere a Hermes that will not bind its port is diagnosed first."],[1899,"The stack's own skill commands"],[2372,"The stage is best-effort: it warns and\ncarries on when the volume root or the leaf is not writable, or when `flock` is\nmissing, and re-tests for the sessions directory each tick because the CLI creates\nthat directory on its first run, which can be long after boot."],[692,"The stage reads the *rendered* file, pulls every `command = \"...\"` value out of it, and\nnames the ones that are not executable files, in the same startup log that wrote the\nconfig. `sed` keeps only a double-quoted value and a TOML path carries no spaces, so an\nempty entry there is an odd line rather than a missing binary."],[2043,"The stale viewers above are detached on the way in, which is where the\n8-clients-on-one-pane count came from."],[4956,"The start itself re-renders\n`config.toml`, so that one line is enough to see the number move; it is also one-shot, so\nclear the stored value with `coder update <workspace> --parameter\ngrok_subagent_max_concurrent=15` or the Variables tab, or the next start narrows it again."],[750,"The start-gated `coder_script.code_server` uses the same local."],[4829,"The startup\n  body's eight stage titles (`workspace startup`\n  stages 1-8, `templates/workspace/startup.sh.tftpl:37-326`) are the map for anything about\n  tmux, the CLI, the shell profile, the skills and the notes library, the editor settings,\n  the Grok profile, ownership and the git credentials, or the repositories."],[658,"The startup script chowns it\n  back to the home owner, and nothing orders that before a sibling body: the start\n  scripts fan out in one errgroup, startup script included, which is the same\n  `script_count=10` burst The one-argument ceiling counts."],[800,"The startup seed rewrites both keys every start (idempotent), and `github-auth fix`\ninstalls the same form, leaving a helper that already ignores the pair alone. This\nhelper is the slot that wins, and the clearing is the subject of the paragraph below."],[4993,"The stored parameter is the thing to clear. Every start re-renders `config.toml`, so a\nrestart on its own re-applies the same stored number; what moves it is\n`coder update <owner>/<workspace> --parameter grok_subagent_max_concurrent=<n>`, or the\nVariables tab. The sweep prints that line per offender with the owner and the\n`# fleet-width:` it read off that profile already filled in, which is why reading the\nfleet is the part worth scripting and the update is the part you run by hand."],[598,"The strip is what makes the render's answer the only one in the file: an operator's\n  `permission_mode` left beside the render's own line gives one `[ui]` table two identical\n  keys, which is invalid TOML."],[2192,"The