2511,"The text of 1-4 is the orchestration protocol (fan-out / fan-in, the edit-conflict gate,\nprobe-one-worker-first, verify-what-a-worker-actually-produced, the git cadence that\ncuts the branch before the first edit and commits each unit as it lands, holding the push\nfor the pull request, and the issue etiquette that reads the report before planning, puts a\nsingle closing keyword in the pull request body, and leaves the actual close to the merge)."],[151,"The theme and the approval mode"],[757,"the theme re-asserted last so the overlay can never veto this workspace's own theme"],[3640,"The thirteen dashboards are provisioned, so they appear on a fresh Grafana in the\n`EVO-T1` folder with no clicking - the section below names each one and the question it\nanswers."],[3891,"The three `secrets`-profile containers, and the CLI verb that reads the flag"],[4313,"The three commands - plan, prove, install - plus one box, JSON, and the target document"],[3912,"the three containers are never selected (`profiles: [\"secrets\"]`)"],[1961,"The three declared MCP servers"],[3828,"The three DGX Sparks are not scrape targets until you make them one."],[3793,"The three exporters"],[3823,"The three exporters feeding those rules sit beside the bundle on the same\n`observability` profile, all published to `127.0.0.1` only:"],[1966,"The three failure shapes"],[4316,"The three failures worth recognising from the CLI's own words"],[1914,"The three feature flags"],[3580,"the three Infisical containers (`infisical`, `infisical-db`, `infisical-redis`)"],[4797,"The three MCP servers (`github`, `context7`, `searxng`) ship by default, so a lane\nmissing from a session has one of three shapes: the block absent from the rendered\nconfig, the `command=` binary absent from the golden image, or the credential absent."],[141,"The three MCP switches and the search port"],[3795,"The three modes"],[1651,"The three paths a suite may use"],[2119,"The three payloads - `templates/common/ez-learn.SKILL.md`, `ez-skillify.SKILL.md` and\n  `ez-create-skill.SKILL.md` - are seeded at workspace start by\n  `coder_script.stack_skills`: each is written into `~/.coder/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and\n  twin-copied to `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, each only while that file is absent."],[2507,"The three payloads are\n`templates/common/ez-learn.SKILL.md`, `ez-skillify.SKILL.md` and\n`ez-create-skill.SKILL.md`, on the same absent-only contract."],[322,"The three payloads now travel in their own body, `coder_script.stack_skills`, which\ncomposes to 36847 bytes."],[1932,"The three persona overlays"],[1993,"The three repository-conversion commands"],[3075,"The three rows after `agent-xhigh` differ from the four above them in routing state\nonly: same model, same three boxes, the thinking level each row names, and no session\npin. See\nthe swarm lane and\nthe fan-out lanes."],[3982,"The three runners that address the compose\nproject - `bazelisk run //scripts:dev-stack`, `//scripts:prod-stack` and `//scripts:update-stack` -\nsource `scripts/lib/infisical.sh` and call `infisical_pull` themselves, immediately before compose\ninterpolates the env file, so a key rotated in the vault lands on the bring-up in front of you\ninstead of waiting for a human to run the verb."],[3894,"The three runners that refresh the env file from the vault before compose renders"],[3450,"The three scaffold flags exist so the source can be pointed elsewhere without editing anything:\nthe env pair covers a mirror or a fork for a whole deployment, and `--template-dir` renders a tree\nyou already hold, which is the offline route and the one the hermetic tests use."],[3857,"The three services"],[1992,"The three stack-seeded skill commands"],[4191,"The three states of `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS`"],[3872,"The three that travel by CLI"],[3227,"The threshold is set explicitly because the\nshipped default is `DEFAULT_HEALTH_CHECK_INTERVAL * 2` = 600 s whatever\n`health_check_interval` says (`router.py:993`); left at the