s TLS for those names and must forward plain\nHTTP to this box's router container **with the original Host header intact** -\n`STACK_ROUTER_CONF` names the conf that container mounts (`proxy/router.gen.conf`,\nrendered by bootstrap from `proxy/router.conf.template`, or the checked-in\n`proxy/router.conf` while the key is empty), and it picks the service from\n`$http_host` on `STACK_PROXY_HTTP_PORT` (default 8080). A rewritten Host comes back\nas `421`."],[1421,"The transitive closure"],[1394,"The tree is declared once in `NAV` inside `docs-site/scripts/gen_nav.py` and generated into\n`docs-site/lib/nav.json`, which the page-tree builder imports and a Zod schema validates."],[4854,"The trio moved out of `startup.sh.tftpl` into that one body, so\n  a startup-script log that says nothing no longer covers it. A `SKILL.md` that is present\n  while its `scripts/*.py` helper is missing is the same story on the helper's own absent\n  guard: the family seeds six payloads, each guarded on its own path."],[3854,"The trust boundary"],[3845,"The truthiness rule"],[2136,"The twelve aliases (`agent`, `agent-low`, `agent-medium`, `agent-xhigh`, `agent-swarm`,\n`agent-explore`, `agent-review`, `agent-xhigh-fast`, `agent-swarm-fast`, `coder`,\n`coder-fast`, `chat`) are defined with `base_url` set to `litellm_url` and\n`env_key = \"LITELLM_API_KEY\"`. The key is injected as an environment variable, so\nit never appears in a file."],[3869,"The twelve managed keys"],[3893,"The twelve managed keys, who consumes each one, and what breaks when it is wrong"],[4087,"The twin payloads"],[1413,"The twin template copies"],[5027,"The two\n`templates/common/` payloads still land (copied with `cp`, which follows\nlinks), which is why the archive is small rather than empty."],[2714,"The two `-fast` aliases, that one and its pinned twin **`agent-xhigh-fast`**, differ\nfrom their parents in one call only: the proxy, not the client, re-serves that\nsession's conversation summary from the Arc group `compaction-fast`, and every other\nturn still runs on a Spark."],[457,"The two `-fast` entries are the Spark lane each is named after, unchanged, with one call\nmoved: the proxy re-serves that session's conversation summary from the Arc group\n`compaction-fast`, which is the whole difference, because the CLI has no compaction-model\nkey of its own."],[3234,"the two attempts the retry chain allows (`num_retries: 2` in `litellm_settings`, and\n`DefaultRetries: 2` inside each Spark lane's `model_group_retry_policy` block)"],[4386,"The two blackbox jobs take the address from the same file and pass it as `__param_target`,\nso the target label carries the box rather than the prober."],[4378,"the two blackbox probe URLs on `SPARK_HTTP_PORT` (`/health` and `/v1/models`)"],[654,"The two bodies nothing execs, `settings.json.tftpl` and\n`grok-config.toml.tftpl`, take no such key."],[2059,"the two Clipboard-API observations -- that a client selection fires\n`navigator.clipboard.writeText`, and that `document.execCommand('copy')` is the\nfallback that still lands on an insecure origin -- come from the earlier\nheadless-Chromium pass over that build with the rendered `settings.json` twin and\nthe tmux payload loaded, when `mouse` was still on and the copy out was a\nShift+drag"],[3756,"The two commands"],[3762,"The two commands an operator runs most"],[4311,"The two containers that make a Spark a Prometheus target, and the fact that neither\nexists until you run `--apply`"],[3951,"The two defences are the deny list above, matched on the normalised case, and the pre-publish\npass that refuses to write the file at all and leaves the previous `agent.env` in place."],[3280,"The two fan-out lanes are absent from that list on purpose. `agent-explore` and\n`agent-review` exist to be pinned by `[subagents.models]`, not chosen from a picker, so\nediting them moves a fleet role's traffic and leaves the Agents dropdowns alone."],[3248,"The two fan-out lanes degrade the way the swarm lane does, one step further than the\npinned lanes, and each hops through the lane that bakes its own level:"],[1984,"The two fast-compaction lanes"],[3281,"The two fast-compaction lanes are absent for a mechanical reason of the same kind: the\nhop keys on the summary instruction the Grok CLI appends, and the aibridge behind those\ndropdowns never sends one, so an Agents chat on `agent-xhigh-fast` is a chat on\n`agent-xhigh` under a longer name. They are a CLI and a workspace-form choice instead."],[3092,"The two fast-compaction lanes are absent for a mechanical reason of the same kind: the hop\nkeys on the summary instruction the Grok CLI appends, and the aibridge behind this\ndropdown never sends one, so a chat on `agent-xhigh-fast` is a chat on `agent-xhigh`\nwearing a longer name."],[2990,"The two fast-compaction lanes, and the proxy callback that moves one summary call of\na session onto a cheaper tier"],[199,"The two gates"],[3507,"The two Grafana environment settings"],[1661,"The two inventory gates that tie a production function to a test"],[213,"The two launcher helpers"],[3040,"The two levers that actually move load off a shedding box:"],[2926,"The two levers that move load"],[1217,"the two lint-and-format tool pins (`shellcheck.executablePath` with\n`shellcheck.customArgs`, `shellformat.path` with `shellformat.flag`)"],[1127,"The two maps in `scripts/BUILD.bazel` and the one in `tests/BUILD.bazel` are the\nmachine-readable record of which repo file each target reads:"],[1915,"The two MCP server blocks"],[1948,"The two modes"],[3578,"the two nginx hops"],[1365,"The two opening lists that become the scan card, and the order they have to sit in"],[831,"The two passes"],[869,"The two passes of `update-configs`, and the flags that select one"],[2776,"The two paths disagree, and only the runtime one runs commands."],[4992,"The two paths now say the same thing, so one read of either is\nenough to act on."],[163,"The two questions"],[3048,"The two reader lanes spread the same way, and each group counts its own in-flight\nrequests, but the box's `PARALLEL` streams are one pool that every alias arriving on it\nshares. Past 15 across the fleet the boxes have no streams left to give, whatever the\nlane."],[1163,"The two research lanes"],[375,"The two research lanes split by question type: a library, framework, CLI or setup\nquestion goes to `context7` (resolve the library id first, then query docs on that\nid), anything else on the web goes to the `searxng` `search` tool, and a URL already\nin hand goes to `searxng`'s `fetch_content`. Grok's native `web_search` is parked\nhere, and native `web_fetch` is unavailable because that tool needs an egress proxy\nendpoint this stack does not run, so `SEARCH_MCP=false` leaves a session with library\ndocs and no way to reach the web."],[1267,"The two research lanes that config can render are split by question type:"],[3076,"The two rows after those are not new lanes. `agent-xhigh-fast` is `agent-xhigh` and\n`agent-swarm-fast` is `agent-swarm`, deployment for deployment, and what differs is\nwhere one call of the conversation is answered - the CLI's summary request, which a\nproxy callback re-serves from `compaction-fast` on the Arc when the summary fits that\nwindow, and from a Spark group at thinking `low` when it does not. See\nthe fast-compaction lanes."],[3850,"The two self-gates"],[3813,"The two single-exporter gap alerts each wait for the *other* exporter to vouch for the\nbox, so both exporters dying at once - a powered-off host, a restarted Docker - was\nsilent; `HostExportersSilent` asks no second opinion and fires on the double absence."],[1280,"the two terminal helpers in `~/.grok/bin`"],[554,"The two terminal-profile tmux helpers are written by their own\n`coder_script \"terminal_launchers\"` body, which runs after this one returns (see\nbelow)."],[2919,"The two top-level blocks"],[1548,"The typing rule for every language in this repo: Python under mypy with no Any, TypeScript under the strictest flags it compiles, Terraform variables with a declared constraint, and what bash and awk owe instead."],[1515,"The uncached pass is not replaced."],[3509,"The unified-storage overrides file"],[710,"the Universal Auth login as the machine identity (`:61-65`)"],[3303,"The unlock itself"],[3316,"The unlock itself, step by step, from the operator's own machine"],[3361,"The unlock key authorizes a root shell on a machine whose disks are still\nsealed, and the initramfs image holding it sits on an unencrypted `/boot`.\nAnyone who can read `/boot` can read that public key."],[601,"The unmanaged case is announced rather than silent, because the render is the only place\na workspace's model catalog and MCP lanes are ever written."],[3043,"The unpinned `agent-swarm` lane is what the writers ride by default, and the one that\ncan afford a wider wave - 15 subagents spread by `least-busy` over three boxes fill\neach box's `PARALLEL` exactly, which is the difference between buying wall-clock and\nbuying queue depth."],[1898,"The upstream `/learn` question"],[5165,"The username text is not checked\n(measured on Coder v2.36.6: `toxicoder`, `x-access-token`, `somebody-else` and `octocat`\neach returned `200`), but an empty username or an empty password is refused, and the\nempty password is what produces the misleading `Invalid username or token. Password\nauthentication is not supported for Git operations.`"],[850,"The usual case: no coder.env"],[4907,"The usual history is:\nsomeone opened the config in vim, the workspace was stopped with the editor still\nup, and the swap is now asking about a session whose container no longer exists."],[625,"The usual way one loses the\nmarker is `grok mcp add` rewriting the file, and the remedy there is\n`bazelisk run //scripts:seed-dev-env -- --force`."],[5036,"The usual wrapper is `Failed to check server \"https://...\" for first user, is the URL\ncorrect and is coder accessible from your browser?`"],[2147,"The variable's own validation accepts any whole number 1..32 it is given, plus that\n  explicit null,\n  because past the fleet's ceiling a bigger number is only a longer queue."],[2753,"The variable's presence is what registers the provider (`plugins/web/searxng` reads\n`SEARXNG_URL` as its key env), and it is the only bundled web provider that\nneeds no API key. The name resolves on the compose network, so this adds no\npublished port."],[3131,"The variables are declared in `templates/workspace/coder.tf:24-52` and its devcontainer\ntwin, and they are what fills `[subagents.models]` in\n`templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl`. The fan-out width rides a different variable\nand does not follow any of these three: it is `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`'s own\nshipped 15."],[3994,"The vault answers on `http://127.0.0.1:8182` (`INFISICAL_PORT`) on the stack host, and on\nthe published LAN face. Expect the two alpine containers to read `running` rather than\n`healthy`: neither declares a healthcheck, because the only consumer waits on\n`service_started`."],[282,"The vault itself - its three services, the operator CLI, the managed key inventory and\nrotation - is operate/secrets.md; what the templates have to keep\ntrue about it is The Infisical boot fetch."],[385,"The vault itself is not this page's subject: the three compose services, the operator CLI,\nthe managed key inventory, the outage bounds and rotation are\noperate/secrets.md. What the templates do with what these keys\nforward is The Infisical boot fetch."],[143,"The vault keys and their two gates"],[4239,"The vault's three containers start only under `profiles: [\"secrets\"]`, which\n`INFISICAL_ENABLED` (off as shipped) selects, so a stack with the flag off has no vault\nbehind that name and answers `502`."],[4706,"The vendor default is 600 s whatever the interval says, because it is computed from a\nconstant (`router.py:993`), so the two keys move together or the filter fails open\nbefore the next sweep."],[1482,"The verb matches basenames over the union of the three payload groups, so the twin set is the\ngraph's answer rather than a convention you have to remember:"],[4045,"The verb mints a fresh value, writes the **vault first**, and only touches `.env` once the\nvault accepted it - so there is no moment where `.env` holds a password the vault does not\nknow about. `rotate` names one managed key; naming anything outside the inventory is an\n`error:` and exit 1."],[1916,"The verbatim escape hatch"],[3859,"The verbs"],[188,"The verbs and the shapes they print"],[1466,"The verbs below are the shapes of those questions."],[653,"The verbs live in one payload, `templates/common/boot-log.lib.sh`, and both twins hand it\nto every exec'd body as the `boot_log_lib` key of that body's `templatefile()` map: the\nstartup body plus ten `coder_script`s in `workspace`\n(`templates/workspace/main.tf:509-510`), and eleven in the `devcontainer` twin, which adds\none body, `dind-bootstrap.sh.tftpl`."],[2573,"The verbs that change the model"],[2732,"The verbs that do change the model:"],[5327,"The verdict table"],[818,"The verdicts are PUSH-READY (200 advertising refs), REFUSED-GRANT\n(403, it authenticates and every write is denied), NOT VISIBLE (404, hidden or absent),\nREJECTED (401, the credential itself is refused, as an expired mint is), or no useful\nanswer (offline)."],[4546,"The verdicts, and what each one costs you"],[1650,"The vitest gate"],[1233,"The volumes belong to the host's daemon, so a host shell is the reliable place to run\nthis: from inside the container the same commands work only while the config's socket\nmount is in place."],[1976,"The wait window and the seeder log"],[1158,"The warm-up"],[2361,"The watcher is single-instance behind a non-blocking `flock` on\n`$HOME/.notes-sync.lock`, in the container's own home rather than the shared volume,\nbecause each of the owner's workspaces needs its own."],[578,"The watcher left at the end is what makes notes survive a recreate that lands *between*\nedits. The boot-time sync runs once, so anything written later lived solely inside that\ncontainer, which is how a whole workspace's notes went missing on a recreate."],[3633,"The watcher warns twice each poll, and the polls in the log this branch was cut from were\n41 to 59 s apart - `source listed zero manifests`, then\n`zero manifests, keeping previous set` - whenever no app publishes a search manifest,\nwhich is every OSS install with nothing provisioned into the app platform; upstream calls\nthat a logging defect (grafana/grafana#137058) and confirms search keeps working, because\nretrying an empty source is intended and only the level is wrong."],[1891,"The web terminal app"],[3500,"The webhook destination is empty as shipped"],[4323,"The whole bundle this depends on sits behind the Compose profile\n`profiles: [\"observability\"]`, and observability.md is the page for\nthe six services that do the scraping."],[3151,"The whole remedy therefore lives server-side, and the measurement behind it\nis the `compact failed: exceeded wall-clock budget 300s` section of\ntroubleshooting.md."],[4951,"The whole surface, for a script or a CI step that wants the answer rather than the prose\n(`--help` prints the same):"],[4503,"The whole surface, for a script or CI"],[1538,"The whole-graph enumeration `unlisted` is built from, which is also the answer to \"how much of the\nrepo do the gates actually see\":"],[609,"The whole-profile volume this template used to mount over all of `~/.grok`,\n`grok-profile-<owner-id>`, is still mounted in `shared` mode, but **read-only** and at\n`~/.grok-legacy`, only so the first start after the split can hoist its `notes/`,\n`memory/` and `sessions/` across (`notes_hoist_legacy` in\n`templates/common/notes-setup.sh`)."],[2357,"The whole-profile volume this template used to mount over all of `~/.grok`,\n`grok-profile-<owner-id>`, is still mounted in `shared` mode, but **read-only** and at\n`~/.grok-legacy`, purely so the first start after that split can copy its `notes/`,\n`memory/` and `sessions/` across once: `notes_hoist_legacy` in\n`templates/common/notes-setup.sh` takes a concern only when the destination is missing\nor empty, and nothing reads that mount afterwards. A later `chore:` removes it."],[320,"the widest body is now the devcontainer startup script at 115967 bytes, 6913 clear of\nthe bound, with the workspace twin at 113767 and 9113 clear."],[2146,"The width and the ceiling are two numbers on purpose, and `main.tf` is where they meet:\n  `grok_subagent_max_concurrent = var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent != null ? var.grok_subagent_max_concurrent : var.grok_swarm_width`\n  So the width is the variable's own shipped 15 whichever lane the writers ride, and the\n  `: var.grok_swarm_width` arm answers only a caller that passes null on purpose;\n  `--var grok_subagents_lane=agent` is the rollback that puts the writers back on\n  the parent's pinned box and leaves that width alone, and an explicit\n  `--var grok_subagent_max_concurrent=N` always wins."],[960,"The width default is this knob's\nown shipped 15 (three Spark boxes at `PARALLEL` 5), the same literal 15 the\ntemplates ship on `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`, on every lane rather than one\nnumber per lane."],[846,"The width, the fleet ceiling, and the depth"],[4672,"The window is still read passively on every run without the needle, from the server's\nown startup lines (`context_pairs` and `startup_estimate` in the report), so a box\nquietly rebuilt with a shorter window is still visible; the needle is the active\nconfirmation of it."],[5248,"The wizard only listens on `:3000` at first boot; after install, use `:4443`."],[4635,"The word the shell says it cannot find is the second tag."],[2580,"The working directory must be a literal path"],[2773,"The working directory the agent runs in is `terminal.cwd`, and it has to be a literal\npath. Hermes validates it in `agent/runtime_cwd.py` with `expanduser()` alone:"],[307,"the workspace banner reads \"A startup script has failed\""],[3848,"The workspace boot fetch"],[478,"The workspace container attaches to **both** `bridge` and that private network; once a\n`networks_advanced` block appears the provider stops letting `network_mode` do the\nattaching, so `bridge` has to be listed explicitly."],[4600,"The workspace container is `coder-<owner>-<ws>` (so `coder-alx-self-coder`); the\n`<wsid>` form names the DinD pieces around it - the sidecar `coder-<wsid>-dind-sidecar`,\non the network `coder-<wsid>-dind`, with its own `coder-<wsid>-dind-lib` volume."],[4780,"The workspace container must resolve `host.docker.internal`; the model lane reaches\nLiteLLM through that host gateway, and so does `LITELLM_BASE_URL`."],[208,"The workspace fork: the install guard and the launch"],[834,"The workspace pass"],[3135,"The workspace side of that seam is\ngrok-build-and-agents.md."],[248,"The workspace twin watches `$HOME/workspace`; the devcontainer twin passes its\n`$dc_dir`, because those clones sit on the `/srv/coder-devcontainers` bind."],[3750,"the write"],[758,"The write is atomic (`<path>.tmp` then `mv`)."],[3737,"Their health endpoints are `http://loki:3100/ready`, `http://tempo:3200/ready` and\n`http://mimir:8080/ready`, all compose-DNS only."],[3609,"Their named volumes survive either way, and `reset` is the one that destroys them."],[3933,"Then `INFISICAL_PULL_ON_START`, whose off path prints that the boot \"keeps the credentials it\nalready has\" and also exits 0. Every other failure path - no `infisical` binary in the image,\nno `HOME`, a refused Universal Auth login, an empty export, a refused publish - exits 0 as well."],[5164,"Then check **how** the credential is sent, because the two GitHub endpoints disagree\nabout the scheme. `api.github.com` and `gh` accept `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. The\ngit data endpoint refuses it: one token answered `/user` with `200` and\n`<repo>.git/info/refs?service=git-receive-pack` with `401` plus\n`remote: invalid credentials` while the token rode a bearer header. git has to send it\nas **Basic** auth with the token as the password."],[5163,"Then check the URL scheme, which no probe can fix: that credential covers\n`https://github.com/...` remotes only, so a `git@github.com:` or `ssh://` URL gets\nneither helper nor askpass token and needs an SSH key you placed yourself, which this\nstack provisions nowhere."],[979,"Then connect your GitHub account in Coder (Settings -> Tokens / external auth)\nand link the same provider to **both** workspace templates (Templates -> edit\n-> External Auth)."],[790,"Then connect your GitHub account. On a running workspace, click **GitHub reauth** on\nthe agent bar (Coder v2.36's `/external-auth/<id>` page; use **Reauthenticate** if the\npage says you are already authenticated). First-time connect also works from the\nworkspace create/update form and from Settings -> Tokens / external auth."],[1876,"Then finish the two browser-only steps:"],[5430,"Then hand the deletions to a human:"],[4895,"Then look at the `== terminal launchers: start ==` run in the workspace start log and\nread its `summary:` line: a green `2 ok, 0 warnings, 0 failed` with no files is the old\ntemplate, and `3 failed` with two `error:` lines is a boot that still cannot write."],[1853,"Then look before you change anything. `--check` is read-only:"],[4842,"Then open a new terminal; `PATH` there already includes `~/.grok/bin`."],[394,"Then push `workspace` (the repo is not mounted into the container, so the directory has to\ntravel as a tar):"],[400,"Then re-pin both values:"],[4260,"Then re-run `bootstrap` and recreate the stack you switched. The commands are in the\nREADME."],[5126,"Then read the store with the pair cleared, because `gh auth status` on its own reports\nthe env pair rather than what is stored:"],[5204,"Then restart the workspace. The six are agent environment values Coder renders per start\n(`templates/workspace/main.tf:549`, `:639-653`) and the body is `run_on_start` (`:720`),\nso a running workspace keeps the empty set until it starts again."],[5198,"Then retry the pull and bring the stack up again, because\ncompose reads the file only when it recreates a container\n(`scripts/infisical.sh:527`):"],[4905,"Then run `bash -lc 'command -v grok'`. A workspace on a current image answers\n`/usr/local/bin/grok`, so an empty answer means the CLI is missing, not the profile."],[4707,"Then separate a sick proxy from a sick box, because each has its own fix."],[4049,"Then the note the CLI prints is the real edge, and it is worth repeating here: compose\nreads `.env` only when a container is recreated, so the rotated password reaches Coder on\nthe next `up`. Nothing hot-reloads it."],[4009,"Then, any time after, `check` is the single command that asks every precondition at once:"],[3727,"Then, from the checkout on the stack host, in this order. Each one splits one symptom from\nthe next."],[5451,"Then, in a new session in the repository you want to convert:"],[354,"Then, per template, it confirms an **active** template version. A push can exit 0 and\nstill leave the template inactive if its Terraform run failed, which shows up as the\ntemplate missing from the create dropdown."],[3258,"There are no rpm, tpm or `max_parallel_requests` caps anywhere, on purpose. A cap parks\nrequests behind an in-memory semaphore inside the proxy; without one, a fully offered\nbox sheds load in its own scheduler."],[3919,"There is a **second gate** under the first: `INFISICAL_PULL_ON_START`, default `false`.\nIt decides only whether a workspace's boot fetch dials the vault at all."],[3980,"There is deliberately no `--json` mode: a JSON answer about a credential is an answer that\nleaks it in a different font."],[3013,"There is no `allowed_fails` key in the config, and the absence is deliberate: naming it\nwith a non-default number selects the counting branch of the cooldown decision instead\nof the rate rule, and that branch counts inside a window of `cooldown_time`."],[2649,"There is no browser card here and nothing to approve elsewhere; the terminal door does\nnot loosen `approvals.mode: manual`, and `--yolo` / `HERMES_YOLO_MODE` have no place in\nthis stack. See Approvals."],[378,"There is no GitHub-token template variable, so no push ever carries a personal access\ntoken. See GitHub credentials for a workspace."],[2382,"There is no longer one `config.toml` to set once for a whole account: each\nworkspace renders its own from the template on start. A hand edit there lasts until\n**that** workspace restarts and touches no other workspace, and the next start after\na template re-push brings the file back from the new template."],[4065,"There is no reason to open `.env` by hand while this subsystem is adopted, and no command\nhere prints a credential. If you are cat-ing the env file to debug a sync, you are reading\nthe wrong file: `status` and `check` answer the same question."],[4793,"There is no second lane behind this one, so run these probes before touching anything\nelse."],[5064,"There is no setting for it: the shipped 4.145.0 registers no OSC 52 key,\nand upstream\nmicrosoft/vscode#318254 is\nopen with two unmerged fixes."],[3628,"These are directory binds, so measured against the pinned image an in-place rewrite\nof a mounted file and a rename of a new one over it both reached the container with no\nrestart and no recreate, which is why the dashboards section below can promise a minute\nrather than a redeploy"],[2188,"These are globs over the parsed command text, so an abbreviated tmux verb\n(`tmux kill-sess`) or a bracketed pattern (`pkill -f [t]mux`) walks past them - the seed\nrule that names the prohibition is the other half, and the plain `bash` profile is how a\nsession reaches a shell once they are all gone."],[2741,"These are the route verbs, and `arc-chat` is the row to route through when a session\nwants the Arc's tool-capable model:"],[4221,"These are what the shipped defaults compose. The operator sets the parts, not these\nstrings: the grammar is `<service>-<environment>-<suffix>.<base>`, always ONE label\nunder the zone."],[3407,"These files belong to the scaffold repository. This repo does not ship them, lint them, or keep a\ncopy: it fetches them at run time and renders them."],[3988,"These four cannot come from the vault, because the vault needs them to start."],[878,"These four sections are also the long form of the `.env.sample` comments that\npoint here: GitHub external auth, Grok profile mode, public hosts, and the\nSpark `agent` model group. Where a topic page already owns a subject, this page\npoints at it instead of restating it."],[3038,"These retries are instant and stay on the same box. A status-less exception means\n`_deployment_ids_to_skip_on_retry` excludes nothing and `_time_to_sleep_before_retry`\nreturns 0 while any deployment is healthy, and on the five pinned groups the\nworkspace-wide `x-litellm-session-id` pin sends every subagent of a workspace to one\nbox anyway. The block makes a refusal less likely to surface. Relocation comes from the\nbox and the fan-out."],[2124,"They are seeded the same way, by\n`coder_script.stack_repo_skills`, from `templates/common/ez-bazel-first.SKILL.md`,\n`ez-strong-types.SKILL.md` and `ez-trunk-based-repo.SKILL.md`, plus the three python\nhelpers they shell out to. Same absent-only contract, same marker-based takeover rule,\nsame `[skills] disabled` escape hatch."],[2527,"They differ from the authoring trio in one structural way: two of them shell out to a\npython helper, so their seed ships `scripts/owned_files_check.py`, `scripts/glob_budget.py`\nand `scripts/type_baseline.py` beside the `SKILL.md`. Those helpers are stack payload like\neverything else here, which means the copy in a workspace is stack-owned while it carries the\nmarker, and the way to fix a helper is to fix the seed under `templates/common/` and\nre-materialize, never to patch the copy that is running."],[3017,"They sit beside `health_check_interval: 120`, `health_check_staleness_threshold: 900`\nand `health_check_concurrency: 2`."],[4890,"They then said nothing about it: `mkdir -p ... 2>/dev/null` swallowed the\nrefusal, `cat >` failed, and the run printed `ok:` for each launcher and closed at\n`summary: 2 ok, 0 warnings, 0 failed`."],[2987,"Thinking levels: what `agent` bakes, and what the baked aliases change"],[3642,"Thirteen JSON files in `observability/grafana/dashboards/` are the only dashboards this\nstack ships. `observability/grafana/provisioning/dashboards/stack.yaml:11` loads them all\ninto one `EVO-T1` folder (`:14`) with `disableDeletion: true` (`:16`),\n`updateIntervalSeconds: 60` (`:17`) and `allowUiUpdates: false` (`:18`)."],[3562,"This box needs all three because a container that dies takes its own log file out of\n`docker compose logs` reach only if you are too late - but a workspace that was slow at\n03:00 is unrecoverable without retention."],[5270,"This bundle closes it by pointing Grafana at\n  `observability/grafana/unified-storage/overrides.yml`\n  through `GF_UNIFIED_STORAGE_OVERRIDES_PATH`, so the call answers `200`. The file sets\n  no limit; its presence is the whole fix, and what the endpoint then reports is\n  Grafana's own default - `{\"usage\":0,\"limit\":1000}` for both dashboards and folders on\n  `grafana/grafana:13.3.1`."],[4328,"This change installs nothing on its own: no deploy, no `up`, no `refresh-configs` creates\na container on a Spark. `--apply` is the only flag that touches a box, and it says so in\nits own header line before the first one (`scripts/spark-monitor.sh:327`)."],[3997,"This creates the super admin, the organization and the machine identity **inside the\n`infisical` container**, and writes the returned identifiers into `.env`."],[2338,"This family is **marker-aware** rather than absent-only like the skills: a copy that still\ncarries the stack marker - the `\"__evoT1Stack\": true` key in the manifest, which has to stay\nparseable JSON, and the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` comment in the shell files - is\nrewritten on every start."],[3232,"This fleet serves chat and streaming completions, so the limit is honest rather\nthan load-bearing, but it is the reason a new modality on these aliases needs its own\nlook before anyone calls it covered."],[5398,"This fleet's own dev-versus-stable split is the reference implementation: separate project\nnames, separate dotenv files, and a subdomain composed from parts rather than from a branch\nname, driven by `bazelisk run //scripts:dev-stack -- up`,\n`bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack -- up`, and `bazelisk run //scripts:update-stack` for the\npull-and-deploy pair."],[4987,"This is a fix to the sweep's wording and not to the finding: the\nbranch used to clear the field and fall through into the missing-line verdict the\nsingle-profile check quotes above, printing `the [subagents] table carries no\n'max_concurrent' line - a hand edit, which no restart undoes` for a line that was present\nand correct, while `--config` on the very same file said it was an un-comparable width."],[560,"This is idempotent, runs as\nthe workspace user so their git credentials are consulted, and refuses to touch an\nexisting non-empty non-git folder there. An empty pre-created target still clones."],[5038,"This is not a broken credential. It happens with a valid token too, because Authelia\ngates every route."],[640,"This is not an invitation to hand-edit the file. `config.toml` is re-rendered from\n`grok-config.toml.tftpl` on every start of this workspace, so an edit a person makes\nthere is overwritten by the next boot and touches no other workspace. The keys\na person actually wants are template variables: `grok_subagent_max_concurrent`,\n`grok_subagent_max_depth` and `grok_subagents_lane` for the fan-out\n(the fan-out seam), and `grok_config_extra`\nfor anything the managed block does not set."],[3908,"This is the **free self-hosted tier**. No dynamic secrets, no cross-project sharing, and\nno `LICENSE_KEY` anywhere in the checkout: both of those features are paid, and the\nbundle ships neither. What is here is static shared secrets in one project, exported as\ndotenv."],[5216,"This is the belt, not the filter. The loop already drops every deny-listed name before a\nline is staged (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:181-189`), compared\nupper-cased so `BASH_ENV`, `bash_env` and `Bash_Env` fall in one arm, and the body's own\ncomment reserves the second pass for a filter that regressed or a staged file edited by\nhand (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:219-229`)."],[313,"This is the escape the stack now uses: the three skill payloads ride\n  `coder_script.stack_skills` rather than the startup argument, because the devcontainer\n  twin had 491 bytes of headroom left and three more inlined payloads could not fit there."],[5348,"This is the human-readable twin of the `trunk-refactor` skill\n(`skills/trunk-refactor/SKILL.md`). The skill is what an agent session follows; this page is\nwhat a person reads, with the examples the skill leaves out to stay short. The branch rules\nthemselves live in Branching - this page is about getting a repository *onto*\nthose rules."],[4350,"This is the only mode that looks at a box. It ferries one read-only probe\n(`scripts/lib/probes/spark-monitor.sh`) base64-encoded through `probe_transport`\n(`scripts/lib/spark.sh:173`), which prints twelve `KEY=value` lines per box:"],[1477,"This is the question that costs the most sessions, because the answer is spread over four different\nmechanisms and each one is normally discovered by a failing gate."],[4346,"This is the run to make before pointing Prometheus at three boxes you have not looked at."],[4888,"This is the same daemon behaviour the\n`~/.shared/vscode/settings.json` entry\ncovers one directory over."],[1541,"This is the trap that makes a hand-check unreliable, and it is the reason the CLI keeps Bazel's\nstderr instead of discarding it. A query can print `ERROR: no such target` and leave stdout empty,\nwhich looks exactly like \"nothing depends on this\":"],[1525,"This is why an unlisted payload directory stays invisible rather than being checked loosely: a file\nthat travels in no runfiles tree is a file no sandboxed action can open, so `test-fast` and `lint`\nnever read it and never fail. Nothing prints a warning about that."],[2525,"This is workflow curation, separate from the memory system, which stores durable facts\n(upstream `/remember`, `/memory`, `/dream`, shipped here as `/ez-learn`), and from\n`AGENTS.md`, which is the always-loaded rules file. A skill loads when its `description`\nmatches, and holds a procedure."],[3116,"This key is the opt-out; a client header is not. An empty or short `x-litellm-session-id`\ndoes not skip the pin at this tag - that header is read verbatim at any length, and only\nthe generic `x-<vendor>-session-id` family is shape-checked - so a caller that tried to\nspread by sending an empty value would collapse every swarm request onto one shared pin."],[4971,"This note is the whole\nreason the sweep keeps the daemon's raw answer rather than filtering inside the call:\nbefore it, one stray tab inside a `coder.workspace_name` label was enough to drop that\nworkspace out of the report with nothing said about it, and `summary: 1 ok, 0 warnings, 0\nfailed` read as a healthy fleet that simply had no third workspace."],[4273,"This repo cannot verify any of it; check it on the Traefik box."],[1446,"This repo keeps its coupling in BUILD files. Three of them carry the record:"],[2528,"This repo keeps its own project-scoped `/trunk-refactor` under\n`skills/trunk-refactor/SKILL.md`, which is the rule of record for *this* repository and\ncites its gates by label. `/ez-trunk-based-repo` is the portable version of the same model:\nit discovers a target repo's own gates at inventory time rather than assuming Bazel, so it\nworks in a Compose, K3s, Ansible or Terraform repository too."],[4175,"This repo ships a `.devcontainer/` of its own —\nthe **contributor** one for a laptop and CI, built from `images/dev/Dockerfile` — and it\nis not that nested kind: `.devcontainer/contributor-env` alongside it makes\n`probe_repo` answer a miss, so a Coder workspace of this repo stays on the `workspace`\ntemplate instead of building its own container inside its own DinD sidecar."],[3402,"This repository already uses the word *template* for a **Coder template**: the Terraform tree\nunder `templates/workspace/` and `templates/devcontainer/` that `push-template.sh` registers with\nthe Coder server."],[2851,"This repository brings up one Compose project on a GMKtec EVO-T1 (Intel Core Ultra 9\n285H, Arc 140T iGPU, 96 GB DDR5) and keeps it runnable by conversation, by dashboard, or\nby `bazelisk`."],[4003,"This seeds the twelve managed keys into the vault, skipping any key the env file does\nnot hold or holds empty - with a `warning:`, never an empty write. It then exports the\nproject again and compares a hash per key, so a set the server accepted and dropped is\nreported as a failure rather than a clean seed."],[2112,"This stack has no x.ai credential: LiteLLM is the sole model transport, with\n  `env_key = \"LITELLM_API_KEY\"` and `base_url` `http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1`, so\n  `~/.grok/bundled/` is never created and there is no bundled copy for `grok inspect` to\n  label."],[5285,"This stack turns it off with\n`multitenancy_enabled: false` in `observability/mimir/mimir.yml`, so the provisioned\ndatasource sends no tenancy header and the compose network is the trust boundary. A\nquery that starts insisting on a header means that file changed, not that the data went\nmissing - and re-enabling tenancy is a change to the `remote_write` credentials as\nwell, not just to Grafana."],[3991,"This writes only the binary, at the path `infisical_cli_install_path` prints, and nothing\nelse changes. The release it fetches is the pin: `INFISICAL_CLI_VERSION` in `.env.example`\n(0.45.8 as shipped), from the goreleaser asset name the seam builds. Nothing here pulls a\nversion out of the network."],[423,"Those\n    four are what the `[ui] permission_mode` key documents, not the whole vocabulary the\n    CLI speaks: its own `--permission-mode` flag spells more, so a mode outside this\n    dropdown belongs in the `[ui]` block of `~/.grok/config.toml` by hand, and the next\n    start replaces it with what this field says - and says so on the boot log, naming the\n    value it dropped."],[5132,"Those clicks are in\nthe reauth entry,\nand the script's own note on a workspace with no connected account points at the same\ntwo buttons."],[3073,"Those eight groups reuse the same `SPARK1/2/3_OPENAI_URL` / `SPARK_n_API_KEY` pairs as\n`agent`. They are separate model groups on the same hardware, not eight more boxes:\nrouting state is per group, so least-busy's counters and the session pin are computed\ninside a group and two chats on different aliases can land on the same box at once."],[3738,"Those exact URLs are the `siteMonitor` of the **Observability** group's cards on the\ndashboard, so the card badge is the probe - and because those four containers have no\nhealthcheck, it is the only automatic one."],[731,"Those four are the whole bar."],[4343,"Those four host exporters publish on the **host's loopback only**, so a probe of them runs\nin a host shell, the same as Prometheus' own UI on `PROMETHEUS_PORT`."],[3018,"Those keys have to sit in `general_settings:`; `health_check_interval` and\n`health_check_concurrency` under `router_settings:` make the proxy raise `ValueError`\nat boot."],[2184,"those killers aimed at a whole user or parent (`pkill -u`, `-U`, `-P`)"],[2095,"Those last two decide what survives the multiplexer: tmux rewrites 24-bit color down\nto the palette an attached client advertises, which is what makes a theme look\nwashed out in the browser, and extkeys is what makes Shift+Enter and Ctrl+. arrive\ndistinct from Enter."],[1802,"Those numbers are also series now: `node_exporter` reads the same `/proc` and `/sys`\nread-only and `cadvisor` covers the containers, so the tile answers \"what is the box doing\nnow, as the dashboard sees it\" and the Grafana board answers \"and what was it at 03:00\".\nThe tile survives the bundle being off; the board does not."],[1107,"Those operator runs are bounded: a script's non-interactive `docker exec` closes stdin\n(`</dev/null`), and the docker wrappers go through `timeout(1)` with `--kill-after`, so a\n`bazelisk run //scripts:<stem>` cannot sit forever the way `docker exec -i` did under\n`bazelisk run`, waiting for an EOF that never came."],[1122,"Those payload groups live one per payload directory (`//litellm:config`,\n`//searxng:settings`, `//homepage:config`, `//homepage:icons`, `//hermes:seed`,\n`//hermes:skills`, `//proxy:confs`, `//images/dev:dockerfile`, `//images/dev:tool_versions`,\nand a `:payload` in each of `templates/common`, `templates/workspace`,\n`templates/devcontainer`), with the root BUILD.bazel holding the groups that have no\ndirectory of their own (`//:compose_file`, `//:env_sample`, `//:env_example`, `//:license`,\n`//:devcontainer`, `//:githooks`, and the `//:ci_*` groups)."],[4729,"Those re-dispatches came from this repo's own config. At the pinned tag\n`ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.102.1` a stream that dies before its first chunk raises\n`MidStreamFallbackError`, which subclasses `ServiceUnavailableError`\n(`litellm/exceptions.py:1114` at that tag), and `get_num_retries_from_retry_policy` walks the\nexception MRO most-specific first, so it lands on `ServiceUnavailableErrorRetries` and\nnever reaches `DefaultRetries`."],[3460,"Those seven are named once, in `NEW_REPO_TOKENS`, and they are the whole contract between this\nscript and the scaffold -- a ceiling rather than an equality, so the template may use a subset of\nthem. A token that survives is a hard failure, not a warning -- a repository that ships with its\nplaceholders showing is worse than no template at all."],[606,"Those three\ntrees are then the same files every other workspace this owner has reads and writes,\nand they survive a rebuild."],[99,"Those three words are environments and never branch names, and\n`bazelisk run //scripts:branch-hygiene` is what keeps that honest: a branch or a\nremote-tracking ref named `dev`, `staging`, `prod`, `uat` or the like - bare, or as the\nfirst segment of a path - is an error and exits 1."],[3093,"Three deployments, one per Spark box, and no `order:` tier. A tier would make the\nlower boxes unreachable while any tier-1 box stayed healthy."],[2327,"Three limits are worth knowing before you trust a clean scan, and each is a choice rather than\nan oversight."],[1943,"Three limits of a clean scan"],[4030,"Three more are credentials that never appear in a compose interpolation, so they\ntravel to their consumer through a CLI rather than through `${VAR}`:"],[3812,"Three of the host alerts exist because the obvious design has a blind spot:"],[2277,"Three of the seven name `spawn_subagent`: `reviewer`, `security-auditor` and `tester`\n(`templates/common/reviewer.AGENT.md:5`, `templates/common/security-auditor.AGENT.md:5`,\n`templates/common/tester.AGENT.md:5`). `explorer`, `architect`, `implementer` and\n`documenter` name none of it, so a mapper cannot recurse and the wave a spawner raises one\nlevel down is made of read-only mappers. The `tools` list is what enforces that ceiling; the\nbody prose of each seed only explains it."],[2240,"three or fewer files in `owns` from one directory family"],[1451,"Three pages this one leans on:"],[1479,"Three payload trees are in play:"],[3807,"Three rule files arrive with Prometheus and need no second registration:"],[1696,"Three runfiles traps bit this gate, and all fail *silently*, so they are worth\nnaming:"],[5006,"Three separate reads, from the stack host. The first prints `unhealthy` rather than\nan error when the daemon fails its own probe, and `no such container` when the\nworkspace has no sidecar at all:"],[3207,"Three settings switch the filter off, and the config avoids all three:"],[3124,"Three spawners with three mappers each is twelve of\nthe fifteen streams the fleet owns, which fits beside a parent still holding its own\nconversation, and the panel is cheap precisely because the writers have all landed by the\ntime it runs: the fleet is then idle, and both the skeptics and the mappers they spawn are\nunpinned traffic that `least-busy` can place on all three boxes at once."],[2194,"Three stack-owned numbers decide whether a fan-out of subagents is parallel here at all:\nhow many slots one session gets, which lane those children's traffic rides, and whether\nthe work was cut finely enough to fill the slots. The first two are the rendered\n`[subagents]` keys just above; the third is a seeded skill and one command the parent runs\nbefore wave 1."],[1690,"Three targets answer \"is this code actually executed by a test\" instead of\nassuming it. They are `manual` like the npm gates, so `//:test-fast` stays fast, and\nthey are members of `//:test-all`, which pre-push and CI run:"],[2521,"Three things about skills matter in practice here:"],[2959,"Three ways to land it and get nothing"],[3183,"Three ways to land this feature and get nothing."],[4196,"Timeouts and WebSockets"],[4774,"Titles that never appear and a long chat that dies at its context budget are the\nhelper lanes pointing at a dead alias. Re-running the script moves them."],[4214,"TLS terminates at Traefik. The `router` sidecar holds no certificate."],[2088,"tmux holds its history once per pane, in the server, and every client of that pane\nshares the one buffer. Hence the split: the deep store is tmux's and the browser\nkeeps a short viewport."],[5070,"tmux keeps no buffer of its own, so `Prefix-]` is unbound and there is\nno `tmux show-buffer` to read: the machine clipboard is the only clipboard here."],[570,"tmux keeps no clipboard of its\n  own next to that: the copy-mode copies, the prefix paste `]`, the buffer picker `=`\n  and the root-table middle-click paste are unbound, and `Prefix m` is only the switch\n  that hands the wheel to tmux for a long scroll and hands it back."],[2092,"tmux reads `history-limit` when a pane is created, so an existing pane keeps the\nnumber it was born with."],[737,"To\nbump: read `https://github.com/coder/code-server/releases`, edit both locals,\n`bazelisk test //tests:bats_coder_apps_test`, `bazelisk run //scripts:push-template`,\nthen restart the workspaces. The pin is a template value and deliberately stays out\nof `images/dev/tool-versions.env`, where every key has to be an `images/dev/Dockerfile`\n`ARG` and this tool ships in no image at all."],[3916,"To adopt it, set the key in the env file that belongs to the project you run - `.env` for\nthe stable stack, `dev-stack.env` for the dev one - and bring the stack up as usual:"],[4897,"To bring one workspace back while the restart waits, re-materialize the two files from a\nshell in it: `bazelisk run //scripts:seed-dev-env -- --home \"$HOME\"`. The **bash**\nprofile in the terminal dropdown stays the route no helper mediates."],[4270,"To cap each tier separately, declare one `loadBalancer` service per tier, each\npointing at the same `http://<this-box-lan-ip>:8080` with `passHostHeader: true` and\nits own transport (`evo-t1-coder` / `evo-t1-hermes` / `evo-t1-grafana` /\n`evo-t1-infisical` at `300s`, `evo-t1-litellm` at `600s`, `evo-t1-kasm` at `3600s`),\nand point each router at its own service."],[723,"To change the body, edit `templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl` and re-materialise\nit with `bazelisk run //scripts:push-template`. It is not one of the twins:\n`scripts/lib/template-push.sh:188` stages the common copy beside each `main.tf` and\noverwrites any same-named file a template dir still carries, and what a running workspace\nholds is Coder's Filestore row for its template version, which the next push replaces too.\nNothing here is fixed from inside a workspace."],[2102,"To give a workspace dictation instead: run PulseAudio on the workstation with its\nTCP module enabled, export `PULSE_SERVER=tcp=<workstation>:4713` into the workspace,\nand install `pulseaudio-utils` there for `parec`."],[2654,"To have the assistant edit files on the host, name the directory:\n`--writable \"${STACK_DEPLOY_PATH:-/opt/stack-deploy}\"` or the checkout path."],[924,"To hide one of the slash commands, set `disabled = [\"ez-learn\"]` (or\n`ez-skillify`, `ez-create-skill`, `ez-bazel-first`, `ez-strong-types`,\n`ez-trunk-based-repo`, or `ez-micro-plan`) under `[skills]` in\n`~/.grok/config.toml`."],[2121,"To hide the slash command, set `disabled = [\"ez-learn\"]` under `[skills]` in\n  `~/.grok/config.toml`."],[2395,"To put native search back on a transport that really serves the tool: flip the key\nto `false` in the seed - both `templates/workspace/grok-config.toml.tftpl` and\n`templates/devcontainer/`'s copy - and re-push, which applies it fleet-wide. For one\nworkspace without a push, the create form's **Grok config extras** field appends\nfree-form TOML verbatim to that workspace's file. Either way start a new session,\nand expect the same 400 back if the endpoint still answers function tools only."],[2798,"To reseed deliberately:"],[4796,"To restore the native tool, flip `disable_web_search` to\nfalse in both template twins and re-push - only for an endpoint that really serves the\ntool, or the 400 comes straight back."],[2120,"To take a copy over, edit it and delete the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker\n  line: a marker-free file is user-owned, and the seeder leaves it alone unless you pass\n  `--force`. A deletion is undone - the boot writes the file again whenever it is absent,\n  and `refresh-configs` re-seeds an absent target, so the next boot restores the stack's\n  copy."],[922,"To take a seeded copy over, edit it and\ndelete the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker line: a marker-free file is\nuser-owned, and the seeder leaves it alone unless you pass `--force`."],[4818,"To take the same reading from inside the workspace, replay the path on `:8080`, the\npublished `router` port. That reaches `coder:3000` through the sidecar while\nbypassing Traefik, Authelia and the WAN, so a reply there that differs from the\nbrowser's `https://` URL names the cloud hops."],[3607,"To turn the bundle off, set the key in the env file that belongs to that project -\n`.env` for the stable stack, `dev-stack.env` for the dev one - and bring the stack up:"],[2933,"Tool calls: the measured limitation"],[2986,"Tool calls: the measured limitation and the path that supports them"],[5246,"Traefik and Authelia have to pass `Upgrade`. Cloudflare's orange-cloud proxy\nhas WebSockets on by default. A page that loads and a Chat tab that dies is\nthis hop, not the basic-auth provider."],[4193,"Traefik configuration"],[2624,"Traefik on the other LAN server (TLS `*.overeazy.io`, Authelia)"],[5232,"Traefik pointed at `:9119` never hits that file. A rewritten Host also\nmisses every block."],[2627,"Traefik's backend is `:8080`, not `:9119`. See public-access.md."],[1649,"Traps that fail silently"],[2824,"Treat `HERMES_API_SERVER_KEY` as a root credential: rotate it by editing `.env` and\nrecreating the container, and give a phone a Shortcut that holds it rather than a URL\nthat carries it."],[4701,"Treat it as a reason to raise the interval, not to chase the box. What 120 s does buy\nis that cycles cannot stack: the sleep sits after the sweep (`proxy_server.py:4234`)\nand concurrency 2 is a hard cap."],[3362,"Treat it as a separate credential with its own purpose: a dedicated key whose\nprivate half lives on the laptop you bring to a reboot, not the key you push to\nevery repository."],[2815,"Treat its approvals the way you treat a root shell. That is the same standing as\npublic Coder."],[3954,"Treat write access to the vault project as the trust boundary it is: it is shell access to\nevery workspace that boots with the fetch on. Read access is a much smaller grant than write,\nand the machine identity the workspaces authenticate as should hold only the former."],[4414,"Troubleshooting"],[4416,"Troubleshooting"],[1881,"Troubleshooting — start here when a step above says no."],[3368,"troubleshooting.md for the symptom-first list once the\nbox is back up."],[5308,"Trunk-based + flags refactor"],[5310,"Trunk-based + flags refactor"],[2,"Trunk-based branch rules: main is the only long-lived branch, work branches are short-lived, and a pull request is the only way back in."],[39,"Trunk-based, GitHub-Flow shaped: one long-lived branch, short-lived work branches, and a pull\nrequest as the only way back into `main`."],[3989,"Turn the flag on: `INFISICAL_ENABLED=true` in the project's env file."],[2662,"Turning it on is two deliberate edits:"],[1960,"Turning native search back on"],[3502,"Turning the bundle off"],[3846,"Turning the flag on"],[5307,"Turning the flag on needs the payload tree, not just the flag: the six bind mounts read\n`observability/**`, so a checkout that has `docker-compose.yml` ahead of the\n`observability/` directory (a partial pull) fails mounting, the same failure shape as\nthe missing bind-mount source at the top of this page."],[2474,"Twenty-six files seed into every new workspace, on first boot and only while the file is\nabsent (the fleet family adds seventeen more paths under `~/.grok/agents`,\n`~/.grok/personas` and the two skill homes, on the contracts in\nThe seeded fleet suite):"],[3782,"Two commands destroy state that has no backup:"],[3626,"Two consequences of the `:ro` mounts, both the same rule the other payload directories\nfollow:"],[4324,"Two containers per box, both created by this CLI and by nothing else:"],[2838,"Two copies of the stack on one box"],[3390,"Two different things called \"template\", and which one this page is about"],[2916,"Two doors, one key"],[1536,"Two exclusions earn their place. `except kind(\"test_suite\", //...)` drops the aggregates, which is\nwhat the CLI filters on so `//:test-fast` cannot answer a per-file question, and\n`except kind(\"sh_test\", //lints:*)` drops the two manual lint targets, `//lints:shell` and\n`//lints:shfmt`, that ride on every script:"],[3117,"Two facts not to get wrong:"],[4200,"Two follow-ups, both by hand"],[1583,"Two gates carry most of it, and both are members of `//lints:all`, so `//:lint`,\n`//:test-all`, and the `bazel` job of `.github/workflows/ci.yml` run them:"],[699,"Two gates, both `default = false`: `infisical_enabled` decides whether the vault is part\nof the workspace at all, `infisical_pull_on_start` only whether a start waits on it\n(`templates/workspace/coder.tf:207-274`)."],[1639,"Two gates, one rule"],[766,"Two helpers are seeded into `~/.grok/bin` on every start, both `chmod +x`:\n`vscode-terminal-tmux` (the default profile) and `grok-build-terminal`. The two\nprofiles in `settings.json` exec exactly those paths, so the seed body reads both\nfiles back and prints `error:` naming the `exit code: 127` a tab gets when one did not\nland, rather than closing green. The missing-file cause and its remedy are in\ntroubleshooting.md."],[4461,"Two hops can answer 502"],[4813,"Two hops can answer 502 on that path: this box's nginx, when `coder:3000` will not\nresolve or connect, and Coder's own Go proxy, whose `ReverseProxy` ErrorHandler\nfires when the app upstream answers nothing. Two reads tell them apart, both from\nthe stack host:"],[3309,"Two keys, two purposes"],[877,"Two kinds of file go stale in this repo, and because neither of them is\nchecked in, `git pull` cannot fix either one for you. `update-configs` is the\none command that refreshes both, and it is written to be safe to run when you\nare not looking closely at the diff."],[3462,"Two kinds of path are removed on the way out:"],[3374,"Two kinds of template"],[3926,"Two kinds of volume meet in that path and they are