exit 2 - Bazel claims the flag as its own build option and the script never starts.\nEvery flag this CLI takes goes after `--`."],[5402,"With Helm the same shape is `values/dev.yaml`, `values/staging.yaml`, and\n`helm upgrade --install app ./chart -n lab-staging -f values/staging.yaml --set image.tag=...`.\nSecrets come from the cluster's own store or an external secret, never from the overlay."],[4375,"With it on, four groups per box:"],[476,"With it on, per workspace:"],[768,"With no\n`tmux` on PATH it falls back to a plain login shell.\nBefore it reads who is attached it detaches any client on those sessions that has\nreported no activity for over 6 hours (`EVO_TMUX_STALE_AFTER`, in seconds): a tab\nwhose browser side went away can leave its client attached and draining nothing,\nand one such client is enough to keep a free session looking busy forever."],[4997,"with no `docker` on PATH: `error: cannot list workspace containers - the docker CLI is\nnot on this host`. A daemon that will not answer is\n`error: cannot list containers - is the docker daemon reachable from this host?`;"],[1029,"With no `SPARKn_HOST` and no `SPARKn_OPENAI_URL` set, compose takes the host from\n`STACK_LAN_HOST`, which is at least a machine this stack owns: `agent` stays\ndefined but unusable and LiteLLM falls back to `coder`, the Arc alias."],[772,"With no `tmux` on PATH, and on any create or\nattach it cannot complete, it hands the tab a plain login shell."],[3269,"With no concurrency cap configured, the proxy neither queued nor shed inside itself,\nand a fully offered box absorbed the overflow in its own scheduler."],[942,"With no terminal to prompt through the pass warns and leaves those keys alone, which is\nwhy `--dry-run` / `--non-interactive` is the shape that belongs in a script or CI."],[2044,"With no tmux (offline first boot) the helper execs a plain login shell, so the\ndefault terminal still opens."],[5433,"with the commands they will run:"],[2026,"With the default `exit-empty` the server itself leaves when its last session\ndoes (tmux#2081), which is why a\nreopen probes the server before raising anything - a tab whose server is gone has\nended normally, and re-raising there would boot a server for a terminal nobody is\nlooking at (tmux has no server probe: `has-session` answers the same for a\nmissing session and a missing server, which is why upstream declined to add\n`check-server`, tmux#2523)."],[701,"With the first gate off the `coder_script` is not merely idle - its `count` is `0`, so the\ntemplate renders no script, no boot log line, and no `INFISICAL_*` agent-env key, and a\nworkspace whose stack never adopted Infisical cannot tell the difference\n(`templates/workspace/main.tf:708-721`). With the first on and the second off the resource\nexists and does nothing but name its gate (`templates/common/infisical-secrets.sh.tftpl:27-30`)."],[3995,"With the flag already on, this first `up` also tries the env-file refresh and gets nothing:\nthere is no `INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID` yet, so the seam prints `note: the pull was refused before it\nran; <file> keeps the values it has` and the runner follows with its `warning:` line. That\npair is noise until step 5 writes the identifiers - it is not a failed bring-up."],[902,"With the flag off - the shipped default - that branch never runs and the file keeps\nevery value it has, and `bazelisk run //scripts:update-stack -- --dry-run` plans the\nfetch and writes nothing."],[3922,"With the flag off the `coder_script` resource is absent outright - no script, no boot log line,\nno `INFISICAL_*` key on the agent environment - and the `.bashrc` hook is not written either,\nbecause that line is gated on `infisical_hook`, which both twins set from `var.infisical_enabled`."],[2062,"With the seed's `mouse off` tmux never sees a button, so a plain drag is the\nclient's own highlight and the seed's `terminal.integrated.copyOnSelection: true`\nputs that highlight on the machine clipboard with no chord (the harness recorded\n`navigator.clipboard.writeText` firing on a client selection, before this switch)."],[509,"With the toggle off - or on a repo that carries no `devcontainer.json`, where the build\nhas nothing to build - the editor attaches to the plain workspace agent instead, opened\non the same clone path."],[697,"With the toggle off the same miss is expected and the editor opens the clone directly."],[507,"With the toggle on, `coder_devcontainer.repo` then builds the repo's own\n`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` on the sidecar through the Coder agent\n(`@devcontainers/cli` is installed into the parent workspace container by a\n`run_on_start` module, and the golden image does not ship it)."],[1118,"With the variable unset the script mounts nothing, which is what a contributor laptop gets."],[4005,"With the vault and `.env` agreeing this writes nothing new. It is the read path, so it\nis the one to run before you trust `push`."],[2140,"within it the summary goes to the Arc group"],[2275,"Within these six, only `implementer` names `search_replace`, and only `implementer` and\n`tester` name `write` at all; the other four name no edit tool and each says in its own body\nthat it edits nothing. The seventh definition `templates/common/` holds, `documenter`, is the\nadvisor family's rather than this one's and names both `search_replace` and `write`\n(`templates/common/documenter.AGENT.md:5`), because the deliverable of that role is an edit to\na page - see The five advisor commands."],[1475,"Without `--json` the same labels are interleaved with the report lines, so piping them straight into\nanother command feeds it `ok: tests-for` as an argument."],[1688,"Without that lock every test action ran its own `npm ci`, and a gate that started while\nanother was still writing the tree died on a SIGBUS reading a short esbuild binary."],[1125,"Without the committed payloads a sandboxed run would read a partial copy of the repo and fail\nfor the wrong reason."],[779,"Without the flag the script passes exactly the parameters it used to pass, and the create\nform's **Git repositories (additional)** textarea stays empty."],[3015,"Without the key the vendor's rate rule decides when a box stops being a candidate; see\nwhat `cooldown_time: 60` is for."],[8,"Work branches"],[5351,"Work happens on short-lived branches cut from the tip of the trunk and merged by pull\nrequest within days: `feat/`, `fix/`, `refactor/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `ci/`."],[5279,"Work it in this order:"],[5295,"Work it in this order:"],[2791,"Working agreement with the assistant: it explains the plan in chat, then waits for the\napproval card in the Chat tab before running anything mutating. If a run looks like it\nis acting without one, stop it and re-read the mode."],[4286,"Workspace agents never reach Authelia either way. The template rewrites the agent URL\nto `http://host.docker.internal:3002`, the plain listener published through\n`CODER_AGENT_TUNNEL_PORT`, so agent traffic stays on the box."],[4452,"Workspace cannot reach LiteLLM -> `CODER_ACCESS_URL`, or `host.docker.internal`"],[4466,"Workspace stuck in *starting* -> startup is blocking"],[3002,"Workspaces and desktops always talk to one base URL,\n`http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1`, and pick a model alias. That is the\nhost-gateway door."],[4287,"Workspaces created before public mode existed need a template re-push plus a\nrestart, to pick up the template's `coder_agent_url` variable (default\n`http://host.docker.internal:3002`). That variable is what keeps agents dialing the\nlocal plain listener whatever the access URL says."],[3293,"Workspaces see a stable OpenAI-compatible URL and stable alias names."],[4465,"Workspaces: startup, images, the toolchain inside them"],[4588,"Workspaces: startup, the golden image, Grok Build (`/ez-learn`, MCP), the toolchain"],[2522,"Write a specific `description` and `when-to-use`. That text is what the model matches\non, so a vague one leaves the skill reachable only by its slash n